2026-05-16	daily	benzinga	complete	# Daily Market Brief — 2026-05-16\n_Covering: Friday May 15, 2026_\n\n## TL;DR (top of mind)\nSPY -1.21%, QQQ -1.51%, SOXX -3.92%, XLK -1.76%, while IGV +1.26% held up better on Friday May 15, 2026; broad risk-off into the weekend hit semis/hardware hardest, while software and a few idiosyncratic winners outperformed.\n\n- **MU Friday May 15, 2026 close: -6.83%** — memory names sold off hard as the market repriced DRAM/HBM strength; no company-specific filing was cited, but the move was consistent with aggressive de-risking in the memory trade (verified tape; market color).\n- **AXTI Friday May 15, 2026 close: +12.33%** — AXT bucked the semiconductor selloff; search results flagged AI demand, a $632.5M equity raise, and record indium phosphide demand tied to AI/data centers (verified tape; Stockstotrade; StockTitan).\n- **WOLF Friday May 15, 2026 close: -10.93%** — Wolfspeed was the sharpest loser in power/WBG, with no fresh filing and selling tied to SiC/EV de-risking and balance-sheet overhang (verified tape; market chatter).\n- **GSIT Friday May 15, 2026 close: -9.42%** — the micro-cap AI/memory-adjacent name was hit hard on positioning and thin liquidity, with no new company catalyst (verified tape; market chatter).\n- **MSFT Friday May 15, 2026 close: +3.63%** — Microsoft stood out on a weak tech tape, reinforcing the relative bid for software/AI monetization over hardware beta (verified tape).\n- **QCOM Friday May 15, 2026 close: +2.03%** — Qualcomm reversed early weakness and finished green; search flow and the tape point to dip-buying and relative strength in mobile/RF versus the rest of semis (verified tape; MarketPulse pre-market conflict noted in probe).\n- **TEAM Friday May 15, 2026 close: +7.39%** — Atlassian was one of the strongest software names, with the move consistent with an earnings/guide-style re-rating in collaboration/dev tools (verified tape; catalyst consistent with earnings reaction).\n\n## Tape recap — Friday May 15, 2026\n### Up\n- **AXTI +12.33%** — outsized move on compound-semiconductor/substrate strength, source: verified tape and Stockstotrade/StockTitan.\n- **TEAM +7.39%** — software leadership, source: verified tape.\n- **NOW +5.02%** — software bid, source: verified tape.\n- **CRM +4.05%** — enterprise software strength, source: verified tape.\n- **ADBE +4.77%** — creative/document software outperformance, source: verified tape.\n- **INTU +4.14%** — quality software bid, source: verified tape.\n- **MSFT +3.63%** — mega-cap software resilience, source: verified tape.\n- **CRM +4.05%** — enterprise software bid, source: verified tape.\n- **SNOW +4.19%** — data software strength, source: verified tape.\n- **DDOG +3.38%** — observability/software strength, source: verified tape.\n- **ZS +4.36%** — cyber strength, source: verified tape.\n- **QCOM +2.03%** — relative strength in wireless semis, source: verified tape.\n- **CSCO +2.08%** — defensive networking/software mix, source: verified tape.\n- **POWI +1.58%** — only notable green name in analog/power, source: verified tape.\n- **AMD?** — no, AMD was down; not listed.\n\n### Down\n- **WOLF -10.93%** — SiC/EV de-risking, source: verified tape.\n- **GSIT -9.42%** — micro-cap AI/memory de-risking, source: verified tape.\n- **MRAM -9.02%** — speculative MRAM selloff, source: verified tape.\n- **AIP -9.19%** — crowded AI/software positioning unwind, source: verified tape.\n- **MU -6.83%** — memory/HBM de-risking, source: verified tape.\n- **NVMI -6.62%** — metrology/process-control derating, source: verified tape.\n- **ARM -6.19%** — valuation-heavy AI/CPU unwind, source: verified tape.\n- **HIMX -6.34%** — display/China hardware weakness, source: verified tape.\n- **POET -15.19%** — speculative optical unwinding, source: verified tape.\n- **ASML -5.17%** — lithography weakness, source: verified tape.\n- **KLAC -4.54%** — process-control weakness, source: verified tape.\n- **AMD -4.45%** — AI GPU profit-taking, source: verified tape.\n- **INTC -5.71%** — foundry skepticism, source: verified tape.\n- **AVGO -3.07%** — AI infrastructure weakness, source: verified tape.\n- **TSM -3.11%** — foundry/advanced packaging pressure, source: verified tape.\n- **SMCI -5.08%** — AI server de-risking, source: verified tape.\n\n## Per-sector / per-theme\n\n### Software & SaaS\n- **TEAM Friday May 15, 2026 close: +7.39%** — Atlassian was the standout leader in collaboration/dev tools; the probe ties the move to earnings/guide-style strength (verified tape; catalyst consistent with earnings reaction).\n- **NOW Friday May 15, 2026 close: +5.02%** — ServiceNow traded higher alongside the software leadership tape, source: verified tape.\n- **CRM Friday May 15, 2026 close: +4.05%** — Salesforce outperformed in a weak Nasdaq session, source: verified tape.\n- **MSFT Friday May 15, 2026 close: +3.63%** — Microsoft advanced despite broad tech weakness, source: verified tape.\n- **SNOW Friday May 15, 2026 close: +4.19%** and **DDOG Friday May 15, 2026 close: +3.38%** — data/observability software stayed bid, source: verified tape.\n\n### Semiconductors\n- **MU Friday May 15, 2026 close: -6.83%** — memory/HBM sold off hard, source: verified tape.\n- **NVDA Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.60%**, **AMD -4.45%**, **AVGO -3.07%**, **TSM -3.11%**, **ARM -6.19%** — AI compute and design-beta were marked lower, source: verified tape.\n- **INTC Friday May 15, 2026 close: -5.71%** — foundry skepticism kept pressure on Intel, source: verified tape and probe chatter.\n- **QCOM Friday May 15, 2026 close: +2.03%** — relative strength versus the red semi tape, source: verified tape.\n\n### AI Infrastructure\n- **SMCI Friday May 15, 2026 close: -5.08%** — AI server builders were sold as hyperscaler/vendor-list and margin worries surfaced, source: verified tape and market chatter.\n- **ANET Friday May 15, 2026 close: -2.86%** and **VRT Friday May 15, 2026 close: -1.98%** — AI data-center networking and power names were de-risked, source: verified tape.\n- **AMZN Friday May 15, 2026 close: -1.64%** — hyperscaler capex exposure was a drag, source: verified tape.\n- **MSFT Friday May 15, 2026 close: +3.63%** — software capture of AI spend held up, source: verified tape.\n\n### Internet & Platforms\n- **MSFT Friday May 15, 2026 close: +3.63%** — best relative move in the group, source: verified tape.\n- **TTD Friday May 15, 2026 close: +3.08%**, **SNAP +2.89%**, **PINS +1.83%** — ad-tech and ad-supported engagement names outperformed, source: verified tape.\n- **GOOGL Friday May 15, 2026 close: -1.15%**, **AMZN -1.64%**, **RBLX -1.91%** — broader internet beta was softer, source: verified tape.\n- **META Friday May 15, 2026 close: -0.21%** and **NFLX -0.52%** — relatively resilient but still red, source: verified tape.\n\n### Communications & Networking\n- **CSCO Friday May 15, 2026 close: +2.08%** — Cisco outperformed on a weak day, with the probe citing its software/security mix and AI networking angle (verified tape).\n- **AAOI Friday May 15, 2026 close: -5.53%**, **LITE -2.83%**, **COHR -2.45%** — optics/photonics names were sold as AI-capex proxy trade de-risked, source: verified tape.\n- **AVGO Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.07%** and **MRVL -1.65%** — AI networking/custom silicon names softened, source: verified tape.\n- **NOK Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.55%** and **ERIC -1.58%** — traditional telecom gear stayed weak, source: verified tape.\n\n### EdgeAI\n- **AKAM Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.34%** — Akamai sold off in the edge/security transition story, source: verified tape.\n- **NET Friday May 15, 2026 close: -1.45%** — Cloudflare pulled back less than AKAM, source: verified tape.\n- **AMBQ Friday May 15, 2026 close: +1.12%** — relative strength in an EdgeAI software name, source: verified tape.\n- **IGV Friday May 15, 2026 close: +1.26%** — software held up better than edge hardware, source: verified tape.\n\n### AI Compute\n- **NVDA Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.60%** — profit-taking and de-risking after a strong run, source: verified tape; probe mentions pre-market strength reversed by close.\n- **AMD Friday May 15, 2026 close: -4.45%** — alternative GPU exposure sold off, source: verified tape.\n- **ARM Friday May 15, 2026 close: -6.19%** — high-multiple architecture story sold hard, source: verified tape.\n- **ALAB Friday May 15, 2026 close: +2.75%** — one of the few green AI-adjacent names, source: verified tape.\n\n### Optical & Photonics\n- **POET Friday May 15, 2026 close: -15.19%** — speculative optical unwind, no fresh PR or filing in the last 24–48h, source: verified tape.\n- **AXTI Friday May 15, 2026 close: +12.33%** — compound-substrate strength on AI optics/RF bottlenecks, source: verified tape plus search results.\n- **AAOI Friday May 15, 2026 close: -5.53%**, **LITE -2.83%**, **LASR -6.22%**, **IPGP -3.16%** — optical hardware, lasers, and industrial photonics were broadly lower, source: verified tape.\n- **AMBQ Friday May 15, 2026 close: +1.12%** — more resilient software-centric edge name, source: verified tape.\n\n### Chip Equipment\n- **ASML Friday May 15, 2026 close: -5.17%**, **KLAC -4.54%**, **LRCX -4.45%** — tool names were sold aggressively, source: verified tape.\n- **AMAT Friday May 15, 2026 close: -0.52%** — relatively resilient versus peers, source: verified tape.\n- **ACMR Friday May 15, 2026 close: +1.02%** — China-domestic WFE beneficiary bucked the tape, source: verified tape.\n- **UCTT Friday May 15, 2026 close: -0.92%**, **ICHR -1.45%** — subsystems moved lower with the tool complex, source: verified tape.\n\n### Memory & Interconnect\n- **MU Friday May 15, 2026 close: -6.83%** — the clearest HBM/memory stress point, source: verified tape.\n- **GSIT Friday May 15, 2026 close: -9.42%** and **MRAM -9.02%** — speculative memory/IP sold off sharply, source: verified tape.\n- **RMBS Friday May 15, 2026 close: -2.75%** — memory IP gave back some gains, source: verified tape.\n- **ASX Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.46%** and **AMKR -2.69%** — advanced packaging/OSAT names traded lower, source: verified tape.\n- **TSEM Friday May 15, 2026 close: -1.08%** and **UMC +0.03%** — mature-node foundry names held up better than leading-edge peers, source: verified tape.\n\n### Analog & Mixed-Signal\n- **AOSL Friday May 15, 2026 close: -5.43%** — sharpest analog loser, source: verified tape.\n- **STM Friday May 15, 2026 close: -4.45%**, **ALGM -4.36%**, **ON -4.13%**, **MPWR -3.16%**, **VSH -3.15%** — broad analog/power de-rating, source: verified tape.\n- **TXN Friday May 15, 2026 close: -1.70%** and **ADI -2.05%** — core analog bellwethers were weaker but less severe than the small caps, source: verified tape.\n- **NXPI Friday May 15, 2026 close: -0.27%** — relative hold-up in auto content, source: verified tape.\n- **POWI Friday May 15, 2026 close: +1.58%** — lone notable green name, source: verified tape.\n\n### Wireless & Mobile\n- **HIMX Friday May 15, 2026 close: -6.34%** — display/China hardware weakness, source: verified tape.\n- **INDI Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.67%** — auto/industrial connectivity sold off, source: verified tape.\n- **AVGO Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.07%** — early pre-market strength reversed, source: verified tape and MarketPulse conflict noted.\n- **SWKS Friday May 15, 2026 close: +3.64%**, **QRVO +2.50%**, **QCOM +2.03%**, **MXL +5.19%** — RF/connectivity names outperformed late in the session, source: verified tape.\n\n### Fab & Foundry\n- **SITM Friday May 15, 2026 close: -5.85%** — timing/IP name sold hard, source: verified tape.\n- **GFS Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.68%** — foundry sentiment weakened, source: verified tape.\n- **ASX Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.46%** — substrate/materials pressure, source: verified tape.\n- **TSM Friday May 15, 2026 close: -3.11%** — foundry leadership was weak, source: verified tape.\n- **UMC Friday May 15, 2026 close: +0.03%** — relative defensiveness in mature-node foundry, source: verified tape