 NVDA / ARM / AVGO** [Friday May 15, 2026 close] — probes flagged valuation and export-control chatter, but no new company filing or earnings catalyst was found (market chatter; confirmed tape moves).\n\n## Stock-specific callouts\n- **AXTI** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **+12.33%** close on AI-datacenter/compound-semiconductor enthusiasm; StockTitan said the company priced a **$550M** offering at **$64.25** and could raise **$632.5M** with the greenshoe — *source: StockTitan; Stockstotrade; confirmed* — angle: supply_chain / positioning.\n- **WOLF** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-10.93%** on SiC/EV de-risking and balance-sheet overhang — *source: verified tape; market chatter* — angle: supply_chain / positioning — confidence: confirmed.\n- **MU** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-6.83%** as HBM/memory positions were cut — *source: verified tape; market chatter* — angle: positioning — confidence: confirmed.\n- **GSIT** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-9.42%** on micro-cap AI/memory de-risking — *source: verified tape* — angle: positioning — confidence: confirmed.\n- **MRAM** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-9.02%** on profit-taking in speculative memory — *source: verified tape* — angle: positioning — confidence: confirmed.\n- **POET** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-15.19%** as speculative optical names were unwound; no fresh 5/15 press release or filing — *source: verified tape; no fresh PR* — angle: positioning — confidence: confirmed.\n- **NVMI** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-6.62%** in process-control derating — *source: verified tape* — angle: positioning — confidence: confirmed.\n- **ARM** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-6.19%** amid export-control and valuation concerns — *source: verified tape; market chatter* — angle: regulatory / positioning — confidence: confirmed.\n- **INTC** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-5.71%** on foundry skepticism — *source: verified tape; probe chatter* — angle: regulatory / supply_chain — confidence: confirmed.\n- **AMD** — Friday May 15, 2026 — **-4.45%** on AI GPU profit-