2026-05-23	daily	benzinga	complete	# Daily Market Brief — 2026-05-25\n_Covering: Friday May 22, 2026_\n\n## TL;DR (top of mind)\n\nDow made new highs in a risk-on session while tech/AI led (**SPY +0.39%, QQQ +0.42%, SOXX +2.33%**, IGV +1.65%, XLK +1.00%) and flows rotated _within_ AI from GPUs into CPUs, servers, networking, power, and select software.\n\n- **NVDA Friday May 22, 2026 close: -2.27% to $215.23** — post‑earnings fade despite FQ1 revenue **$81.6B (+85% Y/Y)**, Q2 guide near **$91B**, a **25x** dividend hike (to $0.25/qtr) and **$80B** buyback; profit‑taking and rotation into “secondary” AI hardware cited (Micron note, sentiment wrap, CPU push) — *Benzinga / earnings & macro recaps*.  \n- **AMD Friday May 22, 2026 close: +4.98% to $466.49** — ripped on Lisa Su’s Taiwan comments: **>$10B** planned AI‑supply‑chain investments, ramp of **Venice CPUs on TSM 2nm**, and view that AI inferencing/agentic workloads are driving CPU demand **>35% CAGR** over five years — *Benzinga (Taiwan AI briefing)*.  \n- **QCOM Friday May 22, 2026 close: +12.48% to $236.80** — one of the biggest semiconductor movers as SMH outperformed; Benzinga tied the move to an expanded Snapdragon Digital Chassis deal with Stellantis plus prior Q2 beat, dividend hike and buyback — *Benzinga (markets Friday)*.  \n- **DELL Friday May 22, 2026 close: +17.19% to $296.01** — hit record highs on AI‑server backlog commentary and Wells Fargo **Overweight / PT to $270** ahead of earnings; Street looking for **$35.75B revenue (+52% Y/Y)** as Dell is framed against **$725B** aggregate hyperscaler capex — *Benzinga (movers, analyst notes)*.  \n- **HPE Friday May 22, 2026 close: +10.98% to $37.44** — squeezed higher as CNAS data showed **NVDA‑led U.S. stack** (including HPE and DELL) supplying the majority of sovereign AI projects globally, positioning HPE as a recurring server vendor into national AI builds — *Benzinga (sovereign AI)*.  \n- **MRVL Friday May 22, 2026 close: +2.71% to $195.01** — printe