ctivity laggard in a strong semi tape — *Wireless & Mobile*.  \n- **ALMU -2.86%** — only decliner in specialty materials/IP basket; no specific news — *Specialty Materials & IP*.  \n\n---\n\n## Per-sector / per-theme\n\n### Semiconductors\n\n- **Sector tape** — Friday May 22, 2026: **SOXX +2.33%**, **IGV +1.65%**, **XLK +1.00%**, **SPY +0.39%**, **QQQ +0.42%**; leadership from **QCOM +12.48%**, **AMD +4.98%**, **TXN +4.20%**, **ARM +3.92%**, **ASML +2.85%**, **MRVL +2.71%**, **KLAC +2.34%**, **LRCX +1.85%**, **INTC +1.26%**, **AMAT +0.92%**, **MU +0.65%**, while **NVDA -2.27%**, **TSM -0.95%**, **AVGO -0.18%** lagged — *Benzinga (Semiconductors)*.  \n- **NVDA -2.27% (close $215.23)** — FQ1 revenue **$81.6B (+85% Y/Y, vs ~$79.15B est)**, data‑center **$75.2B (~92% of total)**, adj. EPS **$1.87 vs $1.77 est**, non‑GAAP GM ~**75%** with similar guide; Q2 revenue guided near **$91B**; dividend hiked from **$0.01 to $0.25**, buyback raised by **$80B**; commentary flagged tight HBM supply and said VeraRubin will be “supply‑constrained for the foreseeable future;” separate coverage noted U.S. controls cutting China AI‑chip share from **~90% to zero** — *Benzinga (earnings, supply, China)*.  \n- **AMD +4.98% (close $466.49)** — Lisa Su said AMD will invest **> $10B** into Taiwan’s AI ecosystem (advanced packaging, substrates, rack‑scale), is ramping **Venice CPUs on TSM 2nm**, sees AI market **> $1T** in **3–4 years** with CPU market growing **>35% annually** for five years; China about **20% of revenue**, but AMD is “not counting on advanced China chip sales” — *Benzinga (Taiwan speech, Reuters recap)*.  \n- **TSM -0.95% (close $403.86)** — despite being AMD’s 2nm partner and ramping 2nm/1nm R&D, Bloomberg‑linked note via Benzinga said Asia’s AI trade is expanding beyond TSM into memory, CPUs, robotics and infra; Street models **EPS $3.69 vs $2.47 YoY** and **revenue $39.76B vs $30.07B YoY** for **estimated July 16, 2026** print, with **P/E 35.1x** and PTs at **$450–$480**