time since 2022; STRC preferred stock fell below $98 par; Peter Schiff declared "death spiral" begun\n- Clean energy ETF PBW +130% since Inauguration Day despite Trump's "Green New Scam" rhetoric — AI data center power demand driving fuel cell, battery stocks\n- NY state legislature moving toward 1-year AI data center construction moratorium; Sanders claims vindication\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **PANW** Q3 rev $3.0B (+31% YoY), adj EPS $0.85, both beat; FY raised; **HPE** Q2 EPS $0.79 vs $0.53 est; **GME** record net income $389.6M, $2B buyback; **ULTA** EPS $7.74 vs $6.86 est |\n| Macro | JOLTS April 7.618M vs 6.860M est; Goldman CEO says rate cut odds "gone down materially"; API crude draw 6.75M bbl vs 3.6M est |\n| Tech | Huang calls MRVL "next trillion-dollar company"; Anthropic files confidential S-1 at ~$965B valuation; ChatGPT hits ~1B monthly users; SpaceX targets $75B IPO raise at $135/share |\n| Commodities | WTI crude ~$90.84; national gas avg $4.29/gal; Moody's Zandi estimates $100B cumulative Iran war cost to US consumers |\n| Geopolitics | Trump says Iran talks "going on continuously"; Rubio sets Hormuz reopening as condition #1; US conducts additional strikes on Iran's Qeshm Island |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **AVGO** Q2 FY26 earnings Wed Jun 3 after close; analysts expect rev $22.1B, EPS $2.32; AI revenue was +106% YoY in Q1 ⚠️\n- **CRWD** Q1 earnings Thu Jun 4 after close; analysts expect rev $1.36B, EPS $0.88; PANW results raised sector expectations ⚠️\n- **MU** earnings Jun 24 (confirmed); analysts expect rev $33.88B, EPS $19.29; stock at new ATH ~$1,063; June is historically MU's worst month (avg -1.35%)\n- **AAPL** WWDC keynote Jun 9; potential smart glasses teaser; N50 glasses timeline reportedly slipped to late 2027\n- **SpaceX** IPO expected mid-June on Nasdaq under ticker SPCX; targeting $1.75-1.8T valuation\n- **CELC** FDA PDUFA date Jul 17 for gedatolisib;