2026-06-10	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-06-10 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: SMCI announces $7B equity raise to fund ~$39B AI server backlog sending shares down ~11%, semiconductors extend last week's selloff with MRVL -11.7% and ARM -8.1%, while U.S.-Iran strikes escalate overnight with IRGC retaliating against bases in Jordan/Bahrain/Kuwait ahead of May CPI at 8:30 a.m.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| MRVL | -11.7% | Mega | Profit-taking; 250% above 200d SMA; no new catalyst | AI Compute / Semis |\n| ARM | -8.1% | Mega | Continued unwind from 5D -20.3%; sector rotation | AI Compute / Semis |\n| GLW | -8.5% | Mega | Gapped down Jun 8; no identified catalyst | Optical / Components |\n| DELL | -6.3% | Mega | Profit-taking after 226% 12mo run; tech selloff | AI Infra / Servers |\n| APH | +5.5% | Mega | No identified catalyst; connectors strength | Industrials / Connectors |\n| BX | +4.8% | Mega | AI XPV Platform launch w/ Apollo, Broadcom ($35B) | Alt Assets / AI Infra |\n| TMO | +4.1% | Mega | No identified catalyst | Life Sciences |\n| INTC | -3.8% | Mega | Reversal from Mon +11%; Cramer skeptical on 2028 foundry | AI Compute / Foundry |\n| MU | -2.9% | Mega | Reversal; Goldman PT raised to $900 (Neutral) | Memory / AI |\n| SMCI | -11.3% PM | Mid | $7B equity raise: $1.25B common + $3.75B pref + $2B ATM | AI Servers |\n| PAYO | +25.5% | Small | Nuvei in advanced talks to acquire at ~$2.3B incl debt | Payments / M&A |\n| ALHC | +24.3% | Small | Momentum continuation; 5D +43.5%; no new catalyst | Healthcare / Managed Care |\n| VELO | +21.7% | Small | Aurelia partnership for gas turbine additive mfg | 3D Printing / Energy |\n| CECO | +17.5% | Small | Thermon acquisition closed; FY26 rev guide $1.275B–$1.375B | Industrials / Env Services |\n| FCEL | +16.2% | Small | Data centers = ~90% of pipeline; Canaccord upgrade to Buy PT $30 | Clean Energy / Data Centers |\n| VECO | +11.1% | Small | Follow-on NSA500 order from logic customer | Semis Equipment |\n| BAP | +11.4% | Large | No identified catalyst; 5D +3.5% | LatAm Financials |\n| CBRS | -5.8% | Large | Gapped down Jun 8; no identified catalyst | AI Compute / Semis |\n| RKT | +7.4% | Large | Upsized $1.5B senior notes from $1.2B | Mortgage / Fintech |\n| HYLN | -13.1% | Small | Needham initiates Buy PT $9 vs $6.32 close; vol spike | EV / Hydrogen |\n| CHWY | — | Large | Q1 EPS $0.43 vs $0.39 est; FY rev guide cut to $13.4B–$13.55B vs $13.84B est ⚠️ | E-Commerce / Pet |\n| ORCL | — | Large | Q4 earnings tonight; est EPS $1.96, rev $19.09B ⚠️ | Cloud / AI Infra |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Semiconductor Selloff Deepens — Rotation + Profit-Taking** `AI Compute / Semis` → ongoing\n\nThe post-Broadcom unwind that began Friday (-4.18% Nasdaq) extended Tuesday and is carrying into Wednesday pre-market. **MRVL** -11.7% leads losses despite no new catalyst — the stock trades ~250% above its 200-day SMA. **ARM** -8.1% (5D -20.3%), **AMD** -4.0%, **DELL** -6.3%, and **MU** -2.9% are all giving back gains from their multi-month AI rallies. **INTC** -3.8% reverses Monday's +11.2% surge on the Google/NVIDIA foundry reports; Cramer called himself "VERY skeptical" about the 2028 timeline. BTIG's Jonathan Krinsky flagged that in 17 of 21 prior instances where Nasdaq fell 4%+ on a Friday, that Friday's intraday low was breached in the next 5 sessions — pattern confirmed Tuesday.\n\n- **MRVL**: 12mo +316.7%; P/E ~99x; consensus Buy, avg PT $225.63; Barclays PT $275\n- **MU**: Goldman Sachs raised PT to $900 (Neutral); earnings Jun 24, est EPS $19.33 vs $1.91 YoY ⚠️\n- **INTC**: Google reportedly ordered >3M AI chips for 2028; NVIDIA testing 18A process; YTD +199%\n- **ARM**: 5D -20.3%; P/E ~159x; no new catalyst identified\n- **DELL**: 12mo +226%; P/E ~35x; trades 17% above 20d SMA; Benzinga Edge momentum score 98.82\n- **STM** -3.5% (5D -8.5%, vol 2.3×) — legacy semi weakness spreading to European chipmakers\n\n**SMCI $7B Equity Raise to Fund $39B AI Server Backlog** `AI Servers` → new\n\n**SMCI** fell ~11% premarket after filing for $7B in concurrent equity offerings: $1.25B common stock, ~$3.75B in depositary shares (mandatory convertible preferred), and a $2B ATM program launching no earlier than Q3 2026.\n\n- Proceeds: to fund ~$39B of orders received "in recent weeks" from >20 customers for AI servers including Data Center Building Block Solutions\n- Bookrunners: JPMorgan, Goldman Sachs, Citigroup\n- Stock was at $40.64 at close Jun 9; trading ~$36 premarket\n- Dilution risk is the immediate concern; backlog disclosure is the offsetting bull case\n\n**U.S.-Iran Escalation Overnight** `Macro / Geopolitical` → new\n\nTrump ordered strikes against Iran Tuesday after a U.S. Apache helicopter was downed near the Strait of Hormuz. IRGC retaliated, targeting U.S. bases in Jordan (Al Azraq), Bahrain (5th Fleet HQ), and Kuwait. Jordan intercepted 5 Iranian missiles. CENTCOM said U.S. strikes have concluded. Trump told WSJ the helicopter incident "wasn't a big deal" and later posted Iran's military is "a complete and total mess."\n\n- Brent crude rose above $91 before settling; WTI +0.48% in early NY session to ~$88.62\n- Gold fell 2.10% to ~$4,170 — not acting as a haven\n- U.S. official told CNN strikes won't disrupt ongoing negotiations\n- Trump said a "very, very good deal" could come in "two or three days"\n- Illinois froze its gas tax inflation hike; national avg gas above $4/gal\n- VLCC tanker orders at all-time-high 262 vessels, surpassing 2008 peak\n\n**May CPI Due 8:30 a.m. — Consensus 4.2% YoY** `Macro` → ongoing\n\n- FactSet consensus: 4.2% YoY, which would be highest since April 2023\n- CME FedWatch: 98.2% probability of no change at June FOMC\n- Markets pricing ~50% odds of a rate *hike* as soon as October\n- 10Y Treasury at 4.53%; 2Y at 4.14%\n- S&P 500 futures -0.54%; Nasdaq 100 futures -0.88% premarket\n- Bitcoin plunged to ~$61,000, down ~9% over past week\n\n**Oracle Q4 Earnings Tonight** `Cloud / AI Infra` → ongoing\n\n**ORCL** reports after the close. This is the single most important earnings event of the session.\n\n- Consensus: EPS $1.96 vs $1.70 YoY; revenue $19.09B vs $15.90B YoY\n- Record revenue if achieved (prior record $17.19B in Q3)\n- Polymarket: 91% odds "Growth" mentioned frequently; 87% "Data Center" ≥10 times; 80% "Cloud" ≥20 times\n- Recent PT raises: TD Cowen to $300, Oppenheimer to $275, BofA to $240, Evercore to $245, Cantor Fitzgerald to $284\n- Stock -2.8% Tuesday to $205.81; down 7.7% over 6 months\n- Company cut ~18%–20K jobs in April per TD Cowen\n\n**Chewy Q1 Beat But FY Guide Cut** `E-Commerce / Pet` → new\n\n**CHWY** reported Q1 EPS $0.43 vs $0.39 est; revenue $3.357B vs $3.352B est (+7.7% YoY). However, FY2026 sales guidance was lowered to $13.4B–$13.55B from $13.6B–$13.75B, well below the $13.84B Street estimate. Q2 EPS guided to $0.36 vs $0.25 est but Q2 revenue $3.30B–$3.33B vs $3.38B est.\n\n**Private Credit Redemption Wave Continues** `Alt Assets` → ongoing\n\nBlue Owl Credit Income Corp (OCIC) raised $500M in investment-grade bonds (5Y notes, 2.55% spread over Treasuries) after gating redemptions at 5%. This follows similar caps at **BX** (BCRED, ~10% requests), Cliffwater (17% requests), Monroe Capital (~10%), and Partners Group ($8.6B fund). Apollo President Jim Zelter warned "we are not through the turbulence yet."\n\n- **BX** +4.8% Tuesday despite BCRED redemption headlines\n- Ares closed Pathfinder Fund III at $8.5B hard cap (target was $6.5B); largest ABF fund globally\n\n**SpaceX IPO Oversubscribed ~3.5x** `IPO / Space` → ongoing\n\nSpaceX IPO drew >$250B in investor demand vs $75B target. Pricing expected Thursday afternoon; debut Friday on Nasdaq. Valuation ~$1.75T — more than all 12 S&P 500 aerospace/defense companies combined (~$1.5T). Goldman Sachs reportedly projects $474B total revenue by 2030. Musk said SpaceX could put 1M tons of payload in orbit in ~5 years. Multiple leveraged ETFs (SPCU, SPCF, SPAL) planned for Jun 12 launch.\n\n**Apple WWDC: Siri AI Runs on NVIDIA/Google Cloud** `Consumer Tech / AI` → new\n\n**AAPL** -3.64% Tuesday post-WWDC. Most advanced AI model will run on NVIDIA chips through Google Cloud, not Apple silicon. Agentic Siri in beta later this year, not yet in Europe/China. JPMorgan maintained Overweight PT $325, calling it a long-term game changer. No separate Apple AI subscription launched.\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **PAYO** +25.5% on 17.5× avg volume: Reuters exclusive reports Nuvei in advanced talks to acquire Payoneer at ~$2.3B including debt — cross-border payments consolidation.\n- **FCEL** +16.2% (5D -29.8%): data centers now ~90% of sales pipeline; 4GW pipeline up 267% QoQ; Canaccord upgraded to Buy PT $30 from Hold/$12.\n- **FLEX** selected to join S&P 500 index; also sold subsidiary Sheldahl to Chase Corp.\n- Social Security trust fund projected to exhaust reserves in 2032 per Trustees' annual report; 22% benefit cuts after depletion for 70M+ Americans.\n- Databricks reportedly eyeing $165B–$175B valuation in new round, potential 2027 IPO.\n- CoreWeave insiders sold >$2.3B since March 2025 IPO; Chanos called it "well above normal behavior."\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **CHWY** Q1 EPS $0.43 vs $0.39 est; FY guide cut to $13.4B–$13.55B vs $13.84B est. **ORCL** reports tonight, est EPS $1.96 / rev $19.09B. **CNM** Q1 EPS $0.72 vs $0.67 est, rev $1.91B; FY guide affirmed. |\n| Macro | May CPI due 8:30 a.m., consensus 4.2% YoY. U.S. trade deficit narrowed to $55.9B in April. NFIB Optimism Index fell 0.6 pts to 95.3 in May. |\n| Geopolitical | IRGC struck U.S. bases in Jordan, Bahrain, Kuwait after Trump ordered Iran strikes; Jordan intercepted 5 missiles; CENTCOM says strikes concluded. |\n| Tech | Apple WWDC: Siri AI runs on NVIDIA/Google Cloud; no separate AI subscription. Meta partners with Reliance for 168MW AI data center in India. |\n| Commodities | Gold -2.10% to ~$4,170; crude +0.48% to ~$88.62; Bitcoin -2.25% to ~$61,490. |\n| M&A | Nuvei reportedly in advanced talks to acquire **PAYO** at ~$2.3B. GSK acquiring Nuvalent for $10.6B ($124/share). Figure Tech acquiring Kiavi for $717M. |\n| IPOs | SpaceX IPO >$250B demand vs $75B target; pricing Thu, listing Fri. OpenAI filed confidential S-1. |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **ORCL** Q4 earnings after close today (Jun 10); est EPS $1.96, rev $19.09B. Options imply ~7% move.\n- **MU** earnings Jun 24; est EPS $19.33 vs $1.91 YoY, rev $33.9B vs $9.3B YoY.\n- **SpaceX IPO** pricing expected Thu Jun 12 afternoon; Nasdaq debut Fri Jun 13. ~$1.75T valuation.\n- **May CPI** release 8:30 a.m. ET today; consensus 4.2% YoY — if confirmed, highest since April 2023.\n- **LEN** (Lennar) Q2 earnings after close Thu Jun 11; est EPS $1.24, rev $8.07B. KBW downgraded to Underperform PT $86.\n- **NAVN** (Navan) Q1 earnings after close today; est EPS $0.01, rev $205.27M.\n- **Russell reconstitution** effective after close Jun 26 — Bloom Energy (BE) moving from R2000 to R1000.\n- **USMCA review** — U.S./Mexico/Canada expected to miss Jul 1 deadline per Bloomberg.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- Micro/nano-cap pre-market movers (CIIT +311%, CHOW +246%, WCT +147%, MSW +130%) — illiquid names with no institutional relevance.\n- Broad "fear and greed" commentary — CNN index at 33.5 ("Fear") is directionally obvious given the tape.\n- AAPL WWDC hot-takes about Siri's long-term monetization potential — the feature ships in beta later this year with no revenue impact in 2026.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 216373, "output_tokens": 4142, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 1.081865, "total_cost_usd": 1.185415, "output_cost_usd": 0.10355, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write