2026-06-12	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 June 12, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Semiconductor equipment stocks surge 11–14% on Cantor/BofA upgrades and INTC's rare double upgrade to Buy, SpaceX begins trading today at $135/share ($1.77T valuation) in the largest IPO in history, ADBE drops ~6% despite a Q2 beat as it defers price hikes for AI freemium push and loses its CFO, while US-Iran MOU draft with 60-day sanctions waiver and $300B reconstruction plan nears signing as oil drops below $84.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| SNDK | +14.0% | Mega | BofA raises PT to $2,100; NAND supply tightening | Memory |\n| KLAC | +13.1% | Mega | Cantor PT to $2,500; Barclays PT to $2,250 | Semis Equipment |\n| LRCX | +12.7% | Mega | Cantor PT to $425 from $320; "multi-year upcycle" | Semis Equipment |\n| ARM | +11.5% | Mega | BofA PT to $335; Mizuho PT to $500; agentic CPU thesis | AI Compute |\n| AMAT | +11.1% | Mega | Cantor PT to $650; Barclays PT to $590 | Semis Equipment |\n| INTC | +10.3% | Mega | BofA double upgrade to Buy, PT $135; CPU TAM $170B by 2030 | AI Compute |\n| MRVL | +9.8% | Mega | New CFO Dan Durn (ex-Adobe); reaffirms Q2 guide; S&P 500 add | AI Networking |\n| MU | +9.4% | Mega | Wolfe PT to $1,250; earnings Jun 24 ⚠️ | Memory |\n| ASML | +8.6% | Mega | Broad semi equipment rally | Semis Equipment |\n| AMD | +8.3% | Mega | BofA PT to $560; top CPU pick for agentic AI | AI Compute |\n| ENTG | +12.9% | Large | Broad semi materials rally | Semis Materials |\n| ESLT | +12.1% | Large | No specific catalyst identified | Defense |\n| SATS | +11.5% | Large | SpaceX stake revaluation; $17B spectrum deal | Space / SpaceX IPO |\n| CPNG | +11.2% | Large | Korea data-breach fine $278M, below feared max | E-Commerce |\n| ASTS | +11.0% | Large | SpaceX IPO halo; BlueBird 8-10 launch Jun 17 ⚠️ | Space / Satellite |\n| SMCI | +4.5% | Large | Rebound after -28% on $7B equity/preferred offering | AI Infrastructure |\n| ADBE | -6.3% | Mega | Q2 beat ($5.96 vs $5.82 est); CFO departs Jun 15; defers price hikes | SaaS |\n| SPCE | +35.3% | Small | SpaceX IPO sympathy; redeemed $30.5M notes | Space / SpaceX IPO |\n| VELO | +34.3% | Small | Aurelia Technologies gas turbine partnership | Additive Mfg |\n| ATEX | +28.1% | Small | Q4 FY26 results; 4 new utility customers signed | Spectrum / Telecom |\n| QH | +43.2% | Small | No specific catalyst identified | Idiosyncratic |\n| VSAT | +17.3% | Mid | U.S. Space Force PTS-G contract; $4B program ceiling | Defense / Satellite |\n| SHAZ | +17.0% | Small | 6-yr NVIDIA deal for 72MW / 40K GB300 GPUs in Australia | AI Infrastructure |\n| FLY | +19.0% | Mid | SpaceX IPO sector sympathy | Space |\n| RKLB | +4.5% PM | Large | Joining Nasdaq-100 effective Jun 22 ⚠️ | Space |\n| VPG | +11.7% | Small | Record Q1 orders >$100M; sensors demand from AI/defense | Sensors / Industrial |\n| CRWV | +4.9% PM | Large | Nasdaq-100 inclusion Jun 22; $3.25B notes priced ⚠️ | AI Infrastructure |\n| CASY | +1.4% | Large | Multiple PT raises (Wells $960, Keybanc $970, BMO $950) | Retail |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Semiconductor Equipment Upgrades — Multi-Year Upcycle Call** `Semis Equipment` → new\n\nCantor Fitzgerald analyst C.J. Muse described the industry as in the "early innings of a multi-year supply-constrained and durable upcycle," triggering a wave of price target increases that sent equipment stocks up 11–13% Thursday.\n\n- **KLAC** +13.1%: Cantor PT raised to $2,500 from $2,000; Barclays PT raised to $2,250 from $1,700 (Overweight)\n- **LRCX** +12.7%: Cantor PT raised to $425 from $320; Barclays PT raised to $335 from $275 (Equal-Weight)\n- **AMAT** +11.1%: Cantor PT raised to $650 from $575; Barclays PT raised to $590 from $500 (Overweight)\n- **ASML** +8.6%: riding the same broad equipment rally\n- **TSMC** (TSM): 3nm capacity expanded to 160K–175K wafers/month in Q2 but demand still exceeds supply; reports suggest up to 15% price hike in H2 2026; next earnings July 16 ⚠️\n\n**CPU Renaissance — Agentic AI Expands the TAM** `AI Compute` → ongoing\n\nBofA's Vivek Arya issued rare double upgrades and target raises across CPU names, framing agentic AI as a structural demand driver that expands the server CPU TAM to $170B by 2030.\n\n- **INTC** +10.3%: BofA double upgrade from Underperform to Buy, PT raised $96→$135; models >$6 EPS by 2030; stock up ~210% YTD — best year since 1975; only in 16% of S&P 500 fund portfolios; next earnings Jul 23 ⚠️\n- **AMD** +8.3%: BofA maintains Buy, PT raised $500→$560; named top CPU pick; Barclays PT $665 (Overweight); TD Cowen PT $600\n- **ARM** +11.5%: BofA PT raised $245→$335 (Neutral); Mizuho PT $500 (Outperform); Barclays PT $360 (Overweight); next earnings ~Jul 29 ⚠️\n- **NVDA**: began pitching Vera AI CPU to Chinese customers, available as early as August; hired veteran lobbyist Bruce Andrews (ex-Intel) as Chief External Affairs Officer; Wedbush's Bryson calls NVDA "undervalued"; next earnings Aug 26 ⚠️\n\n**Memory Pricing Cycle Intensifies** `Memory` → ongoing\n\nMemory names rallied 9–14% as analysts raised estimates on tightening DRAM and NAND supply against accelerating AI data-center demand.\n\n- **SNDK** +14.0%: BofA PT raised $1,550→$2,100 (Buy); stock up >5,000% since Feb 2025 spinoff; five multi-year contracts with $42B minimum committed revenue; FY27E rev $44B, EPS ~$188; next earnings Aug 13 ⚠️\n- **MU** +9.4%: Wolfe PT raised to $1,250 (Outperform), projects FY27 rev $226.5B, EPS $135; Goldman PT $900 (Neutral); Wells Fargo PT $1,220 (Overweight); consensus avg PT $927; next earnings Jun 24 ⚠️\n- **STM** +10.1%: bullish call sweep activity $70 strike Jun 18 expiry\n- Retail investors net-sold equities for 3 consecutive days through Wednesday — first such streak since March 2020 — partially to raise cash for SpaceX IPO; BNP Paribas cited $6.5B retail inflows into MU in past month\n\n**SpaceX IPO — Largest Ever, Market-Wide Liquidity Event** `Space / IPO` → new\n\nSpaceX begins trading today on Nasdaq under SPCX at $135/share, targeting $75B raise at ~$1.77T valuation — the largest IPO in recorded history.\n\n- Retail orders alone exceeded $70B; at least 20% of shares allocated to retail investors\n- Oppenheimer initiated at $190 PT (41% upside); New Street Research PT $165 (Overweight), projects $195.3B revenue by 2030\n- Crypto perps on Hyperliquid/Binance priced at ~$165 (implying $2.2T valuation); Polymarket gives 42% chance of closing above $2.2T\n- Space sympathy: **SPCE** +35.3%, **FLY** +19.0%, **ASTS** +11.0% (BlueBird launch Jun 17 ⚠️), **SATS** +11.5% (SpaceX equity stake from $17B spectrum deal)\n- **RKLB** joining Nasdaq-100 effective Jun 22; **CRWV**, **ALAB**, **NBIS**, **TER** also added; replacing CHTR, CTSH, INSM, VRSK, ZS ⚠️\n- **DXYZ** (Destiny Tech100) up 3.5% PM; 16.2% SpaceX exposure; trades at ~100% premium to $19.97 NAV; 17% short interest\n- Vanda Research: retail net-sold equities 3 straight days, Monday was largest single-day retail sell since Nov 2023, concentrated in chip names to fund SPCX allocation\n\n**Adobe — Beat-and-Sell on AI Freemium Pivot** `SaaS` → new\n\n**ADBE** -6.3% after-hours despite double beat and raised guidance, as management revealed it is deferring Creative Cloud price increases to pursue AI freemium funnel, creating a ~$500M organic ARR headwind in H2.\n\n- Q2 rev $6.62B (+11% YoY) vs $6.46B est; adj EPS $5.96 vs $5.82 est\n- Q3 guide: rev $6.67B–$6.72B vs $6.51B est; adj EPS $6.05–$6.10 vs $5.77 est\n- FY26 guide raised: rev $26.50B–$26.60B (from $25.90B–$26.10B) vs $26.04B est; adj EPS $24.35–$24.45 (from $23.30–$23.50) vs $23.52 est\n- AI-first ARR surpassed $500M, tripled YoY; total ARR $27.1B\n- CFO Dan Durn departs Jun 15; Steve Day named interim CFO\n- **MRVL** hired Dan Durn as its new CFO, effective Jun 15; reaffirmed Q2 guidance\n- Stifel downgrade to Hold, PT $350→$200; Evercore ISI downgrade to In-Line, PT $325→$225; Piper Sandler PT $280→$240 (Neutral); Baird PT $270→$230 (Neutral)\n- Stock now -37.5% YTD, near 52-week low of $204.80\n\n**US-Iran MOU Draft — Oil Drops, Sanctions Waiver Detailed** `Macro / Geopolitics` → ongoing\n\nA 14-point draft MOU between the US and Iran has emerged, with potential signing in Geneva as soon as Sunday around the G7 meeting.\n\n- Key provisions: 60-day sanctions waiver for Iran oil exports; $300B reconstruction plan; reopening of Strait of Hormuz; Iran commits to never acquiring nuclear weapon; nuclear talks within 60 days\n- Crude oil fell 4.6% Friday AM to ~$83.63/barrel; Brent at $89\n- Iran Parliament Speaker Ghalibaf warned "wrong strategies" could create "endless quagmire" and explode energy infrastructure\n- Netanyahu's office: Israel is not party to MOU but appreciates Trump's commitment\n- Iran state media: no final decision from Supreme Leader Khamenei yet\n- US PPI headline rose to 6.5% in May (highest since Dec 2022); core below forecasts\n- 10Y Treasury at 4.44%; CME FedWatch: 96.4% probability of no change at June FOMC\n\n**SMCI — Post-Dilution Volatility Continues** `AI Infrastructure` → ongoing\n\n**SMCI** +4.5% rebounding after -28% Wednesday on $7B equity financing announcement; still -33.8% over 5 days.\n\n- Priced 45.45M common shares at $27.50 + 75M depositary shares at $50 (7% mandatory convertible preferred)\n- Net proceeds: ~$1.22B common + ~$3.68B preferred + $1.25B ATM program\n- Funds to fulfill ~$39B AI server orders from 20+ customers\n- Wolfe Research initiated Peer Perform; Mizuho Neutral, PT $44\n- Consensus Hold from 24 analysts; avg PT $32.70; expected earnings ~Aug 4 ⚠️\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **TSM** 3nm wafer prices may rise up to 15% in H2 2026 due to persistent supply shortages; current capacity 160K–175K wafers/month still insufficient — potential margin tailwind for foundry-dependent chipmakers.\n- **Global Witness report** alleges conflict coltan from DRC reaches NVDA, MSFT supply chains through Rwandan laundering; Apple halted purchases from both Rwanda and DRC; NVDA and MSFT did not respond.\n- **FedEx** announced €3 customs duty on all low-value shipments into EU from Jul 1 as €150 de minimis exemption ends — impacts Temu/Shein cross-border economics (BABA, PDD exposure).\n- **Retail cash rotation**: U.S. equity leveraged ETF assets hit record $175B, mostly in Nasdaq/semi plays; BNP Paribas estimates $50B in combined retail + passive flows could shift to SpaceX, creating potential unwinding pressure in chip names.\n- **BABA** RSI at 29.1; stock -16% over past month; Pentagon expanded blacklist to include Alibaba, Baidu, BYD.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | ADBE Q2 rev $6.62B vs $6.46B est, adj EPS $5.96 vs $5.82; FY26 rev guide raised to $26.50B–$26.60B; CFO departs Jun 15; shares -6.3% |\n| Earnings | RH Q1 loss -$1.97 vs -$2.11 est; rev $800.3M vs $792.8M est; raised FY26 sales guide to +4.5%–8%; launching "RH Estates" high-end line |\n| Earnings | LEN Q2 adj EPS $1.31 vs $1.25 est; rev $7.94B vs $8.02B est (miss); shares -2.7% after-hours |\n| IPO | SpaceX prices at $135/share, $1.77T valuation; $75B raise; retail orders >$70B; Oppenheimer PT $190; begins trading today |\n| Macro | US-Iran 14-point draft MOU: 60-day sanctions waiver, $300B reconstruction, Hormuz reopening; potential signing as soon as Sunday in Geneva |\n| Macro | US PPI May headline 6.5% (highest since Dec 2022); core below estimates; initial jobless claims 229K vs 219K est |\n| Macro | UK GDP April -0.1% MoM as expected; manufacturing production +0.4% vs -0.2% est; Germany CPI May 2.6% YoY as expected |\n| Tech | NVIDIA pitching Vera AI CPU to Chinese customers; available as early as August; hired ex-Intel lobbyist Bruce Andrews |\n| Tech | SHAZ signed 6-year NVIDIA deal: 72MW data center capacity in Australia, up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs; total capacity now 132MW |\n| Analyst | Cantor: KLAC PT $2,500, LRCX PT $425, AMAT PT $650; BofA: INTC upgrade Buy PT $135, AMD PT $560, SNDK PT $2,100 |\n| Index | Nasdaq-100 June rebalance: adding CRWV, ALAB, NBIS, RKLB, TER; removing CHTR, CTSH, INSM, VRSK, ZS; effective Jun 22 |\n| M&A | MRVL appoints Dan Durn (departing ADBE CFO) as new CFO effective Jun 15; reaffirms Q2 guidance |\n| Defense | VSAT wins U.S. Space Force PTS-G prime contract for dual-band mini-GEO satellite; program ceiling $4B; IOC ≥2029 |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **MU earnings Jun 24**: consensus EPS $19.46 (vs $1.91 YoY), rev $34.07B (vs $9.30B); Street-high PT $1,500 from Cantor ⚠️\n- **ASTS BlueBird 8/9/10 launch Jun 17** aboard SpaceX Falcon 9 from Cape Canaveral ⚠️\n- **Nasdaq-100 rebalance effective Jun 22**: CRWV, ALAB, NBIS, RKLB, TER added; passive fund rebalancing creates forced buying ⚠️\n- **SpaceX options trading begins Jun 16** — first hedging tools available for SPCX ⚠️\n- **PLAY earnings Jun 15 after close**: consensus EPS $0.66, rev $578.4M\n- **KR earnings Jun 18**: consensus EPS $1.59, rev $45.49B; JPMorgan PT cut $72→$70 (Neutral)\n- **INTC earnings Jul 23**: consensus EPS $0.19 (vs -$0.10 YoY), rev $14.4B\n- **SMCI earnings ~Aug 4**: consensus EPS $0.69, rev $11.73B\n- **US-Iran deal signing potentially as soon as Sunday** near G7 meeting in Geneva; could resolve Strait of Hormuz shipping and unlock Iranian oil exports within 60 days\n- **June FOMC meeting Jun 17**: 96.4% probability of hold per CME FedWatch\n- **June preliminary U-Mich consumer sentiment** due today at 10:00 AM ET\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **Industry peer comparison tables** (NVDA vs AVGO vs MU vs AMD etc.): auto-generated valuation comparisons with no new data; these recirculate weekly.\n- **QH +43%**: No identifiable catalyst; micro-cap ($542M) with 17.6× avg volume; likely retail-driven momentum with no fundamental anchor.\n- **Political noise** (Ariana Grande vs White House, Trump impeachment expungement, Cl