2026-06-18	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-06-18 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Memory/storage stocks (MU +4.3%, WDC +5.9%, STX +4.8%) extend their rally on Apple's admission that memory costs are "unsustainable" and multiple analyst target raises ahead of MU earnings June 24; INTC surges ~8% premarket after Trump confirms Apple, Nvidia, and Tesla chip manufacturing deals; HOOD +10.7% on Deutsche Bank upgrade and 10% workforce cut; ACN misses revenue estimates; Fed held rates at 3.50-3.75% with hawkish dot plot shift under new Chair Warsh.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| INTC | +8.4% PM | Mega | Trump confirms AAPL/NVDA/TSLA to build chips with Intel; 18A-P risk production | Foundry / AI Compute |\n| ARM | +6.6% | Mega | Multi-week momentum; AI CPU cycle continuation | AI Compute |\n| GEV | +6.0% | Mega | Bernstein initiates Outperform, PT $1,206 | Power / AI Infrastructure |\n| VRT | +6.1% | Mega | AI data center power infrastructure demand | Power / AI Infrastructure |\n| WDC | +5.9% | Mega | Memory price surge; AAPL price hike signal; 5D +47% | Memory / Storage |\n| AMAT | +4.9% | Mega | Citi raises PT to $710; SENZ smart glasses platform launch | Semiconductor Equipment |\n| STX | +4.8% | Mega | Memory/storage rally continuation | Memory / Storage |\n| MU | +4.3% | Mega | AAPL "unsustainable" memory costs; Deutsche Bank PT $1,500; earnings June 24 ⚠️ | Memory / Storage |\n| ASML | +4.3% | Mega | Broad semi equipment rally | Semiconductor Equipment |\n| MRVL | +4.1% | Mega | Nikkei: plans to use TSMC 1.4nm for AI chips; S&P 500 inclusion June 22 | AI Compute / Custom Silicon |\n| DELL | +4.1% | Mega | Broad tech recovery; Silver Lake B-to-C share conversion | AI Infrastructure / Hardware |\n| HOOD | +10.7% | Large | Deutsche Bank PT $105; Argus PT $110; 10% RIF; record June volumes | Fintech |\n| NBIS | +7.4% | Large | Eigen AI acquisition closed; Nasdaq-100 inclusion June 22 | AI Cloud |\n| CPNG | +7.0% | Large | 5D +25.1%; no specific catalyst identified | E-commerce |\n| ACN | -14.1% PM | Large | Q3 EPS $3.80 beat $3.69 est; revenue $18.70B missed $18.75B est | IT Services |\n| CRDO | +4.4% | Large | AI networking momentum | AI Networking |\n| ASTS | +4.3% | Large | BlueBird 8/9/10 satellite launch successful | Space / Telecom |\n| RXT | +28.7% | Small | AMD 30MW AI compute deal signed; 15% workforce cut; $75-85M annual savings | AI Cloud |\n| HQ | +27.6% | Small | 5D +135%; RSI 73.6; no specific catalyst | Quantum Computing |\n| CLPT | +25.4% | Small | Surgical navigation momentum (no specific PR today) | MedTech |\n| BRAI | +18.1% | Small | BillCentral Agentic AI CXaaS partnership | Agentic AI |\n| LZB | +14.9% | Small | Q4 EPS $1.26 vs $0.82 est; $300M buyback authorized | Consumer Discretionary |\n| WNC | +14.1% | Small | 5D +27%; no specific catalyst | Industrials |\n| ARQQ | +12.5% | Small | 5D +72%; quantum computing momentum | Quantum Computing |\n| LEGN | -12.0% PM | Mid | Priced 7.7M ADS offering at $29.35; ~$226M raise | Biotech |\n| SNBR | -46.2% PM | Micro | Nasdaq to delist; Ch. 11 bankruptcy filing; suspension June 23 | Consumer / Bankruptcy |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Memory Super-Cycle Intensifies** `Memory / Storage` → ongoing\n\nThe memory trade broadened further after Apple CEO Tim Cook told WSJ that memory-chip cost increases are "unsustainable" and price hikes across Apple products are "unavoidable," calling it "a 100-year flood." This validates the demand thesis underpinning the year's top-performing stocks and sets up **MU**'s June 24 earnings as the week's most important single-stock event.\n\n- **MU** +4.3% premarket; earnings June 24 ⚠️; consensus EPS $19.66 (vs $1.91 YoY), revenue $34.47B (vs $9.30B YoY)\n- Deutsche Bank raised MU PT to $1,500 (from $1,000); Citigroup raised to $1,200 (from $840); TD Cowen raised to $1,500 (from $660) — all Buy\n- Perplexity CEO Aravind Srinivas predicted MU could surpass META in market cap within 6-12 months if HBM remains the binding constraint\n- **WDC** +5.9%, 5D +47.1%, RSI 75.7 — overbought territory; **STX** +4.8%, 5D +32.2%\n- **SNDK** flat but 5D +22.1%; the storage/NAND side of the trade still running\n- SK Hynix began shipping 12-layer HBM4E samples to major customers; 16 Gbps/pin speeds, 20%+ better power efficiency vs prior gen\n- **Apple** stock up 0.5% afterhours post-Cook interview; iPhone 18 lineup expected September — potential pricing pass-through catalyst\n- South Korea ETF (EWY) +112% YTD; SK Hynix 23.2% of EWY, Samsung 23.1% — together ~46% of fund\n\n**Intel's Foundry Renaissance** `Foundry / Semiconductor Manufacturing` → ongoing\n\n**INTC** surged ~8% premarket after President Trump confirmed on Truth Social that Apple "agreed to work" with Intel, following prior confirmations of Nvidia and Tesla partnerships. Separately, Intel's 18A-P node entered risk production on schedule.\n\n- Trump: Intel market cap surged from ~$100B to >$600B since U.S. government's 9.9% stake acquisition 9 months ago; government stake now worth ~$52B (vs $8.9B cost)\n- 18A-P delivers 9% performance gain or 18% power reduction vs standard 18A; fully design-rule compatible\n- BofA upgraded INTC to Buy with PT $135 (June 11); Barclays raised PT to $100; Wells Fargo to $110\n- Jim Cramer called INTC his "favorite stock," citing CPU-to-GPU ratio expansion in AI infrastructure\n- Next earnings: July 23; EPS est $0.19 (vs -$0.10 YoY), revenue $14.40B (vs $12.86B)\n- Price $131.27 premarket — near 52-week high of $132.75\n\n**Semiconductor Equipment & AI Compute Broadens** `AI Compute / Semiconductor Equipment` → ongoing\n\nAI infrastructure spending continues lifting the full semi stack — from equipment to custom silicon to power.\n\n- **AMAT** +4.9%; Citi raised PT to $710 (from $550), Buy; unveiled SENZ integrated visual platform for AI smart glasses; signed JDA with EssilorLuxottica for AR optics\n- **ARM** +6.6%, 5D +39.9% — AGI CPU cycle momentum continues\n- **MRVL** +4.1%; Nikkei reported plans to use TSMC A14 (1.4nm) for next-gen AI chips; S&P 500 inclusion June 22 ⚠️; Tower Semi shipped 5M+ coherent PICs to Marvell customers\n- **MRVL** analyst targets: B. Riley $345 Buy, Barclays $275 Overweight, Rosenblatt $240 Buy\n- **AMD** +0.5% (premarket +3.2%); Bernstein raised PT to $600 (from $525); signed definitive 30MW AI compute agreement with Rackspace\n- **CRDO** +4.4%; AI networking connectivity momentum\n- **ASML** +4.3%; broad semi equipment rally\n\n**AI Power & Infrastructure** `Power / AI Infrastructure` → ongoing\n\nData center power demand continues to drive the power infrastructure complex higher.\n\n- **GEV** +6.0%; Bernstein initiated Outperform, PT $1,206; Goldman Sachs initiated CEG Neutral PT $305, TLN Buy PT $499\n- **VRT** +6.1%, 5D +16.6%; bullish $440 call sweep activity (Jan 2027 expiry)\n- **NBIS** +7.4%; completed Eigen AI acquisition; Nasdaq-100 inclusion June 22 ⚠️; short interest 20.73% of float\n- Wood Mackenzie: data center metals demand is 3-4x larger than server-room estimates when grid infrastructure included; aluminum/copper demand driven by power buildout\n\n**Robinhood's Momentum Trade** `Fintech` → new\n\n**HOOD** +10.7% on 2.2x average volume, its best session in weeks.\n\n- Deutsche Bank raised PT to $105 (from $98); Argus Research raised PT to $110 (from $90); Needham raised PT to $97 — all Buy/equivalent\n- Company disclosed 10% workforce reduction (~$20M restructuring charge); expects June MTD record trading volumes across equities, options, prediction markets\n- Ark Invest sold 275,572 HOOD shares into Wednesday's +8.8% rally\n- SEC reportedly nearing "innovation exemption" for tokenized stocks; HOOD already sells tokenized equities overseas\n- Q2 earnings expected July 29 ⚠️; EPS est $0.41, revenue $1.19B\n\n**Fed Holds, Warsh Shifts Regime** `Macro` → new\n\nFed Chair Kevin Warsh's debut meeting held rates at 3.50-3.75% unanimously but delivered a materially hawkish shift in forward expectations and eliminated forward guidance.\n\n- Dot plot median: end-2026 rate 3.8% (up from 3.4% in March), implying at least one hike this year\n- Warsh did not submit his own dot; announced 5 task forces to review Fed communications, balance sheet, data, productivity/AI, and inflation framework\n- Citadel Securities warns "second-round effects" will force September rate hike; models inertial Taylor Rule implying 75bps of hikes this year; sees September, December 2026, March 2027 hike sequence\n- CME FedWatch: 63.3% probability of September hike; 72.2% probability of October hike\n- 10Y yield 4.45%; 2Y yield 4.17%\n- Trump on Warsh's hold: "Whatever… hard to believe" — but added "we have a very good guy"\n- Ray Dalio: U.S. "on the brink"; $7T spending vs $5T revenue = 40% overspending; demand for debt "falling"\n\n**Accenture Earnings Miss** `IT Services` → new\n\n**ACN** -14.1% premarket — largest single-stock decliner among major caps.\n\n- Q3 EPS $3.80 beat $3.69 est; revenue $18.70B missed $18.75B est\n- Revenue miss is narrow but the stock reaction is outsized, suggesting positioning was long into the print\n\n**Earnings Season Preview: June 24-25 Cluster** `Earnings` → new\n\nMultiple high-profile reports next week could move sectors.\n\n- **MU** earnings June 24 ⚠️: EPS $19.66 est, revenue $34.47B est\n- **KR** Q1 reported today: EPS $1.58 missed $1.59 est; revenue $46.12B beat $45.47B est; identical sales ex-fuel +1.0%\n- **TCOM** earnings June 24 ⚠️: EPS $0.79 est, revenue $2.33B est\n- **CMC** earnings June 25 ⚠️: EPS $1.75 est, revenue $2.41B est\n- **FUL** earnings June 24 ⚠️: EPS $1.38 est, revenue $923.62M est\n- **AYI** earnings June 25 ⚠️: EPS $5.16 est, revenue $1.18B est\n- **MEI** earnings June 24 ⚠️: EPS -$0.21 est, revenue $238.56M est\n\n**Iran MOU Signed, Oil Drops** `Macro / Geopolitics` → ongoing\n\nTrump and Iranian President Pezeshkian signed the interim MOU at Versailles; 60-day window for permanent deal.\n\n- WTI crude -2.2% to ~$75.10/bbl; Brent -2.2% to ~$77.77\n- Polymarket: 55% probability Strait of Hormuz traffic normalizes by July 31 (up 2%)\n- U.S. intel assessment: Iran can still shut Hormuz "at will" despite deal\n- Housing starts fell 15.4% MoM to 1.18M units annualized — lowest since May 2020; multifamily starts -40.2%\n\n**Macro Data: Resilient Labor, Manufacturing** `Macro` → ongoing\n\n- Philly Fed manufacturing June: 10.3 vs 9.8 est; employment 7.9 vs -2.8 prior\n- Initial jobless claims 226K vs 225K est; continuing claims 1,810K vs 1,800K est\n- U.K.: unemployment 4.9% vs 5.0% est; employment change +100K vs +75K est; average earnings +4.4% vs +4.0% est\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- BGC Group launched BGC Compute Infrastructure Markets division for secondary compute/memory capacity trading — treating GPU/memory as tradeable commodities\n- Noam Shazeer (Gemini co-lead, "Attention Is All You Need" co-author) left Google to join OpenAI; Altman: "10 years in the making"\n- CoreWeave (CRWV) +20% this week; Nasdaq-100 inclusion June 22; run-rate EBITDA $18.76B per bond offering memo; implied backlog ~$125B\n- Rumble rebranded to RUM Group +16%; closed Northern Data acquisition (22,000 H100/H200 GPUs, ~250MW capacity); new Quake AI division\n- Energy Fuels (UUUU) received conditional $725M, 20-year loan commitment from Pentagon's Office of Strategic Capital for rare earth expansion\n- QTREX Quantum (QTEX) +22.6% PM; produced cryogenic chip carrier via AME process for a major U.S. quantum computing firm\n- Butterfly Network (BFLY) +16.9% PM; Midjourney Scanner prototype uses 40 Butterfly Ultrasound-on-Chip modules\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Macro | Fed held at 3.50-3.75%; dot plot median shifted to 3.8% year-end (from 3.4% March); Warsh declined to submit own dot; Citadel models 75bps of hikes by March 2027 |\n| Earnings | ACN Q3 EPS $3.80 beat $3.69, revenue $18.70B missed $18.75B; KR Q1 EPS $1.58 missed $1.59, revenue $46.12B beat $45.47B; LZB Q4 EPS $1.26 crushed $0.82 est |\n| Tech | Apple CEO Cook: memory cost increases "unsustainable," price hikes "unavoidable"; Intel 18A-P entered risk production; Noam Shazeer left Google for OpenAI |\n| Commodities | WTI crude ~$75.10 (-2.2%); Gold $4,288 (+0.7%); Trump-Iran MOU signed at Versailles; Hormuz reopening expected |\n| Equities | HOOD +10.7% on analyst upgrades + 10% RIF; INTC +8% on Trump AAPL/NVDA/TSLA chip confirmations; SNBR -46% on Nasdaq delisting |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **MU earnings June 24**: EPS est $19.66, revenue $34.47B; the single most important report for the memory super-cycle thesis\n- **MRVL and FLEX join S&P 500 June 22**: passive fund buying deadline; MRVL also entering with AI custom chip narrative\n- **NBIS, CRWV, RKLB, ALAB, TDY join Nasdaq-100 June 22**: forced buying from QQQ ($300B+ AUM) and tracking funds\n- **Iran permanent deal window**: 60-day clock started with MOU signing; Strait of Hormuz traffic normalization timeline uncertain\n- **INTC earnings July 23**: first report with full visibility on Apple/Nvidia/Tesla foundry pipeline\n- **HOOD earnings July 29**: first report capturing record June trading volumes and workforce reduction\n- **U.S. markets closed Friday June 19** for Juneteenth; today is last trading day of week\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **SPCX (SpaceX)**: Down 4.9% Wednesday, first red day since listing; meme-stock dynamics dominate; Morningstar fair value $780B vs $2.65T market cap; noise-to-signal ratio extremely high\n- **Gold miners (AU, GFI, KGC, PAAS)**: All down 1-3% after 5D gains of 16-17%; routine mean reversion after geopolitical bid faded; no new fundamental catalyst\n- **Micro-cap pre-market movers without catalysts** (BYAH +40%, WKSP +29%, LNKS +82%): Illiquid names with no institutional-grade catalysts; headline moves overstate tradeable opportunity	\N