2026-06-23	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 June 23, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: A broad tech/mega-cap selloff drives Nasdaq futures down ~2.6% as GOOGL loses AI talent to Anthropic and SPCX extends its post-IPO rout to −30% from highs, while semiconductor/memory names (MU, INTC, SMCI) pull back sharply ahead of MU earnings Wednesday, and BofA's Vivek Arya blanket-raises semi price targets; IBM surges 4%+ on Trump quantum executive orders and a JPMorgan upgrade; PRIM crashes 34% on a guidance cut and COO departure.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| SPCX | −16.4% Mon; pre-mkt flat | Mega | Post-IPO selloff; $20B debt offering; lockup overhang | Space / Idiosyncratic |\n| GOOGL | −5.1% Mon | Mega | Nobel laureate John Jumper leaves DeepMind for Anthropic | AI Hyperscaler |\n| IBM | +4.3% pre-mkt | Mega | Trump quantum EOs; JPMorgan upgrade to OW PT $291 | Quantum / AI |\n| INTC | −7.5% pre-mkt | Mega | Broad tech risk-off; no co-specific news | Semiconductors |\n| MU | −7.2% pre-mkt | Mega | Profit-taking ahead of Wed Q3 earnings; Anthropic strategic deal | Memory / AI ⚠️ |\n| ABBV | +5.8% Mon | Mega | $10.9B cash acquisition of APGE at $135.11/shr | Biopharma M&A |\n| NVO | +6.3% Mon | Mega | CVS expands GLP-1 support; $50/mo Medicare copay | GLP-1 / Healthcare |\n| GLW | +6.6% Mon | Mega | Multi-billion-dollar Amazon fiber-optics deal (Jun 8); Truist PT raise to $205 | AI Infrastructure |\n| VRT | +6.2% Mon | Mega | Power Inflow signal; AI data-center cooling narrative | AI Infrastructure |\n| SNDK | +5.1% Mon | Mega | BofA PT raise to $2,100; Apple CEO warns of "100-year flood" memory shortage | Memory |\n| UMC | +13.9% Mon | Large | Broad foundry/legacy-node rally | Semiconductors |\n| TSEM | +10.4% Mon; −9% pre-mkt | Large | Monday rally reversing on broad semi giveback | Semiconductors |\n| CRDO | +10.3% Mon | Large | Evercore ISI initiates OP PT $325; Stifel PT raise to $350; BofA PT $340 | AI Connectivity |\n| SMCI | +16.5% Mon; +2.4% AH | Mid | NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL4 blueprint; GF Securities upgrade to Buy PT $48; short interest decline | AI Servers |\n| PRIM | −34% pre-mkt | Large | COO departure; FY26 adj. EPS guidance cut to $2.05-$2.60 from $4.80-$5.00 | Infrastructure / Idiosyncratic |\n| SSTK | +23.8% Mon | Small | OpenAI display partnership with Getty Images lifts content ecosystem | AI / Media |\n| HIVE | +15.6% Mon | Small | Paraguay GPU cluster validated by Columbia Univ. research; $300M ATM offering | Bitcoin/AI Mining |\n| BWIN | +15.8% Mon | Small | JP Morgan upgrade to OW, PT raise to $28 from $25 | Insurance |\n| HQ | +27.3% Mon (5D +129%) | Small | Momentum; no single catalyst identified | Quantum |\n| ZETA | +9.5% pre-mkt | Large | Strategic partnership with PLTR for AI marketing infrastructure; $100M+ annual revenue potential | AI / SaaS |\n| ORCL | −2.2% pre-mkt | Mega | Annual filing reveals 21,000 job cuts (~13% workforce) amid AI capex surge; −$23.7B FCF | AI Capex / Cloud |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Broad Tech De-Risking Ahead of Key Catalysts** `AI Hyperscaler / Macro` → ongoing\n\nU.S. equity futures are sharply lower Tuesday morning (Nasdaq 100 −2.58%, S&P 500 −1.40%) after Monday's mixed session in which the Dow rose 0.29% while the Nasdaq fell 1.32%. The de-risking is concentrated in mega-cap tech and semiconductors despite no single-company shock.\n\n- **GOOGL** fell 5.1% Monday after Nobel laureate John Jumper announced departure from Google DeepMind to Anthropic; **AMZN** −4.5%, **META** −2.6%, **MSFT** −2.6%.\n- Apollo's Torsten Slok flags VXN/VIX ratio at 1.61, highest since Jan 2007, signaling options markets are "demanding far more protection on AI names than on the broad market."\n- Dan Niles (Niles Investment Mgmt) says he is trimming hyperscaler and chip stock exposure, warning AI cost trends and routing to cheaper models could pressure Sep guidance.\n- JPMorgan Private Bank's Stephen Parker maintains S&P 500 bull-case target 8,900, says rally is "entirely earnings driven."\n- CME FedWatch: 67.9% probability Fed holds rates in July; 85.6% probability of ≥1 hike by December.\n- 10Y Treasury yield 4.48%; gold spot −1.94% to ~$4,110; WTI crude −0.42% to ~$73.55; BTC −2.79% to ~$62,300.\n- **Flash PMI data** (manufacturing + services) due at 9:45 a.m. ET Tuesday.\n- **PCE price index** (May, Fed's preferred inflation gauge) due Thursday 8:30 a.m. ET. ⚠️\n\n**Semiconductor Supercycle Meets Profit-Taking** `Memory / Semiconductors` → ongoing\n\nThe SOX index logged 9 single-day gains of ≥5% in the last 60 trading days, matching levels last seen in Jan 2009 and previously exceeded only during the dot-com era. The sector is pulling back sharply Tuesday after a historic run (+175% over 12 months).\n\n- **MU** −7.2% pre-mkt after +6.8% Monday. Reports Q3 Wednesday after close. Consensus: EPS $20.20 vs $1.91 y/y; revenue $35.01B vs $9.30B y/y. Needham raised PT to $1,550 from $500; BofA PT $1,500; Stifel PT $1,500; Rosenblatt PT $1,200. Options pricing 14% implied earnings move. Signed strategic supply + Series H investment deal with Anthropic (terms undisclosed). ⚠️\n- **INTC** −7.5% pre-mkt. BofA Vivek Arya maintains Buy, raises PT to $160 from $135. Stock up 263% YTD; Deepwater's Gene Munster calls it "becoming a meme stock" given Apple foundry deal may add only ~5% to revenue.\n- **SNDK** −8.7% pre-mkt. BofA PT raised to (not disclosed in feeds but BofA Arya note series covers semis broadly); Mizuho PT $2,200; Cantor PT $2,900; Susquehanna street-high PT $3,250. Apple CEO Tim Cook: memory shortage is a "100-year flood."\n- **TSM** −5.1% pre-mkt. Susquehanna raised PT to $575 (Jun 22). Next earnings expected Jul 16. ⚠️\n- **SMCI** +16.5% Monday, +2.4% AH. Unveiled NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL4 DCBBS blueprint at ISC 2026; GF Securities upgraded to Buy PT $48; short interest declined from 81.2M to 74.5M shares.\n- **CRDO** +10.3% Monday. Evercore ISI initiated OP PT $325; Stifel PT $350; BofA PT $340. BNP Paribas sees TAM >$10B as agentic AI drives backend/frontend network builds.\n- **UMC** +13.9% Monday. Broad foundry rally.\n- BofA's Vivek Arya raised price targets across the sector: **AMAT** Buy PT $720 (from $540); **LRCX** Buy PT $480 (from $330); **KLAC** Buy PT $317 (from $210); **MKSI** Buy PT $500 (from $380); **TER** Buy PT $525 (from $365); **MRVL** Buy PT $365 (from $240); **ARM** Neutral PT $460 (from $335); **ALAB** Neutral PT $450 (from $240); **QCOM** Underperform PT $195 (from $165).\n\n**SpaceX Post-IPO Reckoning** `Space / Idiosyncratic` → new\n\n**SPCX** fell 16.43% Monday to $154.60, wiping ~$400.8B in market cap—the second-largest single-day value loss for a U.S. company. Shares are now −30% from the $225.64 peak reached June 16.\n\n- IPO priced at $135 Jun 12, opened $150, closed first day $160.95.\n- Mohamed El-Erian: "Investors who bought at the IPO are up 23%, while those who bought the high are down almost 25%."\n- Susquehanna initiated Neutral PT $170, warned valuation "requires premium multiples on very aggressive revenue and EBITDA growth assumptions."\n- Gary Black (Future Fund): "Investors shouldn't be paying 150x 2026 EV/EBITDA" for SpaceX; compares unfavorably to NVDA at 19x.\n- Free float currently only 4.9%; lockup schedule shows float expanding to 11.8% Aug, 25.1% late Oct, 40% Dec, 50.8% Jun 2027; Musk's 46.1% stake becomes eligible Jun 12, 2027.\n- SpaceX announced $20B debt offering; Moody's/S&P/Fitch investment-grade ratings.\n- Annualized AI compute revenue run rate reportedly ~$28B (Anthropic ~$1.25B/mo, Google ~$920M/mo, Reflection ~$150M/mo).\n\n**Biopharma & GLP-1 Tailwinds** `Biopharma` → new\n\n- **ABBV** +5.8% Monday. Agreed to acquire **APGE** for $135.11/shr cash (~$10.9B). Zumilokibart (APG777) Phase 2 AD data: ~2/3 patients achieved significant skin clearance at 16 weeks. Deal accretive to adj. EPS from 2032. UBS downgraded APGE from Buy to Neutral PT $135.11; Wedbush downgraded APGE from OP to Neutral PT $135. ABBV also received EU approvals for MAVIRET (acute HCV) and SKYRIZI (pediatric psoriasis). BofA Allen Lutz raised CVS PT to $110 (Buy).\n- **NVO** +6.3% Monday. CVS announced GLP-1 support expansion: $50/mo Medicare copay, 1-on-1 pharmacist guidance, $49 MinuteClinic virtual weight-management visits. Goldman Sachs: EV adoption could offset 130K-320K bbl/day oil demand by late 2027.\n\n**Quantum Computing Gets White House Backing** `Quantum` → new\n\nPresident Trump signed two executive orders Monday targeting a research-capable quantum computer by 2028 and requiring federal agencies to adopt quantum-resistant encryption by 2030-2031.\n\n- Commerce Dept awarded ~$2B to quantum companies under CHIPS Act, including $1B for **IBM** (matched by IBM's own $1B). IBM CEO Arvind Krishna attended Oval Office signing. Trump praised Krishna and admitted regretting selling IBM stock.\n- JPMorgan upgraded **IBM** to Overweight PT $291 (from $270 Neutral) Tuesday. IBM joined OpenAI Daybreak Cyber Partner Program. IBM shares +4.3% pre-mkt.\n- After-hours moves Monday: **QBTS** +7.1%, **IONQ** +3.2%, **RGTI** +4.4%, **INFQ** +13.3%, **QUBT** +5.5%.\n\n**AI Infrastructure Build Strains & Opportunities** `AI Infrastructure` → ongoing\n\n- **ORCL** −2.2% pre-mkt. Annual filing disclosed 21,000 job cuts (~13% workforce); $1.8B restructuring costs vs $374M prior year; capex +162% to $55.7B; FCF negative $23.7B. "The adoption and deployment of AI technologies across our operations have resulted, and may continue to result, in reductions to our workforce."\n- **ZETA** +9.5% pre-mkt after announcing strategic partnership with **PLTR**: Zeta's Data Cloud rearchitected on Palantir Foundry; PLTR to provide software infrastructure for Zeta to reach Foundry's enterprise customers. Zeta CEO: partnership "can drive more than $100 million in annual revenue to Zeta."\n- **Backblaze** (BLZE) signed $335M 5-year multi-exabyte storage deal with **CoreWeave** (CRWV); issued 3.05M warrants at $7.60 exercise price.\n- **Constellation Energy** (CEG) and **Walmart** (WMT) announced 15-year nuclear PPA for ~176 MW including 30 MW of uprates from Dresden Clean Energy Center, beginning 2029-2030.\n- U.S. DOE plans $17.5B in low-interest loans for utilities to finance Westinghouse AP1000 nuclear reactors (WSJ).\n- NVIDIA's Rubin AI platform uses fully liquid-cooled architecture; reduces cooling-related water consumption from ~2.6M gal/MW annually to near zero.\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- Traders loading up on VIX calls; Bloomberg reports protective positioning rising even as indices near highs.\n- Five Eyes intelligence alliance warns AI could "fundamentally reshape" cyber capabilities within "months, not years."\n- U.S.-Iran 60-day peace roadmap includes Hormuz reopening; Trump threatened "toll collection" if talks fail; oil prices drifting lower (WTI ~$73.55). Gas prices at 6-week low ($3.85/gal national average) but uncertainty remains.\n- Italian PM Meloni reportedly considering calling election as early as April (Bloomberg).\n- Russell reconstitution effective Jun 26; several small-cap names (ELMT, OSS) joining indexes.\n- **FDX** reports Q4 after close Tuesday. Consensus EPS $5.94, revenue $24.04B. ⚠️\n- **CBRS** (Cerebras) reports first-ever public earnings after close Tuesday. Consensus loss $0.16/shr, revenue $180.81M. Options pricing 16.15% implied move. ⚠️\n- **CCL** reports Q2 before open Tuesday. Consensus EPS $0.35, revenue $6.69B. ⚠️\n- **KFY** reported Q4 pre-market: adj. EPS $1.40 beat $1.38 est.; revenue $768.3M beat $743.3M est.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **MU** reports Wed after close; consensus EPS $20.20 vs $1.91 y/y, revenue $35.01B vs $9.30B; options imply 14% move. **CBRS** first public earnings Tue after close; consensus loss $0.16, rev $180.81M. **FDX** Q4 Tue after close; consensus EPS $5.94, rev $24.04B. |\n| Macro | Flash June manufacturing/services PMI due 9:45 a.m. ET Tue. May PCE (Fed's preferred inflation gauge) due Thu 8:30 a.m. ET. CME FedWatch: 67.9% prob of hold in July; 85.6% prob of ≥1 hike by Dec. Redbook retail sales +10% YoY for week ended 6/20. ADP weekly employment change 30.75K vs 25.50K prior. |\n| Tech | Trump signed two quantum computing executive orders targeting research-capable quantum computer by 2028 and quantum-resistant federal encryption by 2030-2031. NVIDIA published data showing AI data centers use 0.2% of U.S. daily water; Rubin platform targets zero cooling water. |\n| Commodities | WTI crude −0.42% to ~$73.55; Brent ~$77.53. Gold spot −1.94% to ~$4,110. Goldman cut gold year-end target to $4,900 from $5,400. U.S. gas national avg $3.93/gal, in 6-week decline. |\n| M&A | **ABBV** acquiring **APGE** for $135.11/shr cash (~$10.9B). **CRH** acquiring **ACA** (Arcosa) all-cash $150/shr (~$8.5B TEV). **BLDP** (Ballard Power) acquiring GeoPura for £275M. **UUUU** (Energy Fuels) acquiring VAC for ~$1.9B equity. **SGMO** (Sangamo) filed Chapter 11; LLY and Astellas stalking horse bidders. |\n| Equities | SOX index: 9 sessions of ≥5% daily gains in last 60 trading days, matching Jan 2009 levels. VanEck Semiconductor ETF (SMH) +79.19% YTD. Apollo: VXN/VIX ratio at 1.61, highest since Jan 2007. |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **MU Q3 earnings** Wednesday Jun 24 after close. Consensus EPS $20.20, revenue $35.01B. Options imply 14% post-earnings swing. Strategic Anthropic deal just announced. ⚠️\n- **CBRS first public earnings** Tuesday Jun 24 after close. Consensus loss $0.16/shr, revenue $180.81M. 16.15% implied move—widest of the week. ⚠️\n- **FDX Q4 earnings** Tuesday Jun 23 after close. Consensus EPS $5.94, revenue $24.04B. 7% implied move. ⚠️\n- **CCL Q2 earnings** Tuesday Jun 23 before open. Consensus EPS $0.35, revenue $6.69B. ⚠️\n- **May PCE price index** (core + headline) Thursday Jun 25 at 8:30 a.m. ET—first inflation data since Warsh's hawkish debut. ⚠️\n- **Flash June PMI** (S&P Global manufacturing + services) Tuesday at 9:45 a.m. ET.\n- **Fed stress test results** Wednesday Jun 25 at 4:00 p.m. ET.\n- **WGO (Winnebago) Q3 earnings** Thursday Jun 25 before open. Consensus EPS $0.78, revenue $758.18M.\n- **Russell reconstitution** effective after U.S. market open Jun 26.\n- **Coca-Cola (KO)** IRS transfer-pricing appeal heard Jun 25 in 11th Circuit; up to $20B in taxes + interest at stake.\n- **SPCX lockup calendar**: free float expands to 11.8% August, 25.1% late October, 50.8% June 2027; Musk's 46.1% stake eligible June 12, 2027.\n- **NKE Q4 earnings** Jun 30 after close. Consensus EPS $0.12, revenue $10.85B. Multiple analyst downgrades since April.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **SPCX day-to-day noise**: The stock is moving on supply/demand mechanics (tiny float, lockup dynamics, debt offering) rather than fundamental deterioration. Pre-mkt is roughly flat after Monday's −16.4%.\n- **Small-cap biotech press releases** (NTHI IND status, SLXN Germany Phase 2/3 approval, DMAC first patient dosed): individually immaterial to broad positioning; no tradeable size.\n- **RSI/overbought "warnings"** on AMC and MSGE flagged in general channel: These are backward-looking momentum readings on low-conviction names with no near-term catalyst.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 673663, "output_tokens": 5293, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 3.368315, "total_cost_usd": 3.50064, "output_cost_usd": 0.132325, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-06-23T13:02:27.307484+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-06-23T13:05:12.037564+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from pub