2026-07-09	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 July 9, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: BABA surges +11.7% on pre-earnings optimism and reports China may allow limited NVIDIA H200 purchases, PENG jumps +28.3% on record Q3 earnings beat, while IONS plunges -22% after eplontersen Phase 3 ATTR-CM trial failure with AstraZeneca, and oil refiners rally as Trump declares Iran ceasefire "over."\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| BABA | +11.7% | Mega | Narrowing losses at instant-commerce; China may allow NVDA H200 buys | China Tech / AI |\n| ANET | +8.5% | Mega | 1.6Tb AI switch validated w/ META, MSFT, ORCL; Russell Top 50 add | AI Networking |\n| AVGO | +5.8% | Mega | Apple $30B+ multiyear chip deal; >15B U.S.-made chips | AI Compute / Semis |\n| AMAT | +5.3% | Mega | Mizuho raises PT from $540 to $650, maintains Outperform | Semicap Equipment |\n| SNDK | +5.1% | Mega | Bounce after -18.7% 5D selloff; Citi flags China memory pricing risk | Memory |\n| NVDA | +4.1% | Mega | BofA reiterates Buy/$350; 7-yr low fwd P/E of 18.7x; China H200 reports | AI Compute |\n| VRT | +4.3% | Mega | Broad AI infra bounce | AI Power/Cooling |\n| DELL | +3.1% | Mega | Evercore raises PT $450→$500; Trump Accounts momentum | AI Servers |\n| MU | +2.2% | Mega | Plans $3B U.S. supply chain investment incl $500M to GlobalWafers | Memory |\n| PANW | -6.2% | Mega | Profit-taking after +80% YTD; Evercore cuts PT $375→$320 | Cybersecurity |\n| PENG | +28.3% | Small | Q3 adj EPS $0.84 vs $0.54 est; rev $479M vs $406M est; FY guide raised | AI Infra / Memory |\n| BZH | +12.4% | Small | Dream Finders raises all-cash bid to $32/share (~70% premium) | Homebuilders / M&A |\n| WULF | +11.9% | Small | Morgan Stanley raises PT $66.5→$72; $19B Anthropic 20-yr lease | AI Data Centers |\n| UCTT | +11.2% | Small | Appoints new CFO Michael Keogh; bounce from -23.9% 5D | Semicap Equipment |\n| KC | +12.4% | Small | Morgan Stanley initiates Overweight w/ $15 PT | China Cloud |\n| PARR | +11.3% | Small | Oil +5-7%; UBS raises PT $60→$65; Iran ceasefire collapse | Refining |\n| FCEL | -13.4% | Small | Priced upsized 10.7M share offering at $21 ($225M gross) | Clean Energy |\n| IONS | -21.9% PM | Large | Phase 3 eplontersen ATTR-CM missed primary endpoint | Biotech ⚠️ |\n| AZN | -8.1% PM | Mega | Partner on failed IONS eplontersen trial | Pharma |\n| BBIO | +12.7% PM | Large | Likely beneficiary of ATTR-CM competitive landscape shift | Biotech |\n| ALNY | +17.7% PM | Large | Competitive read-through from IONS/AZN eplontersen failure | Biotech |\n| VLO | +5.2% | Large | Oil surge on Iran ceasefire collapse; refining margins widen | Refining |\n| MPC | +4.9% | Large | Same Iran/oil catalyst as VLO, PSX | Refining |\n| PSX | +4.9% | Large | Same Iran/oil catalyst | Refining |\n| VG | +5.0% | Large | Q2 LNG sales 466.4 TBtu; 127 cargoes; Strait of Hormuz tensions | LNG |\n| NBIS | +7.9% | Large | Bounce after -8.9% 5D; Meta neocloud threat weighed prior sessions | AI Cloud |\n| MTZ | +6.3% | Large | Mizuho raises PT $498→$502, Outperform | Infrastructure |\n| AKAM | +9.3% | Mid | Named strategic partner for WWT AI Readiness Model (ARMOR) | Cybersecurity / AI |\n| LEVI | -6.0% PM | Mid | Q2 EPS $0.28 vs $0.24 est; rev $1.56B vs $1.52B; guided up but sell-the-news | Consumer / Apparel |\n| PEP | -2.4% PM | Mega | Q2 adj EPS $2.20 vs $2.21 est; N.Am organic rev -0.5%; guide maintained ⚠️ | Consumer Staples |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Iran Ceasefire Collapse Lifts Energy, Pressures Broad Equities** `Macro / Energy` → new\n\nTrump declared the Iran ceasefire "over" at the NATO summit in Ankara; the U.S. launched fresh strikes on Iranian targets, and Iran struck U.S. bases in Kuwait and Bahrain. Oil surged ~7% on Wednesday, with WTI touching ~$75.69. The S&P 500 fell 0.28% and the Dow dropped 1.09% on Wednesday; energy was the sole S&P sector in the green. Gas prices nationally hit $3.85/gal. Thursday pre-market futures are recovering (S&P +0.24%, Nasdaq +0.68%), but the geopolitical overhang persists.\n\n- **VLO** +5.2%, **MPC** +4.9%, **PSX** +4.9%, **PARR** +11.3% — all direct beneficiaries of crude spike and wider refining margins\n- **VG** +5.0% — reported Q2 LNG sales of 466.4 TBtu at weighted avg liquefaction fee of $6.45/MMBtu; 127 cargoes exported; Strait of Hormuz tensions lift LNG pricing\n- **PBR** +3.0% — broader EM oil name catching the crude bid\n- WTI crude $72.92/bbl at press time; Brent ~$77.33/bbl\n- Polymarket: 22% probability of U.S. blockade on Iran by July 31; 44% by Dec 31\n- Fed June minutes cited "AI-related price pressures" as inflationary driver alongside tariffs; market pricing 72.7% chance of no rate change at July FOMC\n- IMF July WEO update: global growth forecast 3.0% in 2026; global headline inflation raised to 4.7%; AI investment boom cited as growth support but no productivity gains yet assumed\n\n**Semiconductor Rebound After Sharp Correction** `AI Compute / Memory` → ongoing\n\nSemis are bouncing Thursday after a bruising week that saw **SNDK** -18.7% 5D, **KLAC** -16.6% 5D, **MRVL** -16.9% 5D, and **MU** -11.4% 5D. UBS stated semis are "far from bubble territory," noting the Philadelphia Semiconductor Index forward P/E of ~26x vs 150x at the dotcom peak.\n\n- **NVDA** +4.1% pre-market — BofA reiterated Buy/$350 PT, calling the 7-yr low forward P/E of 18.7x an "enhanced buy opportunity"; China may allow limited H200 purchases to BABA, ByteDance, DeepSeek per The Information; Q2 earnings est Aug 26: EPS $2.07 vs $1.04 YoY, rev $91.7B vs $46.7B ⚠️\n- **AVGO** +5.8% — Apple announced $30B+ multiyear deal for >15B U.S.-made chips; Broadcom investing $1.5B to expand Fort Collins, CO facility; Erste Group downgraded to Hold on Jul 7; UBS Buy/$485\n- **AMD** +0.6% (but +3.2% in pre-market) — Goldman Sachs Buy/$640 (Jul 6); Wells Fargo $615; Cantor Fitzgerald $700; Q2 earnings Aug 4: EPS $1.55 vs $0.48 YoY ⚠️\n- **MU** +2.2% — announced plans to invest up to $3B to strengthen U.S. semiconductor supply chain; $500M strategic financing to GlobalWafers for 300mm silicon wafer facility in Sherman, TX; 10-yr supply agreement; forward P/E 6.1x vs NVDA 23.3x, AMD 73.5x; next earnings ~Sep 22 ⚠️\n- **SNDK** +5.1% — bouncing from -18.7% 5D; Citi Wealth flagged China memory chips "gaining international recognition" as a global pricing pressure risk\n- **AMAT** +5.3% — Mizuho Outperform, PT raised $540→$650\n- **KLAC** +3.8%, **ENTG** +6.4% — broader semicap bounce after heavy 5D selling\n- **UCTT** +11.2% — appointed Michael Keogh as CFO; bounce from -23.9% 5D\n- Mizuho also raised PTs on Lam Research ($380→$400) and MKS Instruments ($400→$415)\n- VXN/VIX ratio hit 1.7, highest in 23 years — tech vol outpacing broad market vol\n\n**AI Infrastructure Buildout: Neoclouds & Data Centers** `AI Data Centers` → ongoing\n\nDedicated AI infrastructure names are recovering after Meta's cloud ambitions and DeepSeek chip development reports weighed on the group last week.\n\n- **WULF** +11.9% — Morgan Stanley maintains Overweight, raises PT $66.5→$72; 20-yr Anthropic lease at Justified Data campus (~$19B contracted revenue); Needham PT $28→$33; Rosenblatt PT $27→$30\n- **NBIS** +7.9% — bouncing from -8.9% 5D; Meta neocloud entry and DeepSeek chip reports were prior-session headwinds; BofA Buy/$280; next earnings ~Aug 6 ⚠️\n- **CRWV** +7.0% — CoreWeave AI cloud continuing to recover\n- **ANET** +8.5% — launched 7060XE7 1.6Tb AI switching platform validated with Meta, MSFT, ORCL; joined Russell Top 50 Index; co-founder Bechtolsheim sold 240K shares (~$39M) on Jul 2 under 10b5-1 plan; BofA, Morgan Stanley, KeyBanc all raised PTs in June\n- **MTZ** +6.3% — Mizuho Outperform, PT raised $498→$502; infrastructure buildout beneficiary\n- **VRT** +4.3% — AI power/cooling infrastructure recovery\n- **DELL** +3.1% — Evercore ISI raises PT $450→$500, Outperform; AI server revenue cited as fundamental driver; Trump praised DELL at White House event; Trump disclosed 24 DELL stock trades in 2025 financial disclosure\n\n**PENG — AI Memory & Infrastructure Record Quarter** `AI Infra / Memory` → new\n\n**PENG** +28.3% on record Q3 FY2026 results and raised guidance.\n\n- Q3 adj EPS $0.84 vs $0.54 est (+56% beat); revenue $478.7M vs $405.5M est (+18% beat)\n- AI-driven sales grew 104% YoY; AI businesses now 74% of total revenue\n- Raised FY26 adj EPS guide to $2.55–$2.65 from $2.30; FY26 rev guide to $1.64B–$1.69B from $1.60B\n- Preliminary FY27 guide: ~30% growth in both revenue and EPS\n- Integrated Memory revenue $275M, +111% YoY; non-hyperscale AI infra +81% YoY\n- Needham Buy, PT $60→$80; Rosenblatt Buy, PT $75→$80; Stifel Buy, PT $66→$75\n- Added 4 new AI Infrastructure customer logos in Q3; named NVIDIA AI Factory Specialized Partner\n\n**Alibaba's Surge: China Tech Sentiment Shift** `China Tech` → new\n\n**BABA** +11.7% on 2.9x avg volume — the largest single-day gain in ~10 months.\n\n- Pre-earnings update to analysts: instant-commerce losses narrowed in June quarter; overall profitability stable (Bloomberg/Jiemian)\n- The Information reports China may let top AI firms (BABA, ByteDance, DeepSeek) buy limited Nvidia H200 chips\n- Jefferies analyst Thomas Chong: much pessimism already priced in; expects AliCloud to post faster YoY growth on AI services demand\n- BABA banned Anthropic's Claude for employees effective Jul 10, directing use of in-house Qoder\n- Reuters: Chinese authorities discussing restricting overseas access to most advanced domestic AI models\n- U.S. court temporarily blocked Pentagon from treating BABA as military-linked company\n- Ark Invest bought BABA shares on Jul 8; next earnings ~Aug 28 ⚠️\n- **BIDU** +5.7%, **KC** +12.4%, **YINN** +9.6% — broader China tech/cloud bid\n\n**Pharma Trial Failure: IONS/AZN Eplontersen** `Biotech / Pharma` → new\n\n**IONS** -21.9% pre-market, **AZN** -8.1% pre-market after CARDIO-TTRansform Phase 3 trial of eplontersen failed primary endpoint in ATTR-CM patients.\n\n- Adding eplontersen to standard of care (including stabilizers) did not significantly reduce composite of CV mortality and recurrent CV events through Week 140 vs placebo\n- 57% of patients in both arms receiving stabilizer therapy at baseline; no treatment effect observed in that subgroup\n- Monotherapy subgroup showed nominally significant HR of 0.71 (prespecified analysis)\n- Full results to be presented at ESC Congress in August 2026\n- **ALNY** +17.7% pre-market, **BBIO** +12.7% pre-market — competitive read-through as rival ATTR-CM programs gain relative positioning\n\n**Beazer Homes — M&A Bid Escalation** `Homebuilders / M&A` → ongoing\n\n**BZH** +12.4% on 4.4x avg volume after **DFH** raised its all-cash bid to $32.00/share.\n\n- $32 offer represents ~70% premium to BZH undisturbed price of $18.77 on May 8; ~24% increase from prior $25.75 public proposal\n- BZH demanded NDA with 12-month standstill; DFH went public with revised offer\n- BZH says other parties have expressed interest; DFH financing backed by Kennedy Lewis, Goldman Sachs, BofA highly confident letters\n- RSI at 78 — overbought territory\n\n**Consumer Earnings: PEP Misses, LEVI Sells Off Despite Beat** `Consumer Staples / Discretionary` → new\n\n- **PEP** -2.4% pre-market — Q2 adj EPS $2.20 vs $2.21 est (miss); rev $24.18B vs $23.96B est (beat); organic growth 2.4%; N.Am organic rev -0.5% citing tighter consumer budgets; FY26 guide maintained: adj EPS $8.55–$8.71 vs $8.64 est; expects higher input cost inflation in H2\n- **LEVI** -6.0% pre-market despite Q2 EPS beat ($0.28 vs $0.24 est) and raised FY26 guide: adj EPS $1.46–$1.52 (from $1.42–$1.48); organic rev growth 5.5%–6.0%; sell-the-news near 52-week high\n- **SMPL** Q3 adj EPS $0.42 vs $0.35 est; rev $357.0M vs $332.7M est (+7.3% beat)\n- **BYRN** Q2 EPS $(0.44) vs $(0.12) est; rev $16.4M vs $22.3M est — significant miss; stock -23% pre-market\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- Microsoft replacing OpenAI/Anthropic models with in-house MAI in Excel and Outlook; AI chief Suleyman: "our goal is to reduce and ultimately eliminate" Anthropic spend — MSFT -1.5% pre-market\n- SpaceXAI launched Grok 4.5 at $2/$6 per million tokens (input/output), undercutting Anthropic's Claude Opus 4.8 pricing of $5/$25; Counterpoint analyst says could pressure enterprise AI pricing\n- Blue Origin reportedly seeking $10B raise at $130B valuation; $4B commitment from Coatue Management; Bezos contributing $2B\n- PSKY-WBD $110B merger delayed to July 22 as Oregon AG seeks 60-day review; California may file suit as early as next week\n- Fed June minutes: "ongoing strong demand for AI infrastructure would likely sustain upward pressure on prices for technology products and electricity"; no rate cuts expected before early 2027\n- Mag 7 valuation premium over rest of S&P 500 has shrunk to 10% — lowest in over a decade per Morgan Stanley; MAGS ETF -2.5% in H1 2026 while EM equities +24.2%, U.S. small caps +22.6%\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | PEP Q2 adj EPS $2.20 vs $2.21 est; LEVI Q2 EPS $0.28 vs $0.24 est, raised FY guide; PENG Q3 EPS $0.84 vs $0.54 est (+56% beat); BYRN Q2 EPS $(0.44) vs $(0.12) est |\n| Macro | U.S. initial jobless claims 215K vs 218K est; continuing claims 1,814K vs 1,820K est; Germany trade balance May €19.1B vs €14.9B est |\n| Geopolitical | Trump declares Iran ceasefire "over"; U.S. strikes 80+ Iranian targets; Iran strikes U.S. bases in Kuwait/Bahrain; Polymarket 44% odds of U.S. blockade by Dec 31 |\n| Tech | Apple-Broadcom $30B+ multiyear chip deal; Microsoft swapping OpenAI/Anthropic for in-house MAI models; SpaceXAI launches Grok 4.5 |\n| Biotech | IONS/AZN eplontersen Phase 3 ATTR-CM missed primary endpoint; ALNY +17.7% competitive read-through; Fate Therapeutics FDA clears IND for FT839 |\n| M&A | DFH raises BZH bid to $32/share all-cash; Steel Pa