2026-08-05	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-08-05 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: PLTR +29% on 93% revenue growth and largest-ever guidance raise leads a broad semiconductor/AI rally, while SPCX drops ~11% pre-market on $18.4B in quarterly capex despite beating estimates, and AMD falls ~9% after a solid beat failed to deliver the Helios blowout investors wanted.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| PLTR | +29.4% | $374B | Q2 rev $1.94B (+93% YoY) vs $1.80B est; raised FY rev to ~$8.15B | AI Software / Defense |\n| SPCX | +9.4% Tue / -11% pre | $1.6T | Q2 rev $7.81B (+92%) vs $6.93B est; $18.4B capex; lockup Aug 6 ⚠️ | Space / AI Infra |\n| ARM | +17.4% | $300B | Data center royalty growth >100% YoY; semi sector rebound | AI Compute / Semis |\n| MRVL | +12.8% | $191B | New AI memory/storage portfolio unveiled; Q2 earnings Aug 27 ⚠️ | AI Compute / Semis |\n| INTC | +10.8% | $509B | Continued post-Q2 rebound; AI growth narrative intact | Semis / Foundry |\n| SNDK | +10.8% | $211B | Pre-earnings positioning; Q4 FY26 reports after close today ⚠️ | Memory / NAND |\n| AMD | -8.4% pre | Mega | Q2 rev $11.54B vs $11.28B est; EPS $1.66 vs $1.61; Q3 guide ~$13B vs $12.52B; FCF margin declined QoQ | AI Compute / Semis |\n| GLW | +9.0% | $138B | Post-earnings recovery; Truist upgrade to Buy PT $175 | Optical / AI Infra |\n| DELL | +8.9% | $310B | AI server momentum; Nvidia/Dell back AI cloud startup Volta at $2.4B | AI Servers |\n| LRCX | +7.8% | $397B | Broad semi equipment rally on AI capex outlook | Semicap Equipment |\n| ALAB | +12.7% | $62B | Q2 rev $392M (+104% YoY) vs $361M est; Q3 guide $540-560M vs $417M est | AI Connectivity |\n| COHR | +12.3% | $63B | Trump admin drafting ban on Chinese data center optical transceivers | Optical / AI Infra |\n| ENTG | +15.5% | $22B | Q2 EPS $0.93 vs $0.82 est; Q3 guide above consensus on all metrics | Semicap Materials |\n| ASTS | +10.7% | $29B | Successful BlueBird 11/12/13 satellite launch; earnings Aug 10 ⚠️ | Satellite / Telecom |\n| SMCI | +10.7% | $21B | Broad AI server rally; no company-specific catalyst | AI Servers |\n| W | +30.1% | $15B | Q2 EPS $0.95 vs $0.90 est; rev $3.52B vs $3.47B; best US rev growth post-COVID; 18% short float | E-commerce |\n| IBTA | +51.9% | $949M | Q2 beat + Q3 sales guide above est | Ad Tech / Consumer |\n| TSAT | +36.3% | $810M | $2.3B 15-yr Canada defense contract for Lightspeed LEO constellation | Satellite / Defense |\n| PAY | +29.2% | $5.6B | Q2 earnings beat; analysts raise PTs | Payments / Fintech |\n| BLZE | +26.9% | $1.2B | Q2 rev +18% YoY; raised FY26 rev guide; $335M CoreWeave deal | Cloud Storage / AI |\n| ZBRA | +26.5% | $17.6B | Q2 EPS $6.35 vs $4.36 est (incl $73M tariff recovery); raised FY guide | Enterprise Tech |\n| DDD | +25.8% | $581M | Q2 rev $94.6M (+1.4%); printer sales +45%; CEO retirement announced | 3D Printing |\n| UFPT | +25.2% | $2.6B | Q2 rev +15.1%; record adj EPS $2.92; MedTech demand broad-based | MedTech |\n| INSP | +22.8% | $1.8B | Q2 EPS $0.14 vs -$0.27 est; raised FY26 EPS and sales guidance | Medical Devices |\n| SHOP | +25% pre | $160B | Q2 beat; AI-driven orders at ~2x rate of other channels | E-commerce / SaaS |\n| ANET | +13% pre | Large | Q2 rev $3.04B (+37.7%) vs $2.82B est; Q3 guide $3.3B vs $2.94B; raised FY to $12.6B | AI Networking |\n| DIS | +3% pre | $175B | Q3 adj EPS $2.06 vs $1.86 est; rev $25.25B; raised buyback to ≥$9B; Toy Story 5 >$1B box office | Entertainment |\n| WIX | +17.5% | $3.7B | Q2 EPS $1.39 vs $1.16 est; Base44 AI gross margin improving to ~60%; 26% short float | SaaS / AI |\n| FN | +16.5% | $19B | Broad optical rally on proposed Chinese transceiver ban | Optical / AI Infra |\n| HLMN | +14.4% | $1.9B | Q2 rev +10%; Cambridge acquisition ($315M); raised FY guidance | Industrials |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Semiconductor Supercycle Rebound** `AI Compute / Memory / Semicap` → ongoing\n\nThe SOXX ETF's best 4-day gain since March 2020 (+16.8%) continued Tuesday as hyperscaler capex forecasts ratcheted higher and the forced-liquidation overhang from Situational Awareness's collapse faded. The broad rally carried into Wednesday pre-market with most names holding gains, though **AMD**'s post-earnings selloff introduced the first divergence.\n\n- **AMD** Q2 rev $11.54B (+50% YoY) vs $11.28B est; adj EPS $1.66 vs $1.61 est; Q3 guide ~$13B vs $12.52B est — shares -8.4% pre-market as market wanted stronger Helios rack-scale guide. CEO Lisa Su raised AI accelerator TAM to ~$1.4T by 2030 (+45% CAGR) and total HPC/AI market to ~$2T by 2030.\n- **AMD** capex rose to $808M from $282M YoY; server CPU supply "tight" but Su expects 2027 to improve. AMD working with Meta, OpenAI, Anthropic on ROCm optimization.\n- **INTC** +10.8% on continued post-Q2 rebound; Ross Gerber attributed much of July's tech selloff to Situational Awareness fund liquidation rather than fundamentals. Jim Cramer said INTC "belongs at $110."\n- **MRVL** +12.8% after unveiling next-gen AI memory/storage products (Bravera SC6 PCIe 6.0 SSD controller sampling Q4 2026); Q2 earnings Aug 27 ⚠️. Keybanc PT $400.\n- **ALAB** +12.7%: Q2 rev $392.4M (+104% YoY) vs $360.7M est; adj EPS $0.80 vs $0.69 est; Q3 guide $540-560M vs $417M est — Jefferies raised PT to $450, Needham to $425.\n- **ENTG** +15.5%: Q2 adj EPS $0.93 vs $0.82 est; Q3 guide $905-935M rev vs $880M est. Needham PT raised to $170.\n- **SNDK** +10.8% ahead of Q4 FY26 earnings today after close ⚠️. Consensus: EPS $34.45, rev $8.39B. Options imply 15.5% move.\n- **ARM** +17.4%: No new catalyst; momentum from data center royalty >100% YoY growth, AI CPU roadmap. JPMorgan PT $255.\n- **SKHY** (SK hynix ADR) +8.2%: Six analyst initiations in a single day — Cantor OW PT $300, Rosenblatt Buy PT $320, Stifel Buy PT $240, Needham Buy PT $200, RBC OP PT $200, Wolfe OP PT $200. Launched first HBF open standard with SanDisk. Reuters reports Samsung/SK hynix testing Chinese AMEC equipment as hedge.\n- **UMC** +10.4%, **TER** +10.3%, **LRCX** +7.8%, **ONTO** +7.1% — broad semicap/foundry participation.\n- Bank of America expects hyperscaler capex to top $1.2T over next 12 months (up from ~$700B); Morgan Stanley projects ~$800B in 2026, ~$1.2T in 2027.\n- Michael Burry maintains short positions in NVDA, SOXX, MU, CAT, PLTR, TSLA, AMAT; warns of possible 1987-style crash.\n\n**SpaceX — First Public Earnings Under Scrutiny** `Space / AI Infra` → new\n\n**SPCX** rose 9.4% Tuesday then fell ~11% pre-market Wednesday as investors weighed a revenue blowout against enormous AI infrastructure spending and a lockup expiration Thursday.\n\n- Q2 rev $7.81B (+92% YoY) vs $6.93B est; loss of $0.09/sh vs -$0.24 est.\n- Starlink rev $4.29B (+66%); subscribers doubled to 12M across 167 countries.\n- AI segment rev $2.56B (+247% YoY) but lost $1.26B from operations.\n- Total capex $18.37B, including $15.83B for AI infrastructure.\n- Musk: SpaceX committed to Nvidia GPUs exclusively (Vera Rubin); expects >2GW compute by year-end, "several times higher" by end-2027, possibly ~10GW.\n- CFO disclosed $6.7B in new cloud contracts signed in early Q3 ramping from October.\n- Musk pulled forward $1T revenue target from 2031 to 2030, "non-zero chance" of 2029.\n- Gwynne Shotwell: Starlink Mobile with EchoStar spectrum could be "100x better" than current service; plans to take "quite a few" AT&T/VZ/TMUS customers; service launching end-2027.\n- SpaceX bought $295M of Tesla Megapack batteries in Q2 for xAI data centers.\n- SpaceX holds 18,712 BTC (~$1.1B at quarter end); ~$540M unrealized loss QoQ.\n- Short interest at ~34% of float (~$24.6B); ~911.5M insider shares unlock Aug 6 ⚠️.\n- Cantor reiterated OW PT $246; Piper Sandler Neutral, cut PT to $140; Needham reiterated Buy PT $250.\n- Gene Munster called Q2 "a blow out," said "market missing the point" on higher capex.\n\n**Palantir — AI Sovereignty Narrative Delivers Record Quarter** `AI Software / Defense` → ongoing\n\n**PLTR** +29.4% for its best session since Feb 2024 after posting its largest-ever guidance raise.\n\n- Q2 rev $1.94B (+93% YoY) vs $1.80B est; adj EPS $0.41 vs $0.35 est.\n- US commercial rev +149% YoY to $764M; US gov rev +90%.\n- Rule of 40 score reached 155%; adj FCF $1.2B (+115% YoY), 63% margin.\n- 220 deals >$1M, 73 deals >$10M in the quarter.\n- Raised FY26 rev guide to $8.15-8.16B from $7.65-7.66B (vs $7.69B est).\n- Q3 guide: rev $2.16-2.164B vs $1.997B est.\n- CEO Karp framed growth as "AI sovereignty" demand — companies retaining control of data/workflows vs. surrendering to third-party LLMs.\n- CTO Sankar: "The market has created far more intelligence than it has converted into value."\n- Capex only $22M in H1 2026 (<1% of revenue) — asset-light model vs. AI infra builders.\n- Deutsche Bank upgraded to Buy PT $200; Citi raised PT to $245; UBS raised PT to $220; Mizuho raised PT to $215.\n- Cathie Wood's Ark sold $6.4M of PLTR shares on the rally (rebalancing).\n- Valuation: P/S ~68x, P/E ~139x; Burry maintains short position.\n\n**AI Networking & Optical Stocks Surge on China Ban Report** `AI Networking / Optical` → new\n\n**ANET** +13% pre-market, **COHR** +12.3%, **LITE** +8.9%, **FN** +16.5% as multiple catalysts converged: Arista's blowout Q2, Reuters reporting the Trump admin is drafting a ban on new Chinese optical transceiver models from US data centers, and continued AI infrastructure spending momentum.\n\n- **ANET** Q2 rev $3.04B (+37.7%) vs $2.82B est; EPS $1.02 vs $0.89 est; Q3 guide $3.3B vs $2.94B est; raised FY26 rev to $12.6B (third raise, ~40% YoY growth). Deferred rev rose to $6.9B; multi-year purchase commitments ~$9.7B (3x YoY). EtherLynx now deployed by >100 cumulative customers. Needham PT $260; BofA PT $240; Rosenblatt PT $280.\n- **COHR**, **LITE**, **FN**: Reuters reports FCC crafting rule to block new Chinese optical transceiver models; rule expected before year-end. AAOI also +22%.\n- **CRDO** +9.0%: BofA names it among 9 Buy-rated semi stocks with ≥30% upside.\n\n**Earnings Wave: Disney, Eli Lilly, Shopify Report Pre-Market** `Entertainment / Pharma / E-commerce` → new\n\n- **DIS** +3% pre: Q3 adj EPS $2.06 vs $1.86 est; rev $25.25B (+7%) vs $25.40B est (slight miss). Streaming rev +11% to $5.53B; parks rev +10% to $9.97B; US park attendance +3%, per-cap spending +4%. Segment OI +21% to $5.56B. FCF $3.07B. Sold A+E 50% stake to Hearst for ~$1.2B. Raised FY26 buyback target to ≥$9B. Reiterated FY26 adj EPS growth ~16% (~$6.64 EPS, below $6.81 est). TikTok global content partnership announced.\n- **LLY** +3% pre: Reports before open ⚠️. Est: EPS $6.01, rev $20.73B. Options imply 6.56% move — ~$65.9B mkt cap at stake.\n- **SHOP** +25% pre: Q2 beat; exec says AI-driven orders at nearly 2x rate of other channels; Sidekick AI sessions up 4.8x QoQ.\n- **SNDK** reports after close today ⚠️. Est: EPS $34.45, rev $8.93B. Options imply 15.5% move.\n\n**Macro: Iran Deal Hopes, Weak ADP, Fed Watch** `Macro` → ongoing\n\nTreasury Secretary Bessent signaled a Strait of Hormuz deal with Iran could come "today or tomorrow." CENTCOM confirmed southern shipping route remains "free and open." WTI crude fell >5% Tuesday to ~$76; gold rallied 2.2% to ~$4,166.\n\n- ADP nonfarm employment: +44K in July vs +68K est — notably weak.\n- ISM Services PMI due at 10:00 AM ET.\n- CME FedWatch: 58.9% probability of September rate hike.\n- 10Y Treasury yield 4.607%; 2Y at 4.20%.\n- Fed's Kashkari (CNBC): "Now is the time to start slowly moving interest rates up"; goal is to bring down inflation, not slow economy.\n- S&P 500 closed at record 7,736.52 (+1.79%); Dow at record 54,085.88 (+1.71%).\n- Schwab SCFR notes S&P 500 sitting farthest above 50-day MA since early June; short covering may be adding momentum.\n\n**Wayfair, Zebra, Backblaze — Earnings-Driven Mid-Cap Rallies** `E-commerce / Enterprise Tech / Cloud Storage` → new\n\n- **W** +30.1%: Q2 adj EPS $0.95 vs $0.90 est; rev $3.52B (+7.5%) vs $3.47B est; US rev +8.7% (best post-COVID); active customers +3.3% to 21.7M; FCF $301M (best since Q2 2020). Short float 18.4%. Perigold luxury brand grew >35%. Guided Q3 to high single-digit growth. Needham raised PT to $133.\n- **ZBRA** +26.5%: Q2 adj EPS $6.35 vs $4.36 est (includes $73M IEEPA tariff recovery); rev $1.56B (+20.4%) vs $1.50B est. Raised FY26 EPS guide to $20.75-21.25 from $18.30-18.70; FY rev guide to $6.15-6.26B. Memory supply navigated successfully. Needham PT $410.\n- **BLZE** +26.9%: Q2 rev $42.7M (+18% YoY); adj EPS $0.08 vs $0.01 YoY. Raised FY26 rev to $172-174M vs $162M est. Secured $335M CoreWeave storage deal. Oppenheimer PT $25; Needham PT $23.\n\n**Satellite & Space** `Satellite / Defense` → ongoing\n\n- **ASTS** +10.7%: BlueBird 11/12/13 satellites successfully launched aboard Falcon 9; next-gen arrays expected to support peak rates ~200 Mbps. Earnings Aug 10 ⚠️. Piper Sandler initiated OW PT $100.\n- **TSAT** +36.3%: Telesat LEO received $2.3B 15-year Canada defense contract (expandable to $2.7B with options) for Arctic military Ka-band connectivity. Lightspeed service on track for Q1 2028.\n- **RKLB** +3% pre: Won $397M US Space Force SB-AMTI contract to build, launch and operate Flatellite satellites with Neutron rocket.\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- FCC Chairman Carr added foreign-made humanoid robots and quadruped devices to Covered List, blocking new imports; drew ~$5B into US domestic drone manufacturing after similar drone ban. Musk expressed skepticism.\n- Google in talks for $1.5B+ deal with AI coding agent startup Mechanize (Business Insider).\n- Reuters exclusive: "No discussions" between AstraZeneca and Bristol-Myers Squibb over a potential deal, quashing Sunday's merger report. AZN shares had fallen ~9% on the original report.\n- Anthropic's Claude experienced widespread outage Wednesday morning; all Claude 5 models returning elevated errors.\n- Blackstone pitched mega debt package for Anthropic chip deal (Bloomberg); Anthropic signed $10B computing deal with new cloud startup Volta Infra.\n- Japan PM Takaichi reportedly urged BoJ Governor Ueda to buy JGBs if needed; US Treasury and Japan MOF conducted coordinated yen-buying intervention Friday. Yen at 157.42/USD.\n- CLARITY Act crypto legislation passage odds on Polymarket at 27% (down from 82% in Feb); SEC Chair Atkins says agency "ready, willing and able" to issue rules if bill fails by Aug 7 recess deadline.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | PLTR Q2 rev $1.94B (+93%), raised FY guide by ~$498M; ANET Q2 rev $3.04B (+37.7%), raised FY to $12.6B; AMD Q2 beat but -8.4% pre on lack of Helios blowout; DIS Q3 adj EPS $2.06 vs $1.86 est |\n| Macro | ADP July nonfarm employment +44K vs +68K est; Bessent signals Hormuz deal could come today/tomorrow; CME FedWatch 58.9% probability of Sept rate hike; Kashkari says "now is the time to start slowly moving interest rates up" |\n| Tech | Reuters: Trump admin drafting ban on Chinese data center optical transceivers (FCC rule before year-end); SpaceX committed to Nvidia GPUs exclusively (Vera Rubin); Google in talks for $1.5B+ Mechanize deal |\n| Commodities | WTI crude -5.3% Tue to $76.09 on Iran deal hopes; gold +2.16% to $4,165.54; Brent at $78.95 |\n| Space | ASTS launched BlueBird 11-13; TSAT won $2.3B Canada defense LEO contract; RKLB won $397M Space Force satellite contract |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **SPCX lockup expiration Aug 6**: ~911.5M insider shares become eligible for trading, more than doubling the public float. Short interest at ~34% ($24.6B).\n- **SNDK Q4 FY26 earnings today after close**: Est EPS $34.45, rev $8.93B. Options imply 15.5% move (~$30B mkt cap at stake).\n- **LLY Q2 earnings today before open**: Est EPS $6.01, rev $20.73B. Options imply 6.56% move (~$65.9B).\n- **APP Q2 earnings today after close**: Est EPS $3.75, rev $1.94B. Options imply 11.38% move. UBS PT $798.\n- **MRVL Q2 earnings Aug 27**: Est EPS $0.87, rev $2.70B. Keybanc PT $400.\n- **ASTS earnings Aug 10**: Est EPS -$0.29, rev $34.54M. Piper Sandler initiated OW PT $100.\n- **UBER Q2 earnings today before open**: Est EPS $0.83, rev $14.24B. Wayve received TfL vehicle licenses for London autonomous rides; Uber expanding AV footprint to 15 cities by year-end.\n- **ISM Services PMI due 10:00 AM ET**: July reading will test services-sector inflation narrative ahead of Friday's payrolls.\n- **CLARITY Act crypto legislation deadline Aug 7** (Senate recess): Polymarket odds at 27%.\n- **Fed Gov. Lisa Cook speaks 4:05 PM ET**.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **RSI/overbought screener lists** (SNAP, STGW, ECHO): Mechanical RSI readings with no actionable new information beyond prior earnings beats already priced.\n- **Micro-cap pre-market movers** without catalysts (RITR +99%, CISS +51%, various healthcare names ±30%): Illiquid names with no fundamental drivers identified.\n- **Automated peer comparison tables** (NVDA vs. peers, AAPL vs. peers, AMZN vs. peers): Backward-looking ratio comparisons that do not reflect any new information from this session.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 371265, "output_tokens": 6309, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 1.856325, "total_cost_usd": 2.01405, "output_cost_usd": 0.157725, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-08-05T12:47:09.510122+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-08-05T12:50:04.454425+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from published claude.com/api pricing (input, 5m cache write, cache read, output) — Anthropic does not return dollar amounts on the response.", "total_cost_usd": 2.0141, "total_inpu