2026-08-18	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-08-18 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Memory/storage stocks (SNDK +8.3%, MU +4.1%, WDC +5.1%) extend their AI-driven melt-up as Anthropic hits $65B annualized revenue, while FN drops ~10% pre-market on GAAP EPS guidance miss, HD beats on Q2 ($4.92 vs $4.73 est), 30-year Treasury yield hits 5.31% (19-year high), and Trump rejects extending Iran ceasefire pushing Brent above $91.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| SNDK | +8.3% | Mega | AI memory demand; multi-year contract visibility from investor day | Memory / AI Infra |\n| GLW | +5.3% | Mega | AI optical fiber read-through; semiconductor optics demand | AI Optical |\n| MRVL | +5.2% | Mega | Pre-earnings positioning; UBS maintains Buy, cuts PT to $300 | AI Compute |\n| AMAT | +5.2% | Mega | Broad semi rally; UBS maintains Buy, PT $675 | Semis / Equipment |\n| WDC | +5.1% | Mega | SanDisk investor day read-through; AI storage demand | Memory / AI Infra |\n| PWR | +5.0% | Mega | AI infra buildout beneficiary; 5-year return leader | Data Center Infra |\n| MU | +4.1% | Mega | BofA: $640B cumulative FCF through FY30; crosses $1,000 | Memory / AI Infra |\n| SPCX | +3.6% | Mega | 13F disclosures: GOOGL $94B, NVDA $21B, Harvard $2.2B stakes | Space / AI Infra |\n| CAT | +3.0% | Mega | Empire State Mfg at 4-year high; $3M Arkansas workforce initiative | Industrials |\n| CBRS | +15.8% | Large | 13F: Tiger Global $663M new stake; OpenAI Ultrafast API on Cerebras hardware | AI Compute |\n| CRDO | +8.4% | Large | AI optical connectivity demand read-through from COHR/SMTC | AI Optical |\n| COHR | +7.8% | Large | Post-Q4 beat rally continues; Jefferies/MS/Rosenblatt raised PTs | AI Optical |\n| FN | +4.7%→ **-10% pre-mkt** | Large | Q4 adj EPS $4.10 beat $3.82; Q1 GAAP EPS guide $3.39-$3.54 vs $3.78 est ⚠️ | AI Optical / Contract Mfg |\n| MSTR | +5.1% | Large | BTC +1.8%; Jane Street discloses 2.67M-share MSTR position | Crypto / BTC Treasury |\n| AXTI | +18.6% | Mid | No identified catalyst; prior session momentum continuation | Semis / Substrates |\n| HIVE | +15.2% | Small | BUZZ HPC signs $350M 5-year AI cloud deal; +$70M ARR | Crypto / AI Infra |\n| HTHT | +11.2% | Mid | Q2 EPS $0.78 vs $0.70 est; raised FY26 sales guidance | China Hospitality |\n| RUM | +10.5% | Small | Q2 revenue +61% YoY; Q3 guide $87-93M vs $65.2M est | Social Media / AI Infra |\n| SMTC | +10.2% | Mid | 800G/1.6T optical shipment momentum; Needham Buy, $200 PT | AI Optical |\n| DUOT | +9.4% | Small | Q2 EPS $1.37 vs $0.66 est; 55MW AI data center agreements with Axe Compute | AI Infra / Data Center |\n| WOLF | +10.4% | Small | No identified catalyst; momentum continuation | SiC / Power Semis |\n| FIGR | +13.5% | Mid | No identified catalyst from available data | Fintech |\n| HD | flat→ **+1-2% pre-mkt** | Mega | Q2 EPS $4.92 vs $4.73 est; sales $47.86B vs $47.27B; comp +1.7%; affirmed FY guide ⚠️ | Retail / Housing |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Memory & Storage Supercycle** `Memory` → ongoing\n\nThe AI memory trade extended violently for a second week. **SNDK** +8.3% (5D: +43.6%), **WDC** +5.1% (5D: +22%), **MU** +4.1% (5D: +17.4%) all rallied as the sector priced in SanDisk's Aug. 13 investor day targets and a U.S. government signal to block Chinese memory sourcing.\n\n- BofA (Vivek Arya) modeled MU generating >$640B cumulative FCF through FY2030 under a SanDisk-like framework; CHIPS Act buyback restrictions expire Dec. 9, 2026\n- Trivariate Research (Adam Parker) said MU could double and reach $1T market cap; estimates ~$300B in FCF over two years\n- MU crossed $1,000/share; now $1.1T market cap; MU 5D +17.4%, YTD +254%\n- SNDK YTD +653%; management targets adj gross margin ~80%, FCF margin ~50%, 100% excess cash return to shareholders\n- Commerce Secretary Lutnick told WSJ administration is "not in favor" of Apple sourcing DRAM/NAND from Chinese manufacturers CXMT and YMTC\n- Druckenmiller's Duquesne completely exited MU in Q2; Tepper's Appaloosa cut MU by 41%, exited SNDK entirely\n- Cantor Fitzgerald PT $2,000 on MU (Overweight); KeyBanc PT $1,750; Citi lowered PT to $1,150 (Buy maintained)\n- MU next earnings est. Sept. 22 ⚠️; consensus EPS $31.27 vs $3.03 YoY\n\n**AI Optical Interconnect Melt-Up** `AI Optical / Networking` → ongoing\n\nThe AI optical connectivity complex surged broadly, with **COHR** +7.8%, **CRDO** +8.4%, **SMTC** +10.2%, **LITE** +4.7%, **GLW** +5.3%, **MRVL** +5.2%. **FN** reversed from +4.7% to **-10% pre-market** on GAAP guidance miss.\n\n- COHR rallied on post-Q4 beat momentum; Jefferies, Morgan Stanley, Rosenblatt raised PTs (one as high as $500); Needham initiated Buy; FCC proposal to ban Chinese optical transceiver imports cited as tailwind\n- SMTC +10.2%: Needham reiterated Buy/$200 PT after investor meetings; 800G and 1.6T optical module shipments ahead of expectations; CopperEdge ACC adopted by major cloud customer\n- FN Q4 adj EPS $4.10 vs $3.82 est; revenue $1.316B vs $1.275B est (+45% YoY); data center revenue +68% YoY to $669M (51% of total); DCI run rate ~$1B\n- FN Q1 guide: adj EPS $4.10-$4.25 vs $3.96 est; revenue $1.375-1.425B vs $1.321B est; **but GAAP EPS $3.39-$3.54 vs $3.78 est** — drove the sell-off\n- FN CEO Grady: demand "insatiable," "no end in sight"; capacity targeting $12.5-14B revenue run rate; Cisco 20%, Nvidia 16%, Nokia 11%, Amazon 11% of FY26 revenue\n- Needham reiterated Buy/$650 PT on FN\n- MRVL reports Q2 FY2027 on Aug. 27 ⚠️; consensus EPS $0.87, revenue $2.71B; UBS maintained Buy, lowered PT to $300\n- GLW +5.3%: Tepper's Appaloosa exited GLW position entirely in Q2; stock up 96% YTD on semiconductor optics demand\n\n**AI Compute Infrastructure — Cerebras, HIVE, DUOT** `AI Compute / Data Center` → ongoing\n\n**CBRS** +15.8% on institutional accumulation and OpenAI partnership momentum. **HIVE** +15.2% and **DUOT** +9.4% on new AI infrastructure contracts.\n\n- CBRS: Tiger Global disclosed 3.0M-share new position ($663M); Citadel 1.25M shares + calls; ARK bought 106,941 shares on Aug. 13 post-earnings dip\n- CBRS powering OpenAI's "Ultrafast" API tier for GPT-5.6 Sol at 750 tokens/sec (14x standard); OpenAI committed to 750MW of Cerebras capacity by 2028\n- CBRS Q2 core revenue $209.9M (+103% YoY); RPO $25.4B; FY26 revenue guided $880-890M; Wedbush raised PT to $290 (Outperform)\n- HIVE's BUZZ HPC signed $350M 5-year GPU cloud deal with investment-grade customer; +$70M ARR; total annualized revenue to ~$180M; deploying 2,016 NVIDIA Blackwell Ultra GPUs\n- DUOT Q2 EPS $1.37 vs $0.66 est; signed 55MW AI data center agreements with Axe Compute implying $500M+ aggregate payments\n\n**Geopolitics: Iran Ceasefire Expiry / Oil** `Macro / Energy` → ongoing\n\nTrump rejected extending the 60-day Iran ceasefire that expired Monday. Tehran threatened "fully offensive" posture.\n\n- Brent crude above $91/bbl; WTI ~$84.20\n- U.S. Navy awarded RTX's Raytheon $22.9B 7-year Tomahawk contract to expand production from ~60/year to >1,000/year\n- RTX Q2 backlog $289B (+22%); raised FY26 sales guide to $95-96B, adj EPS $7.10-$7.25\n- Sen. Warren: top 5 defense contractors spent >$100B on buybacks/dividends since 2020; bipartisan analysis shows 36% cut in Q1 2026 vs year-ago\n- Gas prices >$4/gallon; Energy Secretary Wright blamed Biden-era clean energy policies alongside Iran conflict\n\n**Treasury Market Stress** `Macro / Fixed Income` → ongoing\n\n30-year Treasury yield hit 5.31%, highest since June 2007. 10-year yield 4.74%.\n\n- China cut U.S. Treasury holdings to $633.4B in June (18-year low), down from $659.3B in May; Japan reduced to $1.12T; total foreign holdings fell to $9.299T\n- TLT fell to lowest since June 2004; Peter Schiff says "5.5% is the next objective"\n- July budget deficit hit record $432B; national debt nearing $40T\n- CME FedWatch: 36.6% probability of September rate hike, down from 48% a week ago\n- FOMC minutes from August meeting due Wednesday Aug. 19 ⚠️\n\n**Retail Earnings / Consumer Health** `Retail` → new\n\n**HD** reported before the bell: Q2 EPS $4.92 vs $4.73 est; sales $47.86B vs $47.27B est (+5.7% YoY); U.S. comp +1.3%; affirmed FY26 adj EPS $14.69-$15.28 and sales $168.8-172.1B.\n\n- Gates Foundation initiated new 1M-share HD position ($352.7M) in Q2\n- Stifel raised HD PT to $340 (Hold)\n- AS (Amer Sports) Q2 adj EPS $0.22 vs $0.11 est; sales $1.633B vs $1.543B est (+32% YoY); raised FY26 EPS guide to $1.27-$1.30; raised FY26 sales to $8.142B\n- Target (TGT), TJX, Walmart all reporting this week ⚠️\n\n**SpaceX 13F Disclosures** `Space / AI Infra` → new\n\n**SPCX** +3.6% as a wave of 13F filings revealed massive institutional ownership.\n\n- Alphabet: 551M shares (~$94B); NVIDIA: 122.76M shares (~$21B); AMD: $565.5M; Harvard: $2.2B (largest single equity holding)\n- Atreides Mgmt: 42% of portfolio in SPCX ($4.67B); Saudi PIF: 154.1M shares (~$26.3B); Fidelity: 302.6M shares\n- Bernstein analyst Harned: full Starship reusability "absolutely central" to AI valuation; forecasts ~$600B SpaceX revenue by 2031; ~3,500 Starship launches in 2031\n- UBS maintains Buy/$210 PT\n- Prediction markets: 71% chance Tesla-SpaceX merger before 2028 (Kalshi); 55% on Polymarket before Dec. 31, 2027\n- SpaceX launched 2 rockets 38 minutes apart Saturday, new record; 650th booster landing\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- Anthropic annualized revenue run rate hit $65B by end of July (7x YoY); Q2 revenue $11.5B (14x YoY); Polymarket: 70% chance Anthropic IPOs before Oct. 31; projects $190-200B revenue by 2028\n- JPMorgan's Bill Eigen warns AI boom resembles 2008 housing cycle; Goldman estimates ~$1.5T in aggregate hyperscaler lease commitments off-balance-sheet; WSJ reports $3T in total hidden Big Tech AI commitments\n- Workday (WDAY) -3.2%: BTIG downgraded to Neutral citing "limited adoption" of Flex Credits; Reuters reported buyout talks with Silver Lake at ~$4