2026-08-20	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-08-20 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: MRK +12.7% and MRNA +177% (prior session) on first-ever Phase 3 mRNA cancer vaccine win; gold miners surge 7–15% as Treasury doubles long-bond buybacks to $4B, Bitcoin breaks $71K on record $2.7B short liquidation, and WMT drops ~6% despite beating on EPS as U.S. comps miss.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **MRK** | +12.7% | Mega | INTerpath-001 Phase 3 mRNA melanoma vaccine hit RFS/DMFS endpoints | Pharma / Oncology |\n| **MRVL** | +9.6% | Mega | Google custom chip deal; warrant for 59M shares at $206.58 | AI Compute |\n| **NEM** | +7.2% | Mega | Gold >$4,500; Treasury buyback doubles to $4B | Gold / Precious Metals |\n| **AEM** | +10.7% | Mega | Gold rally; sector-wide miner breakout | Gold / Precious Metals |\n| **NOW** | +6.1% | Mega | Broad SaaS rotation | SaaS |\n| **LLY** | +5.2% | Mega | Amplitude Therapeutics taRNA vaccine partnership; GLP-1 momentum | Pharma |\n| **DHR** | +5.3% | Mega | Sector rotation into life sciences | Life Sciences |\n| **PGR** | +4.6% | Mega | KBW upgrade to Outperform; PT raised $226→$250 | Insurance |\n| **CRM** | +4.4% | Mega | Cantor Fitzgerald reiterates OW, $250 PT | SaaS |\n| **EL** | **+16.7%** | Large | Q4 adj EPS $0.39 vs $0.32 est; FY27 sales guide $15.5–15.8B vs $15.56B est | Consumer / Beauty |\n| **CDE** | +12.1% | Large | Gold/silver rally | Gold / Precious Metals |\n| **MSTR** | **+10.2%** | Large | BTC >$71K; Treasury buyback; CLARITY Act optimism | Crypto / Bitcoin Treasury |\n| **WPM** | **+10.1%** | Large | Gold/silver rally; Wheaton CEO sees $1B+ streaming deals/yr | Precious Metals Streaming |\n| **ILMN** | +8.2% | Large | Broad genomics rally post-MRNA cancer vaccine win | Genomics |\n| **CRCL** | +7.5% | Large | BTC rally; White House crypto summit; CLARITY Act progress | Crypto / Stablecoin |\n| **CVNA** | +7.4% | Large | Viking Global expanded stake +343% to 12.3M shares in Q2 13F | Auto Retail |\n| **PURR** | **+27.5%** | Small | BTC/ETH rally; crypto short squeeze | Crypto |\n| **TEM** | **+22.8%** | Mid | Merck/Moderna trial validates Personalis acquisition; BTIG PT raised to $80 | Precision Oncology / AI |\n| **TWST** | **+20.5%** | Mid | Anthropic selects TWST as evaluator for AI protein design; 52-wk high | Synthetic Biology |\n| **BTGO** | +17.3% | Small | Korea VASP registration; BTC rally | Crypto Custody |\n| **ASTL** | **+15.3%** | Small | Sector momentum; no specific catalyst identified | Steel |\n| **KC** | **+14.5%** | Mid | Q2 adj loss $(0.03) vs $(0.10) est; AI cloud billings +82% YoY | China Cloud / AI |\n| **BYND** | +15.8% | Small | No identified catalyst | Idiosyncratic |\n| **DRD** | +14.5% | Small | Gold rally; HC Wainwright PT raised $33→$35 | Gold Mining |\n| **HYMC** | +15.0% | Small | Gold rally | Gold Mining |\n| **SOC** | +21.4% | Small | No identified catalyst | Idiosyncratic |\n| **CBRS** | -3.5% (5D: -19.1%) | Large | CS-4 launch; Cathie Wood buying; but profit-taking after +15% Mon rally | AI Compute |\n| **PANW** | -3.9% | Mega | Pre-earnings positioning; multiple PT raises (Cantor $425, Stifel $415) | Cybersecurity ⚠️ |\n| **WMT** | -6.2% PM | Mega | Q2 adj EPS $0.81 vs $0.74 est; U.S. comps +2.6% vs +3.8% est | Retail |\n| **BABA** | -3.2% PM | Mega | Q1 adj EPADS $1.26 vs $1.85 est; AI cloud rev +45% YoY | China Tech / Cloud |\n| **WOLF** | -12% PM | Mid | Q4 adj loss $(2.26) vs $(2.45) est; rev $149.6M miss $224.5M est | SiC Semiconductors |\n| **DE** | beat | Mega | Q3 EPS $5.10 vs $4.70 est; rev $12.6B vs $10.7B est | Industrials ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**mRNA Cancer Vaccine Breakthrough — First Phase 3 Win** `Pharma / Oncology` → new\n\n**MRK** +12.7% and MRNA +177% (Wednesday) on the first positive Phase 3 readout for an individualized mRNA cancer therapy. **TEM** +22.8% as the Merck/Moderna result validates its pending $1.5B Personalis acquisition. **TWST** +20.5% after Anthropic named it evaluator for AI protein design. **ILMN** +8.2% and **TXG** +10.6% ride the broader genomics/precision-medicine wave.\n\n- INTerpath-001 enrolled 1,137 resected stage IIB–IV melanoma patients; intismeran autogene + Keytruda met primary (RFS) and key secondary (DMFS) endpoints vs Keytruda alone at pre-specified interim analysis.\n- First Phase 3 win for any individualized neoantigen therapy and any mRNA-based cancer treatment; first Phase 3 to show improvement over Keytruda monotherapy in adjuvant resected melanoma.\n- Merck/Moderna split costs and profits 50/50; Merck paid $200M upfront (2016) + $250M option exercise (2022).\n- Morgan Stanley upgraded **MRK** Equal-Weight → Overweight, PT $116 → $179; raised **MRNA** PT $39 → $89 (Equal-Weight maintained).\n- MRNA pre-consensus Hold rating, avg PT was $52.95 — stock now trades at ~$155 PM (down ~11% from Wed close of $174.38). Prior analyst high was $110.\n- Nine Phase 2/3 trials in INTerpath program across melanoma, NSCLC, bladder, renal cell carcinoma; Phase 1 in pancreatic, gastric, lung cancers.\n- BTIG raised **TEM** PT to $80, maintains Buy. Personalis provides sequencing platform Moderna uses to identify neoantigens for each patient.\n- **TWST** hit 52-week high; Scorpion Capital published short report calling AI drug-discovery narrative "speculative delusion" — stock showed no negative reaction.\n- BioNTech (BNTX) +22% Wed on peer effect; developing autogene cevumeran (BNT122), similar mechanism, in Phase 2 for colorectal and pancreatic cancers.\n- **LLY** +5.2% partly on Amplitude Therapeutics taRNA vaccine collaboration for infectious diseases; separately, Novo Nordisk testing lower-dose Wegovy pills (WSJ).\n\n---\n\n**Gold & Precious Metals Surge on Treasury Intervention** `Commodities / Precious Metals` → ongoing\n\n**AEM** +10.7%, **NEM** +7.2%, **WPM** +10.1%, **CDE** +12.1%, **KGC** +9.8%, **AU** +10.4%, **DRD** +14.5%, **HYMC** +15.0%, **PAAS** +7.7%, **SSRM** +10.6%, **SA** +7.2%, **SKE** +9.1%, **SBSW** +9.0%. Gold near $4,500/oz; silver +4.3% to $66.06; VanEck GDX +9.4% Wed, MTD +31.3%.\n\n- U.S. Treasury doubled maximum liquidity-support buyback operations for 10–30yr bonds from $2B to $4B per operation, effective Sept. 9 through Nov. 4. 30yr yield fell to 5.20% from 19-year high of 5.33%; 10yr fell to 4.65%.\n- Gold and silver added combined $1.3T in market cap post-announcement (Kobeissi Letter).\n- Dollar index fell to 99, lowest since late May; euro +0.8% to $1.1664.\n- Economist Mohamed El-Erian called buyback a "Band-Aid" and "financial engineering," not debt reduction.\n- Charlie Bilello (Creative Planning) criticized move as "debt reshuffling, not debt reduction."\n- Steve Hanke warned 10yr yield could rise another 50bps; remains "very bearish" on bonds.\n- HC Wainwright raised **DRD** PT $33 → $35, maintains Buy.\n- Wheaton Precious Metals CEO Hodaly sees ~$1B streaming deals annually over next 3–4 years, supported by $2.7B annual FCF.\n\n---\n\n**Bitcoin Breaks $71K — Record Short Liquidation, CLARITY Act, Treasury Easing** `Crypto` → new\n\n**MSTR** +10.2%, **CRCL** +7.5%, **PURR** +27.5%, **BTGO** +17.3%. BTC traded above $72K Thursday AM, up 14.8% on the week — on pace for best weekly gain since November 2024 Trump election week.\n\n- $2.74B in bearish crypto positions liquidated in ~1 hour Wednesday, largest single-day short liquidation event in records going back to 2021 (Coinglass/Bloomberg).\n- Spot Bitcoin ETFs pulled in $517.19M Wednesday, largest since May 4; IBIT led with $284.7M. Weekly inflows crossed $1B with two sessions remaining.\n- Trump urged Congress to pass CLARITY Act at White House crypto summit; Senate Banking Chairman Tim Scott said bill has "really good shot" of advancing in September. Senate procedural vote on calendar for Sept. 15.\n- Polymarket: probability of any Fed rate hike in 2026 slipped to ~50%, down from 64% on Aug. 6; September hike odds ~25%.\n- FOMC July minutes: held rates at 3.50%–3.75% on 9-3 vote; 3 dissents preferred +25bps. Some officials judged financial conditions might not be restrictive enough.\n- **MSTR**: Saylor warned investors to expect "difficult years" with 7–10yr horizon; Strategy holds >$53B in BTC.\n- BitMine disclosed $11.4B in crypto + cash + moonshot holdings including 5.82M ETH; owns 4.8% of total ETH supply.\n- Crypto Fear & Greed Index flipped from Fear to Greed overnight.\n\n---\n\n**Walmart Beats on EPS, Misses on U.S. Comps — Stock Drops ~6%** `Retail` → new\n\n**WMT** -6.2% premarket despite top/bottom line beat.\n\n- Q2 adj EPS $0.81 vs $0.74 est (+19% YoY); revenue $187.94B vs $186.79B est (+5.9% YoY).\n- U.S. comparable-store sales +2.6%, significantly below Wall Street's +3.8% forecast.\n- Global ecommerce sales +23%; global advertising business +38%; membership fee revenue +17% globally.\n- Company rolled back prices on 11,000 items in U.S. in Q2; continues to see growth from higher-income households.\n- Annual forecast assumes slightly better second-half sales vs prior target driven by price investments; assumes fuel and tariffs stay at current rates.\n\n---\n\n**AI Compute Infrastructure — MRVL/Google Deal, CBRS CS-4, Micron Investment** `AI Compute` → ongoing\n\n**MRVL** +9.6% on Google custom chip agreement. **CBRS** -3.5% (5D: -19.1%) after CS-4 launch Tuesday. **MU** announced $10B Boise research hub.\n\n- Google granted Marvell warrant to purchase up to 58.97M MRVL shares at $206.58/share (~$12.2B aggregate exercise). 1.36M shares vest over Year 1; remaining 57.6M vest in 240 tranches per $500M in qualifying revenue through FY2033.\n- MRVL scope: AI inference accelerators, storage controllers, NICs, memory interface controllers, near-memory compute — all attaching to Google TPU ecosystem.\n- AVGO fell ~5% Wednesday on concern MRVL captures growing share of Google AI silicon spending.\n- **MRVL** earnings Aug. 27; analysts expect EPS $0.87 (vs $0.67 YoY), revenue $2.71B (vs $2.01B). Average PT $270.17. TD Cowen Hold/$225; UBS Buy/$300; KeyBanc OW/$400.\n- **CBRS** launched CS-4 rack system with three WSE-3 Turbo chips; claims up to 30x faster inference vs GPU-based systems. First systems shipping this quarter. Cathie Wood bought ~$17M in CBRS shares Wednesday across ARKK/ARKW.\n- Needham reiterated Buy on **CBRS**, PT $300. Cathie Wood also bought ~$20.1M in **AVGO** shares across ARKK/ARKQ/ARKW.\n- **MU** announced planned $10B investment over next decade in Micron Research Labs, Boise-headquartered memory research hub; groundbreaking expected calendar 2027.\n- CoreWeave signed multi-year agreement with Hudson River Trading for AI cloud platform including NVIDIA Vera Rubin with Spectrum-X networking.\n\n---\n\n**Alibaba: Cloud Surges, EPS Misses on AI Spending** `China Tech / Cloud` → ongoing\n\n**BABA** -3.2% premarket. **KC** +14.5% (prior session) on AI cloud beat.\n\n- BABA fiscal Q1 (June quarter): adj EPADS $1.26 vs $1.85 est (-39% miss); revenue $39.64B vs $38.63B est (+9% YoY). Adj net income -38% YoY; net income -75% YoY.\n- AI Cloud and Compute Services revenue +45% to $7.14B; AI-related product revenue $1.82B, 12th straight quarter of triple-digit YoY growth.\n- CEO Eddie Wu prioritizing AI growth over near-term profits; BABA aims for $100B cloud/AI revenue over 5 years.\n- Executive said BABA could break even on AI capex in ~3 years based on current gross margins.\n- China e-commerce revenue -8%; international e-commerce -1%.\n- **KC** Q2: adj loss $(0.03) vs $(0.10) est; revenue $452.8M vs $447.8M est (+31% YoY). AI cloud gross billings +82% YoY, accounting for 56% of public cloud revenue. First positive GAAP operating margin ever; adj operating margin 4.0%.\n\n---\n\n**Estée Lauder Breakout on FY27 Guidance** `Consumer / Beauty` → new\n\n**EL** +16.7%, 4.8x avg volume.\n\n- Q4 adj EPS $0.39 vs $0.32 est; sales $3.63B vs $3.54B est (+6% YoY). Organic net sales +5%.\n- FY27 guidance: adj EPS $3.10–$3.35 vs $3.18 est; sales $15.50–15.80B vs $15.56B est; organic sales growth affirmed at 3–5%.\n- Adj operating margin guided 12.7–13.5%, up from prior 12.5–13.0%.\n- CEO de La Faverie: "reignited growth" with 4th straight quarter of organic sales growth.\n- Middle East conflict reduced Q4 adj EPS by $0.05; tariff refunds provided $0.07 benefit.\n\n---\n\n**Macro & Geopolitics — Iran, Tariffs, Fed** `Macro` → ongoing\n\n- Trump announced "Operation Economic Fury" against Iran, threatening severe consequences for nations supporting Tehran. Brent crude toward $92/bbl; WTI ~$86. U.S. reportedly running covert shipping corridor through Hormuz, moving ~10M bbl/day.\n- U.S. reportedly nearing Canada trade deal: auto tariffs may drop to 15% (from 25%); steel/aluminum to 25% (from 50%). Deadline: Saturday 12:01 AM EDT.\n- Initial jobless claims 206K vs 210K est (prior revised 212K). Philly Fed manufacturing index surged to 47.4 in August (vs 24.1 est), five-year high. Philly Fed employment 27.9 vs 10.0 prior.\n- Fed's Daly: missing inflation goal "by quite a bit"; policy in "good place"; rise in long-term yields is "global issue that blunts signal for Fed."\n- Germany PPI (MoM) July +1.1% vs +0.5% est. Australia employment change July -15.8K vs +11.7K est; unemployment 4.5% vs 4.4% est.\n- U.S. national debt crossed $40T; Nikki Haley warned Social Security could "go bankrupt" in 5 years.\n\n---\n\n**SaaS / Enterprise Software Rotation** `SaaS` → ongoing\n\n**NOW** +6.1%, **CRM** +4.4%, **TEAM** +5.7%, **WDAY** +3.6%, **ACN** +5.0%. Multiple PT raises across cybersecurity and data infrastructure.\n\n- **PANW** -3.9% ahead of Q4 FY26 earnings. Cantor Fitzgerald PT $340→$425 OW; Stifel PT $330→$415 Buy; Truist PT $375→$435 Buy; Mizuho PT $305→$415 OP; UBS PT $300→$390 Neutral. Key test: FY27 NGS ARR guidance vs 22.1% consensus growth. ⚠️\n- **RBRK** received multiple PT raises: Cantor $95→$120 OW; Mizuho $90→$112 OP; Truist $90→$135 Buy; Barclays $90→$110 OW.\n- **SNOW**: Mizuho PT raised to $355 OP; BofA PT raised to $395 Buy.\n- **MDB**: Citizens PT raised $366→$519 Market Outperform.\n- **WDAY**: BofA PT raised $140→$205, maintains Neutral. Short squeeze score hit maximum 100 (S3 Partners).\n- Silver Lake's $43B Workday bid noted as first "SaaSpocalypse" casualty; Futurum Equities warns 95% of SaaS could become "AI plumbing."\n\n---\n\n**Deere Beats, Earnings Season Continues** `Industrials / Earnings` → ongoing\n\n- **DE** Q3 EPS $5.10 vs $4.70 est; revenue $12.61B vs $10.73B est.\n- **AAP** Q2 adj EPS $1.03 vs $0.81 est; revenue $2.00B vs $2.04B est (miss).\n- **ROST** reports after close today; consensus EPS $1.94, revenue $6.15B. ⚠️\n- **COTY** Q4: loss $(0.02) vs $(0.01) est (miss); revenue $1.27B vs $1.19B est (beat). Gucci Beauty license exit to create FY28 step-down. Stock -5.6% PM.\n- **WOLF** Q4: adj loss $(2.26) vs $(2.45) est (beat); revenue $149.6M vs $224.5M est (miss). AI data center revenue +20% sequentially, >2x from FY25→FY26. Q1 guide: $140–160M vs $150.4M est. Stock -12% PM.\n- **BULL** (Webull) Q2: adj EPS $0.12 vs $0.03 est; revenue $198.83M vs $181.26M est (+51% YoY). Customer assets +79% to $28.5B. Stock +14% PM.\n- **BABA** and **FUTU** both reported (see above and below).\n- **FUTU** Q2: revenue $918.2M vs $776.0M est (+36% YoY). Total trading volume record 6.42T HKD (+79% YoY). Funded accounts 3.84M (+34% YoY). Stock +9.5% PM.\n\n---\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **Micron** announced $10B decade-long investment in Boise memory research hub (groundbreaking 2027); comes as Cathie Wood publicly avoids memory stocks, calling HBM "most cyclical" semiconductor segment and citing Cerebras/Groq architectures that reduce HBM dependence.\n- **RARE** (Ultragenyx) +11% PM on FDA accelerated approval of Genglycos (DTX401), first-ever gene therapy for GSD Type Ia; wholesale acquisition cost $2.7M/patient; William Blair models $362M peak sales.\n- **PPC** (Pilgrim's Pride) confirmed JBS made unsolicited acquisition offer at 2.086 JBS shares per PPC share (based on $28.49 close Aug. 18); Board forming special committee.\n- **PANW** FQ4 results imminent — consensus NGS ARR growth of 22.1% is the key bar; CyberArk integration running 3–6 months ahead of synergy targets. ⚠️\n- Data center political backlash intensifying: NRSC warned AI firms that Ohio Senate loss tied to data center opposition could discourage politicians nationwide from backing projects; PA Gov. Shapiro signed executive order imposing new guardrails.\n- OpenAI CFO told employees "will be a public company in 2027 or sooner" (CNBC); Q2 sales growth "tepid" vs Anthropic (WSJ).\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **WMT** Q2 adj EPS $0.81 vs $0.74 est but U.S. comps +2.6% vs +3.8% est, stock -6.2% PM; **DE** Q3 EPS $5.10 vs $4.70 est; **BABA** adj EPADS $1.26 vs $1.85 est; **FUTU** revenue $918M vs $776M est; **WOLF** revenue $149.6M miss $224.5M est |\n| Macro | Treasury doubles long-bond buyback max to $4B effective Sept. 9; initial claims 206K vs 210K est; Philly Fed manufacturing 47.4 (5-yr high) vs 24.1 est |\n| Pharma | Merck/Moderna INTerpath-001 Phase 3 met RFS and DMFS endpoints — first positive Phase 3 for mRNA cancer therapy; RARE FDA accelerated approval of Genglycos gene therapy |\n| Commodities | Gold near $4,500/oz; Brent crude toward $92 on "Operation Economic Fury" vs Iran; U.S. reportedly moving 10M bbl/day through covert Hormuz corridor |\n| Crypto | BTC >$71K, best weekly gain since Nov 2024; $2.74B short liquidation (record); Trump pushes CLARITY Act at White House summit; spot BTC ETF inflows $517M Wed |\n| AI/Tech | MRVL-Google custom chip deal with $12.2B warrant; CBRS CS-4 claims 30x faster inference vs GPU; MU announces $10B Boise research hub; OpenAI CFO says IPO by 2027 |\n| Geopolitics | Trump's "Operation Economic Fury" on Iran; U.S.-Canada tariff deal reportedly near (auto 15%, steel/aluminum 25%); Iran reportedly planning strikes on U.S. targets in Europe |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **MRVL** earnings Aug. 27; consensus EPS $0.87, revenue $2.71B. Google deal details expected on call. ⚠️\n- **ROST** (Ross Stores) reports after close today Aug. 20; consensus EPS $1.94, revenue $6.15B. ⚠️\n- **PANW** FQ4 2026 results expected imminently; consensus NGS ARR growth 22.1% is the key variable. ⚠️\n- **CBRS** CS-4 shipping this quarter; CS-5 planned for 2027; AWS Bedrock availability targeted Q1 2027.\n- CLARITY Act Senate procedural vote on calendar for Sept. 15; remaining sticking point is ethics provision on Trump family crypto interests.\n- U.S.-Canada tariff deadline Saturday Aug. 23 at 12:01 AM EDT; deal reportedly near on 15% auto / 25% steel-aluminum.\n- Treasury expanded buyback program runs Sept. 9 – Nov. 4; $16B 20-year auction today.\n- Fed September meeting: FedWatch shows 32.8% probability of rate hike.\n- **MU** earnings estimated Sept. 22; consensus EPS $31.27, revenue $50.81B.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **BYND** +15.8%, **SOC** +21.4%, **ASTL** +15.3%: no identifiable company-specific catalysts; low-float momentum noise.\n- MRNA premarket -11% is mechanical profit-taking after a +177% single-session move; the fundamental story was fully priced Wednesday.\n- Lengthy HUIZ, ONFO, FLX, JG earnings transcripts in the channel feed — micro-cap names with no relevance to the broader tape.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 336418, "output_tokens": 6807, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 1.68209, "total_cost_usd": 1.852265, "output_cost_usd": 0.170175, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-08-20T13:00:58.966162+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-08-20T13:04:09.255137+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthro