2026-09-01	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 September 1, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Brent crude tops $92 after two Saudi-loaded supertankers are struck in the Strait of Hormuz, pushing 10-year Treasury yields to 4.79% and Fed hike odds to 66.4%, while TSLA +5.7% ahead of Thursday's Cybercab launch, CRWD +6.3% on Fal.Con product wave, and PANW/DELL/AVGO report earnings today and tomorrow with implied moves of 9–11%.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **CRWD** | +6.3% | Mega | Fal.Con product launches; Falcon IQ, Google Cloud, Snowflake integrations | Cybersecurity |\n| **TSLA** | +5.7% | Mega | Cybercab launch event Thursday in Austin | EV / Robotaxi |\n| **PBR** | +4.8% | Mega | Brent crude +4.5% on Hormuz tanker attacks | Energy |\n| **QCOM** | +4.0% | Mega | Analyst Buy ratings; Humain AI PC launch at LEAP 2026 | Semis / Mobile |\n| **EQNR** | +3.6% | Mega | Oil price surge on Middle East escalation | Energy |\n| **DE** | +3.5% | Mega | Baird upgrade to Outperform; PT raised $640→$800 | Ag Equipment |\n| **FTNT** | +3.3% | Mega | Cybersecurity sector momentum post-CRWD beat | Cybersecurity |\n| **PANW** | +3.1% | Mega | Q4 earnings tonight; est. EPS $0.98, rev $3.35B ⚠️ | Cybersecurity |\n| **XOM** | +3.0% | Mega | Crude surge + Venezuela oil deal headlines | Energy |\n| **CRCL** | +9.4% | Large | Cathie Wood/ARK buys; Bernstein $140 PT reiterated | Crypto / Fintech |\n| **RBLX** | +7.2% | Large | Citi flags Q3 bookings tracking ~$1.68B vs $1.61B est. | Gaming |\n| **COIN** | +5.8% | Large | Bitcoin +23% in August; crypto rally momentum | Crypto |\n| **SLB** | +5.5% | Large | Acquiring Kelvion for ~$3.4B; data center cooling play | Energy / Data Center |\n| **ULTA** | +4.3% | Large | No specific catalyst identified | Retail |\n| **LNG** | +3.8% | Large | CCL Stage 3 substantial completion; 5,000th LNG cargo | Energy / LNG |\n| **MSTR** | +3.5% | Large | Strategy buys 4,603 BTC for $370M; "We're Back" | Crypto / Bitcoin |\n| **NEOV** | +23.7% | Small | 5-yr SK On deal for 9 GWh LFP battery cells 2027–2031 | Energy Storage |\n| **TITN** | +17.0% | Small | Mixed Q2 results but ag cycle bottom narrative | Ag Equipment |\n| **STDN** | +13.3% | Small | RBC Capital Outperform; PT raised $11→$13 | Nuclear |\n| **GPRK** | +12.4% | Small | No specific catalyst identified; 7.2× volume | Energy / E&P |\n| **WDAY** | -3.7% | Large | Post-earnings fade after +6% Fri; GS PT $151→$164 Neutral | SaaS / HCM |\n| **ABNB** | -3.7% | Mega | Rosenblatt initiates Buy PT $220; broader risk-off | Travel |\n| **MRVL** | -3.7% pre | Mega | Profit-taking after Q2 beat; gross margin guide soft 57.5-58.5% | AI Compute / Semis |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Strait of Hormuz Escalation & Oil Spike** `Energy / Macro` → ongoing\n\nTwo Saudi-loaded supertankers (Sidr and Senegal Prosperity, each carrying 2M barrels) struck by unknown projectiles 17 nautical miles off Khasab, Oman. Trump threatened further strikes; Iran called "totally defeated." Brent crude surged to $92.31 (+4.5%); WTI at $87.79 (+2.4%).\n\n- **XOM** +3.0%, **PBR** +4.8%, **EQNR** +3.6%, **MPC** +2.5%, **VLO** +2.6%, **SLB** +5.5%\n- **LNG** +3.8%: Cheniere announced CCL Stage 3 substantial completion (7th train turned over Aug 28); total capacity now ~56 mtpa; exported 5,000th LNG cargo\n- U.S. refiners running >95% capacity all summer; GasBuddy analyst De Haan says "no more room" for additional crude processing\n- National avg gas price $4.08/gallon (AAA data Monday)\n- Jim Cramer: "I don't see how rates can go down now" given Warsh hawkishness + oil surge\n- 10-year Treasury yield at 4.79%, highest since Jan 2025; 30-year at 5.26%\n\n**Fed Rate Hike Uncertainty** `Macro / Rates` → ongoing\n\nFed Chair Warsh's Jackson Hole speech drove hike odds sharply higher. Debate splits between hawks and doves heading into Sept 16 FOMC.\n\n- CME FedWatch: 66.4% probability of 25bp hike in September, up from 39.6% a week ago\n- Polymarket: 55% odds of September hike\n- Louis Navellier told Benzinga he'd be "shocked" if Fed hikes; says Warsh's 5 task forces haven't finished work\n- LPL's Jeffrey Roach: "economic data are quite healthy while services inflation is stubbornly elevated" — warrants further tightening\n- Hightower's Stephanie Link: "I don't think he's going to do it in September"\n- 54% of core PCE components above 3% YoY in July 2026 vs 47% a year ago\n- Japan 10-year yield touched 3.003% (30-year high); Bessent says he has "information the market doesn't" on BOJ rate hike\n- Peter Schiff warns 10-year yield heading to 8%; would send mortgages above 10%\n\n**Cybersecurity Earnings Wave** `Cybersecurity` → ongoing\n\n**CRWD** +6.3% (5D +20.7%) continues rally from best-ever Q2 reported last week. **PANW** reports tonight.\n\n- **CRWD**: Fal.Con 2026 product wave — launched Falcon IQ (agentic AI security), Project QuiltWorks expansion, Google Cloud & Snowflake marketplace integrations, Cognizant OT partnership, CLEAR identity integration\n- **CRWD** Q2 FY27: net-new ARR +51% YoY to $333M; total revenue $1.47B; CEO Kurtz: "best quarter in CrowdStrike's history"\n- **PANW** Q4 FY26 earnings tonight ⚠️: est. EPS $0.98 (vs $0.95 YoY), rev $3.35B (vs $2.54B YoY); has beaten rev estimates 11 straight quarters\n- PANW analyst targets: Jefferies Buy $450; BTIG Buy $380; JPMorgan OW $384; BMO OP $415\n- Options imply 8.65–9.91% move for PANW\n- **FTNT** +3.3%, 5D +12.4% — cybersecurity sector tailwind\n- FSB Chair Bailey warned G20 that frontier AI could materially change "speed, scale and economics" of cyber risk\n\n**AI Infrastructure Earnings on Deck** `AI Compute / Semis` → ongoing\n\n**AVGO** reports Wednesday; **DELL** reports Tuesday after close. **MRVL** fading post-earnings despite beat.\n\n- **AVGO** Q3 earnings Wed ⚠️: est. EPS $3.24 (vs $1.69 YoY), rev $29.43B (vs $15.95B YoY); options imply 7.96% move ($139B mkt value at stake)\n- AVGO at VMware Explore: launched VMware Private AI Cloud (150+ AI models), AI Factory, AgentMinder for AI agent governance\n- **DELL** Q2 FY27 earnings Tue after close ⚠️: est. EPS $4.91, rev $44.95B; options imply 9.80–10.67% move; BofA PT raised to $505\n- **MRVL** -3.7% premarket despite Q2 beat (rev $2.74B +37% YoY, adj EPS $0.94 vs $0.92 est); Q3 guide rev $3.15B above $3.03B est but gross margin guide 57.5–58.5% vs 58.9% in Q2\n- Craig-Hallum raised MRVL PT to $300; B. Riley maintained Buy but cut PT to $315; TD Cowen Hold, PT raised to $245\n- **NVDA** -1.3% premarket: invested $3.5B in MediaTek convertible bonds; NVHBM base-die tech targets Broadcom's custom chip market; Counterpoint analyst says NVDA "directly in a market served by Broadcom"\n- BlackRock warns hyperscaler IG bond issuance topped $100B in 2026 (2× 2025 total); urges focus on "scarce AI bottlenecks — power, chips, data center infrastructure"\n\n**SLB's Data Center Pivot** `Energy Services / Data Center` → new\n\n**SLB** +5.5% (5D +11.6%, vol 2.8×) on Kelvion acquisition announcement.\n\n- **SLB** acquiring Kelvion for ~$3.4B cash + ~$0.7B debt assumption from Apollo-managed funds\n- Kelvion: thermal management/heat exchange; 2026E rev $2.3–2.4B, adj EBITDA $350–400M; data center rev $1.2–1.3B\n- Combined data center rev >$2B and ~$300M adj EBITDA pro-forma 2026\n- 2028 target: data center solutions rev $4.5–5.0B, adj EBITDA $700–800M\n- ~$120M annual EBITDA synergies expected within 3 years\n- SLB Data Center Solutions CAGR >90% from 2024–2026; cumulative >2 GW delivered capacity by year-end\n- Piper Sandler OW PT $64; TD Cowen Buy PT $64; Morgan Stanley OW PT $55\n\n**Tesla Cybercab Launch** `EV / Robotaxi` → new\n\n**TSLA** +5.7% ahead of Thursday's invite-only Cybercab unveiling in Austin.\n\n- Cybercab: 2-seat, no steering wheel/pedals, AI4 computer, joins Austin Robotaxi fleet operating since June 2025\n- Musk previously said ~$30,000 price; Polymarket gives 18% chance at $30K or below\n- Ross Gerber: Robotaxi covers ~400 sq miles of 3.5M sq miles in U.S.; "can only grow from here" but warns of scaling timeline\n- Bryn Talkington (Hightower) announced on CNBC she bought more TSLA\n- SpaceX building gas turbine blade foundry in Bastrop, TX — Musk says in-house casting could accelerate turbine deployment by 18 months; SpaceX+Tesla each targeting 100 GW/year solar capacity\n\n**China EV Deliveries** `EV / China` → ongoing\n\n**NIO** reported Q2 and August deliveries. **Li Auto** and **XPeng** also reported August numbers.\n\n- **NIO** Q2: adj EPADS $0.00 (beat -$0.07 est), rev $4.74B (missed $4.78B est); rev +78.5% YoY; vehicle margin 18.5%; Q3 rev guide $4.91–5.02B below $5.07B consensus\n- NIO Aug deliveries: 35,836 (+14.5% YoY); ONVO brand -46.4% YoY\n- **Li Auto** Aug deliveries: 37,679 (+32.1% YoY)\n- **XPeng** Aug deliveries: 39,107 (+4% YoY); received Guangzhou permit for remote testing without safety operator\n\n**Enterprise SaaS Post-Earnings Divergence** `SaaS` → ongoing\n\n**CRM** +23.8% 5D (post-earnings gap); **OKTA** +32.1% 5D; **VEEV** +15.0% 5D; **NOW** +15.5% 5D. But **WDAY** -3.7% fading post-beat.\n\n- **WDAY**: Q2 non-GAAP EPS $2.75 vs $2.61 est (beat); stock rallied 6% Friday then gave it back; Goldman Sachs Neutral PT raised $151→$164; testing key $205 resistance level\n- **CRM**: Argus Research maintains Buy, PT raised to $300; Jeremy Siegel cited CRM as proof "AI investment cycle still has plenty of momentum"\n- **OKTA** +3.2% today, +32.1% 5D\n- **SNOW**: Rosenblatt Buy PT raised $285→$345; Cantor Fitzgerald OW PT raised $282→$405; reports Wed ⚠️ (est. EPS $0.26, rev $1.48B; implied move 12.4%)\n- **GTLB** reports tonight ⚠️: est. EPS $0.18, rev $273.4M; implied move 15%; BTIG Buy PT $36→$52; Cantor Neutral PT $35→$50\n- **MDB** reports tonight ⚠️: est. EPS $1.30, rev $734.2M; implied move 14.9%; Cantor OW PT $416→$540\n\n**Medtronic Pre-Market Beat** `MedTech` → new\n\n**MDT** reported Q1 FY27 before the bell today.\n\n- Q1 adj