2026-09-17	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 September 17, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Broad tech and semi rally led by **INTC** +11.2%, **GNRC** +19.5% on an $8B Amazon data center generator deal, and **VICR** +17.2% on a new AI power licensing agreement, as markets digest the Fed's first rate hike since 2023 (25 bps to 3.75%–4.00%), oil drops 1.6% to $100.81, and 10-year yields retreat to 4.95%.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **INTC** | +11.2% | Mega | SK Hynix Ohio fab talks; Melius $200 2-yr PT; Terafab foundry momentum | AI Compute / Foundry |\n| **ARM** | +8.7% | Mega | CEO Haas says demand "off the charts"; supply constraints for years | AI Compute |\n| **AMD** | +7.8% | Mega | Piper Sandler OW initiation $600 PT; broad semi rebound | AI Compute |\n| **MRVL** | +6.6% | Mega | BofA $365 PT; GFS silicon photonics capacity expansion deal | AI Networking |\n| **DELL** | +6.1% | Mega | AI server demand rebound; +14.2% 5D; RBC OW $640 initiation | AI Infrastructure |\n| **ORCL** | +5.9% | Mega | Technical rebound; $664B backlog; volatile post-earnings recovery | Cloud / AI Infra |\n| **MU** | +5.4% | Mega | Intel CEO warns memory prices up 500%+; shortage may worsen in 2027 | Memory |\n| **SKHY** | +5.4% | Mega | Intel Ohio fab talks; SK Hynix CEO says US plant "necessary" | Memory |\n| **SMCI** | +13.6% | Large | Broad AI infra rebound; DLC rack dominance thesis intact | AI Infrastructure |\n| **HPE** | +9.7% | Large | AI server/networking sector rally; no company-specific catalyst | AI Infrastructure |\n| **TSEM** | +9.6% | Large | Volume shipment of laser-integrated 800G-1.6T optical PICs w/ NewPhotonics | AI Networking / Photonics |\n| **UMC** | +9.0% | Large | Foundry sector sympathy rally with INTC | Semiconductors |\n| **ILMN** | +7.6% | Large | +20.8% 5D; continued genomics momentum (no new catalyst identified) | Genomics |\n| **CIEN** | +7.1% | Large | 3-year targets: ~30% revenue CAGR to FY2029; Morgan Stanley PT to $450 | AI Networking |\n| **GNRC** | +19.5% | Mid | Amazon $8B data center backup generator deal; warrants for 1.69M shares | Data Center Power |\n| **SDGR** | +18.5% | Mid | +50.2% 5D; inducement grants; vol 4.7×; no specific catalyst identified | AI Drug Discovery |\n| **VICR** | +17.2% | Mid | Non-exclusive VPD patent license to unnamed AI OEM | AI Power Delivery |\n| **TEM** | +15.6% | Mid | Morgan Stanley quantifies $80-100M incremental rev from xT pricing | AI Healthcare |\n| **FCEL** | +15.5% | Mid | Data center power complex rally; no company-specific catalyst | Clean Energy / Power |\n| **CYPH** | +27.6% | Mid | +40.6% 5D; TI65 2.2; no specific catalyst identified | Biotech |\n| **SECZ** | +22.7% | Mid | SEC "Innovation Exemption" for tokenized stock trading; vol 3.0× | Tokenization / Crypto |\n| **FLNC** | -14.0% | Mid | FY26 sales guide cut to $2.4B from $2.9-3.1B; EBITDA loss ~$200M | Energy Storage |\n| **CRM** | -2.6% | Mega | FY27 revenue guide raised to high end $46.4B; market wanted more | SaaS / AI |\n| **LEN** | -1.5% | Large | Q3 miss: adj EPS $1.23 vs $1.30 est; rev $8.05B vs $8.37B; guide cut ⚠️ | Homebuilding |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Semiconductor & AI Infrastructure Rebound** `AI Compute / Memory` → ongoing\n\nThe Monday AI-safety selloff has fully reversed. **INTC** +11.2% leads mega-caps on Reuters reporting SK Hynix is in early talks to manufacture memory at Intel's delayed Ohio fabs — either via lease or JV with cloud firms. Melius sees INTC at $200 in two years citing potential Apple/Tesla foundry wins; Tigress raised PT to $145. **AMD** +7.8% on Piper Sandler OW initiation ($600 PT; $2.2T compute market by 2030). **ARM** +8.7% after CEO Haas told CNBC demand has "never been stronger" and supply constraints could persist for years. **MRVL** +6.6% expanded GFS silicon photonics manufacturing deal for AI optical networking. **MU** +5.4% and **SKHY** +5.4% rally on Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan's AI Infrastructure Summit warning that memory prices have surged 5-7x and the shortage could worsen in 2027. **SMCI** +13.6% on broad sector sympathy.\n\n- INTC: SK Hynix exploring lease or JV at Ohio fabs; nothing finalized; SK clarified "no specific plans or arrangements" confirmed.\n- INTC: Melius Buy $165 PT, sees $200 in 2 years if 14A wins Apple/Tesla/hyperscaler; Tigress raised PT $118→$145.\n- ARM: CEO says supply constraints in wafers, substrates, testing, memory could last "several years."\n- MRVL: BofA $365 PT; estimates $30B capture of $60-65B XPU attach market by 2030; analyst day Oct. 6.\n- MU: Reports fiscal Q4 Sept. 30 ⚠️; analysts expect EPS $31.30, rev $50.78B.\n- CIEN: Issued 3-year targets — ~30% revenue CAGR to FY2029, ~50% adj gross margin, 32-35% adj operating margin; Morgan Stanley PT raised to $450.\n- **TSEM** +9.6% on volume shipment of 800G-1.6T laser-integrated optical PICs with NewPhotonics for AI data center interconnects.\n- Huawei unveiled 10+ new AI chipsets including Ascend 960 DT (2x predecessor, Q1 2027 launch) at Huawei Connect in Shanghai.\n\n**Data Center Power & Infrastructure** `Data Center Power` → new\n\n**GNRC** +19.5% (premarket was +33%) after disclosing a long-term supply deal with **AMZN** for up to $8B in backup generators for AWS data centers. Initial deliveries of ~$2.4B in 2027-2028. AMZN issued warrants for 1.69M GNRC shares at ~$200.93. **VICR** +17.2% after licensing its Vertical Power Delivery patents to an unnamed "leading AI OEM" on a non-exclusive basis, adding royalty stream atop product sales. The House passed the Ratepayer Protection Act 417-3, shifting data center generation/transmission costs onto large facilities.\n\n- GNRC: Roth Capital raised PT $214→$250 (Neutral); Canaccord raised PT $275→$375 (Buy).\n- VICR: Needham Buy $320 PT; Craig-Hallum $450 PT; Benzinga Edge momentum score 96.7.\n- Nuclear-adjacent names **OKLO** +12.3%, **XE** +11.5% rallied in sympathy with no company-specific news.\n- ON Semiconductor: CEO says power density is "next massive AI bottleneck"; AI data center rev to more than double in 2026, targeting $2.5B+ by 2030; Stifel Hold PT lowered to $75.\n- Google signed 22-year PPA for up to 50% of Finland's Loviisa nuclear plant output.\n\n**Fed Rate Hike & Macro Dynamics** `Macro` → new\n\nThe FOMC unanimously hiked 25 bps to 3.75%-4.00%, the first increase since July 2023. Sixteen of 18 officials expect at least one more hike this year. Fed Chair Warsh called inflation "too high." The 10-year yield retreated to 4.95% (from 5.04% high) post-decision. Polymarket prices 81% chance of at least one more hike in 2026. Initial jobless claims fell to 196K (vs 207K est). Philly Fed manufacturing 37.8 (vs 31.3 est). Housing starts 1.275M (vs 1.320M est).\n\n- Yardeni cut year-end S&P 500 target from 8,400 to 7,900; raised downturn probability to 30% from 20%.\n- WTI crude -1.6% to $100.81; Brent -2.5% to $103.23 — Trump said he has "directly spoken to Iranians"; Gulf leader meeting planned for Sept. 22-23.\n- US said to delay excess capacity tariffs until after Xi summit (Bloomberg).\n- Gold +2.5% to $4,368.71/oz; silver +4.1% to $65.86.\n- BoE held rates at 3.75%.\n\n**Homebuilders Under Pressure** `Housing` → ongoing\n\n**LEN** -1.5% after Q3 double miss: adj EPS $1.23 vs $1.30 est; rev $8.05B vs $8.37B est. Home-sales gross margin compressed to 15.8% from 17.5%. Full-year delivery guidance cut to 80K-81K from 82K-83K. Q4 guide: 22K-23K deliveries (below 23.8K est), gross margins 15.5%-16%, EPS $1.30-$1.65. Management cited 7%+ mortgage rates, resale competition in Texas/Florida, and immigration-driven labor pressure in ~20% of divisions. Pending home sales +0.3% MoM (vs +2.0% est).\n\n**Salesforce Investor Day Disappoints** `SaaS / AI` → ongoing\n\n**CRM** -2.6% after raising FY27 revenue guide to high end ($46.4B) and reaffirming $63B+ FY30 target at Dreamforce. Market wanted a larger raise. JP Morgan maintained OW $265; Stifel raised PT to $300; Citi Neutral PT to $263. CEO Benioff said Anthropic stake (purchased for "hundreds of millions") is now worth "tens of billions" and will likely be sold to retire $25B ASR debt. Top 100 Agentforce customers generate 2x+ ARR within 18 months; premium license ARR >$1B.\n\n**Crypto & Tokenization** `Digital Assets` → ongoing\n\n**SECZ** +22.7% after SEC issued the "Innovation Exemption" — a 5-year temporary order allowing tokenized U.S. stock trading on public blockchains via automated market makers. CFTC separately expanded no-action relief for crypto software developers. **PURR** (Hyperliquid) +11.4%. **MSTR** +6.8%. Bitcoin held ~$76,400 after House committee advanced Strategic Bitcoin Reserve bill. **CRCL** +7.7% (5D -5.9%) after launching Arc mainnet Sept. 16 with BlackRock, Visa, Mastercard as validators.\n\n**Fluence Energy Guidance Cut** `Energy Storage` → new\n\n**FLNC** -14.0% after slashing FY26 sales guide to $2.4B (from $2.9-3.1B, vs $3.35B est) and guiding adj EBITDA loss of ~$200M (from prior midpoint ~-$10M). Houston contract manufacturing ramp delays cited. Second guidance cut this year. JP Morgan PT cut to $8; RBC to $4; Piper to $5; BNP Paribas to $5.\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- SpaceX now targeting Sept. 28 (delayed from Sept. 22) for Starship Flight 14, its first orbital attempt; Polymarket gives 91% launch probability by Sept. 30. Tesla/SpaceX sued TERA-print over "Terafab" trademark for planned $16.8B Texas AI chip factory.\n- Nebius reportedly hiking GPU cloud prices ~20% effective Oct. 1 (second increase in months); order visibility now extends beyond 24 months. Stock +9% premarket.\n- CoreWeave disclosed $35M ATM offering; separately announced new GPU contracts at ~$40M/MW annualized, up from prior levels; contracted power reached 4.2 GW.\n- Goldman Sachs cut Tesla Q3 delivery forecast to 435K (from 490K); Kalshi traders center around 480K.\n- Japan-US in working-level talks on $12.8-19.3B chip plant with GlobalFoundries as expected operator (Nikkei).\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Macro | Fed hiked 25 bps to 3.75%-4.00% unanimously; 16/18 officials project at least one more hike in 2026; initial claims 196K vs 207K est |\n| Earnings | LEN Q3: adj EPS $1.23 vs $1.30 est; rev $8.05B vs $8.37B; FY delivery guide cut to 80-81K units |\n| Tech | Huawei unveiled 10+ AI chipsets at Huawei Connect; Ascend 960 DT targets Q1 2027 with 2x prior performance |\n| Equities | GNRC issued AMZN warrants for 1.69M shares tied to $8B data center generator supply agreement |\n| Commodities | WTI -1.6% to $100.81; gold +2.5% to $4,368.71; Trump signals Iran war "hopefully" nearing end |\n| Crypto | SEC issued Innovation Exemption for tokenized stock trading; CFTC expanded no-action relief for crypto developers |\n| Geopolitics | US said to delay excess capacity tariffs until after Trump-Xi summit; Trump-Sheinbaum spoke on US-Mexico trade |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **MU fiscal Q4 earnings Sept. 30**: Analysts expect EPS $31.30 on rev $50.78B; Intel CEO warned memory shortage could worsen in 2027.\n- **SpaceX Starship Flight 14 now targeting Sept. 28** (delayed from Sept. 22), pending regulatory approval; first orbital attempt with Starlink V3 satellite deployment.\n- **Triple witching Sept. 18**: Stock index futures, index options, and single-stock options expire simultaneously.\n- **DRI (Darden) reports Q1 pre-market Sept. 24**: EPS est $2.05; rev est $3.21B.\n- **MRVL analyst day Oct. 6**: Investors watching for updated AI market opportunity, margin, and earnings outlook.\n- **Anthropic IPO**: Polymarket gives 87% chance of listing by Dec. 31, 2026; ~73% odds of $2T+ closing market cap on first day.\n- **CIEN**: Halted intraday to announce 3-year targets; ~30% revenue CAGR through FY2029.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **SDGR +18.5%**: No identifiable fundamental catalyst beyond inducement grants and momentum; 4.7× volume suggests speculative activity in a $1.8B name.\n- **CYPH +27.6%**: Micro-cap ($260M) with TI65 of 2.2 and no disclosed catalyst; likely retail-driven momentum.\n- **Whale options flow tables**: High volume on expiring 9/18 contracts (NVDA, AMD, MU) reflects triple-witching positioning, not directional conviction.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 560834, "output_tokens": 4166, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 2.80417, "total_cost_usd": 2.90832, "output_cost_usd": 0.10415, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-09-17T19:21:12.334909+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-17T19:23:11.620736+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from published claude.com/api pricing (input, 5m cache write, cache read, output) — Anthropic does not return dollar amounts on the response.", "total_cost_usd": 2.9083, "total_input_tokens": 560834, "total_output_tokens": 4166, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-09-17", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Channel: tech": 17, "Channel: movers": 13, "Channel: general": 98, "Channel: markets": 26, "Channel: earnings": 17, "Channel: equities": 32, "Channel: commodities": 9, "Ticker Group: r1d_screener": 61, "Ticker Group: vol_spike_5d": 5, "Ticker Group: ti65_mid_small": 2, "Ticker Group: ti65_mega_large": 26, "Channel: macro_economic_events": 19}, "articles_total": 325}, "upserted": 325, "api_by_fetch": {"ticker": {"MU": {"error": null, "api_rows": 12, "in_window": 12}, "XE": {"error": null, "api_rows": 1, "in_window": 1}, "ZS": {"error": null, "api_rows": 2, "in_window": 2}, "ACN": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "AMD": {"error": nu