2026-09-24	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-09-24 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Treasury yields hit 19-year highs as September PMI data cements rate-hike bets, cybersecurity names (PANW +5%, CRWD +5%) defy the selloff, META's Muse ecosystem expands at Connect while GOOGL drops 3.6% on AI-agent disruption fears, and IONQ's real-time quantum error correction milestone lifts the sector.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| PANW | +5.0% | Mega | Q4 FY26 beat all metrics; RPO $21.2B +34% YoY; NGS ARR $9.1B +63% | Cybersecurity |\n| CRWD | +5.0% | Mega | New 52-week high; Ritholtz/Brown picks as preferred cyber name | Cybersecurity |\n| PLTR | +3.7% | Mega | Rosenblatt reiterates Buy/$225 PT; Burry short squeeze speculation | AI / Defense |\n| BP | +3.2% | Mega | JPMorgan upgrade to Overweight, PT raised to 675p (~$54 ADS) | Energy / Oil |\n| NOW | +2.8% | Mega | Sector rotation into quality SaaS; no specific catalyst | SaaS |\n| FSLY | **+13.7%** | Small | Traders circulating data showing 29.3% of Meta Muse traffic; DA Davidson/BofA raise PTs | Edge / CDN |\n| NNBR | **+14.5%** | Small | Vol spike 7.3×; no identified catalyst | Idiosyncratic |\n| SECZ | +10.5% | Small | +84.8% 5D; continued momentum from SEC tokenization framework | Crypto / RWA |\n| VICR | +5.5% | Mid | Raised Q3 revenue guidance; RSI 76.6 overbought; +54% 5D | Power / AI Compute |\n| META | +1.0% | Mega | Connect 2026: $1,299 VR glasses, Muse voice/video, retail partnerships | AI / Consumer |\n| IONQ | +4.4% | Mid | First real-time quantum error correction decoder on single CPU; Superion 256 at NVIDIA NVAQC | Quantum Computing |\n| INTC | -1.0% | Mega | Profit-taking after +21.3% 5D rally on Meta Muse CPU demand thesis | Semiconductors |\n| MSTR | -3.1% | Large | BTC fell to $83.7K; bearish put sweeps; +28.6% 5D | Crypto / Bitcoin |\n| BFLY | -7.3% | Small | Profit-taking after Needham Buy/$10 initiation sent shares +35% | MedTech |\n| SGRY | -7.8% | Small | No identified catalyst; giving back prior 5D +4.5% gap | Idiosyncratic |\n| MGM | -9.4% PM | Large | People Inc. withdrew takeover proposal for all public shares | Gaming / M&A |\n| VKTX | -12.3% PM | Mid | Announced pair of proposed public offerings (equity dilution) | Biotech / GLP-1 |\n| SFIX | -18.2% PM | Small | Q4 EPS -$0.02 beat -$0.06 est; rev $324.4M missed $325.5M; weak FY27 guide $1.31-1.36B vs $1.41B est | Retail |\n| COST | flat | Mega | Q4 earnings after close today; est EPS $6.53, rev $94.82B ⚠️ | Retail |\n| DRI | flat | Large | Q1 EPS $2.05 missed $2.06; rev $3.20B missed $3.21B | Restaurants |\n| SNX | +adj | Large | Q3 EPS $5.68 beat $4.70 est (+20.9%); rev $21.56B beat $18.91B (+14%) | IT Distribution |\n| BB | +adj | Large | Q2 EPS $0.07 beat $0.04 est (+75%); rev $163.3M beat $145.6M (+12.1%) | Cybersecurity / IoT |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Cybersecurity Outperformance Amid Yield Shock** `Cybersecurity` → ongoing\n\n**PANW** +5.0%, **CRWD** +5.0%, **FTNT** +2.6%, **OKTA** +4.5%, **RBRK** +3.3%, **NET** -0.2% — cybersecurity names diverged sharply from the broader tech selloff Wednesday and are extending gains Thursday.\n\n- **PANW** reported Q4 FY26: revenue $3.41B (+34% YoY); RPO $21.2B (+34%); NGS ARR $9.1B (+63%); added ~$1B net new NGS ARR in Q4 alone; ~220 net new platformizations (record). FY27 guidance: revenue $14.1-14.2B (+23-24%); NGS ARR $11.075-11.175B (+22-23%). Closed CyberArk (now Idera) and Chronosware acquisitions ahead of synergy targets. Launched Unit 42 AI-powered security service using Anthropic/OpenAI models; $17M investment.\n- **CRWD** hit new 52-week high $261.44 Wed. Morgan Stanley raised PT to $254 Overweight (Sept. 21); Stephens raised to $280 Overweight (Sept. 18); BofA raised to $260 Neutral. Benzinga Edge Momentum score 98.17.\n- **OKTA** +4.5%: Wells Fargo raised PT $200→$230 Overweight; Barclays raised PT $180→$215 Overweight.\n- **RBRK** +3.3%: Baird raised PT $130→$139 Outperform.\n- Ritholtz Wealth's Josh Brown named PANW, CRWD, FTNT, NET as preferred cyber names; excluded ZS and SentinelOne.\n- AI-driven threat landscape (Anthropic's Mythos model, rogue AI agents) cited as structural tailwind for security spending.\n\n**Meta Muse Ecosystem Expansion vs. Disruption Casualties** `AI / Consumer` → ongoing\n\n**META** +1.0% (5D +10.5%) — Connect 2026 unveiled $1,299 VR glasses (spring 2027 launch, ~100g), camera-free Ray-Ban Audio at $349 (Oct. 13), and expanded Muse capabilities. Muse hit 2.8M downloads in first 12 days.\n\n- Muse retail integrations: Walmart, Best Buy, Gap, Sephora, Wayfair, Dick's Sporting Goods, Ulta, Fanatics, Expedia, Instacart. Shopify/Shop Pay and PayPal payment integrations live. 1,500+ developer connector applications received.\n- Zuckerberg: Muse "free for a huge number of tokens"; revenue model via transaction fees. Cantor Fitzgerald raised PT $680→$860 Overweight; KeyBanc raised PT to $900 Overweight. JPMorgan says Muse could become most widely used consumer AI app since ChatGPT.\n- Dolby Atmos/Vision coming to Meta AI glasses and VR devices.\n- FDA-cleared hearing aid feature for Meta glasses, $149.99 or included with Meta One subscription.\n- **GOOGL/GOOG** -3.6% Wed as investors priced in risk that AI agents bypass search. Gene Munster: Muse is "bad news for GOOG." Goldman Sachs flagged "consumer inertia" stocks at risk: BKNG, EXPE, ABNB, TRIP all fell 4-7% Wed. ABNB also hit by Muse's ability to book homes directly.\n- **FSLY** +13.7% (4.3× vol): Traders circulating independent test showing Fastly carried 29.3% of Meta Muse agent traffic vs. Cloudflare at 37.0%. DA Davidson raised PT $21→$23 Neutral; BofA raised PT $20→$22 Underperform.\n- Citrini Research estimated Charles Schwab earns ~$9B annually from "inertia rent" (low cash yields, high margin rates); AI agents like Muse could erode this advantage.\n\n**Bond Yield Surge — 10-Year at 19-Year High** `Macro` → ongoing\n\nEntire U.S. yield curve reaching multi-year peaks. 10Y at 5.13%, 2Y at 4.90%, 30Y at 5.43%.\n\n- S&P Global flash September PMI showed fastest U.S. private-sector growth in 5+ years, cementing rate-hike expectations.\n- CME FedWatch: 70.9% probability of Fed rate hike after October meeting.\n- Mohamed El-Erian: yield surge driven by government borrowing, Fed signaling, hyperscaler corporate debt; attributes market surprise to "psychological anchoring" from post-2008 low-rate era.\n- Fed Chair Warsh called 2% inflation "a firm, fixed target"; Fed raised benchmark rate 25bp last week (first hike since 2023). August CPI at 3.4%.\n- McDonald's CEO Kempczinski: "inflation's going to be with us for, unfortunately, many more years at an elevated level."\n- Initial jobless claims 197K vs 201K est; continuing claims 1,719K vs 1,750K est.\n- USA current account Q2: -$246B vs -$255B est.\n\n**Oil & Energy — Strait of Hormuz, Diesel Export Ban Debate** `Energy / Commodities` → ongoing\n\n**BP** +3.2%, **EQNR** +2.6%, **COP** +2.2%, **TTE** +2.0%, **DVN** +2.4%, **E** +3.0% — energy broadly higher as geopolitical risk premium returns and diesel debate continues.\n\n- WTI crude +2.4% to ~$93.82; Brent +2.3% to ~$105.41. National average gasoline $4.48/gal; diesel record $6.51/gal (AAA).\n- White House denied 90-day diesel export ban; Energy Secretary Chris Wright broke with Trump, calling ban ineffective. 30+ industry groups including US Chamber urged Trump to reject export restrictions.\n- Iran Security Chief Rezaee: Strait of Hormuz will not reopen without conditions met; warned neighboring countries against enforcing U.S. sanctions.\n- Treasury Sec. Bessent: 80-90% of Iran's external flights shut down under "Operation Economic Outcast."\n- **BP**: JPMorgan upgraded Neutral→Overweight, PT raised to 675p (~$54 ADS). **TTE**: JPMorgan downgraded Overweight→Neutral. **DVN**: Activist Toms Capital urging sale exploration; now top-5 shareholder.\n- **VLO**: Goldman Sachs raised PT $365→$457 Buy. Refiner monthly RSIs "well into 80s" — Fundstrat's Newton warns overbought.\n- Oil & gas PE deal count fell 60% QoQ to 16 in Q2; deal value dropped 65.4% to $3.4B (PitchBook). Shell agreed to acquire ARC Resources for $16.4B.\n\n**Quantum Computing Milestone** `Quantum Computing` → new\n\n**IONQ** +4.4% (3.7× vol, +15.5% 5D) — demonstrated industry's first end-to-end real-time quantum error correction decoder on single commercial CPU. Validated across 408 logical qubits and 31.5M+ quantum operations with 0.02% processing overhead.\n\n- IonQ Superion 256 will be first QPU installed at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC), connected to GB200 NVL72 via NVQLink. Installation 2027.\n- **Infleqtion** (INFQ) announced 30 entangled logical qubits using 80 physical qubits on Sqale platform — first neutral-atom company to reach 30 logical qubits on commercial system.\n- Rigetti (RGTI) +4%, D-Wave (QBTS) +5% in sympathy. Quantum World Congress Sep. 23-25.\n- Wedbush maintained Outperform/$75 PT on IONQ; Rosenblatt maintained Buy/$100 PT.\n\n**AI Capex Sustainability Debate** `AI Infrastructure` → ongoing\n\nHyperscalers expected to spend ~$750B on data centers this year, $1T+ next year, $5T+ across four years. Wharton's Jessica Wachter: companies must achieve 2.7× productivity gains by 2030 to cover costs; otherwise "largest misallocation of capital in history."\n\n- Alphabet posted first negative free-cash flow quarter since 2004 IPO ($5.9B deficit). Morgan Stanley: >50% of $2.9T hyperscaler spend through 2028 financed externally.\n- **TSMC** reportedly planning 3-6% wafer price increases starting Jan 2027; demand visibility extends to 2030; 8-inch fabs above 100% utilization. CLSA: GPU/custom AI chip supply deficit ~73%, shortage could persist to 2030.\n- **CoreWeave** (CRWV): JPMorgan upgraded Neutral→Overweight, PT $120→$125; UBS initiated Buy/$120, calling stock's 3× 2027 revenue multiple evidence of deep skepticism. New multi-year Harell Data biotech AI platform deal.\n- **SoftBank** launched $11.1B bond sale ($10.5B USD + €1B EUR) to fund final $10B OpenAI investment tranche (closing Oct. 1). USD tranches at 8.625%, 9.25%, 9.75%.\n- Stanford survey of ~6,000 executives: ~90% reported no AI productivity increase over 3 years.\n- Fidelity strategist: AI buildout is "inflationary" with "unknown returns."\n\n**TD Synnex / BlackBerry Earnings Beats** `IT Distribution / Cybersecurity` → new\n\n- **SNX** Q3: EPS $5.68 beat $4.70 est (+20.9%); revenue $21.56B beat $18.91B est (+14.0%); YoY revenue +37.8%.\n- **BB** Q2: EPS $0.07 beat $0.04 est (+75%); revenue $163.3M beat $145.6M est (+12.1%); YoY revenue +26%.\n\n**Trump-Xi Summit & Trade Truce Extension** `Macro / Geopolitics` → new\n\n- Chinese President Xi Jinping arrived in U.S. for three-day state visit. Trump welcomed with B-1 bomber flyover at Joint Base Andrews.\n- Bessent announced two-month extension of U.S.-China trade truce to Jan. 10.\n- State dinner Thursday expected to include Tim Cook, Jensen Huang, Sam Altman, Elon Musk (Polymarket: 100% attendance probability).\n- Musk called Xi "great leader" and "very capable" in CGTN interview.\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **Everpure** (P) +6.7% premarket after reaffirming FY27 revenue $5.03-5.07B and issuing preliminary FY28 revenue $7.0-7.3B (+39-45%); Wells Fargo raised PT $135→$145 Overweight. Eight consecutive quarters of accelerating revenue growth.\n- **MGM** -9.4% premarket: People Inc. withdrew its proposal to purchase all public MGM shares.\n- **VICR** +5.5% (+54% 5D): Raised Q3 revenue guidance citing licensed OEM/hyperscaler ecosystem; RSI at 76.6. Benzinga flagged as overbought.\n- **WBD** -0.2% (2.5× vol, +9.6% 5D): Semafor reports Paramount Skydance CEO David Ellison approached Elon Musk for equity investment in WBD merger.\n- **INOD** +2.9% (+29.9% 5D, 3.6× vol): Sustained momentum; no specific catalyst identified for Thursday.\n- Broadcom faces China probe: SASAC found Broadcom switches in up to 90% of state-owned companies; may issue informal guidance to reduce usage.\n- **Netlist** (NLST) announced ITC opened patent investigation into Micron, Supermicro, HPE, Lenovo over possible import ban on Micron memory.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **SNX** Q3 EPS $5.68 beat $4.70 est; rev $21.56B beat $18.91B; **BB** Q2 EPS $0.07 beat $0.04; **DRI** Q1 EPS $2.05 missed $2.06; **COST** reports after close today (est EPS $6.53, rev $94.82B) |\n| Macro | US initial jobless claims 197K vs 201K est; 10Y yield at 5.13% (19-year high); CME FedWatch 70.9% probability of October rate hike; Bessent extended US-China trade truce to Jan. 10 |\n| Commodities | WTI crude +2.4% to $93.82; Brent +2.3% to $105.41; White House denied 90-day diesel export ban; Iran's Rezaee reaffirmed Strait of Hormuz will not reopen without conditions |\n| Tech | Meta Connect 2026: $1,299 VR glasses, Muse voice/video, FDA-cleared hearing aid; Google DeepMind says Gemini 4 could launch "much earlier" than year-end; TSMC planning 3-6% wafer price hikes Jan 2027 |\n| AI Safety | Nvidia CEO Huang: labs should "shut down" if they can't control AI; Sanders cited comment to support ASI ban bill; Altman/Amodei warned UN Security Council of AI risks to humanity |\n| Quantum | IonQ first real-time quantum error correction decoder on single CPU; Infleqtion achieved 30 entangled logical qubits on 80 physical qubits; Quantum World Congress underway |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **MU earnings Sept. 30**: Wall Street expects EPS $31.45 vs $3.03 YoY; revenue $51.05B vs $11.31B. BofA Buy/$1,550; Rosenblatt Buy/$1,500; Wells Fargo OW lowered to $1,400; Citi Buy raised to $1,300. Michael Burry added to MU short position. ⚠️\n- **COST Q4 earnings after close today** (Sept. 24): est EPS $6.53, rev $94.82B. Six straight revenue beats. ⚠️\n- **NKE Q1 earnings Oct. 1**: est EPS $0.44 vs $0.49 YoY; rev $11.34B vs $11.72B. Baird downgraded to Neutral; Morgan Stanley reinstated Underweight/$31. ⚠️\n- **STZ Q2 earnings Oct. 6**: est EPS $3.56 vs $3.63 YoY; rev $2.54B. Multiple analysts cut PTs in September (Citi to $165, Barclays to $122, Evercore to $160). ⚠️\n- **LW Q1 earnings Oct. 6**: est EPS $0.59, rev $1.66B. ⚠️\n- **Trump-Xi bilateral talks and state dinner Thursday**: Taiwan, AI, trade discussions. Tech leaders attending.\n- **Fed Richmond President Barkin** speaks 8:30 a.m. ET Thursday.\n- **New home sales data** (August) at 10:00 a.m. ET; Kansas City Fed manufacturing survey at 11:00 a.m. ET.\n- **SoftBank $11.1B bond sale** pricing for final $10B OpenAI tranche (closing Oct. 1).\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **NNBR** +14.5% on 7.3× volume with no identifiable catalyst — likely micro-cap noise/short squeeze.\n- **BENF** +439% Wednesday then -35% premarket Thursday — restructuring announcement already fully priced; extreme volatility in $3M market cap name.\n- Bulk pre-market mover lists (DCX, WETO, SPHL, CPOP etc.) — all sub-$100M market cap names with no material catalysts; noise for this audience.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 272155, "output_tokens": 5276, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 1.360775, "total_cost_usd": 1.492675, "output_cost_usd": 0.1319, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-09-24T12:37:44.625129+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-24T12:40:24.260832+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from published claude.com/api pricing (input, 5m cache write, cache read, output) — Anthropic does not return dollar amounts on the response.", "total_cost_usd": 1.4927, "total_input_tokens": 272155, "total_output_tokens": 5276, "total_cac