2026-09-25	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-09-25 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: META surges to $2T market cap on Muse momentum with PT raises across the Street, AKAM soars 21% on an $11.6B Anthropic cloud deal, Goldman projects hyperscaler AI capex rising 50% to $1.2T, while Iran signals willingness to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and 10-year Treasury yields sit at 5.17%.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **META** | +4.5% | Mega | Muse AI adoption; Piper Sandler PT $875; JPM PT $920 | Consumer AI / Platform |\n| **LLY** | +3.5% | Mega | FDA approved once-weekly insulin Onswik; $3.25B InnoCare pact | Pharma |\n| **INTC** | +2.8% | Mega | TSMC price hikes 3-6% signal tight foundry capacity; 5D +16% | Semiconductors |\n| **NET** | +2.8% | Mega | Continuation of AI infrastructure theme | SaaS / Edge |\n| **AMD** | +2.0% | Mega | BofA PT raised $620→$720 Buy; $1T+ market cap sustained | AI Compute |\n| **ARM** | −6.7% | Mega | Oracle force majeure notice on Project Jupiter; sympathy sell | AI Compute |\n| **P** | +12.6% | Large | FAM: FY28 rev $7-7.3B guide; FY27 reaffirmed; 7 PT raises | Data Storage / AI |\n| **AKAM** | +21% PM | Large | $11.6B 7-yr Anthropic cloud deal; warrant for ~5% equity | AI Cloud Infrastructure |\n| **NBIS** | +8.4% | Large | BNP Paribas upgrade to Outperform PT $399; ~20% GPU price hike Oct 1 | AI Cloud Infrastructure |\n| **RKLB** | +4.3% | Large | Iridium shareholders approve acquisition; NITE-STAR $981M contract | Space / Defense |\n| **TWLO** | +4.3% | Large | HSBC downgrades to Reduce PT $211 (contrarian to 5D +23% rally) | CPaaS / SaaS |\n| **OKTA** | +1.1% | Large | 17 analyst PT raises in two sessions; Stephens PT $190→$240 | Cybersecurity / SaaS |\n| **CLS** | +4.4% | Large | AI infrastructure buildout momentum; 5D +14.5% | AI Infra Services |\n| **GRAL** | +15.8% | Mid | FDA panel voted 7-2 benefits>risks for Galleri cancer screen | Diagnostics |\n| **GLND** | +84.9% | Micro | Extended Jameson Land farm-out deadlines to 2028; Greenland theme | Oil & Gas Exploration |\n| **CDNA** | +14.4% | Mid | BTIG raised PT $60→$74 Buy | Diagnostics |\n| **WRBY** | +12.4% | Mid | No identified catalyst; strong consumer discretionary bid | Retail / Idiosyncratic |\n| **QMCO** | +17.8% | Small | Momentum continuation; vol 3.5× avg | Data Storage |\n| **TSSI** | +11.0% | Micro | Momentum continuation; vol 3.1× avg | AI Data Center Infra |\n| **FSLY** | −10.2% | Mid | DA Davidson questions Muse traffic revenue potential; BofA UW | CDN / Edge |\n| **COST** | flat PM | Mega | Q4 EPS $6.75 vs $6.52 est; rev $95.72B vs $94.86B est | Retail ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**AI Cloud Infrastructure Spending Accelerates** `AI Compute / AI Cloud` → ongoing\n\nGoldman Sachs projects hyperscaler AI capex rising 50% to $1.2 trillion, reinforcing the demand backdrop for GPU cloud, server and power infrastructure names. **AKAM** +21% premarket after announcing an $11.6B 7-year cloud commitment from Anthropic for CPU workloads, with a warrant covering ~5% of AKAM shares (exercise price $111.33) and ~$5.5B in related capex including $1.7B additional in 2026. **NBIS** +8.4% after BNP Paribas upgraded to Outperform with PT raised $260→$399, citing potential $22B ARR by 2027-end; Nebius also reportedly plans ~20% GPU cloud price hikes effective Oct 1 (H100 to $4.50 from $3.85, H200 to $5.40 from $4.50). **SMCI** +0.8% began shipping NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72 racks; ~$60B order book supports FY27 revenue guide of $65-72B.\n\n- Goldman sees AMZN, GOOG, MSFT, META, ORCL combined 2027 capex potentially exceeding $1.3T.\n- **CRWV** completed $4.2B convertible offering (2.875% notes due 2033); ~$3.57B net of capped-call costs; total debt now $35.5B+ per June 10-Q.\n- Musk says SpaceXAI Colossus 2 could run >1.2M NVIDIA GB200/GB300 chips by year-end.\n- **DELL** −1.1% in sympathy with Oracle force majeure notice on Project Jupiter data center.\n- **ARM** −6.7% on same Oracle sympathy selling despite ARM CEO's prior comment that AGI CPU demand is "off the charts."\n- SoftBank launching $11.1B bond sale to fund final $10B OpenAI investment tranche; ARM exposed via SoftBank ownership.\n- Wells Fargo initiated **ETN** Overweight PT $503; Eaton acquiring COL Group for €810M to expand European data center power capacity.\n\n**Meta's Muse AI Reshapes Consumer Platform Economics** `Consumer AI / Platform` → ongoing\n\n**META** +4.5% to $777, now the world's 7th most valuable public company (~$1.98T cap), overtaking SpaceX. Muse AI agent launched Sept 8 and topped U.S. App Store; CEO Zuckerberg said Muse will be "the centerpiece of Meta." Gene Munster admitted he "missed" the significance, now sees Zuckerberg in "wartime CEO mode" pursuing a re-rating.\n\n- Piper Sandler raised PT $785→$875 Overweight; JPMorgan PT $820→$920 Overweight; Raymond James PT $650→$860 Strong Buy; Tigress PT $945→$995 Strong Buy.\n- JPMorgan's Anmuth says Muse could be "most widely used consumer AI app since ChatGPT"; Evercore expects 100M users in 6-12 months.\n- Jefferies estimates Muse could generate $10.8B annual revenue by 2027 under aggressive adoption.\n- Amazon blocked Muse from its retail site but opened seller data to Anthropic's Claude.\n- Citrini Research published 90-stock "Agentic Subscription Losers Basket" — subscription businesses exposed to AI cancellation agents driven by Muse-type products.\n- **FSLY** −10.2% after DA Davidson analyst questioned whether Muse traffic would materially affect Fastly revenue; estimated full Muse opportunity at ~$16.3M or ~2% of CY26 Fastly revenue.\n- HSBC downgraded **TWLO** to Reduce with PT $211, diverging from the stock's 5D +23% rally.\n\n**Semiconductor Demand Tightens, Foundry Pricing Rises** `Semiconductors` → ongoing\n\n**AMD** +2.0% premarket, sustaining above $1T market cap after crossing the milestone Monday. BofA raised PT $620→$720 Buy. OptionsPlay strategist sees $750 by November.\n\n- **INTC** +2.8%, +15.9% 5D; TSMC reportedly planning 3-6% wafer price hikes starting Jan 2027 with steeper increases for advanced nodes; demand visibility now extends to 2030.\n- CLSA analyst says GPU/custom AI chip demand exceeds supply by ~73%; shortage could persist until ~2030.\n- Mizuho initiated **TSEM** (Tower Semiconductor) Outperform PT $300 (stock at $217).\n- TD Cowen reiterated Hold on INTC, maintaining PT $115.\n\n**Everpure (P) — AI Storage Inflection** `Data Storage / AI` → new\n\n**P** +12.6% after its Financial Analyst Meeting outlined expansion beyond core storage into AI, data software and hyperscale. FY27 revenue reaffirmed at $5.03-5.07B (+37-38% YoY); preliminary FY28 guide: rev $7-7.3B, non-GAAP OI $1.7-1.9B.\n\n- Barclays raised PT $110→$132 Equal-Weight; Piper Sandler PT $133→$162 Overweight; Citigroup PT $130→$160 Buy; Morgan Stanley PT $119→$137 Overweight; Wells Fargo PT $135→$145 OW; 7+ firms raised targets.\n- CEO Giancarlo called it an "inflection point."\n- Q2 EPS 70c beat 58c est; revenue $1.186B beat $1.097B est.\n\n**Diagnostics and Life Sciences Rally** `Healthcare / Diagnostics` → ongoing\n\n**GRAL** +15.8% (5D +67%) after FDA advisory panel voted 7-2 that Galleri multi-cancer screening test benefits outweigh risks (unanimous on safety, 6-4 on efficacy). **ILMN** +8.3%, **A** (Agilent) +5.3%, **NTRA** +4.7%, **CDNA** +14.4% (BTIG raised PT $60→$74), **TMO** +2.4% hitting fresh all-time high, **VCYT** +10.9%. **LLY** +3.5% on FDA approval of Onswik once-weekly insulin + $3.25B InnoCare licensing deal. Mizuho raised GRAL PT $65→$100 Neutral.\n\n**Costco Q4 Beat, Modest Premarket Reaction** `Retail` → new\n\n**COST** flat premarket (−0.2%) despite Q4 EPS $6.75 vs $6.52 est and revenue $95.72B vs $94.86B est. Comparable sales +9.4%; digitally enabled comps +19.5%. Management flagged rising electronics costs from memory inflation and received $184M in IEEPA tariff refunds. FY27 capex guided at ~$7.5B. Bernstein trimmed PT $1,144→$1,143; Mizuho cut PT $1,100→$1,065; both maintained Outperform.\n\n**Geopolitics: Iran Signals, Trump-Xi Summit, Diesel Squeeze** `Macro / Geopolitics` → ongoing\n\nIran FM Araghchi proposed reopening Strait of Hormuz and restarting nuclear talks within 7 days if U.S. meets MoU conditions. USTR Greer says U.S. reached agreements with China on subset of goods; details to be released Monday. Trump called Xi meeting "very productive." WTI crude −1.9% to ~$92.81; Brent −0.5% to ~$106. Diesel at record $6.51/gal; Energy Sec Wright urging refiners to voluntarily cut diesel exports. 10-year yield at 5.17%; 30-year at 5.47%. CME FedWatch shows 66.4% odds of October rate hike.\n\n- August durable goods orders 0.0% vs −0.3% est; core orders +0.3% vs +0.6% est.\n- Iran Parliament Speaker Ghalibaf mocked U.S. over "1970s rates" and high gas prices.\n- USTR confirms "no urgency" on Canada trade talks; Mexico deficit discussions ongoing.\n\n**Rocket Lab Advances Iridium Deal, Wins Space Force Contract** `Space / Defense` → ongoing\n\n**RKLB** +4.3%; Iridium shareholders approved acquisition (mid-2027 close target; $54/share notional value). RKLB also named to Space Force NITE-STAR contract ($981M ceiling, 15 vendors, 10-year). Completed $1.94B ATM equity offering (29.3M shares) to fund Iridium cash payments. Raymond James initiated Outperform PT $80.\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **MSFT** announced new Copilot with Home, Code and Autopilot Agent on usage-based billing — could shift enterprise AI monetization model.\n- Trump told OpenAI and Anthropic to withhold models from UK safety agency (Bloomberg); potential AI governance friction.\n- **OKTA** saw 17 analyst PT raises across two sessions; identity/access management may be benefiting from agentic AI security demand.\n- Kodiak AI (**KDK**) plans to launch unsupervised driverless long-haul trucking on Dallas-Houston lane by year-end.\n- Blue Origin raised $10B at ~$140B valuation; Bezos now in at ~$30B total.\n- Tesla Optimus robot faces "major manufacturing and durability issues" with hands per The Information; production target 1K+/week by end-2026.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **COST** Q4 EPS $6.75 vs $6.52 est; rev $95.72B vs $94.86B; comps +9.4%; flagged memory-driven electronics cost inflation |\n| Macro | Aug durable goods 0.0% vs −0.3% est; core +0.3% vs +0.6% est; 10Y yield 5.17%; diesel $6.51/gal record; CME 66.4% odds Oct hike |\n| Tech | Goldman sees hyperscaler AI capex rising 50% to $1.2T; AKAM $11.6B Anthropic deal; MSFT launches usage-based Copilot billing |\n| Geopolitics | Iran FM proposes 7-day Hormuz reopening framework; USTR says U.S.-China goods agreements to be released Monday |\n| Commodities | WTI −1.9% to $92.81; Energy Sec Wright urges voluntary diesel export cuts; White House denies 90-day ban |\n| Equities | **P** issues FY28 prelim guide: rev $7-7.3B; **GRAL** FDA panel 7-2 favorable vote for Galleri |\n| Crypto | BTC $84,580; whales accumulated ~30,269 BTC ($2.57B) over 96 hours; ARK tokenizes venture fund on Ethereum via SECZ |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **COST** post-earnings analyst day/call reactions expected throughout Friday; multiple PT adjustments already issued.\n- **PEP** earnings due Oct 8; consensus EPS $2.30, rev $25B. BNP Paribas cut PT $183→$161.\n- **MTN** (Vail Resorts) Q4 earnings Monday Sept 28 after close; consensus loss $5.26/share; Stifel PT cut to $161, Mizuho PT cut to $160.\n- **LEVI** Q3 earnings Oct 7 after close; consensus EPS $0.36, rev $1.62B.\n- **ACN** (Accenture) Q4 earnings expected Oct 1 before open; BMO raised PT to $200.\n- Trump, Mike Johnson, tech CEOs meeting on AI oversight reportedly scheduled Sept 29.\n- OpenAI DevDay Sept 29 in San Francisco; GPT-6 Cyber model may be previewed (Fortune report).\n- NBIS GPU price hikes effective Oct 1 — watch for customer/volume response.\n- FDA mifepristone review update due to Louisiana court Oct 7.\n- Google Project Suncatcher (space data center) launches Oct 1.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **GLND** +85%: micro-cap ($234M) speculative Greenland energy play on farm-out extension; extreme volatility with no fundamental cash flow anchor.\n- Multiple micro-cap movers (INLF +97%, APUS +23%, CTNT +53%): thinly traded, no institutional relevance.\n- Extensive transcript coverage of Tamboran Resources (TBN), Sequans (SQNS), Leidos (LDOS) and other smaller earnings calls — no material surprises vs. expectations in any of them.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 391412, "output_tokens": 4284, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 1.95706, "total_cost_usd": 2.06416, "output_cost_usd": 0.1071, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-09-25T13:27:10.182482+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-25T13:29:26.272869+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from published claude.com/api pricing (input, 5m cache write, cache read, output) — Anthropic does not return dollar amounts on the response.", "total_cost_usd": 2.0642, "total_input_tokens": 391412, "total_output_tokens": 4284, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-09-25", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Channel: tech": 4, "Channel: movers": 10, "Channel: general": 100, "Channel: markets": 24, "Channel: earnings": 11, "Channel: equities": 8, "Channel: commodities": 5, "Ticker Group: r1d_screener": 61, "Ticker Group: vol_spike_5d": 14, "Ticker Group: ti65_mid_small": 2, "Ticker Group: ti65_mega_large": 21, "Channel: macro_economic_events": 4}, "articles_total": 264}, "upserted": 264, "api_by_fetch": {"ticker": {"A":