, **ZS** +2.0% all closed green while QQQ fell 0.84% and the 10-year yield surged 16.8 bps to 5.12%. IGV closed +1.26%, the lone broad ETF in the green, reflecting the intra-day rotation into software/security names.\n\n- Morgan Stanley raised **PANW** PT to **$410**, Overweight; Wedbush initiated **$400** Outperform; Bernstein Market Perform $351; Daiwa Buy $390.\n- Unit 42 launched **Continuous Frontier AI Defense**, a subscription service built on Anthropic and OpenAI models combined with Palo Alto threat intelligence — a new ARR-generating product layer.\n- Ritholtz/Josh Brown publicly named **CRWD**, **PANW**, and **FTNT** as preferred cybersecurity holdings; **CRWD** +8.8% over 5 days, **RBRK** +10.1% over 5 days.\n- **OKTA**: five separate analyst PT raises on the same session — BTIG $187→**$219** Buy; Scotiabank $165→**$190** Outperform; Baird →**$200** Outperform; BofA $170→**$200** Neutral; Wells Fargo →**$200**; all citing AI Agents demand and **Oktane '26** conference as near-term catalyst. ⚠️\n- **TWLO** +2.2%, reached highest level since November 2021: Morgan Stanley specifically flagged Meta Muse AI agents as a communications-volume driver for Twilio. Prior session: Rosenblatt and TD Cowen raised PTs (specific targets not disclosed).\n\n---\n\n**Energy Macro: Brent at $103, BP Upgrade, Refiner Diesel Risk** `[Energy / Macro]` → new\n\nBrent crude November futures +3.9% to **$103.08/bbl**; WTI +1.8% to **$92.16/bbl**, lifting the entire energy complex. Simultaneously, diesel-export-restriction headlines created a bifurcation within energy — crude producers rose while refiners faced regulatory overhang.\n\n- **BP** +3.2%: JPMorgan upgraded Neutral→**Overweight**, raised PT 550p→**675p** (~$54 ADR); projected total financial obligations to fall **50% by end of 2027**; upstream volume growth ~3%/year 2030–2035.\n- **COP** +2.2%, **EQNR** +2.6%, **E** +3.0%, **DVN** +2.4%, **TTE** +2.0%: all attributed primarily to crude rally; no ticker-specific catalysts identified.\n- **TTE** +2.0% despite JPMorgan simultaneously downgrading it from Overweight→**Neutral**, citing highest direct Middle East asset exposure among European majors and windfall-tax risk.\n- **MPC** -0.3%, **VLO** -0.3%: President Trump said administration was considering diesel-export restrictions after U.S. diesel hit a record **$6.529/gallon** on Sept 21; Treasury Secretary Bessent said feasibility was being assessed; White House later called a reported 90-day ban "fake news." Jefferies downgraded both **MPC** (Buy→Hold, $413 PT) and **VLO** (Buy→Hold, $401 PT) on Sept 21; both were reportedly down 3–4% intraday before recovering to near flat on the "fake news" denial.\n\n---\n\n**Treasury Yield Shock: 10-Year at 5.12%, Broad Equity Pressure** `[Macro]` → new\n\nThe session's dominant macro fact: 10-year yield +16.8 bps to **5.12%** (19-year high); 2-year yield +12 bps to **4.90%**. Catalyst: hotter-than-expected manufacturing data (specific release values not available in gathered material).\n\n- S&P 500 -0.75% to 7,706; Nasdaq Composite -1.13% to 26,936; Russell 2000 -1.77%; SOXX -1.23%; SMH -1.00%; QQQ -0.84%.\n- **Alphabet** -3.8%, **Amazon** -2.2%, **Nvidia** -1.5% — mega-cap growth led declines.\n- **ARM** -0.19% and **INTC** -1.02% on the day despite +36.3% and +21.3% 5-day gains respectively from prior-week gap events.\n- NY Fed President Williams said on Sept 24 that another rate increase before year-end was "reasonable to consider."\n- Sept 24 macro prints scheduled: Initial jobless claims 8:30 ET (consensus 201K vs prior 196K); August building permits 8:30 ET (consensus 1.39M, est. -2.7% MoM vs prior +4.3%); Q2 current account 8:30 ET (consensus -$255B deficit vs prior -$226.8B); August new-home sales 10:00 ET (consensus 620K vs prior 610K). ⚠️\n- Fed speakers Sept 24: Barkin 8:00 ET, Kugler 8:50 ET, Williams already spoke, Hammack/Paulson also scheduled. ⚠️\n\n---\n\n**Veeva Q2 Beat + Vault CRM Expansion** `[SaaS / Life Sciences]` → new\n\n**VEEV** +3.8% on reported fiscal Q2 FY2027 results.\n\n- Revenue **$928M vs $905M** consensus; adjusted EPS **$2.35 vs $2.22** consensus.\n- Raised FY2027 revenue and profit guidance (specific updated range not disclosed in gathered material).\n- **14 of the top 20** biopharma companies have now selected Vault CRM; another top-20 company announced on Sept 23.\n- **Falcon Router** — agentic case-routing solution — announced with early-adopter availability in **January 2027**.\n\n---\n\n**Salesforce Agentforce ARR: $1.5B+ and Growing** `[SaaS / AI Infrastructure]` → ongoing\n\n**CRM** +1.84% on no new Sept 23 catalyst; the move appears to reflect continued digestion of recently reported figures.\n\n- Agentforce ARR exceeded **$1.5B** in fiscal Q2 FY2027, up **>240% YoY**.\n- Full-year FY2027 revenue guidance: **$46.1B–$46.4B**.\n- FY2026 free cash flow: **$14.402B**; Q2 FY2027 FCF: **$1.098B**.\n- Active **$50B share buyback** program.\n- Milano (President) share withholding Sept 23: 1,001 shares at $233.28.\n\n---\n\n**Fastly Investor Day: Multi-Year Growth Targets** `[Edge / CDN]` → new\n\n**FSLY** +13.7% at 4.3× volume on post-investor-day (held Sept 22) analyst assessment.\n\n- Management FY2029 targets: revenue CAGR **14%–21%**; non-GAAP operating margin **20%–22%**; FCF margin **12%–15%**.\n- RBC Capital Markets cited in connection with post-day assessment; specific rating/PT action not confirmed in gathered material.\n- 5-day gain: **+26.0%**.\n\n---\n\n**IonQ Quantum Error Correction + NVIDIA Partnership** `[Quantum Computing]` → new\n\n**IONQ** +4.4% on Sept 23 at 3.7× volume; +12% pre-market Sept 24.\n\n- IonQ announced (Sept 22) the industry's first end-to-end real-time quantum-error-correction decoder operating on a single standard off-the-shelf CPU — system performs error correction without slowing quantum operations.\n- **Superion 256** quantum system will be installed at NVIDIA's **Accelerated Quantum Research Center** alongside NVIDIA GPU clusters.\n