2026-06-11	losers	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-06-11 — R1D Losers Brief\n\n**One-liner**: A broad semiconductor selloff and an oil-price surge from U.S.-Iran tensions drove losses across multiple names, while **SMCI** cratered 25% on a $7B equity financing announcement.\n\n---\n\n### 📉 Losers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | 1D | Cap | Sector | Driver type | Catalyst (≤12 words) |\n|--------|---:|-----|--------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **GEV** | -6.4% | Mega cap | Utilities | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **CAT** | -6.2% | Mega cap | Industrials | Sector | Oil surge from US‑Iran strikes, inflation fears |\n| **QCOM** | -5.6% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Broader semiconductor correction, profit‑taking after AI rally |\n| **ETN** | -5.3% | Mega cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **PWR** | -5.2% | Mega cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **AVGO** | -4.7% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Semiconductor selloff; maintained AI forecast disappointed |\n| **NEM** | -4.7% | Mega cap | Basic Materials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **WDC** | -4.3% | Mega cap | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **APP** | -4.3% | Mega cap | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **TT** | -4.2% | Mega cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **VRT** | -4.2% | Mega cap | Industrials | Unknown | Analyst initiation; no negative catalyst identified |\n| **SAP** | -4.2% | Mega cap | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **ARM** | -3.9% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Profit‑taking across semiconductor sector, macro headwinds |\n| **STX** | -3.8% | Mega cap | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **TSM** | -3.8% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Broader risk‑off, profit‑taking after strong rally |\n| **SMCI** | -25.3% | Large cap | Technology | Idiosyncratic | $7B equity financing announced, dilution fears |\n| **BE** | -9.7% | Large cap | Industrials | Idiosyncratic | Valuation fears after 1,300% surge; Morningstar overvalued call |\n| **STRL** | -7.8% | Large cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **SW** | -7.0% | Large cap | Consumer Cyclical | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **CCL** | -6.9% | Large cap | Consumer Cyclical | Sector | Rising oil prices from Hormuz tensions hit cruise costs |\n| **NET** | -6.8% | Large cap | Technology | Unknown | Analyst target raises; no clear negative catalyst |\n| **CCJ** | -6.8% | Large cap | Energy | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **NRG** | -6.6% | Large cap | Utilities | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **AU** | -6.6% | Large cap | Basic Materials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **FLEX** | -6.3% | Large cap | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **BOT** | -15.8% | Mid & small cap | Financial Services | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **LAZ** | -13.2% | Mid & small cap | Financial Services | Unknown | Preliminary AUM release; no clear negative catalyst |\n| **CGEM** | -10.7% | Mid & small cap | Healthcare | Idiosyncratic | Clinical data presentation; stock sold off post‑data |\n| **EQPT** | -10.4% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **EZPW** | -10.4% | Mid & small cap | Financial Services | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **CYD** | -10.1% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **UEC** | -9.9% | Mid & small cap | Energy | Idiosyncratic | Q3 loss wider than expected, production costs up |\n| **WOLF** | -9.8% | Mid & small cap | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **ULCC** | -9.8% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Sector | IATA warns jet fuel cost surge on Hormuz closure |\n| **XE** | -9.8% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Thematic / Sector Weakness\n\n**Semiconductor selloff** → `Technology`\n\n- Names: **QCOM** (-5.6%), **AVGO** (-4.7%), **ARM** (-3.9%), **TSM** (-3.8%)\n- Broadcom’s fiscal Q2 report on June 4 maintained its >$100B AI semiconductor revenue forecast for fiscal 2027 rather than raising it, which triggered profit‑taking across premium-valued AI stocks (AVGO article).\n- Qualcomm slid amid a “broader semiconductor correction” after a roller‑coaster stretch that included a spike on unverified social media footage; JPMorgan raised its price target to $265 but kept Neutral (QCOM article).\n- Arm Holdings fell as investors “took profits across the semiconductor sector” and reacted to macro pressures, with the stock still up 190% YTD (ARM article).\n- TSMC dropped in a “broader risk‑off move” despite reporting May revenue up 30.1% YoY; pre‑market weakness was driven by sentiment rather than company‑specific news (TSM article).\n- The common thread is a cooling of AI‑chip sentiment following Broadcom’s unchanged outlook, compounded by a risk‑off day.\n\n**Travel & Leisure hit by oil surge** → `Consumer Cyclical` / `Industrials (Airlines)`\n\n- Names: **CCL** (-6.9%), **ULCC** (-9.8%)\n- Oil prices jumped after new U.S. strikes in the Strait of Hormuz reignited supply concerns; West Texas Intermediate climbed 3.3% to ~$91.07/bbl (CCL, CAT articles).\n- Carnival fell as “cruise operators came under pressure from rising oil prices and a broader risk‑off move,” with elevated fuel costs threatening operating expenses (CCL article).\n- The IATA sliced its global airline profit outlook, warning that the Hormuz closure has roughly doubled jet‑fuel prices, pushed crack spreads to a record $80/bbl, and may limit industry margins to 2%—the weakest since COVID (ULCC article).\n- Both names are directly exposed to fuel costs and share the same geopolitical/oil‑supply catalyst.\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Idiosyncratic Movers\n\n**SMCI** (-25.3%, Large cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Super Micro announced a $7B equity and equity‑linked financing package ($5B concurrent public offerings of common stock and mandatory convertible preferred depositary shares, plus a $2B at‑the‑market program).  \n- Proceeds are intended to fund component purchases for ~$39B in AI‑server orders from >20 customers.  \n- Shares plunged on dilution fears; the Defiance 2X Short ETF (SMCZ) surged ~40% on the day (SMCI articles).\n\n**CAT** (-6.2%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic (linked to sector but no overlapping article among other industrials)  \n- The decline was driven by rising oil prices after U.S. military actions in the Strait of Hormuz, heightening supply concerns and inflation fears.  \n- Higher energy costs raised the risk that rates stay elevated, weighing on demand for heavy equipment (CAT article).  \n- Separately, Caterpillar increased its quarterly dividend from $1.41 to $1.63/share; the dividend move did not offset the macro selloff.\n\n**BE** (-9.7%, Large cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Bloom Energy faced valuation concerns after Morningstar recently called it the most overvalued stock in its coverage, pegging fair value at ~$70 vs. a price >$250.  \n- The stock had rallied ~1,300% over the past year, and the pullback was amplified by a broader risk‑off tone. Tariff adjustments (steel/aluminum derivatives cut to 15% for certain imports) provided only mixed relief (BE article).\n\n**CGEM** (-10.7%, Mid cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Cullinan Therapeutics reported clinical data for its CD19 and BCMA T‑cell engagers, showing remissions in SLE and RA, and outlined global development plans.  \n- Despite the positive‑sounding data, the stock fell sharply in a sell‑the‑news reaction (CGEM article).\n\n**UEC** (-9.9%, Mid cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Uranium Energy reported a wider fiscal Q3 loss of $0.11 per share (vs. -$0.07 a year ago) on no revenue.  \n- Production costs rose to $54.61/lb due to timing of regulatory approvals and higher state taxes.  \n- The company is holding ~1.5M lbs of uranium inventory, betting on higher future spot prices (UEC articles).\n\n**No Material Ticker-Specific News**  \nThe following tickers fell with no company‑specific catalyst identified in the ticker articles provided. Moves likely reflect broad market pressure, sympathy moves, or technical positioning.\n\n- Mega cap: **GEV**, **ETN**, **PWR**, **NEM**, **WDC**, **APP**, **TT**, **VRT**, **SAP**, **STX**  \n- Large cap: **STRL**, **SW**, **NET**, **CCJ**, **NRG**, **AU**, **FLEX**  \n- Mid & small cap: **BOT**, **LAZ**, **EQPT**, **EZPW**, **CYD**, **WOLF**, **XE**\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sector Roll-up\n\n| Sector | Losers (count) | Avg 1D | Shared driver? |\n|--------|---------------:|-------:|----------------|\n| Technology | 12 | -6.9% | Partial (semiconductor selloff for AVGO, QCOM, ARM, TSM) |\n| Industrials | 10 | -7.3% | No (oil impact on CAT, ULCC; others unknown) |\n| Utilities | 2 | -6.5% | No |\n| Basic Materials | 2 | -5.7% | No |\n| Energy | 2 | -8.4% | No (UEC earnings; CCJ unknown) |\n| Consumer Cyclical | 2 | -7.0% | Partial (CCL shared with travel theme) |\n| Financial Services | 3 | -13.1% | No |\n| Healthcare | 1 | -10.7% | N/A |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 Watch\n\n- **QCOM** Investor Day on **June 24** – JPMorgan expects targets for >$3B data center revenue in FY27 and $35B by FY31, plus $17B each in automotive/IoT (QCOM article).  \n- **AVGO** next earnings estimated **Sept 3, 2026** – consensus EPS $3.14, revenue $29.45B; AI outlook updates will be scrutinised (AVGO article).  \n- **TSM** earnings expected **July 16, 2026** – EPS seen at $3.69, revenue $39.76B; a miss could extend the semiconductor pullback (TSM article).  \n- **SMCI** $7B financing – execution risk on component purchases for the $39B order backlog; expect dilution overhang until the deal prices (SMCI articles).  \n- **ULCC** and **CCL** remain sensitive to Hormuz supply developments; IATA flagged a potential profit squeeze if jet fuel stays elevated (CCL, ULCC articles).  \n- **BE** valuation debate – Morningstar’s $70 fair value vs. a $250+ stock; any follow-up rating changes or tariff developments could trigger further volatility (BE article).	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "synthesis", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "api_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_tokens": 67105, "output_tokens": 10605, "pricing_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_cost_usd": 0.029191, "total_cost_usd": 0.038417, "output_cost_usd": 0.009226, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-06-11T10:27:03.836102+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-06-11T10:30:28.801241+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from DeepSeek Chat Completions API response.usage. USD estimated from published api-docs.deepseek.com pricing (input cache miss, cache hit, output).", "total_cost_usd": 0.0384, "total_input_tokens": 67105, "total_output_tokens": 10605, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-06-11", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Ticker: Bottom 15 · 1D return · Mega cap": 23, "Ticker: Bottom 10 · 1D return · Large cap": 22, "Ticker: Bottom 10 · 1D return · Mid & small cap": 7}, "articles_total": 52}, "upserted": 52, "api_by_fetch": {"ticker": {"AU": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "BE": {"error": null, "api_rows": 2, "in_window": 2}, "SW": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "TT": {"error": null, "api_rows": 1, "in_window": 1}, "XE": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "APP": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "ARM": {"error": null, "api_rows": 1, "in_window": 1}, "BOT": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "CAT": {"error": null, "api_rows": 4, "in_window": 4}, "CCJ": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "CCL": {"error": null, "api_rows": 2, "in_window": 2}, "CYD": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_