2026-06-12	losers	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-06-12 — R1D Losers Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Oracle (-9.1%) cratered after a staggering AI capex revision, dragging the entire software complex sharply lower; energy and other names fell on mostly isolated, stock-specific news.\n\n---\n\n### 📉 Losers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | 1D | Cap | Sector | Driver type | Catalyst (≤12 words) |\n|--------|---:|-----|--------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **ORCL** | -9.1% | Mega | Technology | Mixed | FY27 capex $90-95B, $40B capital raise plan |\n| **SAP** | -4.2% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Oracle AI capex shock spills into software |\n| **COP** | -3.8% | Mega | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **APP** | -3.5% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Oracle capex shock sinks broader software |\n| **SPGI** | -3.1% | Mega | Financial Services | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **XOM** | -2.9% | Mega | Energy | Idiosyncratic | Head of global trading retiring |\n| **CRM** | -2.9% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Oracle earnings/capex drags software peers |\n| **BABA** | -2.7% | Mega | Consumer Cyclical | Idiosyncratic | China regulatory warnings, Pentagon listing |\n| **MSFT** | -2.6% | Mega | Technology | Idiosyncratic | Xbox division prepares major layoffs |\n| **CVX** | -2.5% | Mega | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **SPOT** | -2.5% | Mega | Communication Services | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **NOW** | -2.3% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Software selloff after Oracle AI plans |\n| **DHR** | -1.5% | Mega | Healthcare | Idiosyncratic | Piper Sandler initiates with Neutral rating |\n| **TMO** | -1.2% | Mega | Healthcare | Idiosyncratic | Piper Sandler initiates with Neutral rating |\n| **BP** | -1.1% | Mega | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **ADSK** | -5.5% | Large | Technology | Sector | Oracle capex shock hits software |\n| **ADBE** | -4.9% | Large | Technology | Sector | Oracle capex shock hits software |\n| **CBRS** | -4.4% | Large | Technology | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **WDAY** | -4.4% | Large | Technology | Sector | Oracle capex shock hits software |\n| **DVN** | -4.1% | Large | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **VG** | -3.7% | Large | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **FANG** | -3.5% | Large | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **OXY** | -3.4% | Large | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **EQT** | -3.0% | Large | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **EOG** | -2.9% | Large | Energy | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **AD** | -22.9% | Mid & small | Communication Services | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **OXM** | -18.4% | Mid & small | Consumer Cyclical | Idiosyncratic | Mixed Q1 results, narrowed FY26 sales outlook |\n| **DAN** | -15.7% | Mid & small | Consumer Cyclical | Idiosyncratic | Reverse Morris Trust merger with Eaton Mobility |\n| **VCX** | -15.6% | Mid & small | Financial Services | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **PTC** | -10.6% | Mid & small | Technology | Sector | Oracle AI capex shock hits software |\n| **PCT** | -9.4% | Mid & small | Industrials | Idiosyncratic | Priced $395M convertible notes & stock offering |\n| **OCC** | -8.9% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n| **BSY** | -7.1% | Mid & small | Technology | Sector | Oracle AI capex shock hits software |\n| **ZG** | -6.6% | Mid & small | Communication Services | Idiosyncratic | Google expands home listings, threatens Zillow |\n| **BOT** | -6.5% | Mid & small | Financial Services | Unknown | No discrete ticker-specific catalyst identified |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Thematic / Sector Weakness\n\n**AI Capex Shock / Enterprise Software** → `Technology`\n\n- **ORCL** (-9.1%), **SAP** (-4.2%), **APP** (-3.5%), **CRM** (-2.9%), **NOW** (-2.3%), **ADSK** (-5.5%), **ADBE** (-4.9%), **WDAY** (-4.4%), **PTC** (-10.6%), **BSY** (-7.1%)\n- Oracle reported Q4 revenue of $19.18B (beat estimates) and adjusted EPS of $2.11, but guided FY27 gross capital expenditure to $90‑95 billion vs. ~$61B consensus.\n- The company plans to raise approximately $40 billion in debt and equity to fund the AI data‑center buildout, leaving free cash flow deeply negative.\n- The iShares Expanded Tech‑Software ETF (IGV) fell 1.3% on June 11, its worst industry‑group performance; BofA flagged Oracle’s capex hike intensified worries about funding duration.\n- Multiple ticker articles explicitly link the Oracle print to a brutal software session: Salesforce, GoDaddy, PTC and others fell in sympathy as the sector repriced AI spending risk.\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Idiosyncratic Movers\n\n**XOM** (-2.9%, mega) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Reuters reported Exxon’s head of global trading is retiring. No broader energy‑sector catalyst in ticker articles.\n\n**BABA** (-2.7%, mega) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Slid after China’s Beijing regulator summoned Alibaba, JD, PDD and ByteDance over false advertising during the “618” festival; State Administration for Market Regulation issued warnings.\n- The Pentagon added Alibaba to its “1260H list” of firms believed to support China’s military; Alibaba plans to challenge the designation.\n- Dingtalk CEO replaced, raising questions about the unit’s AI strategy.\n\n**MSFT** (-2.6%, mega) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Bloomberg reported Xbox division plans significant layoffs and budget cuts around the fiscal‑year end (June 30), under new CEO Asha Sharma.\n- Stock fell despite a strong Nasdaq session; BNP Paribas separately reiterated Outperform and $555 target on Copilot adoption.\n\n**DHR** (-1.5%, mega) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Piper Sandler initiated coverage with a Neutral rating and $200 price target.\n\n**TMO** (-1.2%, mega) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Piper Sandler initiated coverage with a Neutral rating and $510 price target.\n\n**OXM** (-18.4%, mid & small) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Reported Q1 adjusted EPS of $1.39 (beat $1.29) but sales of $391.4M missed consensus $391.75M. Raised FY26 EPS guidance but narrowed the revenue outlook.\n- Telsey Advisory Group and Truist cut price targets to $44 and $40, respectively.\n\n**DAN** (-15.7%, mid & small) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Announced a Reverse Morris Trust transaction combining with Eaton’s Mobility unit, creating a combined entity valued >$10B. Dana shares fell as Eaton shareholders will own at least 50.1%.\n\n**PCT** (-9.4%, mid & small) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Priced concurrent offerings: $250M of 4.75% convertible notes due 2032 and 17.66M common shares at $8.21, total gross $395M. Proceeds will repurchase higher‑rate 7.25% green notes, diluting existing holders.\n\n**ZG** (-6.6%, mid & small) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Alphabet’s Google officially rolled out nationwide Enhanced Local Services Ads for home listings, directly threatening Zillow’s top‑of‑funnel traffic. Zillow shares fell 5.26% on the day.\n\n**COP, CVX, BP, DVN, VG, FANG, OXY, EQT, EOG, SPGI, SPOT, CBRS, AD, VCX, OCC, BOT** (various caps) → Unknown  \n- No material ticker‑specific news in the window. Moves may be technical, sympathy, or driven by undetected macro/fund flows.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sector Roll-up\n\n| Sector | Losers (count) | Avg 1D | Shared driver? |\n|--------|---------------:|-------:|----------------|\n| Technology | 16 | -4.8% | Partial: Oracle AI capex shock (software cluster) |\n| Energy | 11 | -3.0% | No |\n| Financial Services | 3 | -7.6% | No |\n| Consumer Cyclical | 3 | -11.3% | No (each an isolated event) |\n| Communication Services | 3 | -9.3% | No |\n| Healthcare | 2 | -1.4% | No |\n| Industrials | 1 | -9.4% | No |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 Watch\n\n- **ORCL**: Execution of the $40B debt/equity raise and FY27 capex buildout may further pressure the stock. Gushenheim’s $400 PT contrasts with Stephens’ $164, reflecting deep valuation uncertainty. All eyes on whether OpenAI revenue catches up to the compute it has ordered.\n- **ADBE**: Q2 beat but CFO Dan Durn leaves June 15; the strategy shift to freemium with deferred Creative Cloud price hikes lowers H2 ARR growth. Analysts slashed price targets (Stifel to $200, Evercore ISI to $225), and the stock is near 52‑week lows. Next earnings report in ~3 months.\n- **MSFT**: Xbox layoffs expected shortly after June 30 fiscal year‑end. Additional risk from the increasingly competitive AI landscape and ongoing CEO succession at Adobe/others.\n- **ZG**: Google’s nationwide home‑listing expansion is now live; further traffic erosion could materially impact Zillow’s agent‑advertising revenue.\n- **DAN**: Integration planning for the Eaton Mobility deal will continue through 2027; cost synergies are targeted at $250M but execution risk remains.\n- Upcoming earnings: **NOW** July 22, **DAN** Aug 4, **ADSK** Aug 27, **NVDA** Aug 26 (related to AI capex sentiment).	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "synthesis", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "api_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_tokens": 123964, "output_tokens": 10021, "pricing_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_cost_usd": 0.053924, "total_cost_usd": 0.062643, "output_cost_usd": 0.008718, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-06-12T13:26:20.479801+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-06-12T13:28:53.502853+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from DeepSeek Chat Completions API response.usage. USD estimated from published api-docs.deepseek.com pricing (input cache miss, cache hit, output).", "total_cost_usd": 0.0626, "total_input_tokens": 123964, "total_output_tokens": 10021, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_i