2026-06-17	losers	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-06-17 — R1D Losers Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Broad semiconductor profit-taking after Monday’s Iran-deal surge erased double-digit gains for many names, while **Huntsman** cratered on a merger-of-equals deal and **Gildan Activewear** was crushed by a short-seller report.\n\n---\n\n### 📉 Losers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | 1D | Cap | Sector | Driver type | Catalyst (≤12 words) |\n|--------|---:|-----|--------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **INTC** | -7.8% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after Monday’s Iran-deal rally |\n| **MRVL** | -7.3% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after Monday’s 10% surge |\n| **GLW** | -6.3% | Mega | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **KLAC** | -6.2% | Mega | Technology | Idiosyncratic | Cantor Fitzgerald cut PT to $250 from $2,500 |\n| **AMD** | -6.1% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after Monday’s 7% rally |\n| **MU** | -4.7% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Pullback after Monday’s 11% surge |\n| **ASML** | -4.2% | Mega | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **LRCX** | -4.0% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after Monday’s 6% gain |\n| **AVGO** | -3.9% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after Monday’s rally |\n| **VRT** | -3.5% | Mega | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **NFLX** | -3.3% | Mega | Communication Services | Idiosyncratic | Lost Roku bid to Fox; M&A concerns |\n| **SNDK** | -3.1% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after record highs Monday |\n| **TSM** | -2.9% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after Monday’s 4% gain |\n| **PDD** | -2.3% | Mega | Consumer Cyclical | Idiosyncratic | BNP Paribas initiated Underperform, $89 PT |\n| **ADI** | -2.2% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Sector weakness; no ticker-specific catalyst |\n| **IONQ** | -9.0% | Large | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after Monday’s quantum surge |\n| **LITE** | -8.6% | Large | Technology | Sector | No specific news; sector rotation |\n| **MPWR** | -8.2% | Large | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **CIEN** | -7.3% | Large | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **COHR** | -7.2% | Large | Technology | Sector | +$50M CHIPS Act funding; profit-taking |\n| **FN** | -7.1% | Large | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **TSEM** | -6.3% | Large | Technology | Sector | Positive InP supply deal; profit-taking |\n| **ALAB** | -6.0% | Large | Technology | Sector | Profit-taking after Nasdaq-100 inclusion rally |\n| **ENTG** | -5.9% | Large | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **STM** | -5.8% | Large | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **HUN** | -18.5% | Mid & small | Basic Materials | Idiosyncratic | Announced all-stock merger with Olin |\n| **GIL** | -18.2% | Mid & small | Consumer Cyclical | Idiosyncratic | Jehoshaphat Research short-seller report |\n| **BOT** | -17.4% | Mid & small | Financial Services | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **AXTI** | -15.1% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **VCX** | -13.8% | Mid & small | Financial Services | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **ALTO** | -12.8% | Mid & small | Basic Materials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **ELVR** | -12.1% | Mid & small | Basic Materials | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **BLSH** | -11.0% | Mid & small | Technology | Idiosyncratic | JP Morgan cut PT to $26 from $43 |\n| **QUBT** | -10.3% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n| **WOLF** | -10.2% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker-specific news |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Thematic / Sector Weakness\n\n**Semiconductor & Tech Hardware Profit-Taking** → `Technology`\n\n- **INTC** (-7.8%), **MRVL** (-7.3%), **AMD** (-6.1%), **MU** (-4.7%), **LRCX** (-4.0%), **AVGO** (-3.9%), **SNDK** (-3.1%), **TSM** (-2.9%), **ADI** (-2.2%), **IONQ** (-9.0%), **LITE** (-8.6%), **COHR** (-7.2%), **TSEM** (-6.3%), **ALAB** (-6.0%) and multiple large-cap names without company-specific news (GLW, ASML, MPWR, CIEN, FN, ENTG, STM).\n- The Nasdaq fell 1.15% on Tuesday as investors rotated away from technology stocks that had surged the prior session on the U.S.-Iran peace deal and the Strait of Hormuz reopening.\n- Articles for **MRVL**, **MU**, **ALAB**, and **INTC** explicitly describe the declines as profit-taking following Monday’s sharp rallies; no negative earnings or guidance changes were reported.\n- The sector-wide selloff reflects a reversion of the risk-on move, with the Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund (XLK) down ~1.7% and the VanEck Semiconductor ETF (SMH) leading losses.\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Idiosyncratic Movers\n\n**HUN** (-18.5%, mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Announced an all-stock merger-of-equals with Olin Corporation (OLN). Huntsman shareholders receive 0.5476 OLN shares per HUN share. The combined entity, OlinHuntsman, expects $400M+ in synergies. Market reacted negatively to the dilutive structure; HUN shares fell sharply while OLN shares rose.\n\n**GIL** (-18.2%, mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Jehoshaphat Research published a short-seller report alleging channel stuffing, off-balance-sheet factoring, and an $800M revenue gap for 2H26. The report also highlighted governance concerns including recent executive departures from the Ethics committee.\n\n**NFLX** (-3.3%, mega cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Semafor reported Netflix lost a bidding contest for Roku to Fox, which offered $22B. The article also noted Netflix’s earlier pursuit of Warner Bros. Discovery, raising M&A strategy and integration concerns. Co-CEO Ted Sarandos previously acknowledged building “M&A muscle.”\n\n**PDD** (-2.3%, mega cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- BNP Paribas initiated coverage with an Underperform rating and $89 price target, citing concerns about the Chinese e-commerce firm’s growth outlook.\n\n**KLAC** (-6.2%, mega cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Cantor Fitzgerald maintained Overweight but drastically cut its price target to $250 from $2,500. (The prior target may reflect a data error, but the reported cut served as the day’s only ticker-specific catalyst.)\n\n**BLSH** (-11.0%, mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- JP Morgan maintained Neutral and lowered its price target to $26 from $43. No other ticker-specific news.\n\n**BOT, AXTI, VCX, ALTO, ELVR, QUBT, WOLF** (mid & small cap) → Unknown  \n- No material ticker-specific news in the window. Declines may be technical, sympathy moves, or linked to broader sector pressure.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sector Roll-up\n\n| Sector | Losers (count) | Avg 1D | Shared driver? |\n|--------|---------------:|-------:|----------------|\n| Technology | 27 | -6.2% | Yes – profit-taking/rotation after Monday’s rally |\n| Basic Materials | 3 | -14.5% | No – HUN merger, others unknown |\n| Consumer Cyclical | 2 | -10.3% | No – GIL short report, PDD analyst downgrade |\n| Communication Services | 1 | -3.3% | No – NFLX M&A news |\n| Industrials | 1 | -3.5% | No – unknown |\n| Financial Services | 2 | -15.6% | No – unknown |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 Watch\n\n- **Fed decision (June 18):** Chair Kevin Warsh’s first press conference could amplify tech rotation if the tone is hawkish; markets price 70% chance of a hike by year-end.\n- **MU earnings (June 24):** Micron reports after a 263% YTD run. TD Cowen’s $1,500 target and analyst enthusiasm set a high bar; any disappointment could drag semis further.\n- **INTC earnings (July 23):** Intel’s results will test the recent rally fueled by BoFA upgrade and foundry optimism; consensus still Hold with avg PT well below market.\n- **MRVL earnings (Aug 27):** Marvell trades at 106x earnings; any softening of AI infrastructure demand commentary could intensify profit-taking.\n- **GIL short thesis:** Jehoshaphat’s allegations of channel stuffing and executive exits may attract further scrutiny; watch for a company response beyond the initial refutation.\n- **HUN/OLN merger:** Regulatory reviews and synergy targets will be key; the deal isn’t expected to close until 1H27.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "synthesis", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "api_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_tokens": 103291, "output_tokens": 5568, "pricing_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_cost_usd": 0.044932, "total_cost_usd": 0.049776, "output_cost_usd": 0.004844, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-06-17T02:41:50.120947+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-06-17T02:43:37.520408+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from DeepSeek Chat Completions API response.usage. USD estimated from published api-docs.deepseek.com pricing (input cache miss, cache hit, output).", "total_cost_usd": 0.0498, "total_input_tokens": 103291, "total_output_tokens": 5568, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-06-17", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Ticker: Bottom 15 · 1D return · Mega cap": 52, "Ticker: Bottom 10 · 1D return · Large cap": 11, "Ticker: Bottom 10 · 1D return · Mid & small cap": 12}, "articles_total": 75}, "upserted": 75, "api_by_fetch": {"ticker": {"FN": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "MU": {"error": null, "api_rows": 14, "in_window": 14}, "ADI": {"error": null, "api_rows": 2, "in_window": 2}, "AMD": {"error": null, "api_rows": 10, "in_window": 10}, "BOT": {"error": null, "api_rows": 1, "in_window": 1}, "GIL": {"error": null, "api_rows": 4, "in_window": 4}, "GLW": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "HUN": {"error": null, "api_rows": 6, "in_window": 6}, "PDD": {"error": null, "api_rows": 3, "in_window": 3}, "STM": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "TSM": {"error": null, "api_rows": 5, "in_window": 5}, "VCX