2026-06-24	losers	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 June 24, 2026 — R1D Losers Brief\n\n**One-liner**: A thematic semiconductor rout—sparked by South Korea’s 10% KOSPI crash and pre‑Micron earnings jitters—savaged memory and AI chip stocks across all caps, while **Primoris Services** and **Sunbelt Rentals** suffered idiosyncratic blows.\n\n---\n\n### 📉 Losers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | 1D | Cap | Sector | Driver type | Catalyst (≤12 words) |\n|--------|---:|-----|--------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **SNDK** | -14.1% | Mega | Technology | Sector | S. Korea memory selloff, Micron earnings de‑risking |\n| **MU** | -11.5% | Mega | Technology | Sector | S. Korea memory crash, pre‑earnings positioning |\n| **ARM** | -9.9% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Broad chip selloff, rotation out of growth |\n| **VRT** | -9.7% | Mega | Industrials | Sector | AI‑infrastructure selloff; no company‑specific news |\n| **MRVL** | -8.7% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Sector‑wide profit‑taking in semiconductors |\n| **ADI** | -8.4% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Swept up in semiconductor rout |\n| **TXN** | -8.3% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Swept up in semiconductor rout |\n| **GEV** | -8.2% | Mega | Utilities | Unknown | New Vietnam LNG order, but stock fell; no clear catalyst |\n| **WDC** | -8.1% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Memory selloff, linked to Korea & Micron |\n| **KLAC** | -8.0% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Chip‑equipment names swept lower |\n| **QCOM** | -7.9% | Mega | Technology | Mixed | Analyst caution ahead of AI Investor Day; broad chip weakness |\n| **GLW** | -6.8% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI optical supply‑chain hit in liquidation |\n| **AMAT** | -6.4% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Chip‑equipment selling pressure |\n| **ANET** | -6.4% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Swept up in semiconductor rout |\n| **ETN** | -6.3% | Mega | Industrials | Sector | Electrical equipment/AI‑infra selloff |\n| **TSEM** | -10.2% | Large | Technology | Sector | Tower Semi caught in chip selloff |\n| **CRDO** | -9.8% | Large | Technology | Sector | Communication/AI chip selling |\n| **COHR** | -9.8% | Large | Technology | Sector | Hardware, equipment exposed to chip weakness |\n| **ON** | -9.5% | Large | Technology | Sector | Swept up in semiconductor rout |\n| **MCHP** | -8.7% | Large | Technology | Sector | Swept up in semiconductor rout |\n| **STM** | -8.4% | Large | Technology | Sector | Swept up in semiconductor rout |\n| **SUNB** | -8.3% | Large | Financial Services | Idiosyncratic | Q4 adj EPS $0.74 vs $0.81 YoY; FY27 sales guide issued |\n| **ALAB** | -7.7% | Large | Technology | Sector | AI chip name hit by rotation |\n| **ENTG** | -7.7% | Large | Technology | Sector | Swept up in semiconductor rout |\n| **LITE** | -7.7% | Large | Technology | Sector | Optical/components caught in selloff |\n| **PRIM** | -23.0% | Mid & small | Industrials | Idiosyncratic | COO departure; FY26 guidance slashed |\n| **HYLN** | -19.2% | Mid & small | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window |\n| **HQ** | -18.7% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | Pullback after 5‑day +73.8% run; no fresh news |\n| **AXTI** | -15.4% | Mid & small | Technology | Sector | Swept up in semiconductor rout |\n| **VELO** | -14.7% | Mid & small | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window |\n| **FLNC** | -13.8% | Mid & small | Utilities | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window |\n| **CAMT** | -12.9% | Mid & small | Technology | Sector | Semi‑equipment name pinned to chip selloff |\n| **AAOI** | -12.9% | Mid & small | Technology | Sector | AI‑datacenter optics caught in risk‑off trade |\n| **EOSE** | -12.5% | Mid & small | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window |\n| **SHAZ** | -11.2% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Thematic / Sector Weakness\n\n**Semiconductor Rout ( Memory & AI Chips )** → `Technology`\n\n- **SNDK** (-14.1%), **MU** (-11.5%), **ARM** (-9.9%), **VRT** (-9.7%), **MRVL** (-8.7%), **ADI** (-8.4%), **TXN** (-8.3%), **WDC** (-8.1%), **KLAC** (-8.0%), **GLW** (-6.8%), **AMAT** (-6.4%), **ANET** (-6.4%), **ETN** (-6.3%), **TSEM** (-10.2%), **CRDO** (-9.8%), **COHR** (-9.8%), **ON** (-9.5%), **MCHP** (-8.7%), **STM** (-8.4%), **ALAB** (-7.7%), **ENTG** (-7.7%), **LITE** (-7.7%), **AXTI** (-15.4%), **CAMT** (-12.9%), **AAOI** (-12.9%).\n- South Korea’s KOSPI plunged ~10% Tuesday, with Samsung and SK Hynix each down >12%, triggering circuit breakers and spilling into US chip ETFs (SMH -8%, SOXX -8%).\n- The rout was fueled by an unconfirmed Korean report that SK Hynix may shift HBM capacity toward general‑purpose DRAM, stoking fears of slowing AI memory demand.\n- Micron’s earnings (due after June 24 close) added speculative pressure; options priced a ~14% implied move, and Polymarket showed 96% odds of an EPS beat but an 85% chance of hitting $1,050 this week.\n- Wedbush’s Dan Ives called the selloff a “gut check moment” and said the AI revolution is only in the “third inning.” Bank of America raised its Micron PT to $1,500, citing memory supply tightness into 2028.\n- Futurum Group CEO Daniel Newman described memory as “the GPU of three years ago,” stating the era of memory as a commodity is over.\n- The VanEck Semiconductor ETF (SMH) shed ~6%; the iShares Semiconductor ETF (SOXX) fell ~8%. Software names held firm, showing the selloff was chip‑specific.\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Idiosyncratic Movers\n\n**PRIM** (-23.0%, Mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- COO Jeremy Kinch departed effective immediately; President/CEO will assume most COO duties while a search is conducted.  \n- FY26 guidance was slashed: adjusted EPS lowered from $4.80‑$5.00 to $2.05‑$2.60; Renewables revenue now seen at ~$2.1B (previously ~$3.0B) due to cost overruns on six legacy projects.  \n- KeyBanc downgraded to Sector Weight; Mizuho cut PT to $117; Wells Fargo lowered to $85. Guggenheim kept Buy/$162 PT.  \n\n**QCOM** (-7.9%, Mega cap) → Mixed  \n- Ahead of its June 24 AI Investor Day, BofA maintained Underperform and raised PT to $195; analyst Tal Liani expressed skepticism Qualcomm can become a meaningful late entrant in the “hyper‑competitive AI market.”  \n- Qualcomm also announced the acquisition of Modular Inc., issuing up to 19.2M shares.  \n- Broad chip weakness added pressure, but the pre‑Investor Day caution and acquisition dilution were company‑specific drags.  \n\n**SUNB** (-8.3%, Large cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Sunbelt Rentals reported Q4 adjusted EPS of $0.74 (‑8.64% YoY) on revenue of $2.754B (+8.9% YoY).  \n- FY2027 sales guidance of $11.652B‑$11.986B was issued. Margin pressure overshadowed the revenue beat.  \n\n**HYLN** (-19.2%, Mid & small cap) → Unknown  \n- No material ticker‑specific news in window. Move likely technical or linked to profit‑taking after a recent run (‑18.1% 5D).  \n\n**HQ** (-18.7%, Mid & small cap) → Unknown  \n- No material ticker‑specific news in window. Earlier 5‑day run of +73.8% suggested momentum reversal.  \n\n**VELO** (-14.7%, Mid & small cap) → Unknown  \n- No material ticker‑specific news in window.  \n\n**FLNC** (-13.8%, Mid & small cap) → Unknown  \n- No material ticker‑specific news in window.  \n\n**EOSE** (-12.5%, Mid & small cap) → Unknown  \n- No material ticker‑specific news in window.  \n\n**SHAZ** (-11.2%, Mid & small cap) → Unknown  \n- No material ticker‑specific news in window.  \n\n**GEV** (-8.2%, Mega cap) → Unknown  \n- Despite announcing a major Vietnam LNG turbine order, the stock fell; no clear negative catalyst from the ticker article. Likely swept up in risk‑off rotation.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sector Roll-up\n\n| Sector | Losers (count) | Avg 1D | Shared driver? |\n|--------|---------------:|-------:|----------------|\n| Technology | 25 | -9.0% | Yes – S. Korea memory crash, Micron earnings anxiety |\n| Industrials | 6 | -15.6% | Partial – PRIM idiosyncratic; VRT/ETN part of chip rout; HYLN/VELO/EOSE unknown |\n| Utilities | 2 | -11.0% | No – GEV unknown; FLNC unknown |\n| Financial Services | 1 | -8.3% | No – SUNB earnings‑driven |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 Watch\n\n- **Micron Technology** reports fiscal Q3 after the June 24 close; options imply a ~14% swing. History shows six of the last eight post‑earnings sessions closed lower despite beats. Consensus: EPS $20.76 on revenue $35.75B. Any HBM demand or guidance softness could reignite sector volatility.\n- **Qualcomm** holds its AI‑focused Investor Day on June 24; the market will scrutinize data‑center/AI roadmap, potential M&A (Tenstorrent/Modular), and whether the stock’s rally has priced in overly optimistic expectations.\n- **Primoris Services** will report Q2 results soon; the scale of Renewables cost overruns and any additional project delays will be critical. The company bought back $50M of stock in Q2 at $111.29 average.\n- **South Korea’s KOSPI** rebounded ~3.2% Wednesday after Tuesday’s circuit‑breaker plunge. Stability in Samsung/SK Hynix prices will be a sentiment proxy for the memory trade.\n- **Bank stress test results** due at 4:00 p.m. ET June 24 from the Federal Reserve could add cross‑asset volatility.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "synthesis", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "api_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_tokens": 164801, "output_tokens": 5617, "pricing_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_cost_usd": 0.071688, "total_cost_usd": 0.076575, "output_cost_usd": 0.004887, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-06-24T13:01:09.227751+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-06-24T13:02:40.867436+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from DeepSeek Chat Completions API response.usage. USD estimated from published api-docs.deepseek.com pricing (input cache miss, cache hit, output).", "total_cost_usd": 0.0766, "total_input_tokens": 164801, "total_output_tokens": 5617, "total_cache_read_i