2026-09-23	losers	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-09-23 — R1D Losers Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Weakness was split between two thematic clusters—Meta’s Muse agentic-AI disruption (**BKNG, ABNB, GOOGL, GOOG**) and memory-cycle doubts (**SNDK, SKHY**)—while the deepest single-stock drops were idiosyncratic (**MCD, PAYX, ALKT, VOYG, INNV**).\n\n---\n\n### 📉 Losers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | 1D | Cap | Sector | Driver type | Catalyst (≤12 words) |\n|--------|---:|-----|--------|-------------|----------------------|\n| MCD | -5.4% | Mega cap | Consumer Cyclical | Idiosyncratic | Investor-day $8.5B franchisee support plan spooked; PT cuts |\n| BABA | -4.7% | Mega cap | Consumer Cyclical | Mixed | Sell-the-news after AI chip; cautious large-cap tech/China |\n| BKNG | -4.2% | Mega cap | Consumer Cyclical | Sector | Meta Muse/agentic-AI travel threat; Expedia downgrade spillover |\n| SNDK | -4.2% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Memory boom sustainability doubts; Shkreli/Burry shorts |\n| GOOGL | -4.0% | Mega cap | Communication Services | Sector | Meta Muse seen eroding search/consumer-inertia revenue |\n| BX | -4.0% | Mega cap | Financial Services | Idiosyncratic | Private credit fund caps redemptions; $4.3B exit requests |\n| GOOG | -4.0% | Mega cap | Communication Services | Sector | Meta Muse search disruption concern |\n| APP | -4.0% | Mega cap | Technology | Idiosyncratic | Edgewater: share growth stalled; “show-me story” |\n| ORCL | -3.8% | Mega cap | Technology | Mixed | Tech weakness; Project Jupiter debt, layoffs |\n| BHP | -3.5% | Mega cap | Basic Materials | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| SHOP | -3.5% | Mega cap | Technology | Idiosyncratic | Sell-the-news after Meta Muse partnership rally |\n| SPCX | -3.3% | Mega cap | Industrials | Idiosyncratic | Shotwell Form 144; post-IPO lockup supply overhang |\n| NVO | -3.3% | Mega cap | Healthcare | Idiosyncratic | REDEFINE 4 missed non-inferiority vs tirzepatide |\n| UBS | -3.2% | Mega cap | Financial Services | Idiosyncratic | €5M settlement over legacy Credit Suisse matter |\n| SKHY | -3.1% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Memory cycle worry; Burry short memory boom |\n| PAYX | -8.2% | Large cap | Industrials | Idiosyncratic | EPS beat but Management Solutions below expectations; Q2 guide ~4% |\n| ABNB | -6.8% | Large cap | Consumer Cyclical | Sector | Meta Muse AI travel disruption; Expedia sympathy |\n| ASTS | -6.1% | Large cap | Communication Services | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| PAAS | -6.0% | Large cap | Basic Materials | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| AU | -5.8% | Large cap | Basic Materials | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| WPM | -5.8% | Large cap | Basic Materials | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| GFI | -5.4% | Large cap | Basic Materials | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| TPL | -5.3% | Large cap | Energy | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| DB | -4.7% | Large cap | Financial Services | Idiosyncratic | Named in $6.9B A7 sanctions payments report |\n| RKT | -4.5% | Large cap | Financial Services | Sector | 30-year mortgage rate 7.12%; refi demand down |\n| ALKT | -19.8% | Mid & small cap | Technology | Idiosyncratic | Strategic review concludes; remains independent, disappoints |\n| VOYG | -15.6% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Idiosyncratic | $350M convertible notes offering; arbitrage pressure |\n| INNV | -14.3% | Mid & small cap | Healthcare | Idiosyncratic | Secondary offering 10M shares at $9.25 by sellers |\n| SVIA | -13.5% | Mid & small cap | Financial Services | Unknown | No material catalyst; fell after Tuesday jump |\n| EXK | -11.7% | Mid & small cap | Basic Materials | Idiosyncratic | CIBC downgrade to Neutral, PT C$25→C$20 |\n| VITL | -11.2% | Mid & small cap | Consumer Defensive | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| PGY | -11.1% | Mid & small cap | Technology | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| CCOI | -11.0% | Mid & small cap | Communication Services | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| EOSE | -10.8% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n| BOBS | -10.8% | Mid & small cap | Consumer Cyclical | Unknown | No ticker-specific news |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Thematic / Sector Weakness\n\n**Meta Muse agentic-AI / consumer-inertia disruption** → `Communication Services / Consumer Cyclical`\n\n- **GOOGL** -4.0%, **GOOG** -4.0%, **BKNG** -4.2%, **ABNB** -6.8%.\n- **Booking Holdings** commentary framed the threat as a “gatekeeper swap”: Booking spent ~$8.2B on marketing in 2025, ~30% of revenue, and the article flagged AI agents taking over travel search/booking. The same article noted **Airbnb** and Tripadvisor down >4% Wednesday and **Expedia** down as much as 6% after Morgan Stanley downgraded Expedia to Underweight; Booking was called lower in sympathy.\n- **Alphabet** article stated shares fell as a broader selloff hit companies vulnerable to disruption from Meta’s Muse AI agent. Goldman Sachs’ “consumer inertia” basket includes Expedia and Booking; the concern is that agents handling tasks directly may reduce search/query activity or platform dependence.\n- Link: All four are tied to the same documented Meta Muse agentic-AI threat: Booking/Airbnb on travel/customer inertia; Alphabet on search ad demand.\n\n**Memory/semiconductor cycle doubt** → `Technology`\n\n- **SNDK** -4.2%, **SKHY** -3.1%.\n- **SanDisk** article: Martin Shkreli said he is short Micron and warned “if memory prices drop, it’s all over”; one trader on his desk was long ~$1M SNDK as a “momentum AI play,” while Shkreli separately called semiconductor stocks broadly expensive. A fund manager also warned memory earnings are cyclical and may be misleading near peak.\n- **SK Hynix** article: Michael Burry doubled down on bearish memory bets, citing Acer CEO Jason Chen that memory inventories are building and Chinese suppliers are adding volume; CXMT advanced DRAM production and Samsung/SK Hynix/Micron capacity shifts to HBM were flagged.\n- Link: Both are memory/semiconductor names under the same documented supply/cyclicality debate, with SNDK/SKHY caught in the same memory-boom-doubt trade.\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Idiosyncratic Movers\n\n**MCD** (-5.4%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- 2026 Investor Day: $8.5B franchisee support plan through 2036 (~$5B through 2030) spooked investors; stock hit a four-year low and was headed for a seventh weekly loss, the worst since July 2014.\n- Management targets operating margin low-to-mid 50% by 2030 and free cash flow conversion mid-to-high 80%; admitted “falling short” on consistent execution.\n- UBS PT $320, Citi $310, Morgan Stanley $308; Seaport Global initiated Neutral, saying improvement unlikely before mid-2027.\n\n**BABA** (-4.7%, Mega cap) → Mixed\n\n- Fell after unveiling its new AI chip (Zhenwu V900, described as 3x computing power of M890) and outlining cloud expansion in Turkey, Finland and Netherlands over 12 months; 20 GW data center target by 2032; $53B three-year AI investment plan.\n- Ticker article also cited caution on large-cap technology and China-linked stocks, with the stock ~15.6% below its 200-day SMA after an April death cross.\n\n**BX** (-4.0%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Blackstone’s $77.2B Blackstone Private Credit Fund capped redemptions at 5% after investors sought ~10% of shares; BCRED received $4.3B repurchase requests in Q3.\n- Article also flagged Apollo and Morgan Stanley private credit funds facing elevated redemption pressure, but Blackstone’s own fund action was the direct BX catalyst.\n\n**APP** (-4.0%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Edgewater Research analyst Joe Wittine said MAX share reached a “functional ceiling”; Q4 revenue growth seen at 8-9% q/q, versus Q3 guidance $2.055B-$2.085B on $1.92B prior quarter.\n- Called it a “show-me story”; Unity flagged as competitive threat compressing net revenue spreads.\n\n**ORCL** (-3.8%, Mega cap) → Mixed\n\n- Premarket weakness cited across technology stocks; company-specific overhang from Project Jupiter—$165B New Mexico data center campus—with $18B of tied debt quoted ~89-91 cents on the dollar.\n- Also cut 546 employees from Americas Cloud Infrastructure (~7.6% of 7,185).\n\n**SHOP** (-3.5%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- “Sell the news” profit-taking after Tuesday’s surge on the Meta Muse/Shop Pay partnership; Wedbush reiterated Outperform with a $176 PT.\n- Stock remained above its 20-day, 50-day and 200-day SMAs.\n\n**SPCX** (-3.3%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Gwynne Shotwell filed Form 144 to sell 342,170 shares (~$51.96M) under a 10b5-1 plan; post-IPO lockup expiration Thursday releases up to 328.4M shares.\n- Article also cited record 10-year yields pressuring capital-intensive, pre-profitability infrastructure.\n\n**NVO** (-3.3%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Novo Nordisk’s REDEFINE 4 trial failed to show non-inferiority in weight loss vs Eli Lilly’s tirzepatide.\n- Contemporaneous Viking Therapeutics VK2735 maintenance data added competitive pressure.\n\n**UBS** (-3.2%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Reached €5M settlement with Dutch Public Prosecution Service over a legacy Credit Suisse matter.\n\n**PAYX** (-8.2%, Large cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Fiscal Q1 FY27 revenue $1.631B beat $1.627B; adj EPS $1.34 beat $1.32; but Management Solutions revenue of $1.213B came in “slightly below expectations.”\n- Guided Q2 revenue growth ~4%; maintained FY27 adj EPS $5.90-$6.01 and revenue $6.838B-$6.903B.\n\n**DB** (-4.7%, Large cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Financial Times report on A7 Russia-linked payments said Deutsche Bank clients in Europe received ~$18M; Elizabeth Warren slammed the administration afterward.\n- No additional ticker-specific company news in window.\n\n**RKT** (-4.5%, Large cap) → Sector\n\n- MBA 30-year fixed mortgage rate rose to 7.12%, highest since May 2024; refinance demand down 62% y/y, purchase applications down 11% y/y.\n- Rocket Companies described as earning money on every mortgage; stock hit a 52-week low Monday.\n\n**ALKT** (-19.8%, Mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Concluded strategic opportunities review and will remain an independent public company; reaffirmed FY revenue $528M-$531M.\n- Market reacted negatively to no sale outcome.\n\n**VOYG** (-15.6%, Mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Announced $350M convertible senior notes due 2032, plus $52.5M option; cap call set at least 150% above last sale (~$93.80).\n- Convertible arbitrage shorting likely pressured shares.\n\n**INNV** (-14.3%, Mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Priced secondary offering of 10M shares at $9.25 by Apax Partners and Welsh, Carson, Anderson & Stowe; company selling no shares and receiving no proceeds.\n\n**EXK** (-11.7%, Mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- CIBC downgraded Endeavour Silver to Neutral from Outperformer; PT lowered C$25→C$20.\n\n**Thin / unexplained movers**\n\n- **BHP** (-3.5%, Mega cap), **ASTS** (-6.1%, Large cap), **PAAS** (-6.0%, Large cap), **AU** (-5.8%, Large cap), **WPM** (-5.8%, Large cap), **GFI** (-5.4%, Large cap), **TPL** (-5.3%, Large cap), **SVIA** (-13.5%, Mid & small cap), **VITL** (-11.2%, Mid & small cap), **PGY** (-11.1%, Mid & small cap), **CCOI** (-11.0%, Mid & small cap), **EOSE** (-10.8%, Mid & small cap), **BOBS** (-10.8%, Mid & small cap).\n- No material ticker-specific news in window; moves may be technical, sympathy or unexplained.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sector Roll-up\n\n| Sector | Losers (count) | Avg 1D | Shared driver? |\n|--------|---------------:|-------:|----------------|\n| Basic Materials | 6 | -6.4% | No — EXK downgrade; gold miners no news |\n| Communication Services | 4 | -6.3% | Partial — GOOGL/GOOG Muse; others unknown |\n| Consumer Cyclical | 5 | -6.4% | Partial — BKNG/ABNB AI; others distinct |\n| Consumer Defensive | 1 | -11.2% | No ticker news |\n| Energy | 1 | -5.3% | No ticker news |\n| Financial Services | 5 | -6.0% | No — distinct catalysts |\n| Healthcare | 2 | -8.8% | No — NVO trial; INNV offering |\n| Industrials | 4 | -9.5% | No — distinct company events |\n| Technology | 7 | -7.1% | Partial — SNDK/SKHY memory; rest distinct |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 Watch\n\n- **Micron (MU) reports fiscal Q4 Sept. 30 after close**: Wall Street expects ~$31.33-$31.43 EPS vs $3.03 a year earlier; memory whipsaw risk for SNDK/SKHY if guidance resets.\n- **SPCX lockup expiration Thursday**: up to 328.4M shares eligible for sale; Shotwell Form 144 already filed for 342,170 shares (~$51.96M).\n- **Meta Muse partnership execution**: Zuckerberg signaled more partnerships coming; follow-through risk for travel/search names (BKNG, ABNB, GOOGL/GOOG) if agentic-commerce headlines continue.\n- **PAYX PEO enrollment windows**: management remains cautious ahead of October and January enrollments after Q2 revenue guide of ~4%.\n- **INNV secondary closing Sept. 24**: 10M shares priced at $9.25; watch post-offering share absorption.\n- **Obesity-drug race**: NVO REDEFINE 4 non-inferiority miss vs tirzepatide; Viking plans Phase 3 VK2735 start by year-end.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "synthesis", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "api_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_tokens": 175112, "output_tokens": 20431, "pricing_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_cost_usd": 0.076174, "total_cost_usd": 0.093949, "output_cost_usd": 0.017775, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-09-24T01:23:20.764968+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-24T01:28:16.599750+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from DeepSeek Chat Completions API response.usage. USD estimated from published api-docs.deepseek.com pricing (input cache miss, cache hit, output).", "total_cost_usd": 0.0939, "total_input_tokens": 175112, "total_output_tokens": 20431, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-09-23", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Ticker: Bottom 15 · 1D return · Mega cap": 99, "Ticker: Bottom 10 · 1D return · Large cap": 1