kness\n\n#### Semiconductor / memory / wafer-fab equipment selloff → `Sector`\n\n- **SKHY** -5.2%, **INTC** -6.3%, **AMD** -5.9%, **STX** -5.6%, **LRCX** -5.3%, **AMAT** -4.9%\n- SK Hynix’s Seoul-listed shares fell ~11% on Oct 15, and the KOSPI dropped ~7.6%; memory makers lost roughly **$1.09 trillion** in combined value since Oct 2.\n- Macro data in ticker articles: September **PPI +6.3% y/y**, hottest since Dec 2022; September **CPI +3.7%**; Fed hike odds near **33% for Oct 28**.\n- Broadcom and Intel CEOs flagged **capital and cost of capital** as AI’s biggest bottleneck; Broadcom’s Hock Tan: “The biggest constraint is capital.”\n- China supply fears: **CXMT** DRAM progress and **YMTC** becoming third-largest NAND maker; Elon Musk: “China will be making a LOT of RAM in 2028.”\n- TSMC beat Q3 with **$46.7B revenue**, guided Q4 to **$52.3B–$54.3B**, maintained 2026 capex **$60B–$64B**, but shares still fell.\n- Equipment group: LRCX closed down for **9 straight sessions**; Applied Materials declined to give a WFE forecast on investor day; Evercore cut AMAT PT to **$590**.\n- **Link**: These names share the same semiconductor supply-chain catalysts—AI financing cost, China memory competition, hot inflation, and the chip-sector rout.\n\n#### AI neocloud / debt-funded infrastructure weakness → `Sector`\n\n- **CRWV** -11.9%, **NBIS** -11.9%\n- CoreWeave’s 2031/2032 bond yields neared **15%**, 5-year CDS briefly topped **1,140bp**; debt and lease obligations ~**$52B**, Q2 net interest expense **$640M vs $267M** a year earlier.\n- D.A. Davidson’s Gil Luria said CoreWeave’s equity “is going to be zero” in a downside scenario; company borrows ~9% vs ~1% returns.\n- **Gartner** projected **80% of neoclouds** will cease independent operations by 2030, with **>$3.5T** AI infrastructure spend exposed to impairment; report named CRWV, NBIS, IREN.\n- Nebius article cited AI-infrastructure debt pressure; stock traded **22% below its 20-day SMA**.\n- **Link**: Both are capital-intensive AI-infrastructure providers under pressure from the same debt-financing fear; CoreWeave is the focal point, Nebius trades in sympathy.\n\n*No other shared sector/theme driver identified from ticker articles.*\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Idiosyncratic Movers\n\n**SNOW** (-8.2%, mega) → Unknown  \nNo negative ticker-specific news. Ticker article covered a **Lumen/Snowflake partnership** for AI Data Cloud connectivity. Move is not explained in window; likely sector/sympathy.\n\n**PLTR** (-7.0%, mega) → Idiosyncratic  \nArk Invest sold **61,389 shares (~$12.3M)** over Oct 14–15. Mizuho raised PT to **$245**; prior Goldman upgrade to **$230**. Q2 revenue +93%; Q3 due **Nov 9**.\n\n**PANW** (-6.9%, mega) → Unknown  \nCiti maintained Buy, PT to **$440 from $410**. No negative catalyst in window.\n\n**FTNT** (-6.8%, mega) → Idiosyncratic  \nMizuho maintained **Underperform**, Wells Fargo maintained **Underweight**; both raised PT to **$160**. Bearish ratings likely contributed.\n\n**CRWD** (-6.4%, mega) → Unknown  \nCiti Buy PT to **$295**, BTIG Buy PT to **$312**. No negative catalyst.\n\n**ARM** (-6.0%, mega) → Unknown  \nNo material ticker-specific news in window. Move tracks semiconductor complex.\n\n**NET** (-5.9%, mega) → Unknown  \nNo ticker-specific news in window. May be technical/sympathy.\n\n**MRVL** (-5.0%, mega) → Unknown  \nNo ticker-specific news in window. Tracks semiconductor peer pressure.\n\n**AMAT** (-4.9%, mega) → Mixed  \nEvercore ISI cut PT to **$590 from $700**; RBC maintained **$600**. Falls with wafer-fab-equipment selloff.\n\n**NOW** (-4.9%, mega) → Unknown  \nTicker articles were positive: TD Cowen Buy PT to **$165**, Citi Buy PT to **$170**, Mizuho Outperform PT to **$170**. Article at publication showed shares +4.84%; final 1D decline unexplained.\n\n**BSP** (-16.4%, large) → Unknown  \nNo Oct 15 ticker-specific negative article. Prior session surged ~45% on **Berkshire Hathaway $330M** investment; likely profit-taking.\n\n**TWLO** (-10.9%, large) 