2026-10-17	losers	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-10-17 — R1D Losers Brief\n\n**One-liner**: AI financing fears and CoreWeave debt stress hammered neoclouds, software/cybersecurity, and chip names — **CRWV**, **NBIS**, **SNOW**, **PANW**, **OKTA** — while **MSTR** and **RKLB** fell on idiosyncratic MSCI and Neutron-delay catalysts.\n\n---\n\n### 📉 Losers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | 1D | Cap | Sector | Driver type | Catalyst (≤12 words) |\n|--------|---:|-----|--------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **SNOW** | -8.2% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI debt fears hit software; Lumen partnership no offset |\n| **PLTR** | -7.0% | Mega | Technology | Idiosyncratic | Profit-taking after rally; potential congressional scrutiny |\n| **PANW** | -6.9% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI debt fears hit cybersecurity |\n| **FTNT** | -6.8% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI debt fears hit cybersecurity |\n| **CRWD** | -6.4% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI debt fears hit cybersecurity |\n| **INTC** | -6.3% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI financing fears, Fed hike bets, chip rout |\n| **ARM** | -6.0% | Mega | Technology | Mixed | Qualcomm legal setback; rates; profit-taking |\n| **NET** | -5.9% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI debt fears hit software |\n| **AMD** | -5.9% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI financing fears, rising yields hammer chips |\n| **STX** | -5.6% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Memory/storage selloff; supply concerns |\n| **LRCX** | -5.3% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Chip equipment selloff; SOXX longest skid since 2006 |\n| **SKHY** | -5.2% | Mega | Technology | Sector | CXMT memory progress; KOSPI worst week since 2008 |\n| **MRVL** | -5.0% | Mega | Technology | Sector | AI financing fears hit semis |\n| **AMAT** | -4.9% | Mega | Technology | Sector | Chip equipment selloff; Needham/Evercore cut PTs |\n| **NOW** | -4.9% | Mega | Technology | Unknown | No material negative ticker news in window |\n| **BSP** | -16.4% | Large | Technology | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n| **NBIS** | -11.9% | Large | Technology | Sector | Gartner neocloud shakeout warning; AI debt fears |\n| **CRWV** | -11.9% | Large | Technology | Sector | CoreWeave bonds >15% yield; CDS record |\n| **TWLO** | -10.9% | Large | Technology | Sector | AI debt fears hit software |\n| **OKTA** | -10.7% | Large | Technology | Sector | AI debt fears hit software |\n| **MSTR** | -9.7% | Large | Technology | Idiosyncratic | MSCI proposes excluding non-operating companies |\n| **SMCI** | -9.6% | Large | Technology | Mixed | Export-control plea; CFO named; sector AI slide |\n| **CBRS** | -9.3% | Large | Technology | Sector | AI/semis selloff; SOXX 9-day losing streak |\n| **SMCIP** | -8.3% | Large | Technology | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n| **RKLB** | -8.0% | Large | Industrials | Idiosyncratic | Neutron first flight delayed to 2027 |\n| **GRAL** | -15.4% | Mid & small | Healthcare | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n| **SHAZ** | -14.6% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n| **KOPN** | -13.5% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n| **TLK** | -13.3% | Mid & small | Communication Services | Idiosyncratic | MSCI proposes Indonesia reclassification to Standalone Market |\n| **BAND** | -13.1% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | Morgan Stanley initiates Equal-Weight; move unexplained |\n| **BLZE** | -12.9% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n| **AEHR** | -12.7% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n| **SECZ** | -12.6% | Mid & small | Technology | Unknown | Tokenization report; no clear negative catalyst |\n| **WGS** | -12.6% | Mid & small | Healthcare | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n| **TEM** | -11.9% | Mid & small | Healthcare | Unknown | No ticker-specific news in window |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Thematic / Sector Weakness\n\n**AI Infrastructure / Neocloud Debt Fears** → `Technology`\n\n- **CRWV** (-11.9%, large) and **NBIS** (-11.9%, large) fell on overlapping neocloud credit stress and a Gartner shakeout warning.\n- CoreWeave five-year credit default swaps hit a record **1,194.5 bps** on Oct 15, implying **>60% five-year default probability** per standard market math (ICE/Bloomberg). Its **9.75% notes due Oct 2031** traded at **81.80 cents on the dollar**, yielding **15.08%**; the **9.625% 2032 notes** yielded **>15.4%**.\n- Gartner warned **>80% of neocloud providers** could cease independent operations by 2030; it estimates AI data center owners need **$8.5T cumulative revenue through 2030** vs. **$3.6T forecast**, with **>$3.5T of AI infrastructure spending exposed to impairment by 2030**.\n- Ticker articles explicitly linked the selloff to CoreWeave debt costs and Gartner’s forecast for **CRWV, NBIS, and IREN**; NBIS was down roughly **20% for the week** and tested its **200-day SMA near $174.10**.\n\n**Semiconductor and AI Hardware Rollover** → `Technology`\n\n- **AMD** (-5.9%), **INTC** (-6.3%), **STX** (-5.6%), **LRCX** (-5.3%), **SKHY** (-5.2%), **MRVL** (-5.0%), **AMAT** (-4.9%), **ARM** (-6.0%), and **CBRS** (-9.3%) moved together on memory/China competition plus AI financing-cost pressure.\n- China’s **CXMT** reported progress on a denser **4F-squared DRAM architecture**; Citi (via WSJ) said mass production is unlikely before 2028 but the oversupply risk hit memory names. Counterpoint reported **YMTC became the world’s third-largest NAND maker**.\n- **SOXX fell for a ninth straight session**, its longest streak since 2006; the PHLX Semiconductor Index sits **~22% below its June 22 record**; six memory/storage makers lost **~$1.09T combined since Oct 2**.\n- **SK Hynix ADR** fell **24.3% for the week**; South Korea’s KOSPI logged its **worst week since Oct 2008 (-14.46%)**, with SK hynix **-57% from its summer peak**.\n- Broadcom CEO **Hock Tan** said capital may be the biggest AI constraint; Intel CEO **Lip-Bu Tan** echoed financing/ROA concerns. Hot PPI (**6.3% Y/Y**) and CPI (**3.7% Y/Y**) raised Fed-hike bets, per ticker articles.\n\n**Software / Cybersecurity AI Debt Fears** → `Technology`\n\n- **SNOW** (-8.2%), **PANW** (-6.9%), **FTNT** (-6.8%), **CRWD** (-6.4%), **TWLO** (-10.9%), **OKTA** (-10.7%), and **NET** (-5.9%) sold off under the same AI-financing scare.\n- Benzinga’s midday Oct 16 article stated: **TWLO** led Russell 1000 decliners **-10.7%**, **OKTA** **-8.9%**, **DDOG** **-8.7%**, **CRWD** **-7.4%**, **PANW** **-7.1%**, and **SNOW** **-7.1%**, as software and cybersecurity names got slammed while utilities, staples, and healthcare led.\n- **Broadcom CEO Hock Tan** comments on capital costs and **Gartner’s neocloud warning** fed the rotation out of high-multiple software, per ticker articles.\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Idiosyncratic Movers\n\n**PLTR** (-7.0%, mega) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- Pullback after a strong multimonth rally that took the stock near all-time highs; article framed the decline as profit-taking plus potential congressional scrutiny after expanded lobbying and inclusion on a Groundwork Collaborative target list.\n- Bulls cited Cramer’s $250 view and Goldman’s Buy upgrade / **$230 PT**; Mizuho raised PT to **$245**. No company-specific negative earnings or guidance.\n\n**NOW** (-4.9%, mega) → Unknown\n\n- Ticker articles show ServiceNow shares up/steady on Oct 15 on rotation into enterprise software, with multiple PT raises: Piper Sandler to **$175**, Mizuho to **$170**, TD Cowen to **$165**.\n- No ticker-specific negative catalyst explains Friday’s -4.9% move; likely sector/tech sympathy or profit-taking.\n\n**MSTR** (-9.7%, large) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- **MSCI** announced results of its consultation on **non-operating companies** in MSCI Global Investable Market Indexes; Strategy is among potentially affected issuers. Final list due **Nov 11**, effective **Nov 30 close**.\n- Strategy warned exclusion could trigger liquidation of **~$2.8B in shares**. Company holds **848,250 BTC** worth **~$69.5B**, with unrealized gains near **$6B**.\n\n**SMCI** (-9.6%, large) → Mixed\n\n- Appointed **Mark Long** CFO effective immediately, succeeding David Weigand; export-control pressure persisted after contractor **Ting-Wei “Willy” Sun** pleaded guilty to conspiracy in a **$2.5B scheme** to ship Nvidia AI servers to China.\n- Ticker articles also cited broad AI/tech weakness. SMCI’s **~$60B order book** supports FY2027 revenue outlook of **$65B-$72B**.\n\n**RKLB** (-8.0%, large) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- **Neutron’s first flight delayed to 2027** after manufacturing flaws (air pockets between carbon-fiber layers in the forward propellant dome). Testing targeted for completion in **Q1 2027**, with a launch date after that.\n- Backlog **$2.36B**; Q2 revenue **$234M, +62% Y/Y**; Q3 guide **$250M-$265M**. Analysts trimmed PTs: Citizens **$90**, KeyBanc **$100**; Cantor maintained **$122**.\n\n**TLK** (-13.3%, mid & small) → Idiosyncratic\n\n- **MSCI** launched a consultation on Oct 15 to reclassify **MSCI Indonesia Indexes from Emerging Market to Standalone Market**, citing opacity, suspected coordinated trading, and insufficient reforms.\n- Final decision expected by end of June 2027; MSCI keeps a freeze on FIF/NOS increases and index additions until further notice. TLK fell **14.7% pre-market** on Oct 16.\n\n**Unknown / no material ticker-specific news in window** — remaining losers\n\n- **BSP** (-16.4%, large) — no ticker-specific article in window; move unexplained/technical.\n- **SMCIP** (-8.3%, large) — no ticker-specific article in window.\n- **GRAL** (-15.4%, mid & small) — no ticker-specific article in window.\n- **SHAZ** (-14.6%, mid & small) — no ticker-specific article in window.\n- **KOPN** (-13.5%, mid & small) — no ticker-specific article in window.\n- **BAND** (-13.1%, mid & small) — Morgan Stanley initiated **Equal-Weight, $56 PT**; not an obvious driver for -13%; likely sector/small-cap pressure.\n- **BLZE** (-12.9%, mid & small) — no ticker-specific article in window.\n- **AEHR** (-12.7%, mid & small) — no ticker-specific article in window.\n- **SECZ** (-12.6%, mid & small) — article covers ARK Venture Fund tokenization; no clear negative catalyst.\n- **WGS** (-12.6%, mid & small) — no ticker-specific article in window.\n- **TEM** (-11.9%, mid & small) — no ticker-specific article in window.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sector Roll-up\n\n| Sector | Losers (count) | Avg 1D | Shared driver? |\n|--------|---------------:|-------:|----------------|\n| Technology | 30 | -8.9% | Yes — AI debt/neocloud + semis/software |\n| Healthcare | 3 | -13.3% | No — no shared catalyst |\n| Industrials | 1 | -8.0% | No — Neutron delay |\n| Communication Services | 1 | -13.3% | No — Indonesia MSCI reclassification |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 Watch\n\n- **CoreWeave credit stress**: **9.75% 2031 notes yield >15%**, CDS **1,194 bps**; JPMorgan says the selloff is overdone but watch earnings call for cash-flow guidance; near **52-week low $60.55**.\n- **MSCI index changes**: final list **Nov 11**, effective **Nov 30**; Strategy warns **$2.8B potential forced selling** if excluded — monitor MSTR premium to BTC holdings.\n- **Lam Research earnings Oct 21**: options imply **7.95% move (~$28.6B)**; UBS sees a “very strong” report and robust guidance; stock just logged its longest losing streak ever.\n- **ServiceNow earnings Oct 28**: TD Cowen expects strong Q3, cRPO acceleration; AI annual contract value already **>$1B**.\n- **Palantir Q3 Nov 9**: after 93% Q2 revenue growth; watch congressional scrutiny headlines and support at **$164.50**.\n- **Rocket Lab Neutron**: testing completion expected **Q1 2027**, then launch date; watch backlog conversion and defense awards.\n- **Super Micro**: new CFO Mark Long; export-control case unresolved; FY2027 revenue outlook **$65B-$72B** vs **~$60B order book**.\n- **Indonesia MSCI reclassification**: final decision due by **end June 2027**; interim updates possible — TLK exposed 