2026-05-11	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-05-11 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: DELL +30% on $16.1B AI server revenue (up 757% YoY) and raised FY27 guidance to $165–169B triggers a broad AI infrastructure rally, pulling NTAP +26%, HPE +13%, OKTA +30%, IBM +14%, and NOW +12% higher, while Fed's Schmid warns inflation is "too hot" and Trump leaves Situation Room without approving the proposed 60-day Iran ceasefire extension.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **DELL** | +30.4% | Mega | Q1 rev $43.8B vs $35.5B est; AI server rev $16.1B; FY27 guide raised to $165–169B | AI Infra / Servers |\n| **IBM** | +13.5% | Mega | $10B quantum investment; $5B Project Lightwell open-source security initiative | AI Infra / Quantum |\n| **NOW** | +12.3% | Mega | CMO Colin Fleming departs to become OpenAI Business CMO; sector rotation | SaaS / AI Agents |\n| **PLTR** | +9.7% | Mega | AI/defense sector rotation; no company-specific catalyst | AI Software / Defense |\n| **CRM** | +8.9% | Mega | Post-Q1 recovery; Agentforce $1.2B ARR highlight; analyst targets mostly maintained | SaaS / AI Agents |\n| **ORCL** | +8.8% | Mega | Mega-cap tech rotation; Power Inflow signal at $215.49 | Cloud / AI Infra |\n| **PANW** | +8.2% | Mega | Cybersecurity sector bid ahead of earnings ⚠️ | Cybersecurity |\n| **CRWD** | +8.1% | Mega | Project QuiltWorks cyber-insurance expansion; earnings Jun 3 ⚠️ | Cybersecurity |\n| **ADBE** | +6.4% | Mega | SaaS sector rotation; no company-specific news | SaaS |\n| **OKTA** | +29.5% | Large | Q1 EPS $0.91 vs $0.85 est; rev $765M vs $752M est; FY27 raised | Identity / Cybersecurity |\n| **NTAP** | +25.8% | Large | Q4 rev $1.95B vs $1.87B est; FY27 guide $7.33–7.58B vs $7.20B est; Google Cloud deal | Data Storage / AI |\n| **NXT** | +13.1% | Large | Acquires Prevalon Energy for $365M; raises FY27 rev guide to $4.0–4.4B | Solar / Battery Storage |\n| **TEAM** | +13.0% | Large | Sector rotation into collaboration software; no specific catalyst | SaaS |\n| **HPE** | +12.6% | Large | Dell AI server halo effect; HPE earnings Jun 1 ⚠️ | AI Infra / Servers |\n| **HOOD** | +10.8% | Large | Trump Accounts app launches; Mizuho raises PT to $115; AI agents for trading | Fintech |\n| **WDAY** | +10.6% | Large | Q1 strongest new-bookings growth in 5 years; Google Cloud partnership | SaaS / HR |\n| **SMCI** | +10.0% | Large | Taiwan compliance crackdown; Dell AI server halo effect | AI Infra / Servers |\n| **BURL** | +9.1% | Large | Q1 adj EPS $2.10 vs $1.78 est; comp +6%; FY26 guide raised | Retail / Off-Price |\n| **HPQ** | +8.8% | Large | Q2 adj EPS $0.86 vs $0.71 est; AI PC mix at 44% of shipments | PCs |\n| **SPCE** | +42.8% | Small | Derivative lawsuit settlement ($2.75M); SpaceX IPO proxy trade | Space |\n| **MX** | +31.2% | Small | No identified catalyst; 5D +62% momentum continuation | Semiconductors |\n| **PD** | +29.1% | Small | Q1 adj EPS $0.32 vs $0.25 est; rev $121M vs $120M est | SaaS / Ops |\n| **CHA** | +25.5% | Small | Q1 adj EPS $0.38 vs $0.23 est; $150M buyback announced | Consumer / Beverages |\n| **TSSI** | +23.2% | Small | Director Form 144 filed (300K shares); Dell partnership tailwind | Data Center Services |\n| **GRRR** | +15.2% | Small | No identified catalyst | Idiosyncratic |\n| **ASAN** | +12.8% | Small | Q1 EPS $0.10 vs $0.07 est; acquires StackAI; FY27 guide raised | SaaS / AI Agents |\n| **UMAC** | +5.4% (5D +94%) | Small | Pentagon drone funding talks; partner Powerus enters Phase II of $1B program | Defense / Drones |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Dell's AI Server Blowout Reprices the Entire Hardware Stack** `AI Compute / Servers` → new\n\n**DELL** +30.4% delivered the session's defining print: Q1 revenue $43.84B (+88% YoY) vs $35.45B est; adjusted EPS $4.86 vs $2.94 est. AI server revenue hit $16.1B (+757% YoY), with $24.4B in new AI orders and a record $51.3B AI backlog. Management raised FY27 revenue guidance to $165–169B from $138–142B and AI server revenue target to $60B from $50B. COO Jeff Clarke said some customers are signing multi-year deals without guaranteed pricing to secure supply. Memory/DRAM/NAND supply constraints were flagged as the primary bottleneck.\n\n- Melius raised PT to $565 (street-high); Piper Sandler to $497; Wells Fargo to $505; BofA to $500; Barclays to $550\n- Susquehanna upgraded to Positive with $700 PT\n- Michael Dell's net worth rose ~$32.2B on the day, passing Zuckerberg for 6th on Forbes list\n- Trump told investors to "buy a Dell" on May 8; stock up ~80% since then; $9.69B Pentagon contract awarded this week\n- **HPE** +12.6% rallied in sympathy; reports Jun 1 ⚠️\n- **SMCI** +10.0% benefited from the server halo plus Taiwan compliance crackdown news (3 arrests, 50+ servers seized)\n- **HPQ** +8.8% beat Q2 estimates (adj EPS $0.86 vs $0.71); AI PC shipment mix rose to 44%\n- **NTAP** +25.8% reported Q4 rev $1.95B vs $1.87B est; FY27 guide $7.33–7.58B vs $7.20B est; multi-year Google Distributed Cloud agreement; Barclays raised PT to $199\n- Dell's commentary on memory constraints is bullish for **MU** (+2.7%, 5D +25%) and **SNDK** (+1.2%); Susquehanna raised MU PT to $1,750 and SNDK PT to $3,250\n- MU reports Jun 24 ⚠️\n\n**Enterprise AI Software Accelerates** `SaaS / AI Agents` → ongoing\n\nMultiple SaaS names posted outsized gains as AI agent adoption moved from pilot to production across enterprises.\n\n- **OKTA** +29.5%: Q1 EPS $0.91 vs $0.85 est; rev $765M vs $752M est; cRPO +12% YoY to $2.50B; NRR improved to 107%; FY27 EPS guide raised to $3.79–3.87; agentic AI security pipeline described as "bigger than anything we've ever seen." BTIG raised PT to $119; Needham to $120; Oppenheimer to $125; JP Morgan to $120; Cantor to $125; Guggenheim reiterated Buy at $138\n- **NOW** +12.3%: CMO Colin Fleming left to become OpenAI's Business CMO—market read this as validation of ServiceNow's AI talent pipeline rather than a negative\n- **CRM** +8.9%: Post-Q1 recovery after initial selloff; Agentforce hit $1.2B ARR (+205% YoY); processed 28.6T tokens (+152% QoQ); Q2 rev guide $11.27–11.35B slightly below est; DA Davidson cut PT to $175; Bernstein cut to $173; Wedbush maintained $325\n- **WDAY** +10.6%: Strongest Q1 new-bookings growth in 5 years; expanded Google Cloud partnership for AI agents in HR/finance\n- **ASAN** +12.8%: Q1 EPS $0.10 vs $0.07 est; acquired StackAI (no-code AI workflow platform, ~$75M upfront cash); AI product bookings 17% of net new ARR vs 15% target; FY27 rev guide raised to $855.5–863.5M\n- **PD** +29.1%: Q1 adj EPS $0.32 vs $0.25 est; ARR flat at $496M; Operations Cloud usage-based package launched\n- **TEAM** +13.0%: Broad SaaS rotation; no company-specific catalyst identified\n\n**Cybersecurity Names Rally Into Earnings** `Cybersecurity` → ongoing\n\n- **CRWD** +8.1%: Expanded Project QuiltWorks with Coalition, Liberty Mutual, Lockton for AI cyber-risk insurance framework; SVA Germany deal for Falcon platform; Jefferies raised PT to $775; earnings Jun 3 ⚠️\n- **PANW** +8.2%: No company-specific news; cybersecurity sector tailwind; earnings upcoming ⚠️\n- **FTNT** +5.2%: Sector rotation; no specific catalyst\n\n**AI Infrastructure Capex Wave Broadens** `AI Compute / Memory / Networking` → ongoing\n\nThe AI buildout extended beyond GPUs into memory, networking, storage and cloud platforms.\n\n- **MU** +2.7% (5D +25%): Best month since Nov 1985 (+84% in May); crossed $1T market cap; invested in Anthropic's $65B Series H round; MU reports Jun 24 ⚠️\n- **MRVL** +0.1%: Q1 rev $2.42B vs $2.40B est; raised FY27 rev growth target to >40%; CEO said "agentic AI to further supercharge demand"; Barclays raised PT to $275; Benchmark to $275; Needham to $270; Deutsche Bank to $240\n- **ORCL** +8.8%: Mega-cap tech rotation; $6.5B in CDS outstanding (highest among Big Tech per Kobeissi Letter)\n- **ARM** +4.8% (5D +16%): AGI CPU demand >$2B backlog; Mizuho raised PT to $360 (street-high); Bernstein initiated at $300 Outperform\n- **QCOM** +3.1%: Launched Snapdragon C for entry-level AI laptops\n- Anthropic raised $65B Series H at $965B valuation, surpassing OpenAI; Apollo/Blackstone arranging $36B debt to buy Google TPUs for Anthropic\n\n**Iran Ceasefire Extension Stalls; Oil Eases But Uncertainty Persists** `Macro / Geopolitics` → ongoing\n\nTrump left a Situation Room meeting without approving the proposed 60-day ceasefire extension. Iran disputed key US claims about the MOU terms—Tehran says no nuclear provisions are included and demands $12B in frozen assets. Bolton warned Iran is "buying time."\n\n- Treasury Secretary Bessent said US seized ~$1B in Iranian crypto; described "Operation Economic Fury" as pushing Tehran toward financial crisis\n- Oil fell: Brent ~$91.68, WTI ~$87.86; Brent down ~19% from April peak (steepest monthly drop since 2020)\n- Fed's Schmid: inflation is "too hot"; "I place little stock" in transitory narrative; surging oil weighing on spending power\n- Fed's Bowman: reacting to temporary energy shock could harm economy; "moderately restrictive" policy aimed at both jobs and inflation\n- Fed's Paulson: inflation pressures weighing on economy; holding rates steady gives Fed space to weigh data\n- Core PCE April: +0.2% MoM (below 0.3% est); +3.3% YoY (in line); headline PCE +3.8% YoY (highest since May 2023)\n- Q1 GDP revised down to 1.6% from 2.0%\n- Personal saving rate fell to 2.6%, lowest since 2022\n- Chicago PMI May: 62.7 vs 50.6 est (sharp beat)\n- CME FedWatch: 98.9% probability of hold in June; ~70% chance of 25bp hike by year-end\n\n**Space Mania Intensifies Ahead of SpaceX IPO** `Space / Defense` → ongoing\n\n- **SPCE** +42.8% (5D +99%): Derivative lawsuit settlement approved; treated as SpaceX proxy trade\n- SpaceX IPO target trimmed to $1.8T from $2T per Bloomberg; Q1 net loss $4.28B driven by xAI merger costs; up to 30% of IPO shares may go to retail; IPO targeted for Jun 12 ⚠️\n- UFO ETF surpassed $1B AUM; NASA ETF reached $1.27B in 37 trading days\n- Blue Origin's New Glenn rocket exploded during static fire test Thursday—sentiment headwind for space stocks\n- **RKLB** -4.8%: Profit-taking after 436% 12-month gain\n- **LUNR**: Roth Capital raised PT to $75; pulled back -13% Friday after +13% Thursday\n\n**Drone Dominance Program Accelerates** `Defense / Drones` → new\n\nWSJ reported Trump administration in active talks to take equity/debt stakes in US drone manufacturers through Pentagon's Office of Strategic Capital, mirroring Intel/MP Materials playbook.\n\n- **UMAC** +5.4% (5D +94%): Partner Powerus advanced to Phase II of Pentagon's $1B Drone Dominance Program; Trump Jr. is shareholder and advisory board member\n- 49 companies invited to Phase II qualifying event in June\n- FY2027 defense budget targets 300,000 low-cost attack drones by 2027\n\n**Retail Diverges: Value Wins, Fashion Struggles** `Retail` → ongoing\n\n- **BURL** +9.1%: Q1 adj EPS $2.10 vs $1.78 est; comp +6%; 14% total sales growth; FY26 guide raised to $11.45–11.80 EPS; off-price value proposition resonating\n- **DLTR** +3.0% (5D +23%): Q1 adj EPS $1.74 vs $1.55 est; comp +3.5%; FY26 guide raised; launched DoorDash nationwide partnership\n- **GAP** fell ~17%: Q1 rev $3.5B slightly missed; FY26 rev guide cut to $15.52–15.67B; JP Morgan downgraded to Neutral; merch margin hit 200bp from tariffs\n- **COST** fell ~5%: Q3 EPS $4.93 vs $4.98 est; rev $70.5B beat; comp +9.8%; record fuel volumes but gas margin pressure\n- **AEO** fell ~14%: Q1 results pressured by tariff-related margin headwinds\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n\n- **MDB** +0.9% but 4.5× volume: Q1 rev $688M vs $665M est (+25% YoY); Atlas +29.4%; FY27 guide raised to $2.92–2.96B; Needham raised PT to $400; Citi to $455; stock sold off intraday despite strong results. Reports next quarter in Aug ⚠️\n- **Bitcoin ETFs** bled $2.43B in May (worst month of year); IBIT lost $177M Wednesday; BTC at $73,468—41% below ATH; CryptoQuant warns whale accumulation contracting to 2022 levels; rotation into equities appears underway\n- **Private credit redemptions**: Apollo's Zelter said outflows "not a one-shot" and could accelerate; Oaktree repurchased 6.8% of fund; Goldman's fund saw <5% redemption requests\n- **Jamie Dimon** warned current market exuberance echoes 1972, 1986, 2000, 2007; BofA Bull & Bear Indicator hit 8.5 (contrarian sell zone); only 21 S&P 500 stocks (4%) at new highs—matching March 2000\n- **USMCA renegotiation**: Trump admin seeking 82% North American content (from 75%) and 50% US-produced content for autos; no Canadian content provision\n- **MSFT** building unified "One Copilot" super app combining GitHub Copilot, Copilot Chat, and Autopilot; expected by end of summer; Nvidia/MSFT Windows PC launch at Computex next week\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | DELL Q1 rev $43.84B (+88% YoY) vs $35.45B est; AI server rev $16.1B (+757%); FY27 guide raised to $165–169B |\n| Macro | Core PCE Apr +0.2% MoM (below 0.3% est); headline PCE +3.8% YoY (highest since May 2023); Q1 GDP revised to 1.6% from 2.0%; personal saving rate 2.6% (lowest since 2022) |\n| Geopolitics | Trump left Situation Room without approving Iran ceasefire extension; Iran disputes US claims on nuclear/Hormuz terms; US seized ~$1B in Iranian crypto |\n| Tech | Anthropic raised $65B Series H at $965B valuation; Apollo/Blackstone arranging $36B debt for Google TPU purchases; MSFT building "One Copilot" super app |\n| Commodities | WTI crude $87.86/bbl (-1.3%); Brent down ~19% in May; gold +1.5% to ~$4,564/oz |\n| Fed | Schmid: inflation "too hot," won't call it transitory; Bowman: moderately restrictive policy; Paulson: inflation too high due to multiple forces |\n| Space/Defense | SpaceX IPO target trimmed to $1.8T; Blue Origin New Glenn exploded during static fire; Pentagon exploring equity stakes in US drone makers |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **CRWD** earnings Jun 3 (confirmed): EPS est $0.88, rev est $1.36B; stock +42.5% in 12 months; RSI 75.59 (overbought)\n- **HPE** earnings Jun 1: Dell's AI server commentary directly relevant; stock already +12.6% on sympathy\n- **AVGO** earnings upcoming: Jim Cramer flagged as key test for AI networking; $2T market cap; Apollo/Blackstone arranging $36B for Anthropic's Broadcom-guaranteed TPU deal\n- **MU** earnings Jun 24 (confirmed): EPS est $19.16 vs $1.91 YoY; rev est $33.66B vs $9.30B YoY; stock up 84% in May\n- **SpaceX IPO** targeted Jun 12: Valuation trimmed to $1.8T; Goldman Sachs lead underwriter; up to 30% retail allocation\n- **Computex/MSFT Build** next week: NVDA Huang keynote; first Nvidia-powered Windows PC unveiling; ARM, MRVL, INTC, QCOM execs participating\n- **US jobs report** Friday (Jun 6): JOLTS Tue, ADP Wed, ISM Services Wed, NFP Fri; April payrolls were +115K, unemployment 4.3%\n- **ALAB** earnings May 19 gapper; **GFS** earnings May 22 gapper; **MDB** earnings May 28 gapper—all within 3 sessions ⚠️\n- **USMCA** auto content renegotiation: 82% NAm content, 50% US content demanded; impacts F, GM, STLA\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **PLTR** +9.7%: No company-specific catalyst; pure AI/defense sector rotation; 161× trailing P/E; analyst spread is $140 between bear ($90 RBC) and bull ($230 Wedbush)—noise until Aug earnings\n- **Political headlines**: Trump cognitive test score, Pope Leo feud, Adam Schiff tax allegations—none market-moving\n- **Crypto narrative shifts**: BTC volatility compressing toward gold; HYPE token breakout—interesting but immaterial to equity positioning this session	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 467083, "output_tokens": 5417, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 2.335415, "total_cost_usd": 2.47084, "output_cost_usd": 0.135425, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache