2026-06-09	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-06-09 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Semiconductors extend Monday's rebound with **INTC** +10% on Google/Nvidia foundry reports, **CBRS** +20% on seven analyst initiations, and **MRVL** +6.5% on S&P 500 inclusion; **NUVL** +39% on $10.6B GSK acquisition; OpenAI files confidential S-1 joining SpaceX and Anthropic in an unprecedented IPO wave.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **INTC** | +10.1% | Mega | Google ordered 3M+ AI chips for 2028; Nvidia evaluating 18A node | Foundry / AI Compute |\n| **KLAC** | +8.0% | Mega | Semiconductor rebound post-Friday rout; BofA Buy list | Semicap Equipment |\n| **MRVL** | +6.5% | Mega | S&P 500 inclusion effective Jun 22; 5D +33% | AI Networking |\n| **AMAT** | +6.5% | Mega | Semiconductor sector rebound | Semicap Equipment |\n| **MU** | +6.4% | Mega | Dip-buying; Wells Fargo PT raised to $1,220; Cantor PT $1,500 ⚠️ | Memory / AI Compute |\n| **GLW** | +6.0% | Mega | Amazon multibillion-dollar fiber-optics supply agreement; +1,000 jobs NC | Optical / AI Infra |\n| **ASML** | +5.5% | Mega | Semiconductor sector rebound | Semicap Equipment |\n| **LRCX** | +5.4% | Mega | Semiconductor sector rebound | Semicap Equipment |\n| **TSLA** | +4.8% | Mega | China May retail sales +22.6% YoY; exports +68% YoY | EV / Mobility |\n| **SNDK** | +4.6% | Mega | BofA PT raised to $2,100; Cantor PT $2,900; Mizuho PT $2,200 | Memory / NAND |\n| **CBRS** | +20.0% | Large | 7 analyst initiations; PTs $250–$340; OpenAI $20B+ compute deal | AI Inference |\n| **IONQ** | +10.9% | Large | Quantum sector rebound; broader tech risk-on | Quantum Computing |\n| **IREN** | +10.1% | Large | Crypto/BTC mining rebound after Friday selloff | Crypto Mining |\n| **MSTR** | +8.1% | Large | Strategy bought 1,550 BTC at avg $65,332; $1B cash reserve | Bitcoin Treasury |\n| **ALAB** | +7.8% | Large | Semiconductor sector rebound | AI Networking |\n| **COIN** | +6.9% | Large | Crypto rebound; institutional BTC demand commentary | Crypto Exchange |\n| **DXCM** | +6.7% | Large | CONNECT trial: G7 CGM showed 1.6% avg A1C reduction in T2D | MedTech |\n| **STM** | +6.7% | Large | Semiconductor sector rebound | Analog / Mixed Signal |\n| **SMCI** | +6.3% | Large | Unconfirmed rumor of $5.2B xAI server deal; sector bounce | AI Servers |\n| **FICO** | +5.9% | Large | $2B buyback announced; Needham reiterates Buy PT $1,650 | Analytics / SaaS |\n| **NUVL** | +38.7% PM | Large | GSK acquisition at $124/share ($10.6B); 40% premium | Biotech / M&A |\n| **ENHA** | +32.2% | Small | No identified catalyst; +40% Monday, -11% premarket Tue | Idiosyncratic |\n| **ABAT** | +26.2% | Small | DOE reinstated grant for $115M lithium refinery project | Clean Energy / Battery |\n| **GLXY** | +23.4% | Small | Morgan Stanley/Galaxy crypto lending referral capability; 1.6GW data center | Crypto / AI Infra |\n| **BTGO** | +15.6% | Small | BitGo MENA launches regulated electronic trading under VARA | Crypto Infra |\n| **BOT** | +15.0% | Small | 5D +83.3%; no specific catalyst identified | Idiosyncratic |\n| **KEEL** | +13.2% | Small | Risk-on bounce after $400M convertible notes priced; BTC mining pivot | Crypto / Data Center |\n| **MARA** | +13.1% | Small | Crypto rebound; BTC bounce from $59K low | Crypto Mining |\n| **STI** | -24.0% | Small | $35M private placement dilution; 5D +456% prior run | Battery Tech |\n| **CRWD** | -3.1% | Mega | 5D -15.9%; no specific catalyst; post-selloff continuation | Cybersecurity |\n| **SAIL** | -11% PM | Large | Q1 EPS $0.05 beat $0.04; FY rev guide raised marginally; muted reaction | Identity Security / SaaS |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Semiconductor Rebound & Intel Foundry Catalyst** `AI Compute / Semicap` → new\n\nThe entire semiconductor complex bounced sharply Monday off Friday's 10%+ SOXX rout, with the largest single-stock catalyst being **INTC** +10.1%. The Information reported that Google has ordered 3M+ AI chips from Intel for 2028 delivery, while Nvidia is evaluating Intel's advanced packaging and 18A process node as a backup to TSMC. Jim Cramer remains "VERY skeptical" given the 2028 timeline. Cadence announced expanded DTCO collaboration with Intel Foundry targeting Intel 14A.\n\n- **INTC** closed +11.2% Monday; +1.5% premarket Tuesday; 5D +2.6%; next earnings ~Jul 23 ⚠️; EPS est $0.19 vs loss of $0.10 YoY; rev est $14.40B vs $12.86B\n- **MU** +6.4%; Wells Fargo raised PT to $1,220 (Overweight); Cantor Fitzgerald raised PT to $1,500 (Overweight); earnings Jun 24 ⚠️; EPS est $19.33 vs $1.91 YoY; rev est $33.9B vs $9.3B\n- **KLAC** +8.0%, **AMAT** +6.5%, **LRCX** +5.4%, **ASML** +5.5% — all rebounding in lockstep\n- **SNDK** +4.6%; BofA raised PT to $2,100 (Buy); Cantor raised PT to $2,900 (Overweight); Mizuho raised PT to $2,200 (Outperform); BofA cites multi-year NBM contracts locking in $42B minimum revenue\n- BofA analyst Vivek Arya: AI data center gear TAM to reach $1.7T by 2030 (from $264B in 2025); names NVDA, CRDO, ADI, TXN, KLAC, MCHP, CDNS as Buy picks\n- 22V Research's John Roque warns 2-year Treasury yield breakout toward 5% is "Public Enemy No. 1" for high-multiple chip names; SNDK was 250% above 200-day MA, MRVL 220% above at peak\n\n**Marvell S&P 500 Inclusion** `AI Networking` → new\n\n**MRVL** +6.5% (5D +33%) after S&P Dow Jones Indices announced inclusion in S&P 500 effective June 22, replacing Pool Corp. Jensen Huang recently called MRVL "the next trillion-dollar company."\n\n- Market cap ~$253B; ~$20T in assets indexed to S&P 500 creating forced passive buying\n- YTD +230%; Barclays PT $275; UBS PT $230; Citigroup PT $225; next earnings ~Aug 27 ⚠️\n- EPS est $0.88 vs $0.67 YoY; rev est $2.70B vs $2.01B\n- **Flex** (FLEX) also added to S&P 500 same date; **CPB** and **POOL** removed to S&P SmallCap 600\n\n**Cerebras Analyst Initiation Wave** `AI Inference` → new\n\n**CBRS** +20.0% after seven simultaneous analyst initiations — all Buy or Overweight — with PTs ranging from $270 (Wedbush) to $340 (Citigroup).\n\n- Needham PT $300: highlights wafer-scale engine with 44GB on-chip SRAM vs 178MB on Nvidia B200; 15x faster inference claimed\n- OpenAI compute agreement >$20B: 750MW capacity through 2028, option for 1.25GW more\n- AWS collaboration for disaggregated inference using Cerebras CS-3 systems\n- Additional initiations: Morgan Stanley $250, Rosenblatt $300, UBS $300, Barclays $280, Mizuho $300, TD Cowen $275\n- Stock was in deeply oversold territory (RSI 28.23) before the bounce\n\n**Apple WWDC & Siri AI** `Consumer Hardware / AI` → new\n\n**AAPL** closed -1.9% Monday after unveiling Siri AI at WWDC. Gene Munster (Deepwater) estimates full Siri AI launch delayed to mid-CY27 vs prior fall 2026 expectations. Apple's most advanced AI model (AFM 3 Cloud Pro) will run on **NVDA** chips through **GOOGL** Google Cloud, not Apple Silicon.\n\n- Siri AI available to developers in beta immediately; consumer access expected fall 2026\n- Apple Intelligence not launching in Europe or China due to regulatory issues\n- Tim Sweeney (Epic Games) criticized Apple's AI ecosystem restrictions\n- Apple's picks-and-shovels beneficiaries: **TSM**, **AVGO**, **ARM**, **GLW**, **CRUS**, **SWKS**, **OLED**\n- **GLW** +6.0% separately on Amazon multibillion-dollar fiber-optics supply deal; +1,000 jobs in North Carolina; UBS raised PT to $228\n\n**GSK-Nuvalent Acquisition** `Biotech / Oncology M&A` → new\n\n**GSK** agreed to acquire **NUVL** for $124/share ($10.6B cash), a 40% premium to Monday's close of $88.49. NUVL +38.7% premarket to $122.76.\n\n- GSK's largest acquisition in more than a decade; second-largest ever\n- Three lung cancer assets: zidesamtinib, neladalkib, NVL-330\n- Expected accretive to sales and core operating profit from 2027; core EPS accretive from 2029\n- Global biotech M&A: $106B across 201 transactions in 2026 YTD per PitchBook\n\n**Crypto / Bitcoin Treasury & Infrastructure** `Crypto` → ongoing\n\n**BTC** ~$63,000 after briefly touching $59,101 on Friday. Strategy (**MSTR** +8.1%) bought 1,550 BTC at avg $65,332 for $101M — first purchase since selling 32 BTC at $77,135 last week. Total holdings: 845,256 BTC at avg $75,680.\n\n- MSTR issued $181M in common stock to fund purchase; increased USD reserve to $1B for preferred dividend backstop\n- Peter Schiff: MSTR is at "beginning of the end"; argues selling common below NAV premium is dilutive\n- **GLXY** +23.4%: Morgan Stanley Wealth Management referral capability for crypto-to-ETP lending; Galaxy building largest single-campus U.S. data center (1.6GW)\n- **COIN** +6.9%: Coinbase exec says institutions "not unhappy" buying BTC at discount; family offices and sovereign funds still accumulating\n- **BTGO** +15.6%: BitGo MENA launches regulated electronic trading under Dubai's VARA\n- BTC ETFs: >$4B outflows over 12 consecutive trading days — longest streak since launch\n- Tom Lee (Fundstrat): "Bull market is still intact"; crypto is "downstream story of AI"\n\n**IPO Wave: SpaceX, OpenAI, Anthropic** `IPOs / Capital Markets` → ongoing\n\nOpenAI filed confidential S-1 on Monday. SpaceX IPO set for June 12 at $135/share (~$1.77T valuation, $75B raise). Anthropic filed confidential S-1 last week.\n\n- OpenAI: "We have not decided on timing yet; it may be a while"\n- Polymarket: 48% probability OpenAI closes above $1.5T market cap on day one (up from 31% a week ago)\n- SpaceX: Hyperliquid pre-IPO perpetuals show 85% of 4,528 traders long; 78% underwater; $450M+ notional volume\n- Steve Eisman ("Big Short"): SpaceX capex-to-revenue ratio exploded from 42% (FY2023) to 215% (Q1 FY2026); calls valuation "crazy"\n- Mohamed El-Erian warns of "intense demand for capital" as three mega IPOs coincide with heavy government and corporate bond issuance\n- Databricks reportedly eyeing $165B–$175B valuation in new funding round; potential 2027 IPO\n\n**Geopolitical: Iran-Israel Ceasefire & Energy Costs** `Macro` → ongoing\n\nIran's armed forces announced end to military operations against Israel, warning of "harsher attacks" if Lebanese strikes resume. Netanyahu reserved "full right to self-defense." Trump called for "immediate ceasefire."\n\n- WTI crude eased to ~$89–91 after touching ~$95 overnight; national gas avg $4.16/gallon (AAA)\n- Goldman Sachs scrapped 2026 rate-cut call; now expects no cuts; CME FedWatch: 98.2% chance Fed holds in June\n- Container shipping: Asia-to-US West Coast spot rate jumped 20%+ over past week\n- Gov. Newsom: Americans saddled with extra $55.6B in fuel costs since Iran conflict began\n\n**Pentagon China Blacklist Expansion** `Geopolitics / Trade` → new\n\nPentagon expanded "1260H list" of Chinese military-linked companies, adding **BABA**, **BIDU**, **BYD**, **NIO**, WuXi AppTec, RoboSense, Unitree, CALB, EVE Energy, Hesai, BOE Technology.\n\n- **NIO** says designation "not justified"; threatens legal recourse\n- No immediate sanctions but DoD prohibited from contracting with listed firms; third-party procurement ban from June 2027\n- Alibaba, Baidu, WuXi AppTec challenging inclusion\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **ORCL** reports Q4 FY2026 after close Wednesday Jun 10; EPS est $1.96 vs $1.70 YoY; rev est $19.09B vs $15.9B; Guggenheim PT $400 (88% upside); TD Cowen raised PT to $300 ⚠️\n- **SAIL** (SailPoint) Q1 EPS $0.05 beat $0.04; FY rev guide raised to $1.265B–$1.275B; stock -11% premarket — identity security names under pressure\n- China May exports +19.4% YoY vs +15.0% est; imports +27.4% vs +25.0% est; trade surplus $105.4B — stronger-than-expected external demand\n- Federal judge blocked IRS rule making renewable energy tax credits harder to claim; clean energy stocks (BE, ENPH, FSLR) getting policy tailwind with July 4 tax credit deadline approaching\n- **APLD** (Applied Digital) signed 15-year, 210MW AI data center lease; also announced $1.59B senior secured notes offering for North Dakota Polaris Forge 1 campus\n- **CECO** Environmental: acquired Thermon Group; updated FY2026 combined guidance to $1.275B–$1.375B revenue (+~20% YoY at midpoint), Adj EBITDA $195M–$225M; expects $40M+ in cost synergies\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **SJM** Q4 EPS $2.77 beat $2.64 est; rev $2.268B beat $2.26B est. **UNFI** Q3 EPS $0.77 missed $0.78; rev $7.723B missed $7.803B; narrowed FY guide. **ASO** Q1 adj EPS $0.93 beat $0.91; raised FY adj EPS guide to $6.40–$6.80 vs $6.30 est. **SAIL** Q1 EPS $0.05 beat $0.04; stock -11% PM. **TITN** Q1 EPS $(0.58) beat $(0.68). |\n| Macro | China May exports +19.4% YoY vs +15.0% est; trade surplus $105.4B vs $92.1B est. ADP weekly employment change 29K vs 35.75K prior. UK BRC retail sales +3.4% YoY vs +0.8% est. |\n| Tech | Apple unveiled Siri AI at WWDC; AFM 3 Cloud Pro runs on NVDA chips via Google Cloud. OpenAI filed confidential S-1. SpaceX detailed AI-1 satellite: 120kW avg compute payload, NVDA chips, 70m solar panels. |\n| M&A | GSK acquires NUVL for $10.6B ($124/share cash). CECO completed Thermon acquisition; $40M+ synergies expected. Ingredion acquiring Tate & Lyle for £2.7B. |\n| Geopolitics | Pentagon expanded China military blacklist: BABA, BIDU, BYD, NIO, WuXi AppTec added. Iran halted military operations vs Israel; warned of resumption if Lebanon strikes continue. |\n| Commodities | WTI crude ~$89–91/bbl, off overnight $95+ highs on ceasefire signals. Gold flat at ~$4,335/oz. Tungsten scrap prices +350% since May 2025 per Argus Media; Chinese buyers outbidding US recyclers. |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **ORCL** Q4 FY2026 earnings after close Wed Jun 10; EPS est $1.96; rev est $19.09B; Guggenheim "Best Idea" PT $400 ⚠️\n- **MU** earnings Jun 24; EPS est $19.33; rev est $33.9B; stock down 9.2% over 5D ⚠️\n- **MRVL** S&P 500 inclusion effective before market open Jun 22; forced passive buying imminent ⚠️\n- **SpaceX** IPO trading begins