2026-06-19	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 June 19, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Semiconductors dominate as Trump confirms Apple-Intel chip manufacturing pact sending INTC +10%, memory stocks surge on Apple's "100-year flood" pricing warning, oil collapses to $75 on signed U.S.-Iran MOU reopening Hormuz, while Accenture crashes 18% after cutting FY guidance and the Fed's hawkish dot plot reprices rate hike odds to 53%.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **INTC** | +9.9% | Mega | Trump confirms Apple agreed to design/build chips with Intel | AI Compute / Foundry |\n| **GLW** | +11.1% | Mega | Broad semi/connectivity rally; no specific headline | Connectivity |\n| **MRVL** | +9.9% | Mega | Nikkei: plans to use TSMC 1.4nm for next-gen AI chips; S&P 500 inclusion Jun 22 | AI Compute / Custom Silicon |\n| **KLAC** | +8.2% | Mega | Broad semi equipment rally; 5D -89.1% prior drop reversal | Semicap Equipment |\n| **SNDK** | +8.0% | Mega | Apple CEO: memory price hikes "unavoidable"; "100-year flood" | Memory / Storage |\n| **MU** | +5.4% | Mega | Apple memory warning; Deutsche Bank PT raised to $1,500; earnings Jun 24 ⚠️ | Memory |\n| **TSM** | +6.1% | Mega | 10-year Amkor packaging deal in Arizona; broad foundry bid | Foundry |\n| **GEV** | +5.5% | Mega | Bernstein initiates Outperform, PT $1,206 | Power / AI Infrastructure |\n| **TXN** | +6.5% | Mega | Broad analog/semi rally | Analog Semi |\n| **QCOM** | +5.3% | Mega | Broad semi rally | Mobile / Edge AI |\n| **BE** | +13.6% | Large | Tariff-reset framework; Bernstein initiates Market Perform PT $276 | Clean Energy / Data Center Power |\n| **ENTG** | +11.6% | Large | Broad semicap materials rally; 2.4× avg volume | Semicap Materials |\n| **ALAB** | +10.1% | Large | Broad AI connectivity rally | AI Networking |\n| **ACN** | -18.0% | Large | Q3 EPS $3.80 beat $3.69 est; revenue $18.7B miss; FY rev guide cut to $71.8-72.5B vs $74B est | IT Services |\n| **RKT** | +8.2% | Large | 2.3× volume; no specific catalyst identified | Fintech / Mortgage |\n| **BFLY** | +52.6% | Small | Midjourney Medical scanner uses 40 Butterfly ultrasound chips; Musk reacted | MedTech / AI |\n| **HQ** | +59.3% | Small | Multi-day quantum computing momentum; 7× avg volume | Quantum Computing |\n| **MEI** | +22.6% | Small | No specific catalyst; 2.9× volume | Electronic Components |\n| **SWBI** | +16.6% | Small | Q4 EPS $0.36 beat $0.23 est; revenue $178.4M beat $155.3M est | Consumer / Firearms |\n| **FCEL** | +17.4% | Small | Data center power pipeline momentum; 4GW pipeline +267% QoQ | Clean Energy |\n| **QS** | +12.1% | Small | Joint research agreement with Honda on solid-state batteries | EV / Batteries |\n| **WOLF** | +15.7% | Small | Traders circulate datacenter demand commentary | SiC / Power Semi |\n| **WYFI** | +14.9% | Small | AI infrastructure / data center momentum | AI Infrastructure |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Semiconductor Super-Cycle Enters Manufacturing Phase** `AI Compute` → ongoing\n\nThe session's dominant story was the convergence of three catalysts across the chip complex: Trump's Truth Social confirmation that **Apple** has agreed to work with **Intel** on U.S. chip design/manufacturing, Apple CEO Tim Cook's "100-year flood" memory shortage warning, and Intel's 18A-P node entering risk production.\n\n- **INTC** +9.9%; Trump said Apple, Nvidia, and Tesla's TerraFab will all use Intel foundry. U.S. government's 9.9% stake (purchased at $20.47/share in Aug 2025) now worth ~$52B vs $8.9B cost. Intel also hired former SK Hynix CEO Seok-Hee Lee as EVP of advanced packaging/back-end manufacturing.\n- **MU** +5.4% ahead of Jun 24 earnings ⚠️. Deutsche Bank raised PT to $1,500; Stifel to $1,500; Citigroup to $1,200; Wedbush to $1,300. Consensus Q3 EPS est $19.74 vs $1.91 YoY; revenue est $34.4B vs $9.3B YoY.\n- **SNDK** +8.0%; **WDC** +3.5% (5D +44%); Apple's Cook said DRAM/NAND prices quadrupled, iPhone Pro memory component cost may jump from ~$39 to ~$145. TechInsights estimates iPhone Pro starting price could rise to $1,299 from $1,099.\n- **MRVL** +9.9%; KeyBanc raised PT to $385; Nikkei reported plans to use TSMC's 1.4nm A14 process for next-gen AI chips. S&P 500 inclusion effective Jun 22 ⚠️. Tower Semiconductor announced 5M+ coherent photonic IC shipments to Marvell.\n- **TSM** +6.1%; signed 10-year advanced packaging deal with Amkor in Arizona. Fell to #7 globally by market cap after SpaceX IPO.\n- **ALAB** +10.1%, **ENTG** +11.6%, **LSCC** +7.2%, **UMC** +8.9%, **MKSI** +8.1% — broad semicap/materials/foundry rally.\n- BofA Fund Manager Survey: 80% of global fund managers now call "long global semiconductors" the most crowded trade in history, up from 73% in May.\n- UBS trading desk warned clients to "reduce risk meaningfully" in tech, calling the AI trade "extreme and increasingly binary."\n\n**Oil Collapse & Iran MOU** `Macro / Commodities` → new\n\nThe U.S.-Iran 14-point Memorandum of Understanding was signed at Versailles, sending crude to its lowest since the conflict began and erasing the entire energy war premium.\n\n- WTI fell ~2.2% to ~$75/bbl, touching its 200-day moving average (~$73.54) for the first time since the war began. Brent ~$78.66. Crude now down ~38% from April peak.\n- National average gas fell below $4/gallon for the first time since late March (AAA).\n- BofA cut 2026 Brent forecast to $82 from $93; sees $70 in 2027. Goldman expects Persian Gulf exports to normalize by end-July. IEA projects 5M bpd global surplus by 2027.\n- MOU key terms: U.S. lifts naval blockade within 30 days; Iran allows free commercial transit for 60 days; U.S. terminates all sanctions; $300B reconstruction plan (with "regional partners"); Iran reaffirms no nuclear weapons, agrees to down-blend enriched uranium under IAEA supervision.\n- VP Vance warned Israel against undermining deal; said "not a cent of American money goes to Iran." Iran's Supreme Leader issued written permission for MOU.\n- Polymarket: 55% chance Hormuz traffic returns to normal by Jul 31; 53% chance of ≥1 Fed rate hike by year-end.\n- Energy stocks hammered: XLE back to pre-war levels; CRK -40%, NOG -35%, VG -35%, BTU -28%, PBF -25% from March highs.\n- Airlines rallied on lower fuel: **AAL** +3.4%, **CCL** +3.6%, **RCL** +3.8%.\n- Tanker stocks diverged from oil: **FRO** +3.5% 5D, **STNG** +0.7% — market pricing freight rates, not crude.\n\n**Fed Hawkish Pivot Under Warsh** `Macro` → new\n\nChair Kevin Warsh's first FOMC meeting held rates at 3.50%-3.75% unanimously but delivered a significantly hawkish shift in the dot plot and scrapped forward guidance.\n\n- Median year-end 2026 rate projection raised to 3.8% from 3.4% in March. 9 of 18 officials now expect ≥1 hike before year-end.\n- Warsh declined to submit his own dot, calling it "not helpful." Announced 5 task forces reviewing: communications, balance sheet, data sources, productivity/jobs in AI era, and inflation framework.\n- "This committee will deliver price stability" — inflation has been above 2% target for 63 consecutive months.\n- Citadel Securities warns "second-round effects" will force September hike; inertial Taylor Rule implies 75bp of hikes this year.\n- CME FedWatch: 72.2% chance rates unchanged in July; 63.3% chance of hike by September.\n- Dollar hit 13-month high. 10Y yield 4.45%, 2Y 4.17%.\n- Mohamed El-Erian called press conference a "masterclass in central bank communication"; Claudia Sahm criticized Warsh for refusing to participate in SEP exercise.\n- Markets sold off sharply Wednesday (S&P -1.21%, Nasdaq -1.34%) then rebounded Thursday (S&P +1.08%, Nasdaq +1.91%).\n\n**IT Services Rout on Accenture Guide-Down** `IT Services / Consulting` → new\n\n**ACN** -18.0% to 52-week low after narrowing FY26 revenue guidance to $71.8-72.5B from prior $71.8-73.2B, below consensus $74B. Q3 EPS $3.80 beat $3.69 est but revenue $18.7B missed $18.75B est.\n\n- Announced $4.18B in cybersecurity acquisitions (Dragos, runZero, NetRise).\n- Read-through crushed entire IT services cohort: **CTSH** -10.4%, **GLOB** -9.9%, **EPAM** -9.8%, **G** -8.7%.\n- **IBM** fell ~4% in sympathy; reports Q2 Jul 22 ⚠️.\n\n**AI Infrastructure & Data Center Power** `AI Infrastructure` → ongoing\n\n**BE** +13.6% (5D +29.3%) on tariff-reset framework cutting steel/aluminum derivative tariffs to 15%; Bernstein initiated Market Perform PT $276. Morningstar calls it "most overvalued" name in coverage (>300% above $70 FV estimate after ~1,300% surge).\n\n- **FCEL** +17.4% on continued data center power pipeline momentum; 4GW pipeline +267% QoQ.\n- **NBIS** joining Nasdaq-100 before market open Jun 22 ⚠️; completed Eigen AI acquisition. Cramer called inclusion a "big deal."\n- Amazon reportedly in talks to sell Trainium AI chips to third-party data centers (Bloomberg); AWS AI chief said compute costs getting "cheaper and cheaper."\n- Goldman Sachs warned AI hyperscalers' $770B 2026 capex = 100% of cash flows; depreciation rising from 7% to 12% of revenues by 2027, pressuring ROE.\n\n**SpaceX Post-IPO Volatility** `Space / AI` → ongoing\n\n**SPCX** -3.6% to $185 (still +37% from $135 IPO price); Bloomberg reported bankers preparing ≥$20B bond sale. Stock went from $135→$225→$174 in seven days.\n\n- Performance unlock trigger: if SPCX closes ≥$175.50 for 5 of 10 consecutive sessions, extra 10% of locked shares become eligible. Stock hovering just above that level.\n- Standard 180-day lockup expires ~Dec 8, 2026. Musk's personal lockup expires Jun 12, 2027.\n- First earnings report expected Sep 2 ⚠️.\n- Morningstar FV estimate $62; Polymarket gives 13% chance of $3T valuation this month.\n- Grantham called SpaceX prospectus a "novel slash joke"; warned Mag 7 in "dogfight" not safe monopolies.\n- Cathie Wood's ARK bought $22M in TSLA, dumped $99.6M in ROKU (Fox $22B acquisition).\n\n**Kroger Earnings Disappoint** `Retail / Consumer` → new\n\n**KR** Q1 adj. EPS $1.58 missed $1.59 est; revenue $46.1B beat $45.5B est. Stock fell ~10% pre-market.\n\n- ID sales ex-fuel +1.0%; e-commerce +19%; KPM media +20% growth.\n- Gross margin narrowed to 22.7% from 23.0% YoY on higher transport costs, egg deflation, pricing investments.\n- New CEO Greg Forin outlined "five Fs" strategy; acknowledged operating costs growing faster than sales is "not acceptable."\n- Reaffirmed FY26 guidance: ID sales ex-fuel +1-2%; adj. EPS $5.10-5.30 vs $5.27 est.\n- COGS savings 30% ahead of plan; e-commerce (incl. media) turned profitable this quarter.\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **MRNA** +3.5%: FDA advisory committee voted 9-0 for flu vaccine mRNA-1010 benefit-risk profile; PDUFA date Aug 5, 2026 ⚠️.\n- Kalshi reportedly passed $2B annualized revenue and is in early IPO talks (The Information). Kentucky sued Kalshi and Polymarket as "illegal sportsbooks," naming Coinbase and Robinhood as affiliates.\n- **QS** +12.1%: Honda signed joint research agreement on solid-state battery technology; multi-year development plan.\n- **BFLY** +52.6%: Midjourney Medical scanner prototype uses 40 Butterfly ultrasound-on-chip modules; co-development deal could generate $74M over 5 years. Musk called it "cool."\n- Anthropic's new Claude models beat human teams on robotics planning tasks in Project Fetch Phase 2; CEO Amodei urged G7 leaders against AI fragmentation.\n- Sam Bankman-Fried told fellow inmate he plans to launch a coin upon release (NY Mag profile). Polymarket prices pardon at ~14%.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **ACN** Q3 EPS $3.80 beat $3.69; FY rev guide cut to $71.8-72.5B vs $74B est, stock -18% to 52-week low. **KR** Q1 EPS $1.58 missed $1.59; gross margin narrowed 30bp. **SWBI** Q4 EPS $0.36 beat $0.23, rev $178.4M beat $155.3M. **MU** reports Jun 24 with consensus $19.74 EPS, $34.4B rev. |\n| Macro | Fed held 3.50-3.75%; median 2026 dot raised to 3.8% from 3.4%; Warsh scrapped forward guidance and declined to submit own dot. Citadel warns September hike. Initial claims 226K vs 225K est; Philly Fed mfg +10.3 vs -0.4 prior. |\n| Commodities | WTI -2.2% to ~$75 on signed U.S.-Iran MOU; national gas average below $4/gal first time since March. Gold -2.6% to $4,269; silver -6%. BofA cut 2026 Brent forecast to $82 from $93. |\n| Tech | Trump confirmed Apple-Intel chip manufacturing partnership. Apple CEO Cook warned memory price hikes "unavoidable," called it "100-year flood." Intel 18A-P entered risk production. Google Gemini co-lead Noam Shazeer left for OpenAI; Altman said it was "10 years in the making." |\n| Geopolitics | U.S.-Iran 14-point MOU signed at Versailles; 60-day window for final deal. VP Vance warned Israel against undermining agreement. Iran Supreme Leader issued written permission but said he "had different view." U.S.-Iran Switzerland talks postponed after Israel strikes on Lebanon. |\n| Markets | BofA FMS: 80% call "long global semis" most crowded trade ever. Net 40% of fund managers forecast rate hikes over 12 months (vs 16% in May). SPY +1.04%, QQQ +2.51% on Thursday after Wednesday's -1.21% selloff. U.S. markets closed Friday for Juneteenth. |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **MU earnings Jun 24**: Consensus EPS $19.74 (vs $1.91 YoY), revenue $34.4B (vs $9.3B YoY). Multiple analyst PTs raised to $1,200-$1,500 this week.\n- **MRVL and FLEX join S&P 500 before market open Jun 22**: Triggers mandatory passive fund buying from SPY, IVV, VOO.\n- **NBIS joins Nasdaq-100 before market open Jun 22**: Cramer called it a "big deal"; stock up 25% 5D.\n- **SPCX performance unlock watch**: If stock closes ≥$175.50 for 5 of 10 sessions at the trigger point, 10% additional shares unlock. Currently trading at ~$174-185. First earnings expected Sep 2.\n- **MRNA flu vaccine PDUFA date Aug 5**: VRBPAC voted 9-0 in favor; BLA submitted Dec 2025.\n- **Fed next meeting Jul 28-29**: CME FedWatch prices 72.2% chance of hold; Citadel base case is September hike.\n- **Juneteenth holiday Jun 19**: U.S. equity and bond markets closed Friday. Next trading day Monday Jun 22.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **Automated "industry comparison" articles** for AVGO, MSFT, TSLA, MU, NVDA: Boilerplate peer-comparison tables with no new data or analyst action — already priced context.\n- **MSTR -5.8%**: Bitcoin at $63K driving the move; STRC preferred at record low $85 is the real signal, covered in narrative threads. Daily BTC price noise is not actionable without a structural break below $59K.\n- **Micro-cap after-hours movers** (VSTD +26%, YYGH -38%, SAGT +82%, TNON +83%): All sub-$50M market cap with compliance/delisting issues, reverse splits, or penny-stock dynamics — noise for institutional portfolios.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 628959, "output_tokens": 4930, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 3.144795, "total_cost_usd": 3.268045, "output_cost_usd": 0.12325, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-06-19T13:46:07.376109+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-06-19T13:48:46.246962+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from published claude.com/api pricing (input, 5m cache write, cache read, output) — Anthropic does not return dollar amounts on the response.", "total_cost_usd": 3.268, "total_input_tokens": 628959, "total_output_tokens": 4930, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-06-19", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Channel: tech": 19, "Channel: movers": 34, "Channel: general": 98, "Channel: markets": 15, "Channel: earnings": 22, "Channel: equities": 25, "Channel: commodities": 8, "Ticker Group: r1d_screener": 59,