2026-07-08	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 July 8, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Trump declares the Iran ceasefire "over" after U.S. strikes on Iranian targets following Strait of Hormuz shipping attacks, sending Brent crude up 6% to $78.50 and lifting energy stocks (XOM, SHEL, OXY, CVX all +3–5%) while semiconductors extend their multi-day rout (MU -5.5%, MRVL -9.5%, AMAT -8.3%) and FCEL drops 18% on a dilutive $225M offering.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| XOM | +3.5% | Mega | Brent +6%; Q2 upstream boost ~$3.5-3.9B from higher liquids prices | Energy / Geopolitical |\n| SHEL | +4.9% | Mega | Raised Q2 Integrated Gas production & LNG guidance | Energy |\n| CVX | +3.9% | Mega | Brent +6%; Yasa Polaris tanker struck by drone off Black Sea | Energy / Geopolitical |\n| COP | +4.6% | Mega | Brent crude surge; Mizuho maintains Outperform, PT $146 | Energy |\n| GILD | +4.3% | Mega | Defensive rotation; Truist Buy PT $156, RBC PT $120 | Biopharma / Defensive |\n| IBM | +2.9% | Mega | Power Inflow signal; z17 & LinuxONE 5 rack-mount launch; BofA PT $330 ⚠️ | Enterprise IT |\n| MU | -7.6% | Mega | Samsung sell-the-news; sector-wide semi rout; SK Hynix $28B listing imminent | Memory / Semis |\n| AMD | -7.7% | Mega | Broad semi selloff; Ark sold $4.5M; Goldman PT $640 ⚠️ | AI Compute |\n| MRVL | -9.5% | Mega | Semi selloff; RBC maintains Outperform PT $360 ⚠️ | AI Networking |\n| AMAT | -8.3% | Mega | Semi equipment selloff; Susquehanna PT $900 ⚠️ | Semi Equipment |\n| SNDK | -8.2% | Mega | Samsung sell-the-news; memory profit-taking | Memory |\n| KLAC | -8.8% | Mega | Semi equipment selloff | Semi Equipment |\n| PANW | -3.7% | Mega | Broad tech weakness; Needham raised PT to $425 | Cybersecurity |\n| NET | +8.7% | Large | Scotiabank upgrade to Outperform, PT $225→$300; OpenAI research pilot | Cloud / Edge |\n| OXY | +5.6% | Large | Evercore upgrade to Outperform, PT $58→$65; crude surge | Energy |\n| ALAB | -12.7% | Large | Chairman sold $79.7M stock via 10b5-1 plan; semi selloff | AI Connectivity |\n| BABA | +9.2% PM | Large | China may restrict AI model exports; positive Q2 analyst update | China Tech / AI |\n| FCEL | -11.2% | Mid | Priced upsized $225M offering at $21/share (vs. $25.96 close) | Clean Energy |\n| RIVN | -4.4% PM | Mid | Priced 75M share offering at $15.50 (~23% discount to Mon close) | EV |\n| PENG | +3.6% AH | Mid | Q3 EPS $0.84 vs $0.54 est; rev $479M vs $406M est; raised FY guide ⚠️ | AI Infrastructure / Memory |\n| SVC | +395.4% | Small | Halted/resumed; no identifiable catalyst in data | Idiosyncratic |\n| KRUS | -12.3% PM | Mid | Q3 sales $85.9M missed $86.5M est; cut FY sales guide to $330.5-331.5M | Restaurant |\n| HELE | +6.0% PM | Mid | Q1 EPS $0.17 vs $(0.01) est; sales $402M vs $375M est | Consumer |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Iran Ceasefire Collapse Lifts Crude, Pressures Equities** `Energy / Macro` → new\n\nTrump declared the U.S.-Iran MOU "over" at the NATO summit in Ankara after CENTCOM launched strikes following Iranian attacks on three commercial vessels in the Strait of Hormuz. Iran retaliated against Kuwait and Bahrain. The Treasury revoked General License X permitting Iranian oil sales. Brent crude surged 6% to $78.50/bbl; WTI +6% to ~$74.73.\n\n- **XOM** guided Q2 upstream earnings $3.5–3.9B higher QoQ from liquids prices; chemical margins to add $1.0–1.2B; war disruptions to drag upstream by $(0.8)–$(0.6)B. Earnings July 31 ⚠️\n- **SHEL** raised Q2 Integrated Gas production guide to 610–650K boe/d (from 580–640K); LNG liquefaction to 7.4–7.8Mt (from 6.8–7.4Mt); refinery utilization ~100%. Earnings July 30 ⚠️\n- **CVX** +3.9%; Wolfe Research upgraded to Outperform PT $210 on July 2; Chevron-chartered tanker Yasa Polaris struck by drone off Black Sea coast. Earnings July 31 ⚠️\n- **OXY** +5.6%; Evercore ISI upgraded Underperform→Outperform, PT $58→$65\n- **COP** +4.6%; Mizuho maintains Outperform, PT lowered to $146\n- **EQNR** +6.3%, **DVN** +5.6%, **BP** +3.3%, **ENB** +3.1%, **TRGP** +5.2%, **OKE** +4.7% — broad energy complex rally\n- Economist Justin Wolfers: "Trouble in Iran = Turmoil in global energy markets = Expect higher gas prices"\n- S&P 500 futures -0.96%, Nasdaq futures -1.35%, Russell 2000 futures -1.47%; Bitcoin fell to $62,000; Dollar Index rose\n- 10-yr Treasury yield 4.56%; FedWatch: 72.7% probability of July hold\n- FOMC minutes from Warsh's first meeting as Chair releasing at 2:00 PM ET today\n\n**Semiconductor Rout Deepens — Samsung Sell-the-News, DeepSeek Chip, SK Hynix $28B Listing** `Memory / Semi Equipment` → ongoing\n\nThe multi-day semiconductor selloff extended after Samsung's record Q2 preliminary operating profit of 89.4T won ($58.4B) triggered a 7% drop in Seoul as results met, but did not exceed, whisper numbers. DeepSeek reportedly developing its own AI inference chip. SK Hynix's $28B Nasdaq ADR listing priced with demand multiples above shares available; cornerstone investors indicated ~$7B combined interest.\n\n- **MU** -7.6% (5D: -20.7%); Q2 est EPS $31.24 on rev $50.72B; Cantor PT $2,000, Barclays PT $2,000; Michael Burry disclosed short position calling MU a "destroyer of capital"; Ross Gerber called the short "a joke"\n- **SNDK** -8.2% (5D: -29.2%); BofA raised PT to $2,500, Bernstein PT $3,000\n- **MRVL** -9.5% (5D: -22.9%); RBC maintains Outperform PT $360; earnings Aug. 27 ⚠️\n- **AMAT** -8.3% (5D: -25.8%); Susquehanna PT $900; earnings Aug. 13 ⚠️\n- **KLAC** -8.8% (5D: -29.5%)\n- **AMD** -7.7% (5D: -12.1%); Goldman PT raised to $640, Wells Fargo PT $615, Cantor PT $700; Ark sold $4.5M of AMD on Tuesday; earnings Aug. 4 ⚠️\n- **ALAB** -12.7%; Chairman Manuel Alba sold $79.7M in stock via 10b5-1 plan on July 1\n- **UMC** -8.7% (5D: -12.3%)\n- **INTC** down 2.3% PM after falling 9.66% Tuesday; earnings July 23 ⚠️; Cantor PT $150, Goldman PT $150, BofA PT $160\n- Samsung forward P/E at ~5x vs. long-run average ~14x\n- VanEck Semiconductor ETF (SMH) fell >3% Tuesday\n- Goldman Sachs GSAM warns Russell 2000's AI infrastructure exposure halved to 7% after rebalance\n\n**Cloudflare Breakout on Upgrade & OpenAI Partnership** `Cloud / Edge / AI` → new\n\n**NET** +8.7% on 1.7× volume after Scotiabank upgraded from Sector Perform to Sector Outperform with PT raised $225→$300, citing traction with AI-native enterprise customers. Separately, NET and OpenAI announced a research pilot combining Cloudflare's network signals with OpenAI's search capabilities to improve AI indexing of web content.\n\n- Q2 earnings est: EPS $0.21, revenue $666.17M; report ~July 30 ⚠️\n- 52-week high zone $276.82; stock trading 13.8% above 20-day SMA\n- Citizens maintains Market Outperform PT $270; Truist Buy PT $250\n\n**Penguin Solutions — AI Factory Platform Beats & Raises** `AI Infrastructure / Memory` → new\n\n**PENG** +3.6% after-hours on record Q3 results driven by integrated memory and non-hyperscale AI infrastructure.\n\n- Q3 EPS $0.84 vs $0.54 est (+79% YoY); revenue $478.71M vs $405.53M est (+48% YoY)\n- Integrated memory revenue +111% YoY; AI-driven businesses = 74% of total sales, growing 104% YoY\n- Raised FY26 EPS guide to $2.55–$2.65 (from $2.30); revenue guide to $1.64–$1.69B (from $1.60B)\n- Preliminary FY27 view: ~30% total company sales growth and ~30% EPS growth\n- Needham raised PT from $60 to $80, Buy\n- CFO Nate Olmstead stepping down July 8; Aaron Johnson named interim CFO\n\n**FuelCell Energy Dilution** `Clean Energy` → new\n\n**FCEL** -11.2% (pre-market -18%) after pricing an upsized $225M offering of 10.71M shares at $21.00 — a steep discount to Tuesday's $25.96 close. Proceeds earmarked for manufacturing capacity expansion.\n\n- Stock up 372% over past 12 months prior to this offering\n- 5D decline of -29.1%; still trades above 50-day SMA of $19.97\n\n**Rivian Offering Pressures EV Name** `EV` → ongoing\n\n**RIVN** priced 75M share offering at $15.50/share (~23% below Monday's $20.14 close), expecting ~$1.16B gross proceeds. Greenshoe could add $175M.\n\n- Q2 deliveries 12,194 (beat 9K–11K guide); raised FY26 delivery forecast to 65K–70K (from 62K–67K)\n- Q2 revenue estimate $1.55–1.65B; cash/investments ~$5.3B as of June 30\n- Proceeds for DOE-linked equity contributions and general corporate purposes\n\n**Alibaba Surges on AI Export Curb Reports & Earnings Optimism** `China Tech / AI` → new\n\n**BABA** +9.2% pre-market. Reuters reported China is discussing restricting overseas access to its most advanced AI models, including those from Alibaba, ByteDance, and Z.ai. Separately, Jefferies noted positive Q2 business update with narrowing instant-commerce losses. Alibaba also banned employees from using Anthropic's Claude effective July 10.\n\n- Court win: U.S. judge temporarily blocked Pentagon from treating BABA as military-linked company\n- Earnings est Aug. 28: EPS $2.51 vs $2.06 YoY; revenue $38.72B vs $34.57B ⚠️\n\n**IBM Technical Breakout & Product Launches** `Enterprise IT` → ongoing\n\n**IBM** +2.9% (5D: +9.5%); triggered Power Inflow signal at $302.19, rallied to $311.80 intraday. Launched z17 and LinuxONE 5 rack-mount configurations (first rack-mount offering), GA Aug. 12.\n\n- BofA maintained Buy, PT $330; JPMorgan upgraded to Overweight PT $291; Morgan Stanley Equal-Weight PT $267\n- Earnings July 22: EPS est $3.02 vs $2.80 YoY; revenue $17.86B ⚠️\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- SpaceX filed FCC application for 100,000 Gen3 Starlink satellites; doubled Starlink Aviation plan prices (Global Unlimited: $10K→$20K/mo); equipment price raised to $200K from $145K. Morgan Stanley bull case $600/share.\n- DeepSeek reportedly developing its own AI inference chip per Reuters — could reduce reliance on Nvidia GPU infrastructure if successful.\n- Meta building cloud infrastructure business to sell excess AI compute per Bloomberg — potential competitive threat to neocloud providers (WULF, IREN, CIFR).\n- Goldman Sachs Asset Management warns small-cap "easy money" era is over; Russell 2000 AI infrastructure exposure cut from 15% to 7% after rebalance; interest expense at 31% of EBITDA for R2000 companies.\n- Wolfspeed filed patent infringement suit against Navitas Semiconductor (NVTS -7% PM) covering five patents across GaN and SiC product lines.\n- Sunrun (RUN) launched distributed AI compute pilot program, placing compute nodes in homes with solar+battery systems; first step into edge computing as new revenue stream.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Macro | Trump declared Iran ceasefire "over" at NATO summit; CENTCOM struck 60+ Iranian Revolutionary Guard boats; Iran retaliated against Kuwait and Bahrain; Brent crude +6% to $78.50 |\n| FOMC | Minutes from Warsh's first meeting as Fed Chair release today at 2:00 PM ET; FedWatch shows 72.7% probability of July hold |\n| Earnings | PENG Q3 EPS $0.84 vs $0.54 est, rev $479M vs $406M est; HELE Q1 EPS $0.17 vs $(0.01) est; KRUS Q3 missed sales est, cut FY guide; LEVI reports after close today (est EPS $0.24, rev $1.52B) |\n| Offerings | FCEL priced $225M offering at $21.00/share; RIVN priced 75M shares at $15.50/share |\n| Tech | China discussing restricting overseas access to advanced AI models from Alibaba, ByteDance; Cloudflare + OpenAI research pilot for AI content discovery |\n| Semis | Samsung Q2 prelim OP 89.4T won (+1,810% YoY) sparked 7% selloff; SK Hynix $28B ADR listing demand exceeds shares available; DeepSeek developing own AI chip |\n| Analyst | Evercore upgraded OXY to Outperform PT $65; Scotiabank upgraded NET PT $300; Barclays initiated MA Overweight PT $640, PYPL Underweight PT $42, AFRM Overweight PT $97, XYZ (Block) Overweight PT $100 |\n| Commodities | WTI crude +6% to $74.73; Gold -0.84% to $4,071; Dollar Index +0.05% |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **FOMC minutes** release today July 8 at 2:00 PM ET — first under Chair Warsh; markets will parse hawkish/dovish signals on rate path\n- **SK Hynix Nasdaq ADR listing** expected to price this week (~$28B); institutional demand reportedly multiples above shares available; could redirect capital away from MU, SNDK\n- **JPM earnings** July 14 before the bell — EPS est $5.61 vs $4.96 YoY; UBS PT $384, BofA PT $408\n- **INTC earnings** July 23 — EPS est $0.19 vs $(0.10) YoY; stock -9.66% Tuesday, -2.3% PM Wednesday\n- **IBM earnings** July 22 — EPS est $3.02 vs $2.80 YoY\n- **AAL earnings** July 23 — EPS est $0.04; Melius downgraded to Hold, Susquehanna raised PT to $25\n- **UAL earnings** July 15 — EPS est $1.82 vs $3.87 YoY; Morgan Stanley PT $185\n- **LEVI reports** after close today — EPS est $0.24, revenue $1.52B\n- **NET earnings** ~July 30 — EPS est $0.21, revenue $666M\n- **AMD earnings** Aug. 4 — EPS est $1.55 vs $0.48 YoY ⚠️\n- **SpaceX lockup**: if stock closes above $175.50 on 5 of 10 trading days before earnings (~Aug. 5), an additional 456M shares unlock Aug. 7\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **SVC** +395%: trading halt/resume with no identifiable fundamental catalyst in news flow; likely corporate action or technical event\n- **ALIT** +12%: continuation of multi-day move with no new catalyst identified today; 3,306% 5D move suggests prior corporate event already priced\n- Micro-cap pre-market movers (CPOP -40%, EDHL -18%, IOTR +37%) — illiquid names with negligible market caps and no institutional relevance	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 274498, "output_tokens": 4743, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 1.37249, "total_cost_usd": 1.491065, "output_cost_usd": 0.118575, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-07-08T12:43:56.666895+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-07-08T12:46:07.982154+00:00", "current_step": nul