2026-07-11	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-07-11 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: **META** +6.2% on Muse AI launch / leaked 14GW compute expansion memo / analyst reaffirmations, **VOD** +12.4% on e&'s $5.95B stake sale to Niel family, **SK Hynix (SKHYV)** debuts at $149 raising $26.5B in record foreign IPO, while US-Iran ceasefire collapse and Saturday Hormuz deadline dominate macro risk heading into Tuesday's CPI and bank earnings.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **META** | +6.2% | Mega | Muse Spark 1.1 launch; leaked memo: 14GW compute by 2027; Iris chip Sept production | AI Compute / Advertising |\n| **TMUS** | +3.2% | Mega | No identified catalyst | Telecom |\n| **NVDA** | +3.0% | Mega | Falling-wedge breakout; Q2 rev est $91.7B; fwd P/E 23.5x | AI Compute |\n| **AMAT** | +2.3% | Mega | CEO cites "tremendous visibility" 24mo; Needham PT $740, TD Cowen PT $700, Stifel PT $650 | Semicap Equipment |\n| **AMD** | +2.0% | Mega | ARK says chips "more performant per dollar" than NVDA; Stifel PT raised to $635 | AI Compute |\n| **VOD** | **+12.4%** | Large | e& sells entire 16.2% stake (~$5.95B) to Niel family vehicle at 112.5p/sh | Telecom |\n| **KB** | +7.0% | Large | Korean bank rally alongside SK Hynix US listing momentum | Financials / Korea |\n| **CBRS** | +6.5% | Large | 200MW European AI data center expansion by end-2027; OpenAI >$20B deal | AI Compute |\n| **NKE** | +4.2% | Large | No identified catalyst | Consumer |\n| **CCI** | +4.1% | Large | No identified catalyst | REITs / Towers |\n| **SKHYV** | +13% day-1 | Large | $26.5B ADR IPO at $149; 7× oversubscribed; largest foreign US listing ever | Memory / AI Compute |\n| **PLBL** | **+30.3%** | Small | Volatile bounce after -21% 5D; no identified fundamental catalyst | Idiosyncratic |\n| **RXT** | **+21.8%** | Small | Bounce after -29% Thurs on FY26 rev guide cut to $2.45–2.55B; Palantir partnership | Cloud / AI |\n| **EQPT** | **+16.5%** | Small | Raised FY26 rev guide to $5.25–5.68B; $500M buyback authorized | Equipment Rental |\n| **WDFC** | **+10.4%** | Small | Q3 EPS $2.33 vs $1.56 est; rev $195.1M vs $172.8M est; FY guide raised | Consumer Staples |\n| **CCC** | **+10.2%** | Small | Reuters: exploring sale; Morgan Stanley advising; PE firms interested | InsurTech / SaaS |\n| **CDZI** | +9.4% | Small | BLM right-of-way grant for Northern Pipeline gas-to-water conversion | Water Infrastructure |\n| **DAL** | -0.4% | Large | Q2 adj EPS $1.56 beat $1.47; rev $19.76B beat $17.53B; fuel cost +77% YoY ⚠️ | Airlines |\n| **PEP** | -0.6% | Mega | Q2 core EPS $2.20 missed $2.21; cited high gas prices hurting c-store traffic | Consumer Staples |\n| **IONS** | -9.0% | Large | CARDIO-TTRansform Ph3 missed primary endpoint in ATTR-CM | Biotech |\n| **CRWD** | -5.6% | Large | Profit-taking after post-split rally; no fundamental catalyst | Cybersecurity |\n| **OKTA** | -7.0% | Large | Continued selling pressure; elevated TI65 score | Identity / SaaS |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**SK Hynix US Debut & Memory Liquidity Rotation** `Memory / AI Compute` → new\n\n**SK Hynix (SKHYV)** jumped ~13% on its first trading day after pricing 177.9M ADRs at $149, raising $26.5B — the largest US share sale by a foreign company ever, surpassing Alibaba's 2014 IPO. The offering was 7× oversubscribed with indications from Baillie Gifford, Coatue, and Situational Awareness Partners for up to $7B.\n\n- SK Hynix CEO expects memory shortage to last into next decade (Bloomberg)\n- Forward P/E ~5.4× vs **MU** at ~6.7×; SK Hynix holds ~56.4% global HBM market share\n- **MU** -1.0% Fri after +4.5% Thurs; increased US investment commitment to >$250B through 2035; first concrete poured at NY DRAM megafab ahead of schedule\n- Commerce Sec. Lutnick told Samsung and SK Hynix they have "no choice" but to build US AI memory fabs\n- **SNDK** +1.1%, **STX** +1.6%, **WDC** +0.6% — all gapped up July 9 on semi rebound\n- Wells Fargo upgraded **STX** to Overweight, raised PT to $1,100 from $900\n- Wells Fargo raised **WDC** PT to $730 from $575\n- Semiconductor ETFs drew record $7.1B inflows on Tuesday; SOXX alone took in $5.4B (largest single-day since 2001 launch)\n- JPMorgan names **INTC** a top short despite +372% 12mo gain, citing foundry revenue still minimal\n- Liquidity concern: Firstrade's Callahan warns SK Hynix IPO may drain capital from existing AI/semi holdings\n- Next catalyst: **TSMC** earnings July 16 ⚠️; **LRCX** earnings July 29 ⚠️; **MU** not yet scheduled\n\n---\n\n**Meta's AI Infrastructure & Cloud Ambitions** `AI Compute / Advertising` → ongoing\n\n**META** +6.2% on 2.1× avg volume — the session's dominant mega-cap mover — driven by multiple catalysts converging.\n\n- Zuckerberg returned to X for first time since 2023 to announce **Muse Spark 1.1** (agentic/coding model) via new Meta Model API; priced at $1.25/$4.25 per M tokens — 4–7× cheaper than OpenAI/Anthropic equivalents\n- Citizens analyst Boone: API revenue could reach ~$2B annualized even at 5% share of comparable market; cut PT to $800 from $825 on expected capex raise\n- Leaked internal memo (Reuters): Meta to manufacture custom AI chip "Iris" (Broadcom/TSMC) in September; plans to expand compute to 7GW this year, 14GW in 2027\n- Locked in long-term supply: NAND from SanDisk, DRAM from Samsung, fiber optics from Sumitomo\n- Piper Sandler reiterated Overweight/$800 PT — META remains firm's top large-cap pick\n- **Muse Image** AI feature pulled after privacy backlash; SAG-AFTRA criticized default opt-in of public Instagram photos\n- EU preliminary finding: Instagram/Facebook breach DSA via "addictive design"; potential fine up to 6% global revenue (~$12B)\n- Tencent reportedly leads deal to unwind Meta's $2B Manus acquisition (FT)\n- Zuckerberg said exploring AI cloud business "makes sense" (Bloomberg)\n- Bill Ackman's Pershing Square META position (~2.66M shares) now up ~$20M YTD after starting at ~$1.76B\n- Next catalyst: Q2 earnings late July (not yet confirmed) ⚠️\n\n---\n\n**US-Iran Escalation & Hormuz Shipping** `Macro / Geopolitics` → ongoing\n\nThe ceasefire is functionally dead. The US has given Iran a Saturday deadline to publicly commit to stopping Hormuz attacks.\n\n- Iran's Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei vowed retaliation "must certainly" be carried out for his father's killing\n- Trump: "1,000 missiles are Locked and Loaded" aimed at Iran; Treasury sanctioned Iranian financial facilitator and exchange houses\n- Iran FM Araghchi accused US of violating MOU Para 9; rejected restarting talks without prior US compliance\n- US Central Command struck ~90 Iranian military targets Wednesday after Tehran attacked 3 commercial vessels\n- Only 6 vessels crossed Hormuz Friday–Saturday overnight (Windward data) vs normalized 18–22; dark transits at ~40% of traffic\n- IMO Council rejected Iran's sovereignty claims over Hormuz; urged 176 member states not to recognize\n- IEA: global oil demand recovery "underway" from 97.9M bpd May low; expects >8M bpd rebound by October; crude settled ~$71/bbl, +4% weekly\n- IMF: global growth at 3% in 2026 (better than April's 2.7% forecast); expects V-shaped recovery; Hormuz reopening assumed by mid-July with normalization by March 2027\n- US senators reached agreement with Trump on Russia sanctions bill (Reuters)\n- Next catalyst: Saturday Hormuz deadline; US CPI Tuesday July 15 (est -0.1% MoM, 4.0% YoY) ⚠️\n\n---\n\n**Earnings Season Kickoff** `Earnings` → new\n\nQ2 reporting begins in earnest next week with major banks on Tuesday.\n\n- **DAL** reported Friday: adj EPS $1.56 vs $1.47 est; rev $19.76B vs $17.53B est (+19% YoY); adj fuel expense +77% to $4.41B ($3.93/gal); Q3 guide adj EPS $2.00–2.50 vs $1.99 est; FY adj EPS guide $6.50–7.50 vs $5.93 est; 15% dividend increase\n- **PEP** Q2: rev $24.18B beat $23.96B est (+6.4% YoY); core EPS $2.20 missed $2.21; cited high gas prices hurting c-store traffic; reaffirmed FY organic rev growth 2–4%; Citi downgraded to Neutral, cut PT to $145\n- **WDFC** Q3: EPS $2.33 vs $1.56 est; rev $195.1M vs $172.8M est (+24% YoY); gross margin expanded 140bps to 56.6%; raised FY rev guide to $675–690M; $100M buyback authorized; DA Davidson raised PT to $305\n- FactSet: S&P 500 Q2 earnings growth expected at 23.6% — would mark second consecutive quarter of 20%+ growth\n- **JPM, BAC, GS, C, WFC** report Tuesday July 15 ⚠️; **MS, BK, PNC** report Wednesday July 16 ⚠️\n- **TSMC** earnings July 16; est EPS $3.77, rev $39.76B ⚠️\n\n---\n\n**Semicap Equipment Upgrades** `Semicap Equipment` → ongoing\n\nMultiple analyst upgrades across wafer fab equipment names reflect rising confidence in 24-month demand visibility.\n\n- **AMAT** +2.3%: CEO Dickerson told Nikkei Asia he has "tremendous visibility" into demand over next 24 months; Needham raised PT to $740, TD Cowen to $700, Stifel to $650, Mizuho to $650; earnings Aug 13 est EPS $3.38, rev $9B ⚠️\n- **LRCX** +0.4%: Mizuho and TD Cowen both raised PTs to $400; earnings July 29 ⚠️\n- **ICHR** +3.1%: Stifel and TD Cowen both raised PTs to $115\n\n---\n\n**Apple vs OpenAI Legal Fight** `AI / Legal` → new\n\n**AAPL** filed trade-secret lawsuit against OpenAI in Northern District of California, alleging systematic extraction of hardware secrets.\n\n- Complaint names OpenAI Chief Hardware Officer Tang Tan (former Apple VP) and engineer Chang Liu\n- Alleges OpenAI instructed interview candidates to bring Apple prototypes; asked suppliers Apple-specific manufacturing questions\n- Apple's next Siri upgrade to use Google Gemini instead of ChatGPT\n- OpenAI Applications Chief Fidji Simo stepped down from full-time role due to chronic illness; transitioning to part-time advisor\n- Futurum CEO Daniel Newman: "OpenAI burning it down with one Mag 7 after another. First $MSFT and now $AAPL"\n- Separately: NYT-led publishers seek court sanctions against OpenAI over alleged evidence concealment in copyright case\n\n---\n\n**Private Credit Stress** `Private Credit` → ongoing\n\nBlue Owl (OWL) faced $4.7B in Q2 redemption requests after UBS flagged potential 15% default rates in private credit.\n\n- Blue Owl's largest fund: $3.6B requests (19% of AUM); tech-oriented fund: $1.1B (38% of AUM)\n- Apollo also limited withdrawals; Goldman Sachs bucked trend with only 3.24% redemption requests honored in full\n- Aberdeen: private markets entering "more selective phase"; manager quality and asset selection now paramount\n\n---\n\n**Commerce Department Eases UAE Export Controls** `Chip Export Policy` → new\n\n- Unpublished 17-page rule (effective July 14) grants license exceptions for advanced computing equipment to UAE's G42/Core42 and MGX\n- AAPL, AMZN, GOOGL, META, MSFT, ORCL, xAI get streamlined treatment for controlled equipment in UAE data center projects\n- Sen. Warren called deal "corrupt," citing Trump's reported $263M gain tied to MGX's USD1 stablecoin-funded $2B Binance investment\n\n---\n\n**Fed Chair Warsh AI Task Force** `Macro / AI Policy` → new\n\n- Fed unveiled five external task forces; AI panel led by Marc Andreessen, Stanford's Charles I. Jones, Xbox CEO Asha Sharma\n- Warsh has argued AI could support lower rates by boosting productivity\n- Morgan Stanley: AI could keep rates above post-2009 levels if technology boosts productivity without mass job losses\n- Former Fed Chair Bernanke joined Anthropic's long-term benefit trust as AI oversight body member\n\n---\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **CCC** +10.2%: Reuters reports CCC Intelligent Solutions exploring sale; Morgan Stanley advising; PE firms including unnamed parties circling; market cap ~$3.5B\n- **CRCL** received final OCC approval for Circle National Trust (national trust bank); ARK bought $13.7M CRCL the day before announcement; Goldman Sachs maintains Neutral/$96 PT\n- **QGEN** drew early takeover interest from EQT, Advent, KKR per Bloomberg; potential offers at ≥$50/share; strategic review ongoing with Moelis/Goldman advising\n- **RIVN** +3%: plans 75M share offering (~$1.74B); raised FY delivery guide to 65–70K vehicles on strong R2 demand; BNP Paribas PT raised to $24; earnings July 30 ⚠️\n- Bitcoin $64,150 (+11% from YTD low); spot ETFs saw $95.3M outflows Thursday; Strategy (MSTR) sold $200M+ BTC last week; Standard Chartered maintains $100K year-end target\n- Tech stock VXN/VIX ratio hit 1.7 — highest in 23 years — signaling extreme tech-specific volatility vs. broader market\n- China may allow Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek to purchase some Nvidia H200 chips (The Information)\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **DAL** Q2 adj EPS $1.56 beat $1.47; rev $19.76B beat $17.53B; fuel cost $3.93/gal (+75% YoY); FY adj EPS guide $6.50–7.50 |\n| Macro | US gives Iran Saturday deadline on Hormuz; only 6 vessels crossed overnight; CPI Tuesday est -0.1% MoM / 4.0% YoY |\n| Tech | Meta leaked memo: Iris chip production Sept; 14GW compute by 2027; Apple sues OpenAI over trade secrets |\n| Memory | SK Hynix $26.5B IPO at $149 (7× oversubscribed); CEO expects memory shortage into next decade |\n| Geopolitics | Iran's Khamenei vows retaliation; Trump warns 1,000 missiles "locked and loaded"; IMO rejects Iran Hormuz sovereignty |\n| Policy | Commerce Dept eases UAE chip export controls effective July 14; Fed creates AI task force led by Andreessen |\n| Energy | IEA: oil demand rebounding from 97.9M bpd May low; crude ~$71/bbl (+4% weekly) |\n| Crypto | Circle receives final OCC approval for national trust bank; Bitcoin spot ETFs -$95.3M Thursday |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **Tuesday July 15**: US June CPI (est -0.1% MoM, 4.0% YoY); **JPM, BAC, GS, C, WFC** Q2 earnings before the bell ⚠️\n- **Wednesday July 16**: **TSMC** Q2 earnings (est EPS $3.77, rev $39.76B); **MS, BK, PNC** earnings ⚠️\n- **Saturday July 12**: US deadline for Iran to publicly commit to Hormuz passage; Iran FM Araghchi meeting Omani FM in Muscat\n- **Sunday July 13**: **Q32 Bio (QTTB)** 36-week topline results from SIGNAL-AA Phase 2a bempikibart trial at 8am ET ⚠️\n- **July 22**: **T** (AT&T) Q2 earnings (est EPS $0.59, rev $31.83B); EU extended decision on Paramount/WBD $110B merger due ⚠️\n- **July 23**: **INTC** Q2 earnings (est EPS $0.19, rev $14.40B); **RTX** Q2 earnings (est EPS $1.66, rev $22.87B); **NOK** Q2 ⚠️\n- **July 29**: **ARM** Q1 FY2027 earnings (est EPS $0.36, rev $1.27B); **LRCX** Q4 earnings ⚠️\n- **CLARITY Act**: Senate returns July 13; merged draft may reach floor week of July 20; Polymarket odds at ~40% (down from 74% in May)\n- **SKHYV**: Leveraged ETFs from Direxion, Corgi Funds launching within days of listing\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **PLBL** +30.3%: Violent bounce in illiquid small-cap after -21% 5D drawdown; no identifiable catalyst — noise in a volatile name\n- Elon Musk net worth headlines ($913B, down from $1.32T peak): no tradeable information; SpaceX post-IPO drift is already priced\n- After-hours micro-cap movers (SOBR winding down operations, GMM +174%, HAO +66%): sub-$100M market caps with no institutional relevance	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 430590, "output_tokens": 5078, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 2.15295, "total_cost_usd": 2.2799, "output_cost_usd": 0.12695, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-07-11T21:27:48.159049+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-07-11T21:30:17.320352+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from published claude.com/api pricing (input, 5m cache write, cache read, output) — Anthropic does not return dollar amounts on the response.", "total_cost_usd": 2.2799, "total_input_tokens": 43