adj EPS $2.55 vs $2.28 est; FY raised to $11.50-12.50 | Nuclear Power |\n| SOUN | +26% PM | Mid | Q2 rev $61.9M vs $52.4M est; FY guide raised; 42.35% short float | AI Voice |\n| BLMN | +33.5% | Mid | Q2 adj EPS $0.39 vs $0.29 est; FY EPS guide raised | Restaurants |\n| GTE | +37.5% | Small | Sells Colombia/Ecuador assets for $1.33B to Maurel & Prom | E&P / Asset Sale |\n| APPS | +36.3% | Small | FQ1 rev $166M vs $150M est; FY27 rev guide raised to $650-670M | Mobile Ad Tech |\n| MTRN | +33.0% | Mid | Q2 EPS $1.90 vs $1.51 est; FY guide raised to $6.80-7.20 | Materials / Specialty |\n| FLNC | -16% PM | Mid | FQ3 adj loss $0.24 vs -$0.02 est; FY rev cut to $2.9-3.1B | Energy Storage |\n| PAYC | +14% PM | Mid | Q2 EPS $2.78 vs $2.38 est; FY sales raised to $2.197-2.212B | HCM SaaS |\n| PRGO | +24.9% | Small | Q2 adj EPS $0.50 vs $0.34 est; FY guide affirmed above est | OTC Pharma |\n| KTOS | +7.4% | Mid | Q2 rev $458.8M vs $410.4M est; FY rev raised; Piper upgrades to OW ⚠️ | Defense |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Memory & Storage Sell-Off Despite Beats** `AI Memory / Storage` → ongoing\n\n**WDC**, **SNDK**, and **MU** are all selling off pre-market despite beats, dragging the memory complex and pressuring Nasdaq futures (-0.4%). The market is questioning margin durability as AI shifts from training to inference. **SK Hynix** (SKHY) fell 10.4% in Seoul.\n\n- **WDC** Q4 adj EPS $3.56 beat $3.29 est; rev $3.75B beat $3.69B est (+44% YoY); FQ1 guide $4.0-4.2B rev, EPS $3.85-4.15 vs $3.81 est — PM down ~15%\n- **SNDK** FQ4 adj EPS $39.25 beat $34.45; rev $8.97B beat $8.39B; adj gross margin ~85%; board approved $14B buyback expansion — PM down ~10%\n- **SNDK** CEO Goeckeler: 8 multi-year new business models in place, weighted avg duration >4 years; visibility shifted from 3 months to >4 years\n- **WDC** CEO Tan: AI customers already negotiating storage deals through 2031\n- **MU** PM down ~3.6%; next earnings ~Sept 22; KeyBanc PT $1,750; Cantor PT $2,000\n- Susquehanna analyst Hosseini: key question is whether memory makers can sustain ~80% gross margins\n- Michael Burry holds shorts on MU, NVDA, SOXX; warns of "future ghost towns" and possible "1987-type fall"\n\n---\n\n**Shopify & E-Commerce AI Adoption** `E-Commerce / AI` → ongoing\n\n**SHOP** +18.7% on Q2 results that showed AI-driven orders tripling YoY and new AI buyers arriving at nearly 2x the rate of other channels. The stock's 5D +13.3% rally extends a broader e-commerce rebound.\n\n- Q2 rev $3.58B (+34.3% YoY) beat $3.45B est; adj EPS $0.42 beat $0.40; GMV $115.57B (+32%)\n- Q3 guide: low-30% rev growth, implying ~$3.73-3.78B vs $3.59B est — 6th consecutive quarter >30% growth\n- FCF margin 18%, up 200bps YoY; operating expenses up only 21% vs fears of higher AI spending\n- Goldman Sachs raises PT from $170 to $194 (Buy); Citizens raises PT from $150 to $185\n- President Finkelstein: "Shopify is probably the most AI-pilled company in the world"\n- Cathie Wood's ARK sold 89,033 SHOP shares Wednesday\n\n---\n\n**Gold Miners Breakout on $4,200+ Gold** `Precious Metals` → new\n\nGold's biggest one-day rally since February (+4% to $4,234) is lifting the entire mining complex. ADP private payrolls at 44K (vs 70K est) — weakest in 6 months — reduced Fed hike probability.\n\n- **NEM** +6.9%, **AEM** +9.9%, **KGC** +9.0%, **GFI** +10.2%, **AU** +8.5%, **PAAS** +7.6%, **WPM** +6.7%\n- GDX (VanEck Gold Miners ETF) +7.2% Wednesday — clean technical breakout above 50-day MA\n- CME FedWatch: September hike probability fell to ~55% from ~59%\n- Gold spot $4,267/oz in early Thursday trade, up another 0.5%\n- Silver $61.85/oz (+3.9% Wed); copper hit new all-time high in NY at $6.718/lb on COMEX\n- First Majestic Silver hoarding finished inventory (1M oz silver, 4,730 oz gold) — echoes Goldcorp's McEwen strategy from early 2000s\n\n---\n\n**AI Networking & Compute — Post-Earnings Digestion** `AI Networking` → ongoing\n\n**ANET** +5.6% (still digesting +27% 5D) after Q2 blowout. **ALAB** -9.7% on profit-taking after its own +30.8% 5D run. SpaceX's exclusive Nvidia GPU commitment adds fuel to **NVDA** (+4.7%).\n\n- **ANET** Q2 rev $3.04B (+37.7% YoY) beat $2.82B est; Q3 guide ~$3.3B vs $2.94B est; FY rev raised 3rd time to $12.6B; multi-year purchase commitments nearly tripled to ~$9.7B\n- 12 analysts raised ANET PTs post-earnings; Rosenblatt highest at $280; Barclays $289\n- **ALAB** Q2 rev $392.4M (+104% YoY) beat $360.7M; Q3 guide $540-560M vs $417M est; RBC PT $500\n- **NVDA** Musk on SPCX call: "SpaceX has committed to using Nvidia GPUs exclusively"; SpaceX targeting 5-10 GW compute by 2027\n- Counterpoint Research: 92% of sovereign LLMs worldwide run on Nvidia chips\n- BNP Paribas warns proposed FCC ban on Chinese optical transceivers could tighten AI networking supply, affecting AVGO, MRVL, CRDO, NVDA\n\n---\n\n**Pharma — Eli Lilly GLP-1 Dominance** `Pharma / Biotech` → ongoing\n\n**LLY** +4.2% after Q2 smash and FY revenue guide raise, driven by Mounjaro + Zepbound generating $14.9B combined.\n\n- Q2 adj EPS $8.38 vs $6.01 est; rev $22.97B vs $20.73B est (+48% YoY)\n- FY rev guide raised to $85-87B from $82-85B; adj EPS narrowed to $35.50-36.50 (vs $34.20 est)\n- Mounjaro global rev $9.9B (+91%); Zepbound US rev $4.93B (+44%)\n- Next-gen retatrutide clinical data package complete; CEO Ricks: "Lilly's future has never been brighter"\n- CVS announced GLP-1 collaboration with LLY: $29 MinuteClinic visits, transparent pricing via CVS app\n- Amazon Pharmacy starts delivering GLP-1 medications to eligible Medicare patients for $50/mo\n- Cantor Fitzgerald raises LLY PT from $1,350 to $1,410\n\n---\n\n**Payments / Fintech — Fiserv Guide Cut vs. Block/Paycom Beats** `Payments / SaaS` → ongoing\n\n**FISV** -10.8% PM on FY EPS guide cut dominates the payments space, while **XYZ** (Block) and **PAYC** rally on strong results.\n\n- **FISV** Q2 adj EPS $1.84 missed $1.91; organic rev -5%; FY adj EPS cut to $7.20-7.40 from $8.00-8.30 vs $8.10 est; adj operating margin narrowed to 31.8% from 39.6%\n- **XYZ** (Block) Q2 EPS $1.02 vs $0.87 est; rev $6.62B vs $6.49B; FY adj EPS raised from $3.85 to $4.02; Susquehanna PT raised to $100\n- **PAYC** Q2 EPS $2.78 vs $2.38 est; FY sales raised to $2.197-2.212B; BTIG raises PT to $230; PM +14%\n\n---\n\n**Disney Streaming & Entertainment** `Entertainment / Media` → ongoing\n\n**DIS** +3.5% on FQ3 results showing streaming and experiences strength. CEO D'Amaro outlines Disney+ ecosystem expansion and explores free ad-supported streaming.\n\n- FQ3 adj EPS $2.06 vs $1.86 est; rev $25.25B vs $25.40B est (slight miss); experiences rev $9.97B (+10%)\n- D2C streaming rev +11% to $5.53B; SVOD operating margin 13%; US park attendance +3%, guest spending +4%\n- Toy Story 5 crossed $1B global box office; $100M tariff refund in quarter (immaterial to full year)\n- FY26 adj EPS guide ~$6.64 (includes 53rd week) vs $6.81 est — slightly below Street\n- Share buyback target raised to ≥$9B from $8B; A+E 50% stake sold to Hearst for ~$1.2B\n- Exploring free ad-supported streaming tier; Disney+ ecosystem with games/merch launching spring 2027\n- TikTok global content partnership announced\n\n---\n\n**SpaceX Lock-Up & Valuation Debate** `Space / AI Infrastructure` → ongoing\n\n**SPCX** flat-to-up slightly pre-market after -13.6% Wednesday; first major share unlock begins today with ~911M shares eligible in staggered tranches through Dec 2026.\n\n- Q2 rev $7.81B (+92% YoY) beat $6.93B est; loss -$0.09 vs -$0.24 est; capex ~$18.4B\n- JPMorgan raises PT to $240 (Overweight); implies 122% upside from $108.27 close\n- Management targets $100B ARR run rate by Dec 2026; $1T revenue by 2030 (one year earlier than prior)\n- Gene Munster: CY27 revenue could reach $135B vs Street's $100B on 5% MoM growth assumption\n- Gary Black: buying the dip "makes no sense" with float potentially doubling\n- Musk personal shares locked until June 2027; $111 call options saw premium spike to $6.55\n\n---\n\n**Trav