2026-08-21	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-08-21 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: DE +6.7% on Q2 beat/guide raise, ROST +9% after-hours on Q2 blowout, WMT -9% on slowest US comp growth since 2020, BTC surges 20% on the week past $78K igniting MARA +16%/MSTR +8%/COIN +9%, while 30Y yields snap back to 5.25% erasing Treasury buyback relief.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **DE** | +6.7% | Mega | Q2 EPS $5.10 vs $4.70 est; raised FY NI to $4.75-5B | Ag Equipment / Industrials |\n| **MRVL** | +5.2% | Mega | Google custom-chip deal; $120B cumulative rev warrant; PT raises | AI Compute / Custom Silicon |\n| **SKHY** | +3.4% | Mega | $29B buyback; exploring Japan plant; SK Hynix $72B shareholder return | Memory |\n| **MU** | +3.3% | Mega | $10B Micron Research Labs; CEO says demand 50% > supply | Memory |\n| **FCX** | +3.3% | Mega | Copper rally; critical-minerals ETF flow narrative | Commodities / Mining |\n| **COP** | +3.1% | Mega | Brent >$86; Iran "Operation Economic Fury" sanctions | Energy |\n| **COIN** | +8.8% | Large | BTC >$78K; White House crypto summit; CLARITY Act push | Crypto Infrastructure |\n| **MSTR** | +8.1% | Large | Flips to $1.4B unrealized BTC gain; BTC proxy rally | Crypto / Bitcoin Treasury |\n| **ROST** | ~+9% AH | Large | Q2 EPS $2.66 vs $1.94 est; rev $6.27B vs $6.18B; raised FY guide to $8.61-$8.77 | Off-Price Retail |\n| **LITE** | +6.5% | Large | Sector momentum; heavy options activity at $880 strike | Optical / AI Networking |\n| **ILMN** | +5.0% | Large | Precision-oncology read-through from MRK/MRNA cancer vax | Genomics |\n| **AU** | +5.2% | Large | Gold spot >$4,500; safe-haven bid on yields/geopolitics | Gold Mining |\n| **KGC** | +4.6% | Large | Gold >$4,500; 5D +16.5% | Gold Mining |\n| **MARA** | +16.4% | Mid | BTC proxy; 35,577 BTC on balance sheet; AI pivot | Crypto Mining / BTC Proxy |\n| **HIVE** | +12.7% | Small | BTC rally; Rosenblatt PT raised to $6 | Crypto Mining |\n| **ASST** | +10.1% | Mid | BTC at $78K; 20,246 BTC treasury; perpetual preferred recovers | Crypto / Digital Treasury |\n| **SCSC** | +9.8% | Small | Q4 EPS $1.46 vs $1.14 est; $220.5M MicroAge acquisition; FY27 guide above est | IT Distribution |\n| **PURR** | +9.4% | Mid | Trump vows to bring Hyperliquid to US; Druckenmiller 13F stake | Crypto / DeFi |\n| **ANDG** | +9.3% | Mid | Secondary offering priced at $44/share; 7.4× volume | Idiosyncratic |\n| **WMT** | -9.2% prev | Mega | US comps +2.6% vs +3.8% est (weakest since 2020); Q3 guide below | Retail / Consumer |\n| **MRK** | -2.2% | Mega | Post-MRNA reversal; RBC downgraded to Sector Perform; Morgan Stanley upgraded to OW PT $179 | Pharma |\n| **PANW** | -2.9% | Mega | NTT DATA $1B alliance; but broader risk-off pressure | Cybersecurity |\n| **MDB** | -4.5% | Large | Competition fears; Evercore initiates Outperform PT $525 | SaaS / Database |\n| **EL** | -2.5% | Large | Post-earnings fade after +10.9% 5D run on Q4 beat/FY27 guide | Consumer / Beauty |\n| **OSIS** | -14.5% AH | Mid | Mixed Q4; weak FY27 sales guidance $1.875-1.93B | Security Systems |\n| **QMCO** | -6.5% | Small | 5D -17.6%; no identifiable catalyst | Idiosyncratic |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Bitcoin / Crypto Ecosystem Rally** `Crypto Infrastructure` → ongoing\n\n**BTC** surged 20% in five days to $78,459 Friday morning — its best week since Nov 2024 — igniting the highest-beta crypto equities. The rally was catalyzed by: (1) Treasury's Wed buyback announcement compressing yields briefly, (2) Trump's White House crypto summit Wed where he urged Congress to pass the CLARITY Act by Sep 15, (3) $2.74B in short liquidations (record per Coinglass), and (4) $606.3M in spot BTC ETF inflows on Aug 20.\n\n- **MSTR** +8.1% pre-market; holds 840,447 BTC at avg $75,385; now sitting on ~$1.4B unrealized gain after being underwater most of 2026; repurchased ~$347M of STRC preferred in past 4 weeks\n- **COIN** +8.8%; CEO Armstrong said crypto spot trading bear market (~1 year) may be nearing end; cited Oct-Dec halving cycle seasonality; BTC spot trading now only ~12% of COIN revenue\n- **MARA** +16.4% 1D, +20.1% 5D; holds ~35,577 BTC; secured 241MW of data-center capacity with Anthropic + AMD; $9.8B long-term contracted revenue\n- **HIVE** +12.7%; Rosenblatt raised PT to $6 from $5.50, Buy\n- **ASST** +10.1%, +27.6% 5D; 20,246 BTC treasury as of Aug 14; SATA perpetual preferred briefly returned to $100 par\n- **PURR** +9.4%, +46.1% 5D; Trump said CFTC Chair Selig is working to bring Hyperliquid to US in "fully compliant" fashion; Grayscale HYPE ETF accumulated >$123M AUM in <30 days; Druckenmiller's Duquesne disclosed 2.94M PURR shares ($23.15M)\n- **CRCL** +6.3%; USDC issuer; direct beneficiary of regulatory clarity\n- **RIOT** +9.1%; CEO Les highlighted 241MW contracted, $9.8B long-term revenue\n- Starkiller Capital declared the crypto cycle has bottomed; BTC and ETH both back above 200-day MAs for first time since last cycle end\n- Near-term caution: Coinbase Premium Index remained negative throughout advance; BTC open interest declined 8.7% in BTC terms even as $ OI rose 11.7% — suggesting forced-cover rather than fresh longs\n\n**Gold & Precious Metals at Multi-Month Highs** `Commodities / Safe Haven` → ongoing\n\nGold spot surged above $4,581 Friday, up 1.4% and heading for a third consecutive weekly gain, supported by central-bank buying (~1,000 tons annually), dollar weakness (DXY -0.24%), and safe-haven demand amid Iran tensions and rising fiscal concerns.\n\n- **NEM** +2.0% 1D, +11.7% 5D; appointed former BHP CFO Peter Beaven to board effective Sep 1\n- **AU** +5.2% 1D, +20.2% 5D\n- **KGC** +4.6% 1D, +16.5% 5D\n- **AEM** +0.9% 1D, +16.3% 5D\n- **AG** +2.1% 1D, +12.8% 5D (silver at $68.39)\n- Copper-to-gold ratio at 0.11 — historically a leading signal for lower 10Y yields per Prof. Dror Parnes (Texas A&M); LME copper inventories surged 50% in 3 days easing squeeze fears\n\n**Deere: Ag Cycle Bottom Call + Construction Strength** `Ag Equipment / Industrials` → new\n\n**DE** +6.7% on 3× avg volume after Q2 results and an upbeat cycle-bottom call.\n\n- Q2 EPS $5.10 vs $4.70 est; net sales/rev $12.608B vs $10.730B est (+5% YoY)\n- Equipment operations margin 14.4%; Construction & Forestry sales +18% to $3.618B, margin expanded to 12.1% from 7.7% — driven by data-center builds, infrastructure, rental fleet\n- Raised FY26 NI guide to $4.75-5.0B; equipment ops cash flow $5.0-5.5B\n- EOP planter/sprayer orders up mid-single digits vs prior year; See & Spray factory adoption nearly doubling; 40%+ of planters taking advanced offerings\n- CEO May: "2026 will mark the bottom of the current ag equipment cycle"\n- Tariff refunds $382M YTD ($110M in Q3); direct tariff expense ~$1.1B for FY26 (down from $1.2B prior)\n- Baird raised PT to $640 from $525 (Neutral); Oppenheimer raised PT to $685 from $680 (Outperform)\n- CNH +6%, AGCO +5.2%, NTR +4.3% in sympathy\n\n**Memory Chip Capital Returns & Capacity Expansion** `Memory / AI Infrastructure` → ongoing\n\n**SKHY** +3.4% and **MU** +3.3% as memory-chip makers signal structural demand shift.\n\n- **SKHY**: Announced 40T won ($29B) treasury stock buyback/cancellation; pledged >50% of cumulative FCF 2025-2027 to shareholder returns; exploring new fab in Miyagi, Japan (denied decision made per MK); Wolfe, RBC, Cantor all initiated at Buy/Outperform (PTs $200-$300)\n- **MU**: Unveiled Micron Research Labs — $10B over 10 years, Boise HQ, groundbreaking CY2027; CEO Mehrotra told CNBC data-center clients demand 50% more supply than MU can produce; signed 5-year supply agreements with 16 customers (more added since); analyst consensus Buy, avg PT $1,537.50\n- Both stocks benefit from thesis that AI has ended the memory boom-bust cycle — "no AI without memory" (Mehrotra)\n\n**Marvell: Google Custom-Chip Partnership** `AI Compute / Custom Silicon` → new\n\n**MRVL** +5.2% 1D, +11.6% 5D following multi-year Google custom-chip deal announced Thursday.\n\n- Programs include AI inference offload engine, storage controllers, networking chips and memory interface controllers — NOT the core TPU accelerator\n- Google received warrants for ~59M MRVL shares; 57.6M vest based on purchases through FY2033; full vesting implies ~$120B cumulative revenue (~$19.2B/year over 6.25 years) per JPMorgan\n- JPMorgan: path to ~$11/share CY2028 EPS vs Street $9.52; reiterated Overweight\n- Oppenheimer raised PT to $300 from $250 (Outperform); UBS raised PT to $310 from $300 (Buy); BMO initiated Outperform PT $250; RBC reiterated Outperform PT $360\n- Earnings Aug 27 ⚠️; EPS est $0.87, rev est $2.71B\n\n**Retail Earnings Divergence: ROST Beats, WMT Guides Down, AAP Crashes** `Retail / Consumer` → new\n\nThe consumer picture fractured across three major retailers reporting within 24 hours.\n\n- **ROST** surged ~9% after-hours: Q2 EPS $2.66 vs $1.94 est; rev ~$6.27B vs $6.18B est (+13% YoY); comps +10% driven by traffic; gross margin expanded 625bp (includes 405bp tariff refund benefit); raised FY EPS guide to $8.61-$8.77 from $7.50-$7.74 (above $7.79 est); raised store-opening target to 115 from 110; CEO Conroy said ROST has gained more share than each off-price competitor over past 4 quarters; Baird raised PT to $270, Evercore to $290\n- **WMT** fell 9.2% Thursday: Q2 adj EPS $0.81 beat $0.74 est; sales $187.9B beat; but US comps +2.6% vs +3.8% est — weakest since 2020; pharmacy deflation (maximum fair price rules) created 125bp headwind; Q3 guide: adj EPS $0.62-0.64 vs $0.68 est; CFO Rainey warned gas >$4 causes "psychological impact" and consumer trade-offs; UBS analyst Lasser defended bull case citing 24% US e-commerce growth and 38% ad-revenue growth; 12 analysts cut PTs (Baird to $120, BTIG to $140, Morgan Stanley to $125, DA Davidson to $132, Guggenheim to $130)\n- **AAP** crashed -24.6% Thursday: sales $2.0B missed $2.039B est; comps -0.5%; adj EPS $1.03 beat $0.81 est but included $26M tariff refund (13 cents); DIY demand pressured by household budgets; multiple PTs cut (TD Cowen to $45, Morgan Stanley to $52, DA Davidson to $48, RBC to $52)\n- **BJ** reported Friday AM: Q2 adj EPS $1.36 vs $1.17 est; sales $6.227B vs $5.957B est (+15.9% YoY); merch comps +3.1%; MFI +9.9% to 8.5M members; comp gallons +10.5%; raised adj EPS guide to $4.60-$4.80; Texas expansion tracking 30%+ ahead of membership plan\n\n**Bond Market: Treasury Buyback Fizzles** `Macro / Rates` → ongoing\n\nThe Treasury's Wed buyback announcement — doubling long-end operations from $2B to $4B starting Sep 9 — produced less than 24 hours of yield relief. By Thursday, 30Y hit 5.27% and 10Y rose to 4.71%, nearly erasing the post-announcement decline.\n\n- 30Y yield touched 5.33% Tuesday (highest since Jun 2007) before buyback-driven dip to 5.19%\n- 10Y at 4.69% Friday pre-market; 2Y at 4.18%\n- US gross federal debt crossed $40T; interest payments ~$1.25T annualized (~3.3% GDP)\n- Peter Schiff: "Inflation-sensitive markets are ripping because the Trump Administration pulled the rug out from under Warsh… Commodities now, CPI later"\n- Raoul Pal labeled the intervention "The Bessent Put" — signal enormous, dollars small\n- Conference Board report: Social Security benefits could be $754/month lower by 2036 if trust fund depleted; a $600K home purchased in 2031 could cost $53K more over 30 years under baseline deficit scenario\n- Global context: Japan 10Y at 2.95% (highest since Sep 1996), German Bund highest since 2011, UK 30Y gilt ~5.80% — bond yield surge is not US-specific\n- FedWatch: 34.6% probability of Sep rate hike; ~50% probability of any hike in 2026 (down from 64% on Aug 6)\n\n**Iran Geopolitics & Energy** `Energy / Geopolitics` → ongoing\n\n**COP** +3.1%, **BP** +3.0%, **CNQ** +2.7% as crude remains elevated on Strait of Hormuz tensions.\n\n- Trump announced "Operation Economic Fury" — threatened "most crushing economic operation ever" against Iran; Bessent warned "toughest sanctions in history" and said any tie to Tehran will "hasten a nation's economic oblivion"\n- VP Vance said US military has gotten "a lot of oil and gas out of the Strait of Hormuz"; called situation "delicate" but said economic pressure is the "most effective tool"\n- EPA issued emergency fuel waiver allowing winter-blend gasoline (E10) starting Sep 1 — could lower pump prices 10-25¢/gallon (GasBuddy's De Haan)\n- Brent crude at ~$86.08 pre-market (-0.86%); national gas avg $4.10/gallon; diesel $5.55/gallon\n- WTI near $86; MPC -0.8% (refining); XLE sector led Thursday +1.3%\n\n**NVIDIA Approaching Earnings; Rebellions Deal Talks** `AI Compute` → ongoing\n\n**NVDA** +0.2% pre-market; Bloomberg reported NVIDIA exploring partnership with Korean AI chip startup Rebellions (valued ~$2.3B); could include technical partnership, investment, or acquisition.\n\n- BMO initiated Outperform PT $340; consensus Buy, avg PT $327\n- Earnings Aug 26 ⚠️; EPS est $2.07 (vs $1.04 YoY); rev est $91.91B (vs $46.74B YoY)\n- AVGO discussing up to $100B AI financing with Blackstone/Apollo for custom-chip infrastructure; CEO expects AI chip sales >$100B next year; Apple deal >$30B through 2031\n- Waymo unveiled first custom robotaxi chip (>1,000 TOPS, 5nm), collaborating with AMD, MU, NVDA, TSMC, Samsung, Sandisk, Socionext\n\n**PayPal Acquisition Chatter** `Fintech` → ongoing\n\n**PYPL** +2.2%, RSI at 75.32 (overbought). Stripe and Advent International reportedly in talks to acquire PayPal; initial $60.50/share proposal viewed as too low; negotiations centered on higher price; deal could come within weeks.\n\n- Expanded into higher education payments via integrations with Illumia, Nelnet, TouchNet\n- Investor Tom Hayes (Great Hill Capital) named PYPL a high-conviction turnaround bet, citing $6B annual FCF\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n\n- **Anthropic valuation scrutiny**: NYU's Aswath Damodaran calculated Anthropic would need ~$1.2T in year-10 revenue to justify a potential $2T IPO valuation; current annualized run rate >$65B; Amazon's total Anthropic investment could reach $33B\n- **TGTX M&A speculation**: Traders speculate multiple parties interested in acquiring TG Therapeutics; no confirmed details\n- **Tesla China recall**: 2.98M vehicles recalled for emergency door-release labeling + OTA update; separate 2.74M recall for driver-attention monitoring; Solar Roof tiles reportedly discontinued\n- **DeepSeek V4-Flash-Vision-Exp**: Experimental multimodal model now live on API — potential competitive signal for AI model landscape\n- **US-Canada trade**: Canada trade minister meeting US Trade Rep Greer today 10:30 AM ET; possible Canadian auto tariff cut to 15%, aluminum/steel to 25% per reports\n- **S&P Global August PMIs**: Composite 56.0 vs 54.5 prior; Services 56.8 vs 53.9 est (strong); Manufacturing 53.2 vs 54.0 est (slight miss) — services economy remains resilient\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | **ROST** Q2 EPS $2.66 vs $1.94 est; comps +10%; FY guide raised to $8.61-$8.77. **BJ** Q2 adj EPS $1.36 vs $1.17 est; merch comps +3.1%. **DE** Q2 EPS $5.10 vs $4.70 est; sales $12.6B vs $10.7B est. **WMT** US comps +2.6% vs +3.8% est. **FLO** EPS $0.21 missed $0.23 est. **OSIS** FY27 sales guide $1.875-1.93B (weak). **UI** Q4 EPS $4.73 beat $4.03 est. |\n| Macro | US S&P Global Aug Services PMI 56.8 vs 53.9 est; Manufacturing 53.2 vs 54.0 est; Composite 56.0. 30Y yield snapped back to 5.25% erasing Treasury buyback relief. US national debt crossed $40T. Japan CPI 1.8% YoY as expected. UK retail sales MoM -0.5% vs -0.4% est. |\n| Tech | Waymo unveiled first custom 5nm robotaxi chip (>1,000 TOPS). NVIDIA exploring Rebellions partnership/acquisition. Broadcom discussing up to $100B AI financing. DeepSeek V4-Flash multimodal model live. AMD: BMO initiated Outperform PT $550, Helios shipping Sep 2026. |\n| Commodities | Gold spot >$4,581/oz heading for 3rd weekly gain. Brent crude ~$86. EPA authorized early winter-blend gasoline starting Sep 1. Copper LME inventories surged 50% in 3 days easing squeeze. |\n| Crypto | BTC hit $78,459 (+20% weekly); $2.74B shorts liquidated (record). Spot BTC ETF inflows $606.3M on Aug 20. Trump urged CLARITY Act passage; CFTC working to bring Hyperliquid to US. |\n| M&A | ScanSource acquiring MicroAge for $220.5M cash. Werewolf Therapeutics merging with Ambros Therapeutics (valued $500M) + $150M PIPE. T. Rowe Price acquiring F/m Investments (~$19B AUM). PayPal/Stripe/Advent talks ongoing at price above $60.50/share. |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **NVDA earnings Aug 26** ⚠️: EPS est $2.07 vs $1.04 YoY; rev est $91.91B vs $46.74B YoY. Rebellions deal talks add narrative layer.\n- **MRVL earnings Aug 27** ⚠️: EPS est $0.87; rev est $2.71B. Google warrant deal creates elevated expectations.\n- **PDD earnings Mon Aug 24**: EPS est $2.77; rev est $17.13B. Multiple analysts recently downgraded.\n- **INTU earnings Tue Aug 25**: Q4 EPS est $3.59; rev est $4.27B. Deutsche Bank cut PT to $425 (Buy).\n- **DKS earnings Tue Aug 25**: Q2 EPS est $3.80 (down from $4.38 YoY). Wells Fargo upgraded to Overweight PT $240.\n- **CLARITY Act vote scheduled Sep 15**: Coinbase CEO Armstrong said "90% of what both sides want" is agreed; expects >60 Senate votes.\n- **PANW earnings Sep 1**: Q4 EPS est $0.88; rev est $3.35B. Multiple PTs raised to $415.\n- **Scholar Rock (SRRK)**: Removed Catalent Indiana from apitegromab BLA; PDUFA date through Sep 30 for potential FDA approval at any time.\n- **US-Canada trade meeting today 10:30 AM ET**: Potential tariff cuts on Canadian autos to 15%.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **ANDG** +9.3% on 7.4× volume is a secondary offering pricing event ($44/share), not a fundamental catalyst — mechanical flow.\n- **MRNA** already priced its 177% cancer-vaccine rally Wednesday and gave back 20% Thursday — today's noise is position-squaring, not new information.\n- **Xiaocaiyuan (0999.HK)** and Biren Technology (6082.HK) deep-dives are Hong Kong/China-listed names with no direct connection to the US ticker universe.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 374678, "output_tokens": 6306, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 1.87339, "total_cost_usd": 2.03104, "output_cost_usd": 0.15765, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-08-21T14:00:21.714480+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-08-21T14:03:32.315676+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from published claude.com/api pricing (input, 5m cache write, cache read, output) — Anthropic does not return dollar amounts on the response.", "total_cost_usd": 2.031, "total_input_tokens": 374678, "total_output_tokens": 6306, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-08-21", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Channel: tech": 4, "Channel: movers": 12, "Channel: general": 98, "Channel: markets": 20, "Channel: earnings": 22, "Channel: equities": 10, "Channel: commodities": 3, "Ticker Group: r1d_screener": 62, "Ticker Group: vol_spike_5d": 37, "Ticker Group: ti65_mid_small": 3, "Ticker Group: ti65_mega_large": 21, "Channel: macro_economic_events": 10}, "articles_total": 302}, "upserted": 302, "api_by_fetch": {"ticker": {"P": {"error": null, "api_rows": 1, "in_window": 1}, "Q": {"error": null, "api_rows": 3, "in_window": 3}, "U": {"error": null, "api_rows": 2, "in_window": 2}, "AG": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "AU": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "BP": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "DE": {"error": null, "api_rows": 12, "in_window": 12}, "EL": {"error": null, "api_rows": 14, "in_window": 14},