2026-09-09	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 September 9, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Brent crude surges toward $100 after the U.S. destroys five Iranian tankers and Iran fires ballistic missiles at a U.S. base in Jordan, driving 10-year yields above 4.8% and a 58% rate-hike probability for next week's Fed meeting, while INTC jumps 10% on a Northland upgrade tied to Musk's Terafab, BE rallies 11% on S&P 500 inclusion, and TTAN drops 20% after hours on soft GTV growth and deferred trade expansion.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **INTC** | +9.7% | Mega | Northland upgrade to Outperform; Terafab foundry thesis; 1M+ High-NA EUV wafers processed | Semis / Foundry |\n| **GLW** | +8.9% | Mega | Verizon multi-billion-dollar fiber deal for 80M+ miles; China Renaissance initiates Buy PT $238 | Fiber / AI Infra |\n| **STX** | +8.1% | Mega | Memory sector rally on AI demand / DRAM shortage thesis | Memory |\n| **AMD** | +6.0% | Mega | Sector sympathy; Ark sold 19,491 shares via ARKK | AI Compute |\n| **FCX** | +5.9% | Mega | Copper hits LME all-time high $14,617/mt on AI data-center demand + Chile supply decline | Copper / Commodities |\n| **SCCO** | +5.5% | Mega | Copper rally sympathy | Copper / Commodities |\n| **VRT** | +4.6% | Mega | AI power infrastructure momentum | AI Power |\n| **SKHY** | +4.6% | Mega | SK Hynix ADR rally; DRAM prices up 200%+ YoY; <10 days inventory at Samsung/SK Hynix | Memory |\n| **ARM** | +4.2% | Mega | Semiconductor sector strength; golden cross intact | AI Compute |\n| **CRWV** | +12.2% | Large | Neocloud rally ahead of Oracle earnings Thursday; CoreWeave 3.1× avg volume | AI Infra / Neocloud |\n| **LITE** | +11.4% | Large | Fiber/optical sympathy with GLW-VZ deal; continued post-Q4 beat-and-raise momentum | Optical / AI Infra |\n| **BE** | +11.1% | Large | S&P 500 inclusion effective Sept 21; UBS raises PT to $325; Pelosi holds 15K shares | Power / S&P Rebalance |\n| **NBIS** | +8.5% | Large | Named Palantir's preferred sovereign AI infra partner | AI Infra / Neocloud |\n| **COHR** | +8.0% | Large | Fiber/optical sector rally | Optical |\n| **HPE** | +7.3% | Large | AI server/infrastructure momentum | AI Infra |\n| **CIEN** | +6.9% | Large | Fiber/networking sympathy | Networking |\n| **CLS** | +6.8% | Large | AI infrastructure buildout demand | AI Infra |\n| **NOK** | +6.3% | Large | Sector strength; Mobile Core Early Access platform launch; 2.2× avg volume | Networking / 5G |\n| **BNC** | +52.7% | Small | No identified catalyst; 183× avg volume | Idiosyncratic |\n| **FCEL** | +20.4% | Small | Clean energy / hydrogen sector rally | Clean Energy |\n| **SEI** | +16.1% | Small | Raised Q3 adj EBITDA guide 23% to $110M-$130M; raised Q4 guide 48% | AI Power |\n| **SMR** | +15.5% | Small | Nuclear/SMR sector rally; leveraged ETFs up 30%+ | Nuclear |\n| **DOCN** | +13.7% | Small | No specific catalyst; 2.1× avg volume | Cloud |\n| **EOSE** | +12.8% | Small | Energy storage sector rally; +43% over 5 days | Energy Storage |\n| **AMGN** | -9.6% | Mega | Novartis pelacarsen Phase 3 Lp(a) trial failed primary endpoint; read-across to olpasiran; BMO downgrade | Biotech |\n| **NVS** | -14% (ADR) | Mega | Pelacarsen Phase 3 + del-desiran Phase 3 HARBOR both failed primary endpoints | Biotech |\n| **TTAN** | -19.8% AH | Mid | Q2 beat but soft GTV; deferred trade expansion for MAX; Q3 rev guide $285-$287M vs ~$290M est | SaaS / Vertical Software ⚠️ |\n| **BSX** | -5.3% | Large | Won't meet 2026 guidance after August cyberattack disrupted manufacturing & shipping | MedTech |\n| **SHOP** | -7.7% | Large | Growth stock rotation; Ark trimmed 40K shares Sept 2 | E-Commerce |\n| **CASY** | -9.7% AH | Large | Q1 EPS $7.37 beat $6.72 est; revenue $5.68B beat; but fuel gallons -0.3% and stock sold on guidance | Retail ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Middle East Escalation Drives Oil Toward $100 and Rate-Hike Repricing** `Macro / Energy` → ongoing\n\nThe Iran-U.S. conflict escalated sharply Tuesday with CENTCOM destroying five Iranian crude tankers after IRGC ballistic missile attacks on a U.S. Navy warship. Iran subsequently fired missiles at a U.S. base in Jordan (18 of 20 intercepted). Houthis struck Saudi Aramco facilities, injuring 73. Brent crude closed at $99.47 (+1.6%); WTI at $94.58 (+1.7%).\n\n- 10-year Treasury yield topped 4.80% intraday for the first time since October 2023; settled ~4.78%.\n- CME FedWatch: 58% probability of a 25bp rate hike at Sept. 16 FOMC meeting, up from ~40% pre-payrolls.\n- Former Fed economist **Claudia Sahm** now views a rate hike as "appropriate policy," says she is "no longer confident" inflation returns to 2% without one.\n- Market strategist **James Thorne** warns hiking into an energy supply shock repeats the ECB/Fed's 2008 mistake.\n- Goldman Sachs raised Brent year-end forecast to $90 from $80; sees $120/bbl if Gulf output remains 4M bpd below pre-war levels.\n- National avg gas: $4.15/gal (record Labor Day); diesel: $5.90/gal nationally, nearing $8 in California.\n- USO +1.2% Tuesday; +108% YTD. **MPC** +2.4%, **VLO** +3.5%, **PSX** +2.0% — UBS raised PTs on all three.\n- PPI due Thursday, CPI due Friday — headline CPI seen at 3.4%, core at 2.4%.\n- NFIB Small Business Optimism fell to 98.7 in August from 99.8, missing 99.3 estimate.\n- Iran's IRGC Navy warned all tanker crews near Kuwaiti and Bahraini ports hosting Americans to evacuate.\n- Trump posted that oil prices "will drop precipitously" once the war ends; predicted $2/gal gas.\n\n**Semiconductors & Memory: AI Demand Tightens Supply to Crisis Levels** `AI Compute / Memory` → ongoing\n\nA broad semiconductor rally lifted **INTC** +9.7%, **SKHY** +4.6%, **STX** +8.1%, **AMD** +6.0%, **LRCX** +4.4%, **ARM** +4.2%, driven by converging catalysts: DRAM shortage data, Intel foundry progress, and the GPT-6 Astra launch.\n\n- **INTC**: Northland upgraded to Outperform, PT $120, citing Terafab partnership with SpaceX/Tesla as "materially beneficial" to foundry scale; estimates Terafab at 22.4M advanced wafers/year. Intel confirmed 1M+ wafers processed on High-NA EUV (18A process). DigiTimes reports ~10% PC CPU price hike planned for October. Server CPU supply described as tight.\n- **SKHY** (SK Hynix ADR): ADRs +4.6%, approaching post-IPO highs; +50% from July lows. KB Securities reports Samsung and SK Hynix each hold <10 days of finished memory inventory. TechInsights' Dan Kim rates memory-market conditions 8/10 for "craziness," expects 10/10 through end-2027. DRAM prices forecast up 200%+ YoY. HBM4 consumes ~3× the wafer capacity of conventional DRAM.\n- **ASML** +2.95% pre-market: Joint initiatives with TSMC and Samsung on 12-inch photomask transition for High-NA EUV; Samsung targets 2028 for industry-first High-NA DRAM production.\n- **Amkor Technology** (AMKR) announced Phase 2 of Arizona advanced packaging campus; planned investment increases to ~$12B, adding 60,000 sq meters of cleanroom.\n\n**AI Infrastructure & Neocloud Complex Rallies Into Oracle Earnings** `AI Infra / Neocloud` → ongoing\n\n**CRWV** +12.2%, **NBIS** +8.5%, **FRMI** +13.0%, **CLS** +6.8%, **HPE** +7.3% — the neocloud and AI infrastructure complex surged as positioning builds ahead of **ORCL** earnings Thursday (Q1 FY27). Oracle itself rose ~5%.\n\n- **ORCL** earnings Thursday after close: consensus EPS $1.67, revenue $19.13B; company guided $1.72-$1.76 EPS, $18.96B-$19.25B revenue. Cloud revenue growth projected 58%-64%. RPO exceeds $600B (est. ~50% is OpenAI). Stock at $165.93, still -33% from 52-week high of $345.72.\n- **NBIS**: Named Palantir's preferred sovereign AI infra partner; will bring Nebius compute/inference inside Palantir's enterprise perimeter. Plans modular data-center deployments.\n- **PLTR** -2.1%: Partnership with Nebius announced; Ark sold 38,395 shares ($6.5M). CEO Karp positions "AI ownership" model vs pay-per-token. Michael Burry holds short positions against both PLTR and NBIS.\n- **CRWV** +12.2% on 3.1× avg volume; no specific headline beyond neocloud positioning.\n- Data center construction spending surged 57% YoY in July to record $75B annualized rate.\n- Dan Ives warned 10-15% of U.S. data center projects could be cut due to political backlash.\n- Treasury Secretary Bessent gave AI data center community outreach a "D-minus" but warned U.S. "can't pause" AI race with China.\n- Raoul Pal: data centers "roughly 30% built vs where they should be"; calls it a supercycle.\n- **ABM Industries** Q3: EPS $1.04 beat $1.01 est; revenue $2.317B beat $2.310B. Semiconductor/microgrid/data center revenue ~$775M YTD, +26% organic, +40% incl. WGNSTAR. Data center pipeline "a multiple of where it was a year ago."\n\n**Fiber Optics & Connectivity Stocks Surge on Verizon-Corning Deal** `Optical / Networking` → new\n\n**GLW** +8.9%, **LITE** +11.4%, **COHR** +8.0%, **CIEN** +6.9%, **NOK** +6.3%, **AAOI** +9.2% — a broad fiber/optical rally followed a multi-year, multi-billion-dollar supply agreement between Verizon and Corning.\n\n- Verizon-Corning deal covers 80M+ miles of high-density optical fiber and connectivity solutions, 2027-2032, supporting consumer broadband expansion toward 40-50M passings and a national long-haul AI backbone for hyperscalers.\n- China Renaissance initiated coverage on **GLW** with Buy, PT $238 (vs. $168 close).\n- **LITE**: Extending run from late-August Q4 beat-and-raise (adj. earnings and revenue ~doubled YoY); Mizuho PT $1,140. Stock +563% over 12 months.\n- **NOK**: Launched Mobile Core Early Access platform for telecom testing; 2.2× avg volume.\n\n**Copper Hits All-Time High as AI Data Centers Consume Physical Economy** `Commodities / AI Infra` → ongoing\n\nCopper set an all-time high on the LME at $14,617/mt Tuesday in a second consecutive record session. **FCX** +5.9%, **SCCO** +5.5%.\n\n- JPMorgan estimates a single large AI data center can require up to 50,000 metric tons of copper; data centers as a category will consume ~475,000 mt in 2026.\n- Chile recorded its weakest Q2 output in 19+ years and cut full-year forecast for a second straight quarter (-2.6%).\n- Citigroup forecasts $15,000/ton by year-end, $17,000 if manufacturing recovers or AI demand exceeds expectations.\n- FCX +43% YTD, SCCO +42% YTD, TECK +44.3% YTD, COPX +26% YTD vs SPY +12.9%.\n- Global Manufacturing PMI rose to 52.3 in August (13th consecutive month above 50); ISM Manufacturing at 54.6%.\n\n**Biotech Rout: Novartis Double Trial Failure Cascades Across Sector** `Biotech / Pharma` → new\n\n**NVS** -14% (worst session ever for ADRs), **AMGN** -9.6% (worst day since Oct 2000), **IONS** -13%, **SRPT** -8%, **DYN** -23%.\n\n- Novartis disclosed pelacarsen Phase 3 Lp(a)HORIZON failed primary endpoint (no reduction in CV death, heart attack, stroke vs placebo despite cutting Lp(a) levels). Read-across hit Amgen's rival olpasiran (siRNA mechanism, different from pelacarsen's ASO).\n- Separately, Novartis Phase 3 HARBOR study of del-desiran for myotonic dystrophy type 1 also failed primary endpoint. Cascading read-across hit **DYN** (developing z-basivarsen for DM1) and **SRPT** (developing SRP-1003 for DM1).\n- BMO Capital downgraded **AMGN** from Outperform to Market Perform, maintained $450 PT.\n- **ROIV** +19.7% bucked the trend: Pulmovant's mosliciguat Phase 2 in PH-ILD showed 56.3% PVR reduction (highest ever in any randomized controlled PH trial) and met all secondary endpoints.\n- **XLV** (Healthcare SPDR) -2.2%, worst sector of the day; **IBB** -1.8%.\n\n**S&P 500 / Index Rebalance Catalysts** `Index / Rebalance` → new\n\n- **BE** +11.1%: S&P Dow Jones Indices announced Bloom Energy replaces Molson Coors in S&P 500, effective prior to Sept. 21 open. UBS raised PT to $325 from $300, estimates passive funds could hold 10-15% of shares outstanding. Nancy Pelosi disclosed buying 15,000 BE shares + 200 call options in July at prices ~$160-$214; position now worth ~$4.2M.\n- **SpaceX** (SPCX) +3.7%: JPMorgan estimates Nasdaq-100 weight could jump from 1.25% to 2.25% at Sept. 18 rebalance, generating ~$15.5B in passive buying. TD Securities sees weight potentially exceeding 3.5%. Third share unlock (~700M shares) expected Wednesday. Pivotal Research initiated Buy, PT $220.\n- Dell, Palo Alto, Arista, Sandisk added to S&P 100.\n\n**Enterprise SaaS Under Pressure** `SaaS` → ongoing\n\nRate-sensitive software names continued to bleed as yields spiked. **NOW** -5.4%, **TEAM** -6.4%, **WDAY** -4.8%, **CRM** -3.9%, **SHOP** -7.7%, **GWRE** extended post-earnings slide to -20% cumulative.\n\n- **TTAN** (ServiceTitan) -19.8% after hours: Q2 EPS $0.40 beat $0.35; revenue $292.8M beat $286M (+21% YoY). But GTV growth of 17% was ~200bps below recent quarters due to softer lead volumes in HVAC. Company deferred expansion into new commercial trades/residential exteriors to focus investment on MAX (agentic OS). MAX locations doubled in Q2 to 100+; targeting 700+ by year-end. FY27 revenue guide narrowed to $1.139B-$1.144B; operating income $152M-$154M. Revenue recognition timing and PS revenue headwind of $4-5M in H2 from MAX mix shift.\n- **BRZE** (Braze) -9.9% after hours: Q2 EPS $0.19 beat $0.16; revenue $227.2M beat $219.9M (+26% YoY). Raised FY27 revenue guide to $910M-$913M from $895M-$899M vs $898M est. NDR >110%.\n- **GWRE** -8.5%: Continued post-earnings slide; FY27 ARR growth guide ~18% (down from 19%); Q1 revenue guide ~$375M, ~3% below $387.6M consensus.\n- **CASY** Q1: EPS $7.37 beat $6.72; revenue $5.68B beat $5.57B. Inside same-store sales +3.2% (vs +4.3% prior year). Stock -9.7% after hours despite beat — fuel gallons -0.3%, muted forward guidance.\n\n**Nuclear/SMR Stocks Rally** `Nuclear / Power` → ongoing\n\n**SMR** (NuScale) +15.5%, leveraged ETFs SMRX +37%, SMU +31%. **OKLO** also rose.\n\n- NuScale rally driven by boron-oxide pellet manufacturing milestone with MillenniTEK and AI tools deployment for engineering.\n- Broader nuclear appetite tied to AI data-center power demand expectations.\n\n**Quantum Computing Gets $200M in CHIPS Act Funding** `Quantum` → new\n\n- **QBTS** (D-Wave) +5.8% (6.6× avg volume): Finalized definitive agreement with Commerce Dept for up to $100M in CHIPS Act funding; Commerce receives minority non-controlling equity stake.\n- **RGTI** (Rigetti) +5.7%: Signed $100M definitive agreement with Commerce Dept under CHIPS Act for superconducting quantum R&D; Commerce also receives equity stake.\n- **IONQ** +6%: Raised FY26 revenue outlook to $450M-$460M following SkyWater acquisition completion. Published blueprint showing ~20,000-qubit system could break Bitcoin's secp256k1 in ~26 days.\n\n**Trade War Escalation: Canada Tariffs + Trump Moves on Canadian Products** `Macro / Trade` → ongoing\n\n- Canada's retaliatory tariffs (15-50%) on U.S. goods took effect Tuesday midnight ET, hitting steel, milk, video game consoles, golf clubs, clothing and more. Covers >$20B in goods.\n- Trump directed GSA/USTR to remove Canadian-origin products from GSA schedules unless Canada restores "full and fair reciprocity."\n- Trump weighing additional 7.5% tariff on Chinese goods ahead of planned Xi meeting later this month.\n- U.S. bilateral trade deficit with China narrowed by a third to $73.9B in H1 2026; overall U.S. goods deficit widened to $118.8B in July (widest since March 2025), driven by AI hardware imports.\n- U.S. Transportation Dept sent letter to Ford CEO criticizing partnerships with Chinese companies (CATL, Geely).\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n\n- **Anthropic** walked away from $6B Decart acquisition; IPO adviser says offering could be "heavily oversubscribed" at ~$2T valuation. Bankers from MS and GS in talks with credit agencies for investment-grade rating post-IPO. Trades above $1T in private markets.\n- **Buyout debt pipeline** at $138B, highest since pre-financial crisis, per JPMorgan; most issuance expected before November elections.\n- **SpaceX** third share unlock (~700M shares) expected Wednesday; Musk's stake locked until June 2027.\n- **Apple** "Surprise and Shine" event Wednesday 1pm ET: iPhone 18 Pro models + first foldable iPhone expected at ~$2,099; BofA maintains Buy, PT $380. First event under new CEO John Ternus.\n- **GameStop** Q2: Revenue $790.2M beat $756.9M est; EPS $0.27 inline. Collectibles revenue +57% YoY to $356.3M (45% of sales). Raised FY26 adj EBITDA guide to >$650M from >$600M. Holds $5.4B in cash/securities/digital assets including 43.4M eBay shares.\n- **GE Aerospace** agreed to acquire Consolidated Precision Products (CPP) for $11.75B ($7B cash + debt), expanding casting capacity for commercial/defense aviation.\n- **Chime** (CHYM) to acquire Stride Bank for $590M cash; expects Q3 revenue $705M (+30% YoY); raised FY26 revenue guide to $2.76B-$2.77B.\n- **Robinhood** struck deal with Crypto.com to bring OG prediction-market contracts onto its app + took equity stakes in Crypto.com and OG. Goldman raised PT to $142; Cantor to $150. Landed first-ever IPO underwriting role (Oura).\n- Home purchase cancellation rate hit 14% in July, highest since Nov 2023; sellers outnumber buyers by ~51%.\n- **MSTR** made no Bitcoin purchases last week; holdings flat at 845,050 BTC. Repurchased 1.81M STRC shares for $176.3M instead. Doubled digital credit securities repurchase program to $2B.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Macro | CENTCOM destroyed 5 Iranian tankers Sept 8; Iran fired ballistic missiles at U.S. base in Jordan (18/20 intercepted); Brent $99.47; 10Y yield breached 4.80%; Fed hike probability 58% for Sept 16 |\n| Commodities | Copper LME all-time high $14,617/mt; diesel national avg $5.90/gal; California diesel nearing $8/gal; Goldman raises Brent year-end to $90, flags $120 risk scenario |\n| Earnings | TTAN Q2 beat but -20% AH on soft GTV and deferred trade expansion; BRZE beat-and-raise but -10% AH; CASY beat on EPS/rev but -10% AH; ABM beat with data center pipeline "a multiple" of year-ago; GME rev beat, raised EBITDA guide; UNFI Q4 beat, FY27 adj EPS guide $3.00-$3.50 |\n| Tech | Intel 1M+ High-NA EUV wafers; ASML/TSMC/Samsung 12-inch photomask initiative; Verizon-Corning multi-billion-dollar fiber deal; Apple foldable iPhone expected Wednesday at ~$2,099; Palantir-Nebius sovereign AI partnership |\n| Biotech | Novartis pelacarsen Phase 3 and del-desiran Phase 3 both failed primary endpoints; Amgen olpasiran read-across; Roivant mosliciguat Phase 2 met all endpoints with record PVR reduction |\n| Trade | Canada retaliatory tariffs 15-50% on $20B+ of U.S. goods effective Tuesday; Trump directs removal of Canadian products from GSA schedules |\n| Index | Bloom Energy joins S&P 500 Sept 21; SpaceX Nasdaq-100 rebalance could trigger $15.5B passive buying Sept 18; D-Wave and Rigetti each receive $100M CHIPS Act funding with Commerce equity stakes |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **Wed Sept 10**: Apple "Surprise and Shine" event at 1pm ET — iPhone 18 Pro, foldable iPhone, Apple Watch Series 12 expected. SpaceX third share unlock (~700M shares).\n- **Thu Sept 11**: PPI (August) at 8:30am ET. **Oracle** (ORCL) Q1 FY27 earnings after close — consensus EPS $1.67, revenue $19.13B. **Adobe** (ADBE) Q3 earnings after close — consensus EPS $5.84, revenue $6.70B. ECB rate decision expected (+25bp to 2.50%).\n- **Fri Sept 12**: CPI (August) at 8:30am ET — headline CPI est. 3.4%, core CPI est. 2.4%. U. of Michigan consumer sentiment (prelim Sept) at 10am ET. **AeroVironment** (AVAV), **RH**, **American Eagle** (AEO), **Academy Sports** (ASO), **Chewy** (CHWY), **Signet** (SIG) earnings.\n- **Mon Sept 15**: Clarity Act vote in Senate (crypto regulatory framework).\n- **Tue Sept 16**: FOMC rate decision — 58% probability of 25bp hike.\n- **Thu Sept 18**: SpaceX Nasdaq-100 rebalance effective at close (passive buying).\n- **Mon Sept 21**: S&P 500 quarterly rebalance effective at open — BE, ILMN, EVPU join; TAP, BLDR, TTD exit.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **BNC** +52.7% on 183× avg volume: No identifiable catalyst; micro-cap ($216M) with no news flow — likely a technical/short-squeeze anomaly.\n- Historical stock return articles (GWW, ADI, GE, ENTG, TPR, LLY, etc.): Backward-looking compound return calculations with zero forward-looking content.\n- Hunter Biden LAPTOP memecoin launch on Base: No public-market impact; political theater with no connection to listed equities.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 405402, "output_tokens": 6893, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 2.02701, "total_cost_usd": 2.199335, "output_cost_usd": 0.172325, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-09-09T03:58:58.179338+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-09T04:02:16.532019+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from Anthropic Messages API response.usage. USD estimated from published claude.com/api pricing (input, 5m cache write, cache read, output) — Anthropic does not return dollar amounts on the response.", "total_cost_usd": 2.1993, "total_input_tokens": 405402, "total_output_tokens": 6893, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-09-09", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Channel: tech": 20, "Channel: movers": 27, "Channel: general": 100, "Channel: markets": 23, "Channel: earnings": 29, "Channel: equities": 32, "Channel: commodities": 14, "Ticker Group: r1d_screener": 20, "Ticker Group: vol_spike_5d": 1, "Ticker Group: ti65_mid_small": 4, "Ticker Group: ti65_mega_large": 12, "Channel: macro_economic_events": 16}, "articles_total": 298}, "upserted": 298, "api_by_fetch": {"ticker": {"BE": {"error": null, "api_rows": 8, "in_window": 8}, "ACN": {"error": null, "api_rows"