2026-09-23	daily	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 September 23, 2026 — Pre-Market Brief\n\n**One-liner**: Memory/storage names (SNDK +8.6%, MU +4.6%, STX +5.7%) extend a multi-week AI-infrastructure rally; SHOP +8.8% on Meta Muse/Shop Pay integration; IONQ +12% premarket on real-time quantum error correction breakthrough; CTAS and GIS beat estimates while futures dip as Trump threatens to "annihilate" Iran at UNGA and 10Y yield sits at 4.96%.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Top Movers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | Move | Cap | Catalyst | Theme |\n|--------|------|-----|----------|-------|\n| **SHOP** | +8.8% | Mega | Meta Muse/Shop Pay integration; Wedbush reiterates $176 PT | E-Commerce / AI Agents |\n| **SNDK** | +8.6% | Mega | Rosenblatt initiates Buy $2,400 PT; datacenter rev +437% YoY | Memory / NAND |\n| **STX** | +5.7% | Mega | Continued AI storage demand rally; 5D +19.4% | Memory / Storage |\n| **SCCO** | +4.8% | Mega | Copper strength; Canada mining capex deduction | Commodities |\n| **MU** | +4.6% | Mega | Pre-earnings positioning; Q4 EPS est $31.30 vs $3.03 YoY ⚠️ | Memory / DRAM |\n| **AMGN** | +4.2% | Mega | Phase 3 dazodalibep Sjögren's trial hits primary endpoint | Biotech |\n| **NEM** | +3.5% | Mega | Gold pullback limits gains; RBC raised PT to $155 | Gold Mining |\n| **MPWR** | +8.8% | Large | AI power delivery momentum continues; 5D +21.1% | AI Power |\n| **TWLO** | +7.8% | Large | TD Cowen raises PT to $300; agentic AI voice demand thesis | SaaS / AI Agents |\n| **MDB** | +7.0% | Large | Continued AI database rally; 5D +14.2% | SaaS / Database |\n| **ALAB** | +6.8% | Large | AI connectivity demand; 5D +42.9%; bullish call sweeps | AI Compute / Connectivity |\n| **LEN** | +6.6% | Large | Berkshire Hathaway discloses 23.7M share stake (~$1.2B) | Homebuilders |\n| **BFLY** | +21.7% | Small | Needham initiates Buy $10 PT; embedded ultrasound thesis | Med-Tech |\n| **EAF** | +20.0% | Small | No identified catalyst; 5D +57.4% | Industrials |\n| **INOD** | +19.1% | Small | Hunterbrook long report: "Meta's Muse could be big win" | AI Data Services |\n| **VICR** | +18.0% | Small | Raised Q3 rev guidance >20% seq. growth on VPD royalties | AI Power |\n| **SGRY** | +16.3% | Small | No identified catalyst; vol 5.0× avg | Healthcare Services |\n| **IONQ** | +12% PM | Mid | First real-time quantum error decoder on standard CPU | Quantum Computing |\n| **ONON** | +8.3% | Mid | $1B buyback; 2029 targets ≥CHF 5.6B sales, ≥22% adj EBITDA | Consumer / Apparel |\n| **VLO** | -3.7% | Mega | Jefferies downgrades to Hold $401 PT (was Buy) | Refining |\n| **DELL** | -4.8% | Mega | No new catalyst; Googlebook partnership with QCOM announced | Hardware |\n| **HPQ** | -2.1% | Large | 8-K: planning assumption for mid-single-digit PC unit decline in CY27 | Hardware |\n| **TEAM** | -3.1% | Large | No identified catalyst | SaaS |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Narrative Threads\n\n**Memory & Storage: AI Inference Demand Keeps Pricing Elevated** `Memory` → ongoing\n\n**SNDK** +8.6%, **MU** +4.6%, **STX** +5.7%, **WDC** +3.7% — the memory/storage complex extends a multi-week rally driven by AI inference and training storage requirements. DRAM is the only AI input metric Fidelity's Jurrien Timmer says is "still going up."\n\n- Rosenblatt initiated **SNDK** at Buy with a $2,400 PT; datacenter revenue grew 437% in FY26 to $5.15B; Q4 datacenter rev $2.98B (+1,298% YoY); non-GAAP gross margin hit 84.6% in Q4.\n- **SNDK** has signed 10 multi-year supply agreements totaling $93.9B minimum contracted revenue at floor pricing; ~50% of FY27 bits and ~67% of FY28 bits covered.\n- **MU** reports Q4 earnings Sept. 30 ⚠️; consensus EPS $31.30 vs $3.03 YoY; revenue est. $50.62B vs $11.31B YoY. RBC maintains Outperform with $1,500 PT.\n- Michael Burry added to MU shorts and SOXX shorts, citing Acer CEO's warning that memory inventories are "actually overflowing" and Chinese supplier CXMT capacity ramp.\n- CLSA analyst says talk of AI chip cycle peaking in 2028 is "utterly wrong"; estimates GPU/custom chip demand exceeds supply by ~73%, shortage lasting until ~2030.\n- Nasdaq 100 up 180.1% since start of 2023, best 4-year run since 1999; SNDK +695.8% YTD, MU +278.9% YTD, INTC +229.6% YTD.\n\n**Agentic AI Reshapes CPU & Commerce Economics** `AI Compute / SaaS / E-Commerce` → ongoing\n\nMeta's Muse AI agent triggered a broad revaluation across CPU, commerce, and communications names. **AMD** +1.0% (5D +23.2%), **INTC** +1.2% (5D +26.4%), **SHOP** +8.8%, **TWLO** +7.8%, **INOD** +19.1%.\n\n- **AMD** crossed $1T market cap Monday on agentic AI CPU thesis; CEO Lisa Su raised 2030 server CPU TAM forecast from $60B to >$120B; AMD +187% YTD vs NVDA +22% YTD — widest gap since ChatGPT launch.\n- **SHOP** partnered with Meta to integrate Shop Pay into Muse; CEO Lütke and Zuckerberg confirmed on X. Amazon blocked Muse from shopping on its platform, citing Conditions of Use violation.\n- **TWLO**: TD Cowen raised PT to $300 (from $260), Buy; Rosenblatt raised to $290, Buy — both cite voice as AI agent growth vector and Muse-driven communications demand.\n- **INOD** +19.1% after Hunterbrook Media published long thesis: "Meta's Muse Could Be Big Win For Innodata."\n- JPMorgan's Doug Anmuth: Muse could be "most widely used consumer AI app since ChatGPT"; ~2.5M U.S. downloads through Sept. 19; iOS downloads outpaced ChatGPT's first 12 days (1.43M vs 1.37M). PT $820 Overweight on META.\n- OpenAI launched GPT-6 Sol and Luna with API prices up to 50% lower than GPT-5.6; Box CEO Levie says falling AI costs "dramatically increase" agent use cases.\n- **MSFT** planning 30-50% Copilot discounts for large customers (1,000+ seats: ~30% off; 10,000+ seats: ~50% off); Stifel upgrades to Buy $575 PT; Oppenheimer raises to $570 PT.\n\n**AI Power Delivery & Connectivity** `AI Compute / Power` → ongoing\n\n**VICR** +18.0%, **MPWR** +8.8%, **ALAB** +6.8% continue rallying on AI datacenter power and connectivity demand.\n\n- **VICR** raised Q3 sequential revenue growth guidance from ~10% to >20% on royalties from new Vertical Power Delivery licensing agreement. Roth Capital reiterates Buy $375 PT; Needham reiterates Buy $320 PT.\n- **MPWR** 5D +21.1%, vol 2.5× avg — AI power delivery momentum extending from Monday's 7.5% gain.\n- **ALAB** 5D +42.9%; bullish call sweeps on Jan 2027 $150 strike ($90K notional).\n\n**Quantum Computing Sector Catalyst** `Quantum` → new\n\n**IONQ** +12-14% premarket after demonstrating industry-first end-to-end real-time quantum error correction decoder on a single standard CPU — validated across 408 logical qubits and >31.5M quantum operations with 0.02% processing overhead.\n\n- IONQ also announced Superion 256 quantum computer to be first installed in 2027 at Nvidia's Quantum Research Center.\n- D-Wave (**QBTS**) +5.6% after hours; partnered with CGI for enterprise quantum adoption.\n- Rigetti (**RGTI**) +5.6% after hours; signed $100M CHIPS Act funding agreement with U.S. Commerce Department.\n- Quantum World Congress Sept. 23-25 with DOE, OSTP, Microsoft, IBM executives expected to address commercialization.\n- IONQ carries Buy consensus, avg PT $67.75; Wedbush maintains Outperform $75 PT (Sept. 22). Next earnings ~Nov. 4 ⚠️.\n\n**Earnings: CTAS, PAYX, GIS, CBRL Beat Estimates** `Earnings` → new\n\n- **CTAS** Q1 adj. EPS $1.39 vs $1.35 est (+2.2%); sales $3.014B vs $2.984B est (+1.0%); organic revenue +8.9%. Raised FY27 adj. EPS guide to $5.45-$5.54 (from $5.36-$5.50) vs $5.50 est; raised FY27 sales guide to $12.15B-$12.27B vs $12.22B est.\n- **PAYX** Q1 adj. EPS $1.34 vs $1.32 est; sales $1.631B vs $1.627B est. Lowered FY27 adj. EPS guidance to $5.90-$6.01 vs $5.96 est; lowered FY27 sales guide to $6.838B-$6.903B vs $6.867B est.\n- **GIS** Q1 adj. EPS $0.75 vs $0.72 est; sales $4.390B vs $4.351B est. Organic net sales essentially flat; CEO reaffirms FY27 guidance.\n- **CBRL** Q4 adj. EPS $0.99 vs $0.15 est (+560%); sales $849.3M vs $836.9M est; shares +7.9% premarket.\n\n**Precious Metals & Copper: Gold Pulls Back, Copper Firm** `Commodities` → ongoing\n\n**NEM** +3.5%, **AEM** +3.2%, **WPM** +4.6%, **PAAS** +4.8%, **SCCO** +4.8%, **FCX** +3.5%.\n\n- Gold spot fell 0.90% to ~$4,319/oz as hawkish Fed signals (Musalem: further hikes may be needed) offset geopolitical bid.\n- China imported >1,000 tons of gold in first 8 months of 2026, spending record $158.8B — far exceeding all of 2025 (866 tons, $96.5B).\n- NEM: RBC maintains Outperform, raised PT to $155; Bernstein Outperform $144 PT; consensus Strong Buy avg PT $141.80.\n- Canada's "Productivity Mega Deduction" cuts marginal effective tax rate on new mining investment from ~13% to 6.4% — lowest of any major economy. TD Cowen picks Barrick ($59 PT, 38% upside) and Equinox Gold (C$20 PT).\n\n**Refiners Under Pressure** `Energy / Refining` → ongoing\n\n**VLO** -3.7%, **MPC** -2.4%, **PSX** -0.9%.\n\n- Jefferies downgraded both **MPC** (Buy→Hold, $413 PT) and **VLO** (Buy→Hold, $401 PT).\n- Goldman Sachs maintains Buy on VLO, raises PT from $365 to $457 — divergent view from Jefferies.\n- Trump energy adviser Jarrod Agen pointed to "refining capacity" bottleneck for fuel prices; national avg diesel $6.53/gal, gasoline $4.47/gal.\n- WTI crude -0.30% to ~$90.25; Brent -0.27% to ~$98.98. ARK Invest says oil could drop to $30-35/bbl once Strait of Hormuz reopens.\n- Trump at UNGA: "Will a deal be made with Iran…or do I annihilate the Islamic Republic?" Also noted "positive" talks via mediators.\n\n**Homebuilders: Berkshire Bid Lifts LEN** `Homebuilders` → new\n\n**LEN** +6.6% after Berkshire Hathaway disclosed 23.72M Class A shares (≥10% beneficial ownership); added 2.67M shares Sept. 17-21 at $76.39-$79.41 weighted avg.\n\n- LEN Q3 adj. EPS $1.23 missed $1.30 est; revenue $8.05B missed $8.31B est. New orders -9% YoY; ASP on new orders $359K vs $370K est.\n- KB Home Q3 EPS $1.05 beat $0.89 est; revenue $1.297B beat $1.294B est; shares -1.8% after hours.\n- Keefe Bruyette maintains Underperform on LEN, lowers PT to $75.\n\n**📡 Undercurrents** *(developing, not yet dominant)*\n- **Howard Marks** (Oaktree) warns >$5T in AI datacenter investment through 2030 competes with U.S. Treasury issuance for capital, putting upward pressure on interest rates. 10Y at 4.96%; FedWatch shows 57.6% probability of Fed hike at October meeting.\n- **HPQ** filed 8-K disclosing preliminary planning assumption for mid-single-digit PC unit volume decline in CY2027 — a headwind for the PC hardware cycle.\n- **Broadcom** faces China probe: Sasac investigating AVGO switch prevalence in state-owned data centers (found in up to 90%); may issue guidance to reduce usage.\n- **FWDI** +5.6% (5D +40.2%) commenced ~$25M offering of 3.125M shares at $8/share; described as "leading Solana treasury company."\n- **RCL** +1.8% premarket on $3B deal for 50% stake in Sandals Resorts at ~10× forward EBITDA; expected close early 2027. Morgan Stanley financing.\n\n---\n\n### 📰 Channel Pulse\n\n| Channel | Material fact |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Earnings | CTAS Q1 adj. EPS $1.39 beat $1.35 est; raised FY27 EPS guide to $5.45-$5.54. CBRL Q4 adj. EPS $0.99 vs $0.15 est. GIS Q1 adj. EPS $0.75 beat $0.72 est. |\n| Macro | Flash U.S. manufacturing & services PMIs due 9:45 AM ET. 10Y yield 4.96%; FedWatch 57.6% chance of Fed hike in October. CNN Fear & Greed at 35 ("Fear"). |\n| Geopolitics | Trump at UNGA: threatened to "annihilate" Iran if no peace deal; separately said "very good meeting" with Iranian delegation. WTI ~$90.25. |\n| Tech | OpenAI launched GPT-6 Sol and Luna with 50% API price cuts. Microsoft planning 30-50% Copilot discounts for large enterprise. Alibaba expanding cloud regions to Turkey, Finland, Netherlands within 12 months. |\n| Commodities | Gold -0.90% to ~$4,319/oz. WTI crude -0.30%. China gold imports >1,000 tons in Jan-Aug 2026 ($158.8B). |\n| Analyst Actions | Jefferies downgraded MPC & VLO to Hold. Rosenblatt initiated SNDK Buy $2,400 PT. Needham initiated BFLY Buy $10 PT. UBS initiated CORZ, CIFR, CRWV, APLD all at Buy. Stifel upgraded MSFT to Buy $575 PT. |\n| Cybersecurity | ShinyHunters claims FBI data breach affecting "almost all" agents; some data verified against credit records including FBI Director Kash Patel. |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 On The Radar\n\n- **MU Q4 earnings Sept. 30** ⚠️: Consensus adj. EPS $31.30 (vs $3.03 YoY); revenue $50.62B (vs $11.31B YoY). Michael Burry adding to short position.\n- **ACN Q4 earnings Oct. 1** ⚠️: Consensus EPS $3.18 vs $3.03 YoY; revenue $18.04B. Wells Fargo downgraded to Equal-Weight $194 PT on Sept. 14.\n- **DRI Q1 earnings Sept. 24** ⚠️: Consensus EPS $2.05; revenue $3.21B. Seaport initiated Buy $240 PT.\n- **McDonald's Investor Day Sept. 23**: Targets operating margin low-to-mid 50% by 2030; plans $8.5B in franchisee support through 2036.\n- **Trump-Xi state dinner Thursday**: Tech CEOs (Musk, Altman, Bezos, Cook, Huang, Pichai) expected; Chinese business delegation participation uncertain over investment disputes.\n- **Quantum World Congress Sept. 23-25**: DOE, OSTP, Microsoft, IBM executives discussing quantum commercialization.\n- **IONQ** next earnings ~Nov. 4; EPS est. loss $0.72; revenue est. $143.5M (vs $39.87M YoY).\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 What to Ignore Today\n\n- **EAF** +20.0% and **SGRY** +16.3%: No identifiable catalyst for either move; likely low-float momentum/short-squeeze dynamics.\n- **JAGX** after-hours noise: +1,190% Tuesday on FDA fee waiver for Mytesi — a procedural waiver, not an approval; $17.9M market cap micro-cap with extreme vol.\n- Political commentary on Medicaid work requirements, birthright citizenship, and AI regulation bills — no near-term legislative or market impact.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "step4_synthesis", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "api_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_tokens": 288686, "output_tokens": 4937, "pricing_model": "claude-opus-4-6", "input_cost_usd": 1.44343, "total_cost_usd": 1.566855, "output_cost_usd": 0.123425, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tok