2026-06-28	losers	benzinga	complete	### 🗓 2026-06-28 — R1D Losers Brief\n\n**One-liner**: A sweeping AI‑chip rout pounded semiconductor and hardware names as money rotated into software, while ON Semiconductor’s $7 bn all‑stock Synaptics deal, a Visteon downgrade, and redemption strains at Morgan Stanley added distinct company‑specific pressure.\n\n---\n\n### 📉 Losers At a Glance\n\n| Ticker | 1D | Cap | Sector | Driver type | Catalyst (≤12 words) |\n|--------|---:|-----|--------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **WDC** | **-12.0%** | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | AI‑chip selloff; profit‑taking after Micron’s blowout quarter. |\n| **STX** | **-11.3%** | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Memory/hardware rout; fall‑out from Broadcom AI guidance disappointment. |\n| **SNDK** | -7.4% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | NAND names hit by sector rotation out of chips. |\n| **ADI** | -6.8% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Analog chip weakness amid broad semiconductor profit‑taking. |\n| **VRT** | -6.5% | Mega cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n| **QCOM** | -6.1% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Fell with chips despite mid‑week investor‑day positivity. |\n| **ANET** | -6.1% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Networking hardware swept up in AI‑infra unwind. |\n| **TXN** | -5.4% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Analog/embedded chips dragged by sector weakness. |\n| **MRVL** | -5.1% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Data‑center chip play under pressure in chip rout. |\n| **ARM** | -5.0% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Valuation reset as AI‑exposed chip stocks sold. |\n| **MU** | -4.8% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Profit‑taking after post‑earnings surge; broader risk‑off. |\n| **TT** | -4.7% | Mega cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n| **KLAC** | -4.2% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Wafer‑fab equipment caught in chip decline. |\n| **DELL** | -4.2% | Mega cap | Technology | Sector | Hardware name facing AI‑memory cost margin fears. |\n| **MS** | -4.1% | Mega cap | Financial Services | Idiosyncratic | Flagship private‑credit fund limited redemptions amid heavy exit requests. |\n| **ON** | **-23.2%** | Large cap | Technology | Idiosyncratic | $7 bn all‑stock Synaptics acquisition dilutes ON shares. |\n| **BE** | **-10.1%** | Large cap | Industrials | Idiosyncratic | Profit‑taking after run‑up; no fresh negative news. |\n| **FLEX** | -8.6% | Large cap | Technology | Sector | Electronics manufacturing hit by chip/tech selloff. |\n| **TSEM** | -8.3% | Large cap | Technology | Sector | Israeli foundry fell with semiconductor slide. |\n| **ENTG** | -8.1% | Large cap | Technology | Sector | Chip materials/equipment names swept lower. |\n| **NOK** | -8.1% | Large cap | Technology | Sector | Network gear dragged by risk‑off in tech. |\n| **UMC** | -7.5% | Large cap | Technology | Sector | Pure‑play foundry sold as semis under pressure. |\n| **GFS** | -7.0% | Large cap | Technology | Sector | Global foundry declined with industry rotation. |\n| **MCHP** | -6.8% | Large cap | Technology | Sector | Chipmaker pulled back in broad semiconductor selloff. |\n| **NXPI** | -6.7% | Large cap | Technology | Sector | Automotive/industrial chip name fell with sector. |\n| **COCO** | **-13.1%** | Mid & small cap | Consumer Defensive | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n| **TMDX** | **-12.3%** | Mid & small cap | Healthcare | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n| **DIOD** | **-11.5%** | Mid & small cap | Technology | Sector | Discrete semis follow broader chip rout. |\n| **ARQQ** | **-11.2%** | Mid & small cap | Technology | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n| **VC** | **-10.3%** | Mid & small cap | Consumer Cyclical | Idiosyncratic | Baird downgraded to Neutral, maintained $121 target. |\n| **FORM** | **-10.1%** | Mid & small cap | Technology | Sector | Semiconductor test/measurement hit in sector selloff. |\n| **BHC** | **-10.0%** | Mid & small cap | Healthcare | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n| **EROC** | -9.2% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n| **FRO** | -8.6% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n| **HYLN** | -8.5% | Mid & small cap | Industrials | Unknown | No material ticker‑specific news in window. |\n\n---\n\n### 🧭 Thematic / Sector Weakness\n\n**Semiconductor / AI‑Infrastructure Rout** → `Technology`\n\n- **WDC** (-12.0%), **STX** (-11.3%), **SNDK** (-7.4%), **ADI** (-6.8%), **QCOM** (-6.1%), **ANET** (-6.1%), **TXN** (-5.4%), **MRVL** (-5.1%), **ARM** (-5.0%), **MU** (-4.8%), **KLAC** (-4.2%), **DELL** (-4.2%), **FLEX** (-8.6%), **TSEM** (-8.3%), **ENTG** (-8.1%), **NOK** (-8.1%), **UMC** (-7.5%), **GFS** (-7.0%), **MCHP** (-6.8%), **NXPI** (-6.7%), **DIOD** (-11.5%), **FORM** (-10.1%).\n- The VanEck Semiconductor ETF (SMH) sank 3.4% on Friday as investors rotated out of chipmakers and AI‑hardware names into software and defensives (IGV +3.2%).  \n- Selling was “deepening across the complex” and extended pressure that had been building since Broadcom’s recent AI‑revenue guidance disappointed (Benzinga Pro).  \n- Sharpest pain was in memory and storage: WDC dropped over 10% after Micron’s blowout quarter earlier in the week failed to sustain gains; profit‑taking hit STX, SNDK, and MU.  \n- Broader AI‑infra supply chain and equipment names (ANET, KLAC, ENTG, FORM) followed the unwind.  \n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Idiosyncratic Movers\n\n**ON** (-23.2%, Large cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- ON Semiconductor announced an all‑stock acquisition of Synaptics in a ~$7 bn enterprise‑value deal.  \n- ON shares tumbled as the fixed 1.35‑share‑for‑1 exchange ratio implied dilution; the transaction is expected to close in mid‑2027 and ON reaffirmed its outlook, but the stock was penalized sharply.  \n\n**MS** (-4.1%, Mega cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Morgan Stanley’s $7 bn North Haven Private Income Fund fulfilled only 43% of second‑quarter redemption requests after investor demands reached ~11.6% of outstanding units.  \n- The partial gating, following similar moves by Apollo and Blackstone, underscored ongoing liquidity strains in private credit.  \n\n**VC** (-10.3%, Mid & small cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Baird downgraded Visteon to Neutral from Outperform, keeping a $121 price target, triggering a sharp selloff despite the company earlier announcing an $800 mn buyback plan.  \n\n**BE** (-10.1%, Large cap) → Idiosyncratic  \n- Bloom Energy pulled back after recently hitting new highs; no fresh negative corporate news. Traders cited profit‑taking and cooling risk appetite as S&P 500 futures fell.  \n\n**COCO, TMDX, ARQQ, BHC, EROC, FRO, HYLN** → Unknown  \n- No material ticker‑specific news in the provided Benzinga articles. Moves may reflect technical factors, thin liquidity, or sympathy with broader market weakness.  \n\n**VRT, TT** (Mega cap, Industrials) → Unknown  \n- No ticker‑specific articles explain the declines. Likely part of a broader industrial pullback or rotation, but direct catalyst not confirmed.  \n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sector Roll-up\n\n| Sector | Losers (count) | Avg 1D | Shared driver? |\n|--------|---------------:|-------:|----------------|\n| Technology | 23 | -7.8% | Yes – AI‑chip sector rout. |\n| Industrials | 5 | -7.8% | Partial – BE idiosyncratic; others thin news. |\n| Consumer Cyclical | 1 | -10.3% | No – downgrade driven. |\n| Consumer Defensive | 1 | -13.1% | No – unknown catalyst. |\n| Financial Services | 1 | -4.1% | No – idiosyncratic private‑credit gating. |\n| Healthcare | 2 | -11.2% | No – unknown catalysts. |\n\n---\n\n### 👁 Watch\n\n- **Memory cycle durability**: Micron’s strong quarter was immediately sold; next memory read‑across comes from **Western Digital** earnings expected **July 29**.  \n- **Synaptics integration**: ON Semiconductor’s $7 bn deal won’t close until **mid‑2027**; regulatory and shareholder approvals are pending, and the $235 mn/$320 mn termination fees keep risk elevated.  \n- **Private‑credit liquidity**: Morgan Stanley’s gating follows similar steps from Apollo, Blackstone, BlackRock; continued heavy redemption requests could pressure net asset values and investor sentiment.  \n- **Russell reconstitution**: The annual Russell rebalance effective **June 26** may exaggerate end‑of‑week moves for small‑ and mid‑cap names as index funds adjust.	\N	{"calls": [{"step": "synthesis", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "api_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_tokens": 11, "output_tokens": 4958, "pricing_model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "input_cost_usd": 0.000005, "total_cost_usd": 0.005267, "output_cost_usd": 0.004313, "cache_read_cost_usd": 0.000948, "cache_write_cost_usd": 0.0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 261632, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}], "call_count": 1, "started_at": "2026-06-28T16:58:26.223158+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-06-28T16:59:27.096862+00:00", "current_step": null, "pricing_note": "Token counts from DeepSeek Chat Completions API response.usage. USD estimated from published api-docs.deepseek.com pricing (input cache miss, cache hit, output).", "total_cost_usd": 0.0053, "total_input_tokens": 11, "total_output_tokens": 4958, "total_cache_read_input_tokens": 261632, "total_cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}	{"asof": "2026-06-28", "counts": {"prompt": {"by_section": {"Ticker: Bottom 15 · 1D return · Mega cap": 68, "Ticker: Bottom 10 · 1D return · Large cap": 27, "Ticker: Bottom 10 · 1D return · Mid & small cap": 7}, "articles_total": 102}, "upserted": 102, "api_by_fetch": {"ticker": {"BE": {"error": null, "api_rows": 4, "in_window": 4}, "MS": {"error": null, "api_rows": 3, "in_window": 3}, "MU": {"error": null, "api_rows": 25, "in_window": 25}, "ON": {"error": null, "api_rows": 24, "in_window": 24}, "TT": {"error": null, "api_rows": 0, "in_window": 0}, "VC": {"error": null, "api_rows": 7, "in_window": 7}, "ADI"