 hike: revenue $90.1M (+54% YoY) vs. ~$76.5M FactSet consensus, adjusted EBITDA ~$25M (~28% margin, nearly doubled), net income more than doubled; full‑year 2026 revenue growth outlook raised from 35%+ to ~40%+ (reported around 2026-05-08)", "Disclosure of a new Big Tech/hyperscaler engagement expected to contribute about $51M of revenue in 2026, alongside broader Big Tech customer expansion and launch of an Evaluation and Observability Platform for agentic AI systems, positioning Innodata as core AI data/infra rather than a generic services vendor (highlighted in post‑earnings commentary and coverage around 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-11)", "Massive post‑earnings re‑rating and momentum follow‑through: stock ripped ~85–92% in a single session on volume >6x normal, moving from mid‑$40s to an $84.89 close on 2026-05-08, then spiking intraday to ~$114.77 and closing around $101.83 in the next session; the name is now appearing on top‑20d/top‑5d return and volume‑spike screens, pulling in momentum/quant and short‑covering flows (2026-05-08 to 2026-05-12)", "Supportive Street response despite rich valuation: Wedbush reaffirmed Outperform, raised its price target to $80, and kept Innodata on the IVES AI 30 list; consensus targets clustered around ~$90 while the stock traded around or above that level, reinforcing an 'AI premium' narrative even as valuation screens (e.g., Simply Wall St DCF, P/E vs peers) flag the stock as overvalued (coverage updates in the days after Q1 2026 earnings)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=100"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.41x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 20.0, "reason": "dr5=99.1% atr=13.4% norm=3.31"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 20, "reason": "3 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 2d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=116.8, 60d=101.8)"}}, "news_materiality": 3, "theme_fit_reason": "This directly matches the trader’s stated thesis: raised revenue guidance, hyperscaler customer pull-through, and an agentic-AI/product angle. It also fits multiple core watchlist patterns around AI infrastructure, big-ticket customer wins, and re-rating momentum.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "The news strongly supports and extends the trader’s existing thesis: guidance was raised, hyperscaler demand is real and quantified, and the company is being repositioned as an AI infrastructure/data platform story. Combined with the extreme momentum breakout, this is exactly the kind of beat-and-raise plus thematic AI customer-wins setup the trader likes.", "last_event_magnitude": 6.25, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-11", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a highly material catalyst: Q1 revenue and profitability blew past expectations, management raised full-year growth guidance, and the company disclosed a new Big Tech/hyperscaler engagement expected to add about $51M of 2026 revenue. The combination of beat-and-raise plus a named hyperscaler-related demand driver is the kind of news that can fundamentally re-rate the stock."}, {"dr_1": -0.66, "dr_5": 53.25, "atr20": 9.27, "dr_20": 66.08, "dr_60": 77.85, "sector": "Industrials", "ticker": "RKLB", "sources": ["top_5d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "PICK", "industry": "Aerospace & Defense", "theme_fit": 3, "market_cap": 67916426799, "rsi_mktcap": 99, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Rocket Lab USA, Inc.", "news_summary": "The recent surge in RKLB is primarily a fundamental re‑rating off a very strong Q1 2026 beat-and-raise plus a step‑function jump in long‑term visibility. Rocket Lab delivered record revenue and margins, a $2.2B backlog that’s growing faster than current sales, and high-profile U.S. defense work (Space-Based Interceptor and a separate ~$190M contract under the Golden Dome initiative, alongside a $30M Anduril hypersonics deal), all of which reposition it as a core national security and space-systems supplier rather than just a sma