ews and thematic fit this trader likes: a real earnings beat-and-raise plus named, quantified defense contracts that expand the long-term story. The stock is also in a clear momentum breakout, which reinforces the setup rather than substituting for it. This news supports and extends the re-rating thesis by turning Rocket Lab from a launch-name into a broader national-security and space-systems growth story.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.1725, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-11", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a major fundamental catalyst: a blowout Q1 beat-and-raise, record gross margins, a larger backlog, and multiple high-value defense wins including Space-Based Interceptor work, a separate ~$190M contract, and a $30M Anduril hypersonics deal. The news is clearly material and not just a sympathy move, because it changes the medium-term revenue and margin visibility for the business."}, {"dr_1": -17.98, "dr_5": 68.69, "atr20": 12.68, "dr_20": 43.04, "dr_60": 14.68, "sector": "Utilities", "ticker": "FLNC", "sources": ["top_5d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "PICK", "industry": "Renewable Utilities", "theme_fit": 3, "market_cap": 4655607632, "rsi_mktcap": 100, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Fluence Energy, Inc.", "news_summary": "The big move in FLNC over the last week is primarily a re‑rating off its early‑May earnings and backlog narrative, not a random squeeze. The company showed a clean inflection toward profitability (swinging to positive net income with improving margins), confirmed a multi‑billion‑dollar contracted backlog and sharply higher order intake, and highlighted a fast‑growing data‑center/hyperscaler pipeline that ties it directly into the AI power build‑out. That combination – proof the business model is working, visibility on multi‑year demand, and an emerging hyperscaler angle – triggered aggressive buying in a name that had been heavily sold and volatile, amplifying the move via short covering and technical breakout behavior on 1.7x+ normal volume.", "current_price": 21.17, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "hyperscaler-ai-infrastructure", "optical-and-data-center-gear", "turnaround-and-recovery", "special-situation-re-rating", "new-product-or-platform-inflection"], "momentum_score": 84.15, "verdict_claude": "PICK", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 1.71, "composite_score": 93.66, "last_event_date": "2026-05-08", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-surprise-momentum", "data-center-infrastructure", "ai-power-buildout", "turnaround-and-recovery", "special-situation-re-rating", "small-cap-relief-rally"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["FQ2/FY25 earnings print with improved profitability and positive net income (net income ~$6.3M vs loss prior quarter), alongside FY revenue run-rate in the ~$2.7B range and maintained path to profitability (reported in early May 2026)", "Order momentum and backlog strength: management commentary around record contracted backlog in the mid‑single‑digit billions of dollars and year‑to‑date order intake roughly doubling YoY, with ~50% of new orders from new customers, signaling sustained demand for utility-scale storage", "Data-center / hyperscaler growth narrative: company discussion of rapidly expanding data-center storage pipeline (double‑digit GWh, up sharply QoQ) and MSAs signed with two major hyperscalers, with first purchase order expected in the near term, fueling an AI/data‑center–infrastructure re‑rating", "Sector and sentiment tailwinds: investors rotating into grid-scale storage and AI‑power infrastructure names following stronger demand commentary across power/energy‑storage peers, plus a high‑short‑interest squeeze/technical breakout after a multi‑month trough and prior 52‑week low near $4–5"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=100"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.71x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 16.15, "reason": "dr5=68.7% atr=12.7% norm=2.42"}, "multi_screen":