 YoY to $443M; reaffirmed full‑year 2026 sales guidance of $2.6–$2.7B (in line with ~$2.64B Street) and reiterated adjusted EPS loss guidance (-$0.20 to -$0.15) (2026-05-07)", "Momentum/turnaround re‑rating from penny‑stock levels: stock moved from sub‑$1 (as low as ~$0.88–0.91 in mid‑April) to >$2 into earnings on growing AI/private‑cloud narrative and new senior leadership in operations/international for Private Cloud (appointments on 2026-04-08, discussed in early‑May coverage)", "Post‑earnings/partner short squeeze and technical chase: shares up ~200%+ since May 7 with multiple 50%+ single‑day spikes, heavy volume (~1.5x+ 10‑day average, 40–50M share days) and indicators like RSI >80, 20‑day/200‑day SMAs far below current price, suggesting forced short covering and momentum buying (2026-05-08 to 2026-05-12)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=99"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.57x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 17.96, "reason": "dr5=132.9% atr=22.1% norm=2.69"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 20, "reason": "4 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=356.5, 60d=1247.0)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This strongly matches the trader’s own thesis of \\"Specific governance enabling AMD compute boxes - New vertical,\\" because the AMD collaboration directly extends that idea. It also fits the trader’s recurring appetite for AI infrastructure, turnaround/re-rating, and momentum breakouts.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "The current news supports and extends the trader’s existing thesis rather than weakening it: Rackspace is showing a turnaround inflection, and the AMD AI/governed-compute angle gives the move a credible thematic backbone. Even though the move is amplified by short covering and momentum, the combination of earnings upside, guidance stabilization, and a thesis-aligned AI partnership is enough to qualify as a PICK.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.1599, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-12", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a real catalyst: Rackspace posted a Q1 2026 beat with a return to GAAP profitability, improved public cloud growth, and reaffirmed FY26 guidance, while also highlighting an AMD AI infrastructure partnership. It is material, but not a game-changing marquee customer win or multi-year named contract."}, {"dr_1": -2.98, "dr_5": 42.86, "atr20": 11.69, "dr_20": 82.4, "dr_60": 85.67, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "GSIT", "sources": ["top_20d", "top_5d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "PICK", "industry": "Semiconductors", "theme_fit": 3, "market_cap": 341985721, "rsi_mktcap": 99, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "GSI Technology, Inc.", "news_summary": "The market is reacting less to a single hard fundamental event and more to a re‑rating of GSIT as a speculative AI/APU hardware play, amplified by a large recent funding round that shores up its balance sheet and gives it runway to pursue that strategy. Recent earnings and commentary around AI‑driven demand have provided just enough fundamental support for this narrative, but the magnitude of the move is being driven by momentum dynamics—high beta, low float, a major volume spike on May 11, and heavy retail/technical interest—rather than a specific named hyperscaler win or a transformational contract. In other words, this is primarily an AI‑theme/technical squeeze with some earnings and capital‑raise context, not a clear-cut big-ticket customer or guidance inflection.", "current_price": 11.4, "matched_themes": ["ai-compute", "edgeai", "memory-and-interconnect", "breakout-and-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst", "special-situation-re-rating"], "momentum_score": 90.93, "verdict_claude": "PICK", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 2.52, "composite_score": 86.37, "last_event_date": "2026-05-11", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["ai-compute", "edgeai", "memory-and-intercon