t and the follow-on analyst re-rating. The key catalyst was Progyny’s 2026-05-07 report: adjusted EPS of $0.50 versus $0.26 expected on revenue of about $328.5M, which triggered a sharp post-earnings surge and renewed momentum. The move also got support from higher price targets and signs of continued client wins, including roughly 900,000 lives added in the selling season. ", "current_price": 23.2724, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "turnaround-and-recovery", "breakout-and-momentum"], "momentum_score": 65.27, "verdict_claude": "PICK", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 1.17, "composite_score": 86.11, "last_event_date": "2026-05-08", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "earnings-surprise-momentum", "breakout-and-momentum", "turnaround-and-recovery"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Progyny reported Q1 2026 results on 2026-05-07 and the stock surged about 19-24% intraday afterward, with adjusted EPS of $0.50 versus a $0.26 FactSet consensus estimate and revenue of about $328.5M, indicating a large earnings beat.", "Multiple analyst updates followed the print, including BofA raising its price target to $34 from $30 (about 28 days ago in the provided feed) and Cantor Fitzgerald lifting its target to $31 from $28 while keeping Overweight, reinforcing the post-earnings re-rating.", "The company’s strong quarterly print and better-than-expected selling season added roughly 900,000 lives, which points to fresh commercial momentum rather than just technical trading.", "Separately, the stock also reached a new 52-week high at $27.52 after a roughly 87% gain over the past year, with reported management share repurchases and a $200M buyback program supporting sentiment."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=96"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 1.17x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 15.27, "reason": "dr5=23.8% atr=4.7% norm=2.29"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 0.0, "reason":