 trader flagged. Management raised full-year optical guidance ~27% ($110–130M → $150–170M) and signaled Q2 acceleration, anchored by named Keystone transceiver ramp and multi-hyperscaler wins with 2027 backlog building."}, {"dr_1": -14.59, "dr_5": 8.3, "atr20": 14.94, "dr_20": 96.25, "dr_60": 133.37, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "NVTS", "sources": ["top_20d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "PICK", "industry": "Semiconductors", "theme_fit": 3, "market_cap": 5293599450, "rsi_mktcap": 99, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Navitas Semiconductor Corporation", "news_summary": "The market is mostly reacting to a structural re‑rating of Navitas as a leveraged way to play AI data‑center power and next‑gen energy infrastructure, anchored by its strategic alliance with NVIDIA and the ramp of its SiC/GaN platforms. The recent product launch of 5th‑gen 1200 V GeneSiC SiC MOSFETs for AI data centers and grid/EV use, plus Q1 2026 results that emphasized a large and growing design‑win pipeline, have given investors a tangible path from story to revenues. Those fundamental catalysts have then been amplified by momentum: NVTS has nearly doubled in 20 days and more than doubled in 60 days, with very high RSI and volume, so a meaningful part of the latest swing (including the -14.6% 1‑day giveback) reflects technical/positioning dynamics rather than fresh news.", "current_price": 19.37, "matched_themes": ["ai-hyperscaler-deals", "ai-power-buildout", "power-and-wide-bandgap", "new-product-or-platform-inflection", "breakout-and-momentum"], "momentum_score": 63.66, "verdict_claude": "PICK", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 1.18, "composite_score": 85.46, "last_event_date": "2026-05-11", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["ai-hyperscaler-deals", "ai-power-buildout", "power-and-wide-bandgap", "new-product-or-platform-inflection", "breakout-and-momentum", "earnings-surprise-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Strategic allian