t reiterated its full‑year 2026 guidance, signaling that the Conway capacity ramp and single‑serve/canned beverage growth are tracking on plan (company release, 2026-05-07)", "Valuation re‑rating following prior Benchmark and other broker targets: after being cut to $7–8 in late 2025, Benchmark subsequently raised its WEST price target to $10 while maintaining a Buy, implying material upside from where the stock had been trading near its lows (Benchmark note summarized on Investing.com, 2026-early 2026)", "Improving profitability trajectory vs. past misses: investors are reacting to the shift from sizeable EPS losses in FY25 (e.g., Q4 2025 EPS of -$0.23 vs -$0.06 consensus) toward anticipated profitability in 2026, with the Street modeling positive EPS and higher adjusted EBITDA as Conway’s new facility and can lines scale (various earnings and guidance updates through 2025–2026)", "Momentum/technical follow‑through: the stock had been near 52‑week lows around $3.6–$4.0 late in 2025; the combination of better reported numbers, reaffirmed 2026 guide, and higher analyst targets has triggered a high‑volume re‑rating and short‑covering/CTA buying, reflected in a 5‑day +49% move, 2.7x normal volume, and RSI in the 98th percentile"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=98"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 2.74x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 18.85, "reason": "dr5=49.4% atr=7.8% norm=2.83"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 2d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=74.3, 60d=72.9)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This fits the trader’s preference for turnaround/recovery, beat-and-raise setups, and re-rating/momentum names. It is somewhat less aligned with their top conviction themes like marquee customer wins or AI/data-center infrastructure, but the clean earnings inflection and follow-through move are clearly on 