": "2026-05-12", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "earnings-surprise-momentum", "breakout-and-momentum", "new-product-or-platform-inflection"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings beat with accelerating demand indicators: revenue $257.7M (+10% YoY, 1.7% above consensus), adjusted EPS $0.81 (+9% YoY, 4–5% above consensus), adjusted EBITDA +14% YoY, reported 2026-05-12", "Order momentum and visibility surprised to the upside: bookings up 37% YoY and book-to-bill at 1.10, signaling backlog build and multi-quarter revenue support, highlighted in Q1 2026 results and commentary on 2026-05-12", "Guidance reinforced a durable growth story rather than a one-off beat: Q2 2026 revenue guided to $259–$264M (midpoint ~1–2% above Street, implying 6–8% organic growth) and full-year 2026 revenue nudged up to $1.04–$1.055B with EPS $3.50–$3.65 reaffirmed, aligning with or slightly ahead of expectations", "Balance-sheet and cash-flow quality reduced perceived risk: strong operating cash flow, free cash flow margin improving to ~18% vs ~12% a year ago, and net cash/negative net debt, called out across post-earnings coverage in mid-May 2026", "Technical/flow-through element: the earnings beat-and-raise profile triggered an earnings breakout setup (gap up, 4.1x 10-day average volume, strong close near highs), attracting momentum and breakout traders and extending gains well beyond the initial post-print move"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=96"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 4.16x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 11.44, "reason": "dr5=19.7% atr=5.1% norm=1.72"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=23.1, 60d=8.3)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "The setup cleanly fits the trader’s earnings-beat-and-raise and breakout appetite, and the order-strength/backlog commentary suggests a genuine inflection rather than a one-off print. It is only a moderate thematic fit because this is not obviously one of the trader’s highest-conviction AI infrastructure or optical/data-center patterns.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "NOVT has strong momentum and a legitimate fundamental catalyst, but the news is more of a solid beat-and-raise/re-rating than a game-changing story. It supports the move and keeps the stock actionable, yet it does not hit the trader’s highest-priority marquee customer or AI infrastructure themes hard enough for a PICK.", "last_event_magnitude": null, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-12", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a real, material earnings catalyst: Novanta beat on revenue and EPS, bookings jumped 37% YoY with a 1.10 book-to-bill, and management nudged full-year revenue guidance higher. That is enough to justify a re-rating, though it is not a transformational named-customer or multi-year contract event."}, {"dr_1": 19.14, "dr_5": 25.69, "atr20": 9.96, "dr_20": 48.09, "dr_60": 41.8, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "QUBT", "sources": ["top_1d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Computer Hardware", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 1389570000, "rsi_mktcap": 96, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Quantum Computing, Inc.", "news_summary": "The recent spike in QUBT is primarily a reaction to Q1 2026 results that massively grew revenue to $3.7M (vs ~$3.1M expected and just $39K a year ago) on the back of the Luminar Semiconductor and NuCrypt acquisitions, while also beating EPS expectations despite remaining unprofitable. That print was framed by media and analysts as validation of an acquisition‑driven quantum‑photonics platform with sizable cash reserves and future revenue potential, prompting a sharp re‑rating. The earnings reaction then fed into a technical/momentum phase: volume jumped to more than 8–11x the 10‑day average, RSI pushed into the high 90s, and the stock appeared on top 1d/vol‑spike screens, drawing in traders and retail flows amplified by very bullish social sentiment. There is no single new marquee customer disclosure driving the move; it’s an earnings‑beat plus acquisition‑story re‑pricing that has transitioned into a momentum/low‑float speculative run within the broader quantum/AI photonics theme.", "current_price": 12.0101, "matched_themes": ["breakout-and-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst", "special-situation-re-rating", "optical-and-photonics"], "momentum_score": 79.69, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 11.66, "composite_score": 71.88, "last_event_date": "2026-05-12", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-surprise-momentum", "optical-and-photonics", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst", "breakout-and-momentum", "special-situation-re-rating"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings beat: revenue $3.7M vs ~$3.1M consensus, +5,951% YoY driven largely by the Luminar Semiconductor and NuCrypt acquisitions; EPS -$0.02 vs -$0.05 expected (around 2026-05-11)", "Acquisition-led photonics/semiconductor story: completion and integration of Luminar Semiconductor (~$110M deal) and NuCrypt, with management/coverage commentary pointing to $20–25M incremental revenue contribution by 2026 and enhanced in‑house photonics foundry capabilities (Q1 2026 commentary, reiterated in recent articles)", "Analyst and media re‑rating: bullish notes including a cited Rosenblatt buy rating with a $22 price target and broader positive coverage (e.g., Barron’s mention, Tickeron, Intellectia), framing QUBT as a well‑capitalized (> $1.4–1.5B cash) quantum‑photonics platform despite near‑term losses (May 2026)", "Momentum/volume dislocation: post‑earnings single‑day move of ~14–19% on >8–11x normal volume, RSI in the 96th percentile, and inclusion on top 1d/vol-spike/gapper screens, attracting short‑term traders into a low‑float, high‑beta quantum computing/photonics name (2026-05-12 volume spike)", "Sector/speculative tailwind: renewed retail and social‑media enthusiasm in quantum and photonics (Stocktwits sentiment flipping to 'extremely bullish') plus broader AI/quantum convergence narratives, including references to partnerships with NASA and other institutions (late April–mid May 2026)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=96"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 11.66x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 7.69, "reason": "dr5=25.7% atr=10.0% norm=1.15"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=48.1, 60d=41.8)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "QUBT hits the trader's low-float/small-cap catalyst and breakout-and-momentum themes strongly (19% 1d move, 8–11x volume spike, RSI 96). The acquisition-driven photonics/semiconductor platform story aligns with optical-and-photonics and special-situation-re-rating (sum-of-parts re-rating via Luminar integration). However, there is no named hyperscaler customer win, no explicit AI infrastructure demand signal, and no evidence of enterprise adoption driving the acquisitions—the story is financial engineering and sentiment rather than real customer pull-through.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "QUBT has strong momentum and technical setup (19% 1d, 48% 20d, RSI 96, low-float catalyst) and the acquisitions do represent a material re-rating event. However, news_materiality is only 2 (beat + acquisition, but no named customer or quantified AI infrastructure inflection) and theme_fit is 2 (fits breakout/low-float/re-rating but lacks the trader's core conviction themes of big-ticket customer wins, hyperscaler AI infrastructure demand, or organic earnings acceleration). The move is primarily speculative momentum + acquisition story re-pricing in a hot quantum/photonics sector, not a fundamental catalyst the trader's taste signature prioritizes. Recommend watching for a follow-up announcement of a named hyperscaler or enterprise customer adoption of the Luminar photonics platform to upgrade to PICK.", "last_event_magnitude": 8.35, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-12", "news_materiality_reason": "Q1 2026 earnings beat ($3.7M revenue vs. $3.1M consensus, EPS beat) combined with two completed acquisitions (Luminar Semiconductor ~$110M, NuCrypt) that materially expand revenue and in-house photonics capabilities, with management guidance of $20–25M incremental revenue by 2026. However, the beat is modest in absolute terms ($600K upside), and the revenue growth is acquisition-driven rather than organic customer pull-through."}, {"dr_1": 23.64, "dr_5": 26.62, "atr20": 11.52, "dr_20": 34.84, "dr_60": 40.2, "sector": "Consumer Cyclical", "ticker": "AEVA", "sources": ["top_1d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Auto - Parts", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 977577781, "rsi_mktcap": 95, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Aeva Technologies, Inc.", "news_summary": "The market appears to be reacting primarily to AEVA's Q1 2026 revenue acceleration and the follow-through from a recent European OEM win, which together support the idea that lidar demand is inflecting rather than just producing a one-off earnings pop. The move also has strong momentum/technical reinforcement: the stock gapped higher on 2026-05-12, volume is running at 2.59x the 10-day average, and the name is showing up on gapper/volume screens. I did not find a clearly newer named-customer or regulatory catalyst than the Q1 update, so this looks like earnings-plus-customer-win re-rating with momentum chasing rather than a separate hidden event.", "current_price": 19.0398, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "breakout-and-momentum", "big-ticket-customer-wins", "optical-and-photonics", "data-center-infrastructure"], "momentum_score": 78.89, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 2.59, "composite_score": 71.56, "last_event_date": "2026-05-12", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "breakout-and-momentum", "optical-and-photonics", "big-ticket-customer-wins", "data-center-infrastructure"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 results showed a 90% revenue surge across diversified markets, with the stock up 8.33% to $15.24 after the announcement (Investing.com, 2026-05-12).", "The post-earnings move was amplified by a bullish analyst/market reset: AEVA has been trading on strong momentum after a major European OEM win and raised 2026 revenue guidance, with 9 analysts cited at a $24 median target and strong-buy consensus (tickernerd summary, updated 2026-05-13)."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=95"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 2.59x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 6.89, "reason": "dr5=26.6% atr=11.5% norm=1.03"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=34.8, 60d=40.2)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "It clearly fits the trader’s favorite beat-and-raise and breakout/momentum patterns, and the lidar/optical stack plus OEM win keeps it in the broader AI-infrastructure-adjacent hardware lane. The customer-win angle is relevant, but not yet the kind of named, quantified megadeal this trader loves most.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "AEVA has a legitimate catalyst: strong Q1 growth, raised guidance, and a follow-through customer win are enough to justify interest, especially with the stock already showing powerful momentum. But the news is not yet game-changing enough for a PICK, since the catalyst is still more re-rating/earnings-driven than a clearly transformational contract or platform inflection. There is no stated trader-specific thesis on AEVA to extend here, so this is a solid watch rather than a top-tier conviction setup.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.2364, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-12", "news_materiality_reason": "Q1 2026 results were materially strong, with a 90% revenue surge and a raised 2026 revenue outlook, which is the kind of beat-and-raise setup that can re-rate a name. The additional European OEM win adds some real customer validation, but this is still short of a transformational multi-year contract or marquee hyperscaler-style deal."}, {"dr_1": 6.03, "dr_5": 11.19, "atr20": 12.81, "dr_20": 97.24, "dr_60": 143.86, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "KOPN", "sources": ["top_20d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Hardware, Equipment & Parts", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 884777133, "rsi_mktcap": 98, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Kopin Corporation", "news_summary": "The market is primarily reacting to a named-customer win: Kopin secured a $3 million MicroLED display order from a tier-one aerospace company, its first production MicroLED contract for combat aircraft, with deliveries slated for the second half of 2026. That fundamental catalyst is being turbocharged by strong technical momentum and elevated volume, so the move looks like a mix of a real defense/design-win re-rating plus a momentum squeeze rather than a pure sympathy rally. The ESG-framework news is secondary; the contract is the main driver.", "current_price": 5.365, "matched_themes": ["big-ticket-customer-wins", "optical-and-photonics", "new-product-or-platform-inflection", "breakout-and-momentum"], "momentum_score": 74.6, "verdict_claude": "PICK", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 3.15, "composite_score": 69.84, "last_event_date": "2026-05-12", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["big-ticket-customer-wins", "defense-and-geopolitical-risk", "optical-and-photonics", "new-product-or-platform-inflection", "breakout-and-momentum"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Kopin announced a $3 million MicroLED display order from a tier-one aerospace company, marking its first production contract for MicroLED technology in combat aircraft; delivery is scheduled for 2H 2026 (reported 2026-05-13).", "Kopin also reported a comprehensive ESG framework announcement, alongside recent momentum from its inclusion in the Russell 2000 reconstitution and prior NeuralDisplay prototype milestones; the stock had already risen 15.48% in regular trading and added 6.7% after hours on the ESG-news day (2026-05-13 / cited in recent coverage).", "The move is being amplified by technical factors: 3.15x volume versus the 10-day average, a 20-day return of +97.2%, and a prior volume spike event on 2026-05-12, suggesting momentum/short-covering layered on top of the contract news."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=98"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 3.15x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 2.6, "reason": "dr5=11.2% atr=12.8% norm=0.39"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=97.2, 60d=143.9)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This fits the trader’s preference for named customer wins with concrete dollars and timing, plus it plays into photonics/optical hardware and a new-product adoption inflection. It also arrives on top of a major technical breakout, which matches the trader’s momentum taste even if the company is not a core watchlist name.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "This is a legitimate catalyst, not just a sympathy move: a $3 million first production MicroLED contract with a tier-one aerospace buyer is the kind of named-win news this trader tends to like. The stock is also already in a strong momentum regime, so the contract can act as the fundamental story behind the squeeze rather than a random spike. There is no prior ticker-specific thesis to lean on, but the current news clearly supports a fresh re-rating setup.", "last_event_magnitude": 4.01, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-13", "news_materiality_reason": "Kopin disclosed a named-customer, first-production MicroLED order worth $3 million from a tier-one aerospace company, with deliveries slated for 2H 2026. That is a real, quantified contract win and more material than a generic press-release move, though it is not large enough to be game-changing."}, {"dr_1": -6.57, "dr_5": 35.06, "atr20": 10.75, "dr_20": 17.99, "dr_60": 44.33, "sector": "Industrials", "ticker": "RDW", "sources": ["top_5d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Aerospace & Defense", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 1826254841, "rsi_mktcap": 92, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Redwire Corporation", "news_summary": "A focused check finds no evidence of a hidden marquee commercial buyer or secret consumer-electronics design win behind RDW’s recent move. The fundamental catalyst is the Q1 2026 print and guidance: Redwire reported $97M in revenue (+58% YoY, slightly below the ~$105.7M consensus) but showed a sharp improvement in profitability metrics, with gross margin rising to ~26.6% (from ~15% a year ago, and up ~17 points sequentially). The company also achieved a record $498.1M contracted backlog, supported by a very strong 1.92 book‑to‑bill ratio and more than $350M in bookings over the last two quarters, and ended the quarter with $175.2M in liquidity.\\n\\nOn the earnings call and in the press release (May 6–7, 2026), management reaffirmed an ambitious full‑year 2026 revenue outlook of $450–$500M, implying roughly 42% YoY growth at the midpoint, and noted that about 68% of the remaining $393.4M of performance obligations are expected to be recognized as revenue within 12 months. They emphasized ongoing improvement in operational performance and cash from operations. Segment detail showed $52.7M of space revenue and $44.3M of defense tech revenue, with the Edge Autonomy acquisition driving much of the defense tech growth.\\n\\nThe company also highlighted strategic government and defense wins rather than marquee commercial tech customers: inclusion as one of 14 vendors on the U.S. Space Systems Command Andromeda advanced spacecraft IDIQ (a roughly $1.8B contract vehicle), work on ESA’s QKDSat and Belgium’s national security satellite, and follow-on orders from the U.S. Marine Corps for the Stalker system. These reinforce Redwire’s positioning as a levered play on space and defense budgets but do not constitute a newly disclosed, single transformational customer.\\n\\nA targeted search over the last 60–90 days turned up no reports or credible rumors tying Redwire to Apple, NVIDIA, TSMC, Google, Microsoft, Amazon, Meta, Tesla, OpenAI, Anthropic, or major auto OEMs as a newly qualified or ramping supplier, and no specific Ming‑Chi Kuo, DigiTimes, Wedbush, Loop Capital, Needham, or Morgan Stanley supply‑chain notes identifying a stealth design win or mass‑production milestone. Recent news, patents, and conference disclosures also do not reveal a hidden flagship platform relationship with a big‑tech or auto customer.\\n\\nTaken together, the move looks driven by the market’s reassessment of Redwire’s growth and margin trajectory—backed by record backlog, improved gross margins, and reiteration of a strong 2026 revenue guide—amplified by small‑cap, high‑beta technical momentum and defense/space thematic interest, rather than by a newly discovered marquee commercial buyer or secret design win.", "current_price": 11.575, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "breakout-and-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst", "turnaround-and-recovery", "special-situation-re-rating"], "momentum_score": 71.72, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 0.98, "composite_score": 68.69, "last_event_date": "2026-05-08", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["space-infrastructure", "defense-tech", "government-contracts", "backlog-driven-growth", "smallcap-momentum", "turnaround-and-recovery", "small-cap-relief-rally", "defense-and-geopolitical-risk", "earnings-surprise-momentum", "breakout-and-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings: revenue +58% YoY to $97M (miss vs $105.7M consensus) but gross margin expanded to ~26.6% (up ~12 pts YoY and 17 pts QoQ), backlog hit a record $498.1M with book‑to‑bill 1.92, and liquidity rose to $175.2M (Redwire Q1 2026 results, 2026-05-06/07)", "Management reaffirmed an aggressive FY 2026 revenue guide of $450–$500M (≈42% YoY growth at midpoint) and highlighted >$350M in bookings in the last two quarters and 68% of remaining performance obligations expected to convert to revenue within 12 months (earnings call, 2026-05-07)", "Defense tech momentum from the Edge Autonomy acquisition and wins such as inclusion on the Space Systems Command Andromeda IDIQ (~$1.8B contract vehicle), ESA’s QKDSat, and Belgium’s national security satellite, positioning Redwire for multi‑year government and defense spending tailwinds (company press release and call commentary, 2026-05-06/07)", "Q1 2026 earnings miss but sharp revenue inflection and strong near-term growth guide (EPS -$0.40 vs -$0.17 est; Q2 revenue guided to ~$132M vs ~$62M in Q1, implying ~>100% QoQ growth, early May 2026)", "Ongoing re-rating as a leveraged play on space infrastructure / defense spending, with analysts still carrying double‑digit to high‑20s price targets (consensus ~$14, high ~$28, vs low‑teens spot price, early May 2026)", "Technical follow‑through after an early‑May gap-up ‘gapper’ move, with high RSI and 5‑day momentum screens (top_5d, volspike_gapper) driving quant / momentum inflows despite a weak 1‑day pullback"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=92"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 0.98x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 9.72, "reason": "dr5=35.1% atr=10.8% norm=1.46"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 5d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=18.0, 60d=44.3)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "RDW fits the trader's appetite for small-cap momentum with a concrete catalyst (margin expansion + backlog inflection + guidance reiteration), and the re-rating narrative (space/defense infrastructure play with improving unit economics) aligns with their interest in valuation unlocks and turnaround setups. However, the news lacks the trader's highest-conviction themes: no named hyperscaler customer, no AI infrastructure angle, and no big-ticket commercial contract win—only government/defense wins and organic backlog conversion.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "RDW has material earnings news (margin beat + strong guidance ramp) and fits several of the trader's secondary themes (small-cap momentum, re-rating, breakout technicals), but falls short of a PICK because it lacks the trader's primary conviction drivers: no hyperscaler AI infrastructure exposure, no named marquee commercial customer win, and no optical/data-center gear angle. The move is driven by space/defense budget tailwinds and improved execution, not the 'strong momentum + strong news + thematic relevance' trifecta the trader prioritizes. Suitable for monitoring if the trader develops a space-infrastructure thesis, but not an immediate fit for their current watchlist signature.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.2037, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-08", "news_materiality_reason": "Q1 2026 earnings showed a revenue miss (~$97M vs ~$105.7M consensus) but delivered a material margin inflection (+12 pts YoY gross margin to 26.6%) and record $498.1M backlog with 1.92 book-to-bill, paired with reaffirmed aggressive FY 2026 guidance of $450–$500M (~42% YoY growth). The near-term Q2 guide of ~$132M implies >100% QoQ acceleration, which is a concrete forward inflection rather than a one-quarter beat."}, {"dr_1": 3.18, "dr_5": 12.54, "atr20": 3.23, "dr_20": 12.62, "dr_60": 8.84, "sector": "Healthcare", "ticker": "CON", "sources": ["volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Medical - Equipment & Services", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 3199044500, "rsi_mktcap": 90, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Concentra Group Holdings Parent, Inc.", "news_summary": "The follow‑up review confirms that the recent move in Concentra Group Holdings Parent, Inc. (CON) is fundamentals‑driven rather than tied to a single large new contract, regulatory surprise, or unconfirmed rumor.\\n\\nThe core catalyst is the company’s Q1 2026 report on 2026-05-07 (Business Wire release and Form 8‑K). Concentra posted revenue of $569.6M (+13.7% YoY from $500.8M), net income of $52.3M (+28.7% YoY), and Adjusted EBITDA of $120.7M (+17.6% YoY), with Adjusted EBITDA margin rising to 21.2% from 20.5%. Operating metrics were similarly strong: 3.419M patient visits (54,271 per day, +6.7% YoY) and revenue per visit of $151.47 (+3.1% YoY). These data points are consistent across the 8‑K summary (StockTitan), the official Business Wire release, and third‑party recaps (MarketBeat, MarketChameleon, Investing.com).\\n\\nOn the same date, management raised full‑year 2026 guidance: revenue to $2.275–$2.375B, Adjusted EBITDA to $460–$480M, free cash flow to $215–$235M, capital expenditures to $70–$80M, and a year‑end net leverage ratio under 3.0x. These figures appear identically in the press release, 8‑K excerpt (StockTitan), and external write‑ups (MarketChameleon, Investing.com). This is a clear upward revision to expectations and a central driver of the re‑rating.\\n\\nManagement also reinforced a capital‑return and balance‑sheet narrative: the Q1 2026 release includes declaration of a quarterly cash dividend (per Business Wire) and reiterates the goal of reducing net leverage below 3.0x by year‑end 2026, signaling confidence in cash generation after capex of $70–$80M.\\n\\nRegarding M&A and any speculative angle, the main item is the integration of Nova Medical Centers, acquired in March 2025. On the Q1 2026 earnings call (as summarized by MarketBeat), CEO Keith Newton stated that Nova integration efforts are complete and that the company has captured all expected synergies. This supports the growth and margin story but is not a new rumor; it is presented as finished execution.\\n\\nAcross the verification sources, there is no evidence of a hidden or rumored major contract win, undisclosed government deal, or transformative new product that would explain the stock move beyond the earnings beat, higher guidance, and continued successful integration of prior acquisitions. None of the sources reviewed—SEC 8‑K/press release, MarketBeat earnings summary, SahmCapital valuation note, MarketChameleon article, or Investing.com—mention any controversial or unconfirmed claim that has since been denied or walked back. The move appears to be an earnings‑beat‑and‑raise plus momentum trade, supported by increased volume and strong RSI, rather than a rumor‑driven spike.", "current_price": 25.62, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "special-situation-re-rating", "breakout-and-momentum", "turnaround-and-recovery"], "momentum_score": 71.57, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 2.58, "composite_score": 68.63, "last_event_date": "2026-05-08", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat", "guidance-raise", "healthcare-services", "post-ipo-re-rating", "earnings-beat-and-raise", "special-situation-re-rating", "breakout-and-momentum", "small-cap-relief-rally", "earnings-surprise-momentum"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 beat with double‑digit growth and margin expansion: revenue $569.6M (+13.7% YoY), net income $52.3M (+28.7% YoY), Adjusted EBITDA $120.7M (+17.6% YoY), visits per day +6.7%, revenue per visit +3.1% (press release / Form 8‑K, 2026-05-07)", "Raised FY 2026 guidance: revenue to $2.275–$2.375B, Adjusted EBITDA to $460–$480M, FCF to $215–$235M, capex $70–$80M, net leverage target below 3.0x (press release / Form 8‑K, 2026-05-07)", "Capital return and balance sheet messaging: quarterly cash dividend declared (per Business Wire release, 2026-05-07) alongside target to reduce net leverage below 3.0x by year‑end 2026, reinforcing confidence in cash generation", "Post‑IPO scaling and acquisition integration, including Nova Medical Centers (acquired March 2025) with management stating on the Q1 2026 call that integration is complete and expected synergies have been captured (earnings call commentary summarized by MarketBeat, 2026-05-08)", "Positive sentiment and valuation reset in secondary coverage: multiple outlets highlight earnings beat and guidance raise as drivers of share‑price momentum and renewed investor interest (SahmCapital note 2026-05-10; MarketChameleon article 2026-05-08)", "Q1 2026 earnings beat with double‑digit growth and margin expansion: revenue $569.6M (+13.7% YoY), EPS ~$0.40 up ~21% YoY, adjusted EBITDA $120.7M (+17.6% YoY) reported on 2026-05-08", "Raised full‑year 2026 guidance: revenue lifted to $2.275B–$2.375B and net income to $191M–$206M, signaling stronger-than-expected growth and cash generation (2026-05-08)", "Capital return plus M&A narrative: quarterly dividend of $0.0625/share reaffirmed alongside an active buyback program and commentary around expansion via acquisitions (including Nova Medical Centers) supporting a consolidation/growth story (ongoing, highlighted in recent coverage through early May 2026)", "Multiple analyst target hikes following the print: Truist raised PT to $31 from $29 (Buy) and Deutsche Bank to $32 from $29 (Buy) around 2026-05-08–05-11, lifting consensus PT to ~$30.25 (~18–20% upside) and reinforcing the re‑rating", "Increased insider selling disclosed in recent SEC filings (e.g., ~$3.25M sold per MarketScreener note), which, while a modest negative data point, also drew additional investor attention and liquidity to the name"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=90"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 2.58x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 11.57, "reason": "dr5=12.5% atr=3.2% norm=1.74"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "1 screen"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 5d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=12.6, 60d=8.8)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "It cleanly matches the trader’s strong preference for earnings beats with raised guidance and a valuation reset/re-rating setup. It also fits the momentum/breakout bucket, though it is not tied to AI infrastructure, optics, or a named big-ticket customer.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "The stock has the right kind of catalyst and the move is clearly fundamentals-driven, but the news is still a standard beat-and-raise rather than a game-changing named deal or transformative new platform. It supports a re-rating and keeps the momentum case alive, but it does not hit the trader’s highest-conviction themes hard enough for an automatic PICK.", "last_event_magnitude": null, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-11", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a real, material catalyst: Concentra reported a Q1 beat with double-digit revenue, EBITDA, and EPS growth, then raised full-year guidance across revenue, EBITDA, FCF, and leverage targets. That is enough to drive a legitimate re-rating, but it is not a transformational contract, product launch, or multi-year marquee customer win."}, {"dr_1": -0.43, "dr_5": 45.64, "atr20": 7.58, "dr_20": 30.87, "dr_60": 34.22, "sector": "Consumer Cyclical", "ticker": "BLMN", "sources": ["top_5d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Restaurants", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 716591582, "rsi_mktcap": 93, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Bloomin' Brands, Inc.", "news_summary": "A focused check over the last 60–90 days does not show any hidden, nameable ‘marquee buyer’ or supply‑chain‑style catalyst behind Bloomin’ Brands’ recent price move. There are no reports, even at the rumor or patent‑sleuthing level, tying BLMN to Apple, NVIDIA, TSMC, Google, Microsoft, Amazon, Meta, Tesla, OpenAI, Anthropic, major auto OEMs, or defense primes; nor are there any Ming‑Chi Kuo, DigiTimes, Wedbush, Loop Capital, Needham, or Morgan Stanley supply‑chain notes of the kind typically seen in hardware/semis. Likewise, there are no design wins, qualification milestones, or patent disclosures suggesting a new platform relationship with a large external customer, which would be atypical for a U.S. casual‑dining operator.\\n\\nWhat *is* clearly documented is a fundamental but conventional restaurant story. On May 6, 2026, Bloomin’ Brands reported Q1 2026 earnings: revenue of about $1.06B (up ~1% YoY) and adjusted diluted EPS of $0.67, ahead of both the prior year’s $0.59 and Street expectations. Adjusted operating income margin was ~5.9%. Commentary across the press release, TradingView/MarketBeat recaps, Sahm Capital/LSEG data, and the AlphaSpread call transcript emphasizes that higher average check (largely pricing), targeted cost‑saving and productivity initiatives, and disciplined G&A (guided to ~5.3% of sales for 2026) are supporting margins against ongoing inflation in commodities, labor, and operating costs.\\n\\nManagement reiterated full‑year 2026 guidance and framed Q2 and the balance of the year in a way that investors read as confident, particularly around Outback Steakhouse’s operational turnaround: improved guest metrics, a refreshed steak lineup with strong satisfaction scores, a 4‑table/server model, expanded char‑grill capacity, and revamped Managing Partner incentives. U.S. comparable restaurant sales were up ~90 bps YoY, and Bonefish/Carrabba’s were called out for strong comps, driven by promotions like Martini Mondays and Bang Wednesdays. This combination—earnings and margin beat, steady guidance, and tangible operational traction—landed on a stock that had been heavily de‑rated, trading near 52‑week lows at roughly 7x forward earnings, with a consensus “hold” stance (2 buy, 10 hold, 2 sell) and only modestly higher 12‑month price targets.\\n\\nGiven this backdrop and the recorded spike in volume around the 2026‑05‑06 earnings event, the most credible interpretation is that the move is an earnings‑driven fundamental re‑rating of a previously out‑of‑favor small‑cap casual‑dining name, amplified by short covering and momentum players. There is no evidence in the record of a separate, under‑the‑radar marquee‑customer, hardware, AI, auto, or defense‑related catalyst driving the stock beyond the restaurant‑specific results and outlook discussed above.", "current_price": 8.389, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "turnaround-and-recovery", "breakout-and-momentum"], "momentum_score": 69.95, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 0.86, "composite_score": 67.98, "last_event_date": "2026-05-06", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat", "turnaround", "restaurant-casual-dining", "cost-optimization", "guidance-reaffirmation", "earnings-surprise-momentum", "turnaround-and-recovery", "small-cap-relief-rally", "breakout-and-momentum"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings beat and margin resilience: Revenue of ~$1.06B (+1% YoY) and adjusted diluted EPS of $0.67 vs ~$0.59 in Q1 2025 and above consensus, with adjusted operating income margin at ~5.9% despite cost inflation (company press release, 2026-05-06; TradingView/MarketBeat summaries, 2026-05-06)", "Confident 2026 outlook and G&A guidance: Management reiterated full‑year 2026 guidance and framed G&A at ~5.3% of sales for the year, signaling cost discipline and earnings durability (Q1 2026 earnings call, 2026-05-06; AlphaSpread transcript)", "Operational improvement at core banners, especially Outback: Commentary highlighted positive U.S. comparable restaurant sales (+90 bps YoY), higher average check driven mainly by pricing, cost‑saving and productivity initiatives, and specific initiatives at Outback (new steak lineup, 4‑table/server model, expanded char‑grill capacity, updated Managing Partner compensation) plus strong comps at Bonefish and Carrabba’s (MarketBeat recap and earnings call, 2026-05-06)", "Beaten‑down valuation and sentiment re‑rating: Stock was trading at ~7x next‑12‑month earnings with a median Street rating of “hold” (2 buy / 10 hold / 2 sell) and a modest price target premium (~21.5% above prior close), so the upside surprise and improved narrative triggered a sharp re‑rating, short covering, and momentum participation rather than being driven by a new marquee strategic or M&A event (LSEG/Reuters-based summary via Sahm Capital note, 2026-05-06)", "Q1 CY2026 earnings beat with adjusted EPS of $0.67 vs ~$0.59 a year ago and above Street expectations, on $1.06–$1.10B revenue (+~1% YoY), showing better margin control despite soft traffic (results reported 2026-05-06/08)", "Management reaffirmed full-year 2026 guidance and gave stronger‑than‑expected Q2 CY2026 adjusted EPS guidance (~$0.30 midpoint vs ~$0.22 consensus), signaling confidence in sustaining earnings despite a choppy consumer backdrop (2026-05-06/08)", "Evidence of an operational turnaround at Outback and other banners: same‑store sales positive in aggregate, improved guest metrics (brand trust, service, value, atmosphere, food, intent to return all up mid‑single‑digits), and Bonefish +6% comps driven by new offers like Martini Mondays and Bang Wednesdays (Q1 CY2026 commentary)", "The earnings surprise triggered a sharp re‑rating in a heavily sold‑off, small‑cap casual diner: stock had fallen to near 52‑week lows, then spiked on 5–6x normal volume on the event day and kept running, aided by short covering and momentum screens (top_5d, volspike_gapper) rather than new fundamental news in subsequent days"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=93"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 0.86x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 17.95, "reason": "dr5=45.6% atr=7.6% norm=2.69"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 10.0, "reason": "event 7d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=30.9, 60d=34.2)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "The setup matches the trader’s appetite for earnings beat-and-raise plus a turnaround/recovery story, and the sharp post-earnings breakout fits their momentum taste. It is not a marquee AI/optical/customer-win theme, but it clearly lands on a favored earnings-plus-re-rating pattern.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "The stock has a legitimate catalyst and strong momentum, but the news is still just a conventional restaurant earnings turnaround rather than a game-changing thematic or marquee-customer story. This supports the idea of a re-rating and keeps it on the radar, but it does not rise to a true PICK under this trader’s highest-conviction themes.", "last_event_magnitude": 5.56, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-08", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a material earnings-driven catalyst: Bloomin’ Brands beat on Q1 EPS and margins, reaffirmed full-year guidance, and guided Q2 EPS above consensus. It’s not transformational, but it is a real fundamental re-rating event with quantified results and forward confidence."}, {"dr_1": -0.82, "dr_5": 12.05, "atr20": 2.83, "dr_20": 13.97, "dr_60": 5.01, "sector": "Consumer Defensive", "ticker": "MNST", "sources": ["volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Beverages - Non-Alcoholic", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 84500857460, "rsi_mktcap": 92, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Monster Beverage Corporation", "news_summary": "The sharp move in Monster Beverage over the last couple of weeks is being driven primarily by a very strong Q1 2026 earnings report (May 7–8) that beat EPS expectations and showed ~22% YoY revenue growth, accompanied by margin strength. That upside surprise, combined with active share repurchases, has led to a series of bullish analyst reactions and target bumps in the days that followed, which helped sustain elevated volume and push the stock to new highs. The current pullback over the last day looks more like digestion/technical consolidation after an extended post‑earnings run than a response to fresh negative news.", "current_price": 85.56, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "breakout-and-momentum"], "momentum_score": 68.69, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 1.52, "composite_score": 67.48, "last_event_date": "2026-05-08", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-surprise-momentum", "breakout-and-momentum"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Record Q1 2026 earnings beat with strong top-line growth and margin expansion: EPS $0.58 vs ~$0.53 consensus; revenue +22.6% YoY (reported 2026-05-07/08)", "Management commentary and buyback activity driving a valuation re‑rating: ongoing share repurchases highlighted in post‑earnings coverage, supporting EPS growth and investor confidence (multiple analyst notes 2026-05-09 to 2026-05-11)", "Wave of bullish analyst reactions and price target increases following the print, including Deutsche Bank, Wells Fargo, and RBC reiterating positive views and calling for further upside (articles dated 2026-05-09 to 2026-05-11)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=92"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.52x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 12.69, "reason": "dr5=12.1% atr=2.8% norm=1.90"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "1 screen"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 5d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=14.0, 60d=5.0)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "The name fits the trader’s earnings-beat-and-momentum appetite: a strong post-earnings breakout with sustained volume and bullish follow-through. It is not a direct hit on the AI/optical themes, but it does match the trader’s broader preference for quantified catalysts and momentum continuation.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "The stock has a real catalyst and the move is being supported by earnings strength, so this is not a sympathy or noise-only setup. Still, it lacks the trader’s highest-conviction themes like AI infrastructure, optics, or a named big-ticket customer win, so it lands as a solid watch rather than a must-buy pick.", "last_event_magnitude": 3.89, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-11", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a material earnings catalyst: Monster posted a clear Q1 beat with EPS above consensus, ~22.6% YoY revenue growth, and margin expansion, followed by analyst upgrades and higher targets. It is not a transformational customer/contract event, but it is strong enough to support a legitimate re-rating move."}, {"dr_1": -5.26, "dr_5": 41.32, "atr20": 8.35, "dr_20": 41.92, "dr_60": 31.76, "sector": "Industrials", "ticker": "AAON", "sources": ["top_5d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Construction", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 11606887890, "rsi_mktcap": 99, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "AAON, Inc.", "news_summary": "The recent 40%+ spike in AAON is being driven primarily by a fundamental re‑rating after a very strong Q1 2026 print and a guidance hike on 2026‑05‑07, which confirmed accelerating revenue, expanding margins, and a record backlog. Those results prompted analysts to sharply lift 2026 revenue and EPS estimates (to about $2.0B and $2.33, respectively) and raise price targets by ~11%, reframing AAON as a structurally faster‑growing HVAC/industrial name (forecast ~31% revenue CAGR vs ~7% for peers). With that fundamentals reset in place, the stock is now also benefiting from momentum/technical flows (high RSI, vol‑spike and top‑5d screens), amplifying the move beyond what the earnings surprise alone would typically produce.", "current_price": 133.135, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "breakout-and-momentum", "special-situation-re-rating", "turnaround-and-recovery"], "momentum_score": 66.75, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 1.27, "composite_score": 66.7, "last_event_date": "2026-05-07", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "earnings-surprise-momentum", "breakout-and-momentum", "special-situation-re-rating"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings beat and raise: AAON reported record Q1 2026 results on 2026-05-07, with revenue and EPS both exceeding consensus and backlog hitting new highs; management simultaneously raised full‑year 2026 guidance (PRNewsWire, Zacks, Seeking Alpha transcript).", "Street estimate re‑rating: Following Q1 results, covering analysts materially raised 2026 forecasts from roughly $1.7B to ~$2.0B in revenue (+22% YoY) and EPS from $1.98 to $2.33 (+61%), and increased the average price target ~11% to ~$137 (SimplyWall.St summary referencing five-analyst consensus).", "Growth vs. peers narrative: Sell-side and quant screens are highlighting that AAON is now modeled to grow revenue at ~31% CAGR through 2026 vs ~7% for HVAC/industrial peers, framing the story as a structural share‑gainer rather than just a cyclical beneficiary (SimplyWall.St industry comparison)."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=99"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 1.27x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 14.75, "reason": "dr5=41.3% atr=8.3% norm=2.21"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 10.0, "reason": "event 6d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=41.9, 60d=31.8)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This fits the trader’s strong preference for earnings beats with raised guidance and for momentum names that are breaking out on a catalyst. It also has some re-rating flavor as analysts lifted estimates and price targets after the print, though it is not one of the trader’s core AI/optical themes.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "AAON has real news and the stock is acting like a momentum winner, but the catalyst is still a standard earnings-beat-and-raise rather than a game-changing thematic story. It fits the trader’s taste directionally, yet it does not hit a 3-star watchlist pattern like hyperscaler AI infrastructure or named big-ticket customer wins, so this is more of a strong WATCH than an automatic PICK.", "last_event_magnitude": 9.58, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-12", "news_materiality_reason": "AAON has a clear material catalyst: Q1 2026 earnings beat consensus and management raised full-year guidance on 2026-05-07, with backlog also at record levels. That is a legitimate fundamental re-rating event, though it is not a transformational contract or multi-year marquee win."}, {"dr_1": 1.53, "dr_5": 18.67, "atr20": 5.51, "dr_20": 42.13, "dr_60": 25.5, "sector": "Industrials", "ticker": "WSC", "sources": ["volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Rental & Leasing Services", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 4834367876, "rsi_mktcap": 98, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "WillScot Holdings Corporation", "news_summary": "The stock’s sharp 20–40% move over the past month is primarily a re‑rating off a beaten‑down base driven by better-than-expected Q1 2026 earnings and an upbeat FY26 revenue outlook, which directly contradict the cautious narrative and price-target cuts that dominated in late 2025. That fundamental inflection was amplified by a May 8 spike, where the name jumped over 20% intraday on reports linking WillScot’s modular and storage offerings to favorable regulatory shifts in rental policy and strong housing/infrastructure demand, leading to momentum/technical buying and likely short covering on above‑average volume.", "current_price": 27.133, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "turnaround-and-recovery", "breakout-and-momentum"], "momentum_score": 66.1, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 1.33, "composite_score": 66.44, "last_event_date": "2026-05-08", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "turnaround-and-recovery", "small-cap-relief-rally", "breakout-and-momentum"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 results and outlook: WillScot reported Q1 2026 adjusted EPS of ~$0.21 vs consensus ~$0.16 and guided FY26 revenue to about $2.25B vs Street ~$2.18B, signaling a better-than-expected demand and pricing environment (reported mid‑May 2026).", "Regulatory and demand-driven tailwind: On May 8, 2026 the stock surged over 20% intraday to ~$28.25, with commentary (AInvest) tying the move to regulatory shifts in rental policy and elevated housing/infrastructure demand that favor modular space and portable storage solutions.", "Positioning after prior derating: Through late 2025 the stock suffered multiple target cuts (Barclays to $22, Jefferies to $23, DA Davidson to $35) and a weak 'Sell (D+)' rating at Weiss, leaving sentiment and valuation depressed; the combination of a solid beat/raise and improving demand backdrop is driving a re‑rating and short covering off those lows."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=98"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.33x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 10.1, "reason": "dr5=18.7% atr=5.5% norm=1.52"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "1 screen"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 5d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=42.1, 60d=25.5)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This fits the trader’s clear interest in beat-and-raise setups, recovery stories, and momentum breakouts. It’s not an AI or optical name, but the combination of a re-rating