high RSI, volume >2x average, gapper screens), rather than any single new contract or regulatory event in the last few days.", "current_price": 24.26, "matched_themes": ["breakout-and-momentum", "special-situation-re-rating", "earnings-beat-and-raise"], "momentum_score": 63.84, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 2.16, "composite_score": 65.54, "last_event_date": "2026-05-06", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-surprise-momentum", "breakout-and-momentum", "special-situation-re-rating"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Explosive move in silver itself: front‑month silver futures recently spiked ~9% in a single session to around $84–85/oz and are up well over 100% YoY, putting the metal into what commentators (e.g., Keith Neumeyer interview, YouTube, early May 2026) are calling a new, structurally higher price regime", "Strong company‑specific fundamentals into that metal rally: First Majestic reported better‑than‑expected Q4 2025 results (EPS ~$0.30 on ~$0.5B revenue, Feb 19, 2026) and record Q1 2026 revenue/production, with realized silver prices up sharply (Q4 realized AgEq price up ~91% YoY to ~$59/oz and FY 2025 up ~47% to ~$41.5/oz)", "High leverage of AG’s earnings to silver prices plus fresh capital structure moves: management and coverage highlight a 2–3x beta of AG’s equity to silver; this has been reinforced by a US$350M convertible senior notes deal (late 2025) and an ongoing strategy shift including the proposed sale of the Del Toro mine (up to US$60M) and prior Gatos Silver acquisition, which investors are now re‑rating under the much higher metal price deck", "Analyst and sentiment tailwinds: Zacks assigns AG a #2 (Buy) with a high momentum score; H.C. Wainwright and other brokers have recently raised price targets citing margin expansion under the new silver price environment, while some services (e.g., GuruFocus GF Score, Robinhood/Investing.com coverage) flag valuation as rich but acknowledge strong momentum and improved operating metrics", "Technical and flow factors: AG has delivered ~300%+ returns over the past year and is trading near/above prior 52‑week highs with volume running more than 2x its 10‑day average, high RSI percentile (~96), and appearance on vol‑spike/gapper screens, drawing in systematic/momentum money and short‑covering on top of the fundamental silver move"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=96"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 2.16x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 13.84, "reason": "dr5=26.4% atr=5.7% norm=2.08"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "1 screen"}, "recent_event": {"points": 10.0, "reason": "event 7d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=12.7, 60d=5.7)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This fits the trader’s appetite for breakout/momentum names with a clear catalyst, and there is also a re-rating angle as higher silver prices materially improve AG’s economics. It is less of a direct hyperscaler/optical story, but it does align with the trader’s general preference for strong momentum plus a catalyst.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "AG has strong momentum and a legitimate catalyst, but the story is mainly a commodity leverage trade on silver’s explosive move plus solid recent operating results. That makes it attractive, but not quite a top-tier PICK by the trader’s most specific taste for named customer wins, AI infrastructure, or transformational special situations. The current news supports and extends the existing momentum/re-rating thesis, but it does not introduce a clearly game-changing new company-specific event.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.1042, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-11", "news_materiality_reason": "The move is backed by real company and sector news: First Majestic posted better-than-expected Q4 2025 results and record Q1 2026 revenue/production, with realized silver prices sharply higher. That is a material fundamental catalyst, though the latest burst is still mostly a leveraged reaction to the silver price spike rather than a single transformative company announcement."}, {"dr_1": 11.75, "dr_5": 6.08, "atr20": 4.14, "dr_20": 7.02, "dr_60": -8.31, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "ZBRA", "sources": ["top_1d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Communication Equipment", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 10672631883, "rsi_mktcap": 82, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Zebra Technologies Corporation", "news_summary": "The sharp 1‑day move in ZBRA is primarily a continuation and amplification of the positive re‑rating that started with its early‑May Q1 2026 earnings beat (EPS $4.75 on ~$1.5B revenue, both ahead of expectations) and management’s decision to hold full‑year guidance despite tariff/macro risks. That print, plus analyst commentary about resilient demand in automation/IoT end markets, has shifted sentiment toward a cyclical recovery story after a weak prior 60 days. Today’s double‑digit jump on ~5x normal volume looks like momentum and positioning catching up to that improved backdrop rather than a brand‑new discrete headline: traders are piling into a perceived turnaround/earnings‑surprise winner, pushing RSI into elevated territory and driving a breakout-style move.", "current_price": 242.625, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "turnaround-and-recovery", "breakout-and-momentum"], "momentum_score": 62.88, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 5.23, "composite_score": 65.15, "last_event_date": "2026-05-12", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-surprise-momentum", "turnaround-and-recovery", "breakout-and-momentum"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings upside and demand tone: Zebra reported Q1 2026 EPS of $4.75 on ~$1.5B revenue, beating consensus EPS by ~11.5% and revenue by ~1–2%, and the stock reacted with a ~14% pre‑market surge on the print (reported in early May 2026).", "Improving outlook and macro read‑through: Commentary around maintaining full‑year guidance despite tariff and macro headwinds, plus analyst materials highlighting upside to automation/IoT demand, has reinforced the view that Zebra is exiting a downturn and is leveraged to ongoing digital transformation in retail, logistics, and healthcare.", "Momentum/technical follow‑through: The stock now shows an 11–12% 1‑day move on 5x normal volume, high RSI, and placement on top‑1d and volume-spike screens as traders chase the post‑earnings re‑rating and mean‑reversion after a weaker 60‑day tape."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 10.5, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=82"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 5.23x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 4.38, "reason": "dr5=6.1% atr=4.1% norm=0.66"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "partial (20d=7.0, 60d=-8.3)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This fits the trader’s preferred earnings-surprise and turnaround pattern, with a clear post-print re-rating and technical breakout behavior. It is not a marquee hyperscaler/AI infrastructure or named big-customer theme, but it does match the trader’s appetite for momentum plus a credible catalyst.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "ZBRA has strong momentum and a legitimate earnings-driven catalyst, but the news is not big enough to reach PICK because there is no quantified raise, named customer win, or more transformational thesis item. The current move supports the turnaround/recovery setup and extends the post-earnings re-rating, but it is still more of a solid earnings beat than a game-changing story.", "last_event_magnitude": 4.19, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-12", "news_materiality_reason": "The catalyst is a real, material earnings event: Q1 2026 EPS and revenue both beat expectations, and management held full-year guidance despite tariff/macro headwinds. That is enough to justify the move, but it is still an earnings-surprise/re-rating setup rather than a game-changing contract or transformational customer win."}, {"dr_1": -3.73, "dr_5": 1.56, "atr20": 16.15, "dr_20": 92.01, "dr_60": 89.74, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "ALMU", "sources": ["top_20d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Semiconductors", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 399324211, "rsi_mktcap": 97, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Aeluma, Inc.", "news_summary": "A second-pass, more targeted search still does not uncover any marquee commercial buyer (Apple, NVIDIA, TSMC, Google, Microsoft, Amazon, Meta, Tesla, OpenAI, Anthropic, major auto OEM, or defense prime) being explicitly or implicitly tied to Aeluma’s devices in the last 60–90 days via supply-chain notes, patents, or conference disclosures. No recent notes from Ming-Chi Kuo, DigiTimes, Wedbush, Loop Capital, Needham, or Morgan Stanley specifically flag Aeluma as a named supplier or design-win beneficiary.\\n\\nThe fundamental driver that does exist is the cluster of government- and ecosystem-related contracts plus a clearer commercial path, rather than a secret tier‑1 OEM design win. On February 11, 2026, Aeluma reported Q2 FY26 results and reiterated FY2026 revenue guidance of $4–6M. The release detailed: (1) a NASA contract for quantum work; (2) additional contract funding from RFSUNY to integrate quantum dot lasers into the AIM Photonics 300mm silicon photonics platform; (3) several additional award notices pointing to further contracts expected in 2026; (4) a strategic focus on three to seven new development contracts that provide non‑dilutive R&D funding; and (5) a large increase in cash and equivalents to $38.6M, extending the runway for manufacturing readiness and commercialization. These elements were subsequently repeated and summarized by MarketScreener, GuruFocus, Intellectia, and TradingView/Quartr through May 13, 2026, reinforcing the narrative that Aeluma is funded to pursue its roadmap and is gaining validation via U.S. government and photonics‑ecosystem partners.\\n\\nBenchmark’s earlier Buy rating and $25 price target (David Williams, initiation in mid‑2025) continues to be referenced in recent coverage such as Intellectia’s AI‑driven note, which reiterates the thesis that Aeluma’s large‑diameter silicon wafer process can significantly lower costs while delivering high performance in sensing and communications. However, there is no fresh rating change or new major‑broker initiation in the last 60–90 days that would independently explain the recent price surge.\\n\\nNo sources in the verification pass point to a newly disclosed design win, qualification, or mass‑production milestone with a flagship consumer, data‑center, or auto platform. The disclosed contracts (NASA, RFSUNY/AIM Photonics) are important technical and ecosystem validations but are still R&D‑oriented; they do not yet map to a clearly dated, high‑volume end‑product ramp the way, for example, a named socket in a 2027 smartphone or vehicle program would.\\n\\nTaken together, the best-supported explanation is that the stock’s move is driven by: (a) reinforced confidence in FY26 revenue guidance and a visible stream of non‑dilutive government and ecosystem contracts; (b) a de‑risked cash position that allows Aeluma to scale manufacturing and business development without near‑term dilution; and (c) a small‑cap, high‑short‑interest setup that magnifies flows and momentum once those contract and funding headlines are in place. There is still no evidence, even after focused searching, of a hidden marquee customer adoption or supply‑chain leak that the market is trading on ahead of public disclosure.", "current_price": 27.38, "matched_themes": ["optical-and-photonics", "optical-and-data-center-gear", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst", "breakout-and-momentum", "new-product-or-platform-inflection"], "momentum_score": 62.29, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 0.91, "composite_score": 64.92, "last_event_date": "2026-05-11", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["compound-semiconductors", "silicon-photonics", "quantum-and-lasers", "defense-and-aerospace", "early-commercialization", "small-float-high-short-interest", "defense-and-geopolitical-risk", "optical-and-photonics", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst", "breakout-and-momentum"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Aeluma reaffirms FY2026 revenue guidance of $4–6M and outlines concrete commercialization roadmap, including 3–7 new development contracts and expanded outsourced wafer manufacturing (company Q2 FY26 release, 2026-02-11)", "Company highlights NASA quantum contract and additional RFSUNY silicon-photonics laser contract funding, plus multiple new award notices that support expectations for further contracts in 2026 (company Q2 FY26 release, 2026-02-11)", "Subsequent commentary and summaries (Intellectia, GuruFocus, TradingView/Quartr, MarketScreener) amplify the FY26 guidance, contract momentum, and cash balance of $38.6M, reinforcing a de‑risked funding runway for scaling (2026-02-11 through 2026-05-13)", "Benchmark analyst David Williams maintains a Buy rating and $25 price target, emphasizing Aeluma’s large‑diameter silicon wafer process as a potential disruptor in high‑performance sensing and communications semiconductors (Benchmark initiation reiterated in secondary coverage, 2025-07-23; still referenced in recent articles)", "Aeluma announced more than $4 million in new U.S. government contract awards for quantum materials and laser-related semiconductor work (announced 2026-05-13).", "The company also scheduled its Q3 FY2026 financial results release for 2026-05-13, but the larger move appears tied to the government-contract headline rather than earnings alone.", "The stock has been trading with very high short interest (about 26.3% of float) and a small-cap/small-float setup, which can magnify contract-news reactions and create momentum squeezes."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=97"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 0.91x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 0.29, "reason": "dr5=1.6% atr=16.1% norm=0.04"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 2d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=92.0, 60d=89.7)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "ALMU fits the trader's optical-and-photonics and picks-and-shovels AI infrastructure themes via silicon-photonics laser work and quantum-dot integration into the AIM Photonics platform. The small-float, high-short-interest setup with a concrete government-contract catalyst aligns with the low-float-catalyst pattern (e.g., XNDU, BULL watchlist entries). However, the news is ecosystem/R&D validation rather than a direct hyperscaler AI infrastructure win or a named big-ticket customer adoption that would elevate this to a 3.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "ALMU has strong momentum (92% 20d, 89.7% 60d, RSI 97, recent gapper) and material news (government contracts + de-risked runway), hitting the trader's optical-photonics and small-cap-catalyst themes. However, news_materiality=2 (no marquee customer, no earnings beat+raise) and theme_fit=2 (fits known themes but not a 3-star conviction pattern like SIMO's breakout or a direct hyperscaler adoption) means this does not meet the PICK threshold (requires ≥2 on both AND ≥3 on at least one). The setup warrants close monitoring—if a named hyperscaler or defense-prime design win surfaces, or if Q3 results show accelerating revenue tied to these contracts, this could re-rate sharply. For now, it's a thematic fit with solid technicals but insufficient news weight to commit.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.1656, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-13", "news_materiality_reason": "Aeluma announced $4M+ in new U.S. government contracts (quantum materials, laser semiconductors) on 2026-05-13, paired with reaffirmed FY26 guidance ($4–6M revenue), a de-risked $38.6M cash position, and a visible pipeline of 3–7 new development contracts. This is material validation of commercialization roadmap and non-dilutive funding, but falls short of a marquee named customer win or a quantified earnings beat with raised guidance."}, {"dr_1": 6.46, "dr_5": 20.69, "atr20": 5.24, "dr_20": 7.22, "dr_60": 3.6, "sector": "Basic Materials", "ticker": "HBM", "sources": ["volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Copper", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 10119547500, "rsi_mktcap": 90, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Hudbay Minerals Inc.", "news_summary": "The recent 5–20 day surge in Hudbay shares is being driven primarily by a strong Q1 2026 earnings print that delivered record revenue and adjusted EBITDA, with sales (~$757M) and net income (~$190M) coming in ahead of expectations. That beat is being reinforced by shareholder-friendly capital returns (new dividend and a 5% buyback authorization) and a series of bullish analyst actions that have moved Street targets higher, effectively endorsing the improved earnings power. Underpinning this is a broader re‑rating story from the last 1–2 months: mine‑life extensions, a stronger 3‑year production outlook, and strategic moves in key copper assets (Copper World, Copper Mountain, Arizona Sonoran) in a supportive copper/gold macro. The 1‑day spike on elevated volume and high RSI therefore looks like momentum buying and positioning on top of a fundamental beat-and-re‑rating narrative, rather than a stray technical move with no news.", "current_price": 27.04, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "special-situation-re-rating"], "momentum_score": 61.77, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 2.36, "composite_score": 64.71, "last_event_date": "2026-05-06", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-