, so this is not just a sympathy spike or pure technical noise. But the catalyst is a mining earnings/re-rating story, not one of the trader’s highest-conviction lanes like hyperscaler AI infrastructure or optical/data-center gear, so it clears the materiality bar without being an outright PICK.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.0743, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-01", "news_materiality_reason": "Hudbay’s latest catalyst is a real fundamental event: Q1 2026 results came with record revenue and EBITDA, net income well ahead of expectations, plus a new dividend and 5% buyback authorization. It’s material, but not a transformational contract or multi-year step-change announcement."}, {"dr_1": -0.07, "dr_5": 48.89, "atr20": 20.52, "dr_20": 104.25, "dr_60": 145.61, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "POET", "sources": ["top_20d", "top_5d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Semiconductors", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 1694374333, "rsi_mktcap": 98, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "POET Technologies Inc.", "news_summary": "I could not verify a new marquee-buyer catalyst behind POET's recent surge. The checked material does not show a named Apple/NVIDIA/TSMC-style customer win, supply-chain note, design-win confirmation, qualification-to-mass-production milestone, or patent/conference disclosure that clearly points to a specific large end customer. The only clearly dated recent item I found was POET's 2026-05-12 COO appointment, which is not a fundamental demand catalyst. Based on the available evidence, the move still looks more consistent with a technical / momentum / squeeze-driven re-rating than with a newly discovered fundamental contract or platform win.", "current_price": 13.705, "matched_themes": ["optical-and-photonics", "breakout-and-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst"], "momentum_score": 77.1, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 1.01, "composite_score": 60.84, "last_event_date": "2026-05-11", "last_event_type": "gapper", "ne