ell Energy positioned as a key beneficiary.", "New 12.5 MW data‑center‑focused fuel‑cell platform: on Mar 23, 2026 FuelCell Energy announced a packaged 12.5 MW ‘utility‑grade power block’ solution and related manufacturing expansion plans aimed specifically at large data‑center operations.", "Explosive pipeline growth tied to data centers: management and press coverage cite ~275% growth in the business development pipeline since early 2025, with ~80%+ of it linked to data centers and digital infrastructure clients, signaling a step‑change in prospective demand.", "Sector sympathy to Bloom Energy and peers: FCEL has repeatedly gapped higher in sympathy with strong results and optimism at Bloom Energy and Plug Power (e.g., Bloom’s strong Q1 print noted around Apr 30, 2026), fueling a broad fuel‑cell/on‑site power rally.", "Momentum/technical follow‑through on prior gaps: the stock is up ~130%+ over 20 trading days with 1.7x normal volume, a 20‑day ATR ~14%, and very high RSI, indicating trend‑chasing and breakout/momentum flows amplifying the fundamental AI‑power narrative rather than any single new event in the last day."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=98"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.74x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 4.65, "reason": "dr5=22.6% atr=14.5% norm=0.70"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 2d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=130.9, 60d=133.4)"}}, "news_materiality": 1, "theme_fit_reason": "FCEL does fit a hot AI power-buildout theme because the story is about on-site generation for data centers and a new platform aimed at that demand. It is relevant to the trader’s appetite for breakout/momentum and new-platform inflections, but it lacks the marquee named-customer evidence that would make it a top-tier match.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "This is a strong momentum name, bu