uidance for 20–25% revenue growth, ~40% gross margin, and positive EBITDA despite macro and supply‑chain headwinds, reinforcing a multi‑quarter growth narrative (2026-05-06/07)", "Earlier strategic repositioning: sale of Bressner Technology GmbH for ~$22.4M and focus on becoming a ‘pure play leader in ruggedized AI, ML and edge compute solutions,’ leaving OSS with roughly $34–40M net cash and >20% growth / >40% GM core profile, prompting analysts like Roth/MKM to raise price targets (2025-11 to 2026-02 window)", "$10.5M in new U.S. Navy / defense awards plus a $1.2M Safran Federal Systems order, reinforcing a growing, higher‑margin defense and ruggedized AI compute franchise that supports the re‑rating (February–March 2026)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=97"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 1.03x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 14.02, "reason": "dr5=57.3% atr=12.2% norm=2.10"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 20, "reason": "3 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 10.0, "reason": "event 7d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=75.9, 60d=77.2)"}}, "news_materiality": 3, "theme_fit_reason": "OSS hits multiple high-conviction trader themes: (1) earnings beat with maintained/raised guidance on a small-cap name (earnings-beat-and-raise); (2) explicit repositioning as a 'pure play leader in ruggedized AI, ML and edge compute solutions' with named defense wins (ai-compute + special-situation-re-rating); (3) strategic divestiture unlocking a cleaner, faster-growing core business with visible backlog and balance-sheet strength (special-situation-re-rating); (4) low-float small-cap with a concrete catalyst and credible narrative (low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst). The defense/ruggedized AI angle aligns with the trader's appetite for infrastructure-adjacent AI exposure tied to real customer demand.", "verdict_rationale": "OSS qualifies as a PICK: news_materiality=3 (beat + record bookings + strategic r