ather than a low-multiple EMS (analyst notes following Q4 print, 2026-05-06 to 2026-05-07)", "Technical and momentum follow‑through: stock gapped from mid‑$90s to >$120 intraday and closed at $134.73 on 2026-05-06 (+~39%), with continued high-volume trading and valuation re‑rating to >40x P/E as traders price in AI infrastructure growth and spin-related sum‑of‑parts upside (price/volume action and media recaps, 2026-05-06 to 2026-05-07)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=99"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 1.14x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 20.0, "reason": "dr5=45.1% atr=6.2% norm=3.28"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 10.0, "reason": "event 7d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=73.3, 60d=116.2)"}}, "news_materiality": 3, "theme_fit_reason": "It directly matches the trader’s highest-conviction pattern: AI infrastructure exposure plus a clear re-rating/sum-of-parts story. It also strongly confirms the trader’s own thesis on FLEX, especially the CPI spin and hyperscaler-driven infrastructure growth.", "verdict_rationale": "This is exactly the kind of setup this trader likes: strong earnings, a big guidance raise, and a spin-off that could unlock a higher multiple for the AI/data-center segment. The current news supports and extends the trader’s existing FLEX thesis rather than weakening it, because it reinforces the CPI re-rating story and shows demand is still accelerating. The stock’s breakout and follow-through also fit the trader’s momentum bias.", "latest_material_date": "2026-05-07", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a major catalyst: a clean earnings beat, a materially raised FY27 guide, and a planned spin-off of the high-growth Cloud & Power Infrastructure business. The combination is transformational rather than incremental, and it directly changes how the market can value the company."}, {"ok": true, "dr_1": 0.19, "dr_5