ofitability inflection: management raised full‑year 2026 guidance (accelerated growth commentary) and highlighted the Realize platform as re-accelerating the business, prompting a re-rating toward a more durable, profitable growth story (Benchmark and other post-earnings notes around May 7, 2026).", "Analyst target hikes and sentiment shift: Benchmark lifted its price target from $4.50 to $6.50 and reiterated Buy on May 7, 2026, while other brokers such as TD Cowen moved targets to around $6.00, driving follow‑through buying; consensus PT is now about $5.90 vs. a ~$5.1–5.2 stock price.", "Capital return and valuation support: an existing $200M buyback authorization (up to ~22% of shares) plus a modest P/E (~13–14x forward EPS with ~29% expected EPS growth) are being re-appraised post‑print, reinforcing the bull case as the stock breaks out to new 52‑week highs."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=96"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 0.89x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 20.0, "reason": "dr5=34.7% atr=4.8% norm=3.25"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 10.0, "reason": "event 6d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=50.7, 60d=53.9)"}}, "news_materiality": 3, "theme_fit_reason": "TBLA hits multiple core trader themes: (1) earnings beat + raise with quantified guidance reset and margin inflection (weight=3.0), (2) turnaround narrative—swing from loss to profitability with a named platform (Realize) driving re-acceleration, and (3) re-rating unlock where the market is repricing a faster-growing, more profitable segment inside a previously-discounted wrapper. Analyst target hikes (Benchmark $4.50→$6.50, TD Cowen ~$6.00) and cheap forward valuation (~13–14x with 29% EPS growth) reinforce the re-rating thesis.", "verdict_rationale": "TBLA qualifies as a PICK: material earnings inflection (news_materiality=3) with strong alignment to the trader's co