Rackspace.\\n\\nWhat *is* clearly documented is a conventional but meaningful turnaround catalyst: on **2026-05-07**, Rackspace reported **Q1 2026** results with revenue of **$678.1M**, up roughly **2% YoY**, versus consensus around $672–673M; public cloud revenue grew about **6.7–7% YoY to ~$443M**, partially offsetting continued private-cloud declines. GAAP net income swung to a **profit of $8.3M (EPS $0.03)** from a **$71.5M loss** a year prior, and non-GAAP operating profit climbed roughly **20%** to **$30.7M**, with loss from operations narrowing materially. In the same communication, the company laid out **FY 2026 guidance**: revenue **$2.6–$2.7B**, adjusted EBITDA **$305–$315M**, and non‑GAAP EPS loss of **-$0.15 to -$0.20**, which is broadly consistent with the prior Street view and signals stabilization rather than renewed deterioration.\\n\\nThe other identifiable fundamental leg is Rackspace’s **AI collaboration with AMD**, described in the MarketChameleon Q1 analysis (2026-05-08) as part of a strategic shift toward governed enterprise AI and higher-value managed services. While AMD is itself a marquee silicon vendor, the disclosed partnership is at the level of joint solutions and infrastructure offerings; there is **no indication** in public sources that this corresponds to a specific, large, locked-in deployment by any of the mega-cap cloud or consumer-tech names listed in the query.\\n\\nBeyond these items, there is **no evidence** of:\\n- A newly uncovered design win, qualification, or mass-production milestone tied to a top-tier OEM program;\\n- A patent filing, conference disclosure, or leak that ties Rackspace to a previously unreported, high-volume customer roadmap; or\\n- A major new sell-side supply-chain thesis from the named brokerages in the last 90 days.\\n\\nGiven that, the enormous move (+1,200% over 60 days with large gap days and high RSI) appears to be a **sharp fundamental re‑rating** off the May 7 print and AMD narrative, **amplified** by short covering, low starting valuation, and momentum/quant flows, **not** by a stealth marquee-customer design win or other as-yet-unpriced end-market ramp. The verification pass therefore refines but does not overturn the first-pass conclusion: the real drivers are the earnings/guide inflection and the AMD AI positioning, with the rest of the magnitude best explained by positioning and technical dynamics rather than a hidden fundamental bombshell.", "current_price": 5.6601, "matched_themes": ["hyperscaler-ai-infrastructure", "ai-compute", "turnaround-and-recovery", "special-situation-re-rating", "breakout-and-momentum", "new-product-or-platform-inflection"], "momentum_score": 93.96, "verdict_claude": "PICK", "composite_score": 87.58, "last_event_date": "2026-05-12", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["ai-infrastructure", "hybrid-cloud", "turnaround", "short-squeeze-and-momentum", "ai-hyperscaler-deals", "hyperscaler-ai-infrastructure", "data-center-infrastructure", "turnaround-and-recovery", "special-situation-re-rating", "earnings-surprise-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst", "breakout-and-momentum"], "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 upside inflection and first positive GAAP net income since 2024: revenue $678.1M (+~2% YoY) vs ~$672–673M consensus, net income $8.3M and GAAP EPS $0.03 vs loss a year ago, with public cloud revenue up ~6.7–7% YoY and improved non‑GAAP operating profit (results reported 2026-05-07)", "Reaffirmed / detailed FY 2026 outlook that frames a stabilized, cash‑generative turnaround: revenue guidance $2.6–$2.7B (in line with Street), adjusted EBITDA $305–$315M, and non‑GAAP EPS loss narrowed to -$0.15 to -$0.20 (company guidance reiterated across MarketBeat and MarketChameleon coverage, 2026-05-07 to 2026-05-08)", "High‑profile AI infrastructure collaboration with Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) highlighted in Q1 commentary and follow‑up coverage, positioning Rackspace as a governed AI / hybrid‑cloud partner for AMD GPU and CPU deployments rather than a legacy hoster (discussed in MarketChameleon 2026-05-08 article and echoed in subsequent news flow)", "Extreme re‑rating from distressed levels amplified by short covering, momentum and technical breakouts after earnings: shares rallied from sub‑$1 levels in April to the low‑$2s by May 12, 2026, with multiple gap‑up sessions, 1.5x+ normal volume and RSI in the 99th percentile; no additional fundamental disclosures of comparable magnitude after the May 7 print have appeared in primary news or filings", "Strategic AI partnership with Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) to power governed enterprise AI/private‑cloud offerings, announced alongside Q1 2026 results (2026-05-07)", "Q1 2026 revenue beat: $678.1M, +2% YoY vs ~$660.8M consensus, with public cloud +7% YoY to $443M; reaffirmed full‑year 2026 sales guidance of $2.6–$2.7B (in line with ~$2.64B Street) and reiterated adjusted EPS loss guidance (-$0.20 to -$0.15) (2026-05-07)", "Momentum/turnaround re‑rating from penny‑stock levels: stock moved from sub‑$1 (as low as ~$0.88–0.91 in mid‑April) to >$2 into earnings on growing AI/private‑cloud narrative and new senior leadership in operations/international for Private Cloud (appointments on 2026-04-08, discussed in early‑May coverage)", "Post‑earnings/partner short squeeze and technical chase: shares up ~200%+ since May 7 with multiple 50%+ single‑day spikes, heavy volume (~1.5x+ 10‑day average, 40–50M share days) and indicators like RSI >80, 20‑day/200‑day SMAs far below current price, suggesting forced short covering and momentum buying (2026-05-08 to 2026-05-12)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=99"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.57x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 17.96, "reason": "dr5=132.9% atr=22.1% norm=2.69"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 20, "reason": "4 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=