e gains near 200% and elevated volume (about 1.43x the 10-day average), consistent with investors reacting to an earnings/turnaround inflection plus momentum follow-through rather than a single unrelated rumor."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=95"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.43x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 8.03, "reason": "dr5=25.8% atr=9.6% norm=1.20"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "1 screen"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 2d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=8.6, 60d=99.0)"}}, "news_materiality": 3, "theme_fit_reason": "It directly hits several of the trader’s favorite patterns: a named, multi-year big-ticket contract; explicit AI/data-center infrastructure exposure; and a strong earnings/turnaround re-rating with backlog visibility. This is very close to the trader’s watchlist taste for game-changing customer wins and infrastructure-driven inflections.", "verdict_rationale": "BW checks both boxes the trader wants: the stock has strong momentum and the news is genuinely powerful, not just a technical squeeze. The Base Electron contract plus the earnings beat/reaffirmed guidance and large backlog build create a credible re-rating story, and the AI data-center angle makes it especially aligned with the trader’s preferred themes. This supports the turnaround/thesis narrative rather than weakening it.", "latest_material_date": "2026-05-11", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a material, company-specific catalyst: BW reported a major Q1 earnings beat with revenue up 44% YoY, adjusted EBITDA up 296% YoY, reiterated full-year EBITDA guidance, and disclosed a transformational multi-year ~$2.4B Base Electron contract tied to AI-data-center power demand. The backlog/bookings surge and deleveraging make this more than a routine earnings print."}, {"ok": true, "dr_1": -9.79, "dr_5": 10.8, "dr_20": 319.78, "dr_60": 363.42, "sector": "Technology", "ti