ational operating event."}, {"ok": true, "dr_1": 13.5, "dr_5": 19.73, "dr_20": 23.1, "dr_60": 8.35, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "NOVT", "sources": ["top_1d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Hardware, Equipment & Parts", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 4995018324, "rsi_mktcap": 96, "company_name": "Novanta Inc.", "news_summary": "The stock’s sharp 1–4 week move is being driven primarily by Novanta’s Q1 2026 print and guidance: a clean top-line and EPS beat, a 37% YoY surge in bookings with a 1.10 book‑to‑bill, and Q2/full‑year outlook that supports mid‑single‑ to high‑single‑digit organic growth in attractive medical and advanced industrial end markets. These data points told the market demand is re‑accelerating and that the growth runway looks more durable than feared, with improved free cash flow and a solid balance sheet lowering risk. Once that fundamental surprise hit, the name behaved like a textbook earnings breakout—large gap, 4x normal volume, and a strong close—which pulled in momentum capital and extended the move beyond what the raw earnings beat alone would justify. There is no evidence of a specific new mega-customer or regulatory shock; this is a re‑rating on better growth visibility and order momentum, amplified by technical buying.", "current_price": 158.62, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "breakout-and-momentum", "new-product-or-platform-inflection"], "momentum_score": 83.44, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "composite_score": 73.38, "last_event_date": "2026-05-12", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "earnings-surprise-momentum", "breakout-and-momentum", "new-product-or-platform-inflection"], "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings beat with accelerating demand indicators: revenue $257.7M (+10% YoY, 1.7% above consensus), adjusted EPS $0.81 (+9% YoY, 4–5% above consensus), adjusted EBITDA +14% YoY, reported 2026-05-12", "Order momentum and visibility surprised to the upside: bo