ail/online chatter around those holdings has triggered a sharp re‑rating and heavy inflows, with volumes running ~4x normal and the stock repeatedly hitting top‑performance and volume‑spike screens. There is no fresh earnings beat, structural change, or named new portfolio holding announced in the last 30–60 days that would directly explain an ~80% move; instead, the market appears to be chasing the theme (AI/SpaceX access) and the technical setup in a relatively constrained vehicle, which can decouple significantly from underlying NAV.", "current_price": 53.5923, "matched_themes": ["special-situation-re-rating", "breakout-and-momentum"], "momentum_score": 92.2, "verdict_claude": "SKIP", "composite_score": 56.88, "last_event_date": "2026-05-11", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["special-situation-re-rating", "breakout-and-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst", "earnings-surprise-momentum"], "headline_drivers": ["Fund is heavily exposed to high‑profile private AI names like Anthropic and SpaceX; retail and social‑media hype around those holdings has driven a speculative re‑rating of the closed‑end fund’s shares far above its underlying portfolio value (highlighted in retail broker write‑ups, e.g., Public.com note that the fund has ‘jumped 1,200% on Anthropic and SpaceX hype,’ early May 2026).", "Persistent elevated trading volumes and repeated appearance on ‘top 20d / top 5d / volspike_gapper’ momentum screens indicate a momentum/technical chase and short‑squeeze dynamics in a relatively low‑float closed‑end fund, rather than a discrete new fundamental event (volume ~4x 10‑day average and recent volume spike magnitude 5.46 on 2026‑05‑11).", "No new 8‑K, earnings release, large acquisition, or named-customer fundamental development in the last 30–60 days that would independently justify a near‑term ~80% move; the vehicle’s own website and regulatory filings continue to describe the same strategy (closed‑end fund investing in top 100 venture‑backed tech companies) with no structural change to mandate or fee structure."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=99"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 3.92x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 12.2, "reason": "dr5=39.4% atr=9.6% norm=1.83"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 20, "reason": "3 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 2d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=78.0, 60d=78.6)"}}, "news_materiality": 0, "theme_fit_reason": "The name fits the trader's appetite for re-rating setups and technical momentum, especially when a fund trades far above its underlying value. It is only a 2 because the catalyst is mostly speculative sentiment rather than a true business or adoption inflection.", "verdict_rationale": "DXYZ has strong momentum, but the news does not clear the bar for real materiality: there is no new fundamental event, no beat-and-raise, and no named deal or operational inflection. It does fit a speculative special-situation/momentum theme, but without a substantive catalyst this looks more like a sympathy/chase move than the kind of news-driven setup the trader is screening for.", "latest_material_date": "2026-05-11", "news_materiality_reason": "There is no discrete company-specific catalyst here such as earnings, a named customer win, or a structural corporate event. The move is described as a speculative re-rating driven by hype around existing holdings and momentum/short-squeeze dynamics, which is not material fundamental news."}, {"ok": true, "dr_1": 0.73, "dr_5": 16.1, "dr_20": 12.14, "dr_60": 1.84, "sector": "Consumer Cyclical", "ticker": "TXRH", "sources": ["volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Restaurants", "theme_fit": 1, "market_cap": 12099901297, "rsi_mktcap": 94, "company_name": "Texas Roadhouse, Inc.", "news_summary": "The recent move in TXRH is primarily a continuation of the strong post–Q1 2026 earnings reaction. The company delivered a clean EPS beat, only a minor revenue shortfall, and pointed to solid traffic with some relief on commodity inflation, which improved confidence in margins and earnings power. That earnings-driven gap higher on May 8 has since been followed by momentum buying and a supportive rating/valuation narrative, rather than any new customer, M&A, or regulatory catalyst. In other words, the market is still repricing Texas Roadhouse off better-than-expected Q1 fundamentals and a perceived runway for further operating leverage, not reacting to a separate discrete event this week.", "current_price": 184.235, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise"], "momentum_score": 65.53, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "composite_score": 56.21, "last_event_date": "2026-05-08", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-surprise-momentum", "breakout-and-momentum"], "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings: GAAP EPS of $1.87 beat consensus by ~$0.08, while revenue of $1.63B was only slightly below estimates by about $10M; management highlighted strong same-store sales and traffic trends alongside easing commodity inflation pressures (earnings release and call, 2026-05-07/08)", "Post-earnings reaction: shares gapped up roughly 12% after the Q1 beat and constructive commentary on margins and cost inflation, with multiple outlets (MarketBeat, CNBC, Seeking Alpha, TipRanks) noting the stock’s surge and reaffirmed or constructive guidance (2026-05-08 coverage)", "Valuation and rating narrative: despite a modest price-target trim from Citigroup to ~$174 earlier in May, several research/ratings outlets (e.g., Wall Street Zen, GuruFocus-style fair value analyses) have highlighted TXRH as undervalued or a 'moderate buy,' reinforcing a re-rating after strong Q1 execution (late April–mid May 2026)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=94"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 0.90x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 15.53, "reason": "dr5=16.1% atr=3.1% norm=2.33"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "1 screen"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 5d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=12.1, 60d=1.8)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "TXRH fits the earnings-beat-and-raise theme partially—there is a quantified beat and constructive margin commentary—but the trader's pattern emphasizes explicit guidance raises and accelerating revenue/margin inflection. Here, management highlighted 'constructive guidance' but no formal raise is documented in the summary, and the revenue miss (even if small) undercuts the 'beat and raise' narrative. This is a solid beat but not the full trader-preferred pattern.", "verdict_rationale": "TXRH has genuine momentum (16.1% 5d return, RSI 94, post-earnings gap) and a material earnings beat, but falls short of the trader's core themes. The news is a classic earnings-driven re-rate with no big-ticket customer win, no AI/infrastructure angle, no new product inflection, and no special-situation re-rating catalyst. The stock is repricing off better Q1 fundamentals and margin relief, which is real but not the 'game-changing' or 'thematic' catalyst the trader's watchlist patterns suggest they hunt for. Momentum alone is not enough; this is a solid consumer cyclical beat, not a structural inflection or named catalyst the trader typically targets.", "latest_material_date": "2026-05-08", "news_materiality_reason": "Q1 2026 earnings beat ($1.87 GAAP EPS vs. $1.79 consensus) with constructive commentary on same-store sales, traffic, and margin relief from easing commodity inflation. The beat is clean and the forward narrative on operating leverage is material, though the revenue miss (minor, ~$10M) and lack of explicit guidance raise tempers the impact."}, {"ok": true, "dr_1": -6.13, "dr_5": 30.33, "dr_20": 9.14, "dr_60": -13.79, "sector": "Consumer Cyclical", "ticker": "BZH", "sources": ["volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "SKIP", "industry": "Residential Construction", "theme_fit": 1, "market_cap": 687719037, "rsi_mktcap": 91, "company_name": "Beazer Homes USA, Inc.", "news_summary": "The sharp 5-day move in Beazer Homes USA (BZH) with ~3x normal volume appears to be a delayed/technical reaction around its recently reported Q2 FY26 results and broader sector/macro flows, not a fresh, discrete catalyst in the last few days.\\n\\nOn April 30, 2026, Beazer reported Q2 FY26 results: homebuilding revenue of $397.7M, down 28.5% YoY, driven by a 29.8% drop in home closings to 757 units, partially offset by a 2.0% increase in average selling price to $525.4K. Homebuilding gross margin fell to 12.0% (−310 bps YoY), or 15.6% ex‑impairments, abandonments and amortized interest (−270 bps YoY). SG&A was $63.6M, down 6.5% YoY, but rose to 15.5% of revenue (+350 bps) due largely to the lower top line. Net new orders were 1,048 (−4.6% YoY) on a 7.2% decline in sales pace to 2.1 orders per community per month, partly offset by a 2.9% increase in average active communities to 167. A third‑party recap (QuiverQuant) pegs total Q2 revenue at $409.8M vs consensus $453.3M, with operating profit −$19.0M and net income to common −$0.9M, highlighting a miss and a swing into loss.\\n\\nThose April 30 earnings are the only clear, recent fundamental event. Since then, a second-pass review finds no additional material news: no new guidance update, no major land or M&A transactions, no notable insider buying/selling beyond routine patterns, no 13F-driven ownership shock, no high-profile analyst upgrade/downgrade, and no industry conference commentary specific to Beazer that would normally move the stock 30% in a week. There are also no rumors of large strategic partnerships (e.g., with Big Tech), and as a homebuilder BZH is not tied to the Apple/TSMC/NVIDIA-style supply-chain narratives that often drive squeezes elsewhere.\\n\\nGiven the timing (post-earnings digestion), the stock’s prior underperformance over 1–2 months, high RSI percentile, and appearance on volume-spike/gapper screens, the most plausible explanation is a positioning/technical move in a thinly followed small-cap homebuilder within a volatile, rate-sensitive sector. The price action looks like a squeeze/momentum burst off depressed levels rather than a reaction to new incremental information after the 2026-04-30 earnings release.", "current_price": 23.89, "matched_themes": ["breakout-and-momentum", "low-float-or-small-cap-catalyst"], "momentum_score": 64.72, "verdict_claude": "SKIP", "composite_score": 45.89, "last_event_date": "2026-05-11", "last_event_type": "volume_spike", "news_theme_tags": ["homebuilding", "housing-cycle", "small-cap", "rate-sensitive", "earnings-reaction", "technical-and-positioning", "breakout-and-momentum", "small-cap-relief-rally"], "headline_drivers": ["Q2 FY26 results: homebuilding revenue $397.7M (−28.5% YoY) on 757 closings (−29.8% YoY), ASP up 2% to $525.4K; homebuilding gross margin 12.0% (−310 bps YoY), ex‑impairments 15.6% (−270 bps); SG&A 15.5% of revenue, $63.6M (−6.5% YoY) (company press release, 2026-04-30)", "Q2 FY26 profitability and order trends: net new orders 1,048 (−4.6% YoY) with orders/community/month 2.1 (−7.2% YoY) and average active communities 167 (+2.9% YoY), indicating softer demand but modestly higher community count (company press release, 2026-04-30)", "Market reaction to Q2: BZH Q2 revenue $409.8M (−27.5% YoY) below Street consensus $453.3M, with operating profit −$19.0M and net income to common −$0.9M; stock traded lower on the print but has since seen elevated volume and volatility (QuiverQuant / earnings recap derived from company filing, 2026-04-30)", "Sector / macro context: move occurring against broader homebuilder and rate‑sensitive small‑cap volatility rather than any new post‑earnings company‑specific catalyst; no evidence of large M&A, marquee customer wins, major analyst initiation/upgrade, or regulatory events since Q2 report (multiple news/filing checks through mid‑May 2026)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=91"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 10, "reason": "vol 3.06x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 13.72, "reason": "dr5=30.3% atr=6.6% norm=2.06"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "1 screen"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 2d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "partial (20d=9.1, 60d=-13.8)"}}, "news_materiality": 1, "theme_fit_reason": "The name is showing a strong technical move with elevated volume, which fits the trader's momentum appetite. But it does not connect to the trader's higher-conviction themes like hyperscaler AI, opticals, big customer wins, or a meaningful re-rating story.", "verdict_rationale": "BZH is mainly a post-earnings technical/momentum move in a rate-sensitive homebuilder, not a fresh fundamental catalyst. The news is stale and actually soft on the fundamentals, so this does not meet the trader's preference for strong, materially inflective stories. It is off-theme relative to their usual AI/infrastructure and named-customer setup.", "latest_material_date": "2026-04-30", "news_materiality_reason": "The only real catalyst is the late-April Q2 FY26 earnings report, which was a miss on revenue and showed weaker margins and orders. There is no fresh discrete event in the last few days beyond post-earnings price digestion and sector volatility, so this is a minor catalyst rather than a strong news story."}], "failures": [], "failed_count": 0, "judged_count": 59, "score_weights": {"news": 0.3, "theme": 0.3, "momentum": 0.4}, "verdict_counts": {"PICK": 21, "SKIP": 5, "WATCH": 33}, "skipped_no_news": [{"ticker": "CVS", "company_name": "CVS Health Corporation"}], "pick_composite_min": 75, "watch_composite_min": 55, "skipped_no_news_count": 1}, "00_universe.json": {"date": "2026-05-13", "drops": [{"ticker": "RIGL", "drop_reason": "excluded_industry:Biotechnology"}, {"ticker": "INSM", "drop_reason": "excluded_industry:Biotechnolo