egrated Memory for AI/data‑center workloads, with margins improving even as Advanced Computing and Optimized LED margins are squeezed; investors treating this as an AI infrastructure lever rather than a legacy hardware vendor (earnings commentary Feb–Mar 2026)", "Forward earnings upgrades: Street models now bake in ~13–14% EPS growth next year and ~60%+ longer‑term earnings CAGR, driving a major P/E re‑rating despite consensus target still around $27–29 (MarketBeat / Simply Wall St updates through mid‑May 2026)", "Breakout to new all‑time highs and inclusion on momentum / top‑20d / gapper screens (+150%+ over 2 months, 52‑week range $16–$54) is pulling in systematic and retail momentum flows despite low incremental volume vs. 10‑day average"], "verify_triggered": false, "watchlist_thesis": null, "has_material_news": true, "latest_material_date": "2026-02-27"}, {"ticker": "GENI", "summary": "The recent 20–30% multi-week move in GENI is primarily a fundamental re‑rating around the Q1 2026 print and, more importantly, the much higher 2026 guidance issued after closing the Legend acquisition. Management is now guiding to nearly $1.0b in 2026 revenue and $270–280m in adjusted EBITDA (28% margin), versus prior $810–820m and $180–190m (~23% margin), which has led analysts and platforms to frame upside scenarios of $1.2–1.3b revenue and solid profitability by 2029 and price targets around $10–12+. With that step‑change in scale/margins established, the stock has then been pulled into momentum/technical screens (top‑5d, gapper) and bought by growth and retail traders, amplifying the move despite only modestly higher volume.", "theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "margin-and-growth-inflection", "story-driven-momentum"], "company_name": "Genius Sports Limited", "verify_reason": "skip_verify", "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 results: revenue $188m (+31% YoY) and adjusted EBITDA up 21%, reinforcing a strong growth/margin trajectory despite a wider net loss of ~$55m (earnings 