": "vol 1.97x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 5.21, "reason": "dr5=21.0% atr=12.0% norm=0.78"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 20, "reason": "3 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=54.6, 60d=137.1)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This is squarely in the trader’s AI infrastructure lane: funding GPUs, AI cloud/HPC buildout, and leverage to the AI compute cycle. It fits the pick-and-shovels infrastructure pattern they repeatedly favor, even without a named hyperscaler customer.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "SHAZ has both a concrete catalyst and a strong thematic fit: the Oaktree-led $350M financing is directly tied to scaling AI compute infrastructure, which is exactly the kind of story-backed momentum this trader likes. This is more than a sympathy move; it is a fresh capital event that supports the existing AI-infrastructure thesis and helps explain the breakout. No prior correction is relevant here.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.1625, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-22", "news_materiality_reason": "The $350M convertible note financing led by Oaktree is a real, disclosed capital event and it directly funds GPU and AI cloud infrastructure expansion. It is material, but it is not yet a marquee customer win, beat-and-raise, or transformational contract."}, {"dr_1": 2.48, "dr_5": 30.44, "atr20": 9.57, "dr_20": 42.6, "dr_60": 143.45, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "ALAB", "sources": ["main_view", "top_5d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "PICK", "industry": "Semiconductors", "theme_fit": 3, "market_cap": 52601668320, "rsi_mktcap": 100, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Astera Labs, Inc. Common Stock", "news_summary": "The market is mainly reacting to a strong Q1 2026 beat-and-raise plus an accelerating Scorpio product ramp in AI data-center connectivity. That fundamental upside has been reinforced by a broad AI semiconductor bid, which has helped push the stock into breakout territory and keep momentum buyers involved. I did not find a single new named-hyperscaler contract in the provided results that clearly explains the entire 5d/20d move on its own; this looks like a combination of earnings-driven re-rating and sector sympathy.", "current_price": 303.51, "matched_themes": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "ai-infrastructure-enablers", "memory-and-interconnect", "breakout-and-new-highs", "story-driven-momentum"], "momentum_score": 79.48, "verdict_claude": "PICK", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 0.86, "composite_score": 81.79, "last_event_date": "2026-05-19", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["earnings-beat-and-raise", "ai-infrastructure-enablers", "memory-and-interconnect", "breakout-and-new-highs", "story-driven-momentum"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Q1 2026 earnings and guidance: Astera Labs reported revenue of $308.4M, up 93% y/y, and raised Q2 2026 guidance to $355M-$365M with EPS of $0.44-$0.46, reinforcing the Scorpio ramp and AI-infrastructure demand (reported May 2026).", "Sector catalyst: ALAB has been moving with the broader AI infrastructure / semiconductor rally, with peers and the Nasdaq hitting fresh highs and semis catching a bid in late April-May 2026; this appears to be amplifying the post-earnings breakout.", "Bullish sell-side / target-reset narrative: Loop Capital and other analysts have continued to frame ALAB as a key AI data-center interconnect name, with some reports citing targets as high as $250-$250+ after the company’s growth and product ramp, supporting momentum trading into new highs."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=100"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 0.86x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 9.48, "reason": "dr5=30.4% atr=9.6% norm=1.42"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 20, "reason": "3 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 4d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=4