r in the last 60-90 days.", "No named Ming-Chi Kuo / DigiTimes / Wedbush / Loop Capital / Needham / Morgan Stanley note on Syntec Optics showed up in the search results, and I did not find a new design win or mass-production milestone tied to a specific marquee buyer.", "The strongest newly verified catalyst remains company-specific execution and balance-sheet relief in defense/space photonics, not a newly discovered external customer win; the recent surge still looks largely story- and momentum-driven around record bookings, shipment timing normalization, and the post-offering liquidity reset.", "Production surge in flagship ultra‑precision space optics line, with March 2026 monthly output reportedly 4x year‑over‑year, triggering a ~12% stock jump around $8.62 (GuruFocus / company disclosure, 2026-05-04)", "Record and diversified demand in defense, space (incl. low Earth orbit satellites), and biomedical optics, with Q4 2025 net sales of $7.505M (+2.5% YoY, +8% QoQ) and FY 2025 revenue of ~$28.1M while narrowing full‑year loss to -$0.049 per share (earnings release and commentary, 2026-03-31)", "Guidance for a strong rebound in Q2 2026 net sales to $7.5–$8.5M after a softer Q1, tied to record space-optics bookings and operational efficiencies (earnings call / Investing.com summary, 2026-03-31 & Q1 commentary in early May 2026)", "Strategic positioning to benefit from U.S. National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA) onshoring mandates for advanced optical systems, highlighting long-term defense and space backlog potential (company statement, 2026-03-23)", "Underwritten public equity offering of ~2.86M shares at $7.00 (plus 0.43M greenshoe) to raise ~$20M for acquisitions, capex and working capital, effectively clearing near-term funding overhang and being followed by price strength well above the offer level (offering announcement, 2026-04-28)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=98"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 