marquee customer win or a clearly quantified beat-and-raise setup. Strong momentum is there, and the theme is adjacent to the trader’s AI power-buildout interest, but this is not yet a clean PICK under the stricter rule because the catalyst is not sufficiently game-changing. No prior correction is relevant here.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.1887, "latest_material_date": "2026-04-28", "news_materiality_reason": "Q1 2026 earnings and the 8th-gen MOSFET/BatteryFET launch package are a real catalyst, but not a game-changing one: it’s a material quarterly update with product-news support rather than a named customer win or transformational contract. The late-May spike looks more like follow-through/short-covering on that April 28 event than a fresh, standalone news shock."}, {"dr_1": 16.22, "dr_5": 22.14, "atr20": 11.37, "dr_20": 40.56, "dr_60": 129.35, "sector": "Industrials", "ticker": "FLY", "sources": ["top_1d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Aerospace & Defense", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 7931642895, "rsi_mktcap": 99, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Firefly Aerospace Inc.", "news_summary": "The recent surge in FLY is primarily a reaction to Firefly Aerospace’s successful Alpha Flight 7 ‘Stairway to Seven’ launch in late May, which confirmed that its small-launch platform is working reliably in the market and reinforced earlier evidence that individual launches can be run at positive gross margins. That technical and commercial validation is feeding into an existing high‑growth narrative (revenue roughly doubling year-on-year, positive launch-level margins) and prompting a momentum and valuation re‑rating in a space/defense‑sensitive tape, rather than being driven by a fresh earnings beat or a newly announced mega‑contract. In other words, the stock’s 1–2 month spike looks like a combination of genuine fundamental validation from the successful mission plus ‘story‑driven’ buying in a thinly profitable, high‑multiple name.", "current_price": 49.38, "matched_themes": ["margin-and-growth-inflection", "story-driven-momentum", "breakout-and-new-highs", "special-situations-with-optional-downside"], "momentum_score": 67.81, "verdict_claude": "WATCH", "vol_vs_10d_avg": 1.1, "composite_score": 67.12, "last_event_date": "2026-05-22", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["margin-and-growth-inflection", "defense-and-geopolitical-tension", "story-driven-momentum", "breakout-and-new-highs", "special-situations-with-optional-downside"], "dropped_at_stage": null, "headline_drivers": ["Successful Alpha Flight 7 'Stairway to Seven' launch: Firefly Aerospace’s Alpha rocket completed a fully successful mission, widely reported with the stock up ~19% intraday on the news (Investing.com, 2026-05-20). This mission validates Alpha’s performance and unit economics and reinforces confidence in Firefly’s small‑/medium‑lift launch thesis.", "Evidence of improving unit economics and growth: Recent commentary and analysis highlight that Firefly’s revenue roughly doubled in the first nine months of 2025 to about $102M and that Alpha launches are generating positive gross margins (~27% in Q3 2025), supporting a ‘margin-and-growth-inflection’ narrative even though the company remains deeply unprofitable (YouTube analysis, Jan 2026).", "Momentum/valuation re‑rating post-launch: At a ~$7–8B market cap and ~38x sales, FLY is trading at a ‘story stock’ multiple; the successful Alpha mission has become a fresh proof point that is driving a momentum chase and short‑term re‑rating rather than a single discrete earnings surprise (various data points from TradingView, Robinhood, Gotrade)."], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=99"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 0.0, "reason": "vol 1.10x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 5.81, "reason": "dr5=22.1% atr=11.4% norm=0.87"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 12.0, "reason": "2 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=40.6, 60d=129.3)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This fits the trader’s preference for story-driven momentum with an operating inflection angle: the launch success reinforces a growth-and-margin narrative and is helping drive a breakout in a high-multiple name. It is not a direct AI or optical theme, but it does match the trader’s appetite for concrete catalysts behind a big move.", "has_material_news": true, "verdict_rationale": "Strong momentum, but the catalyst is a single successful launch rather than the kind of named-customer, earnings, or backlog event that usually earns a clean PICK. The news does support the emerging margin-and-growth-inflection story, but it’s still more of a validation-driven re-rate than a game-changing step-change. Consistent with the trader’s recent preference to avoid pure chart-chase, this is on-theme but not quite strong enough on materiality to be a PICK.", "last_event_magnitude": 0.1622, "latest_material_date": "2026-05-20", "news_materiality_reason": "The successful Alpha Flight 7 mission is a real, company-specific operational validation, not just sympathy trading. It materially supports Firefly’s launch reliability and unit economics, but it is still a single mission result rather than a transformative contract, beat/raise, or multi-year commercial unlock."}, {"dr_1": 12.97, "dr_5": 27.26, "atr20": 6.89, "dr_20": 68.07, "dr_60": 143.6, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "VSH", "sources": ["main_view", "top_1d", "top_5d"], "verdict": "WATCH", "industry": "Semiconductors", "theme_fit": 2, "market_cap": 6430999995, "rsi_mktcap": 99, "drop_reason": null, "company_name": "Vishay Intertechnology, Inc.", "news_summary": "I could not verify any hidden marquee-customer win, supply-chain rumor, or major analyst note tying VSH to a specific Apple/NVIDIA/TSMC-style customer roadmap. The strongest confirmed catalyst remains the 2026-05-13 Q1 print: revenue of $839.2M, EPS of $0.05, 21.