son": "both up (20d=62.3, 60d=79.4)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "HIVE fits the trader’s preferred AI infrastructure-enabler bucket and also has the exact kind of story-driven momentum they tend to like: a strategic pivot from crypto mining into GPU cloud / AI HPC with visible operating improvement. The record growth, uplisting, and expansion plans make this much more than a sympathy move.", "verdict_rationale": "Strong momentum plus real, material fundamentals is enough here: the stock has a fresh catalyst, not just chart heat. The news supports and extends the trader’s likely thesis on HIVE as a high-beta AI-infrastructure-and-crypto turnaround, with improving revenue, margins, and a concrete HPC buildout story rather than vague AI branding.", "latest_material_date": "2026-05-20", "news_materiality_reason": "This is a real, material company-specific catalyst: record Q3 FY2026 revenue (+219% YoY), positive adjusted EBITDA, a stated AI/HPC expansion plan, and an uplisting plus equity raise to fund it. It is not a marquee hyperscaler contract or multi-year named buyer win, so it stops short of a 3."}, {"ok": true, "dr_1": 16.25, "dr_5": 20.97, "dr_20": 54.63, "dr_60": 137.05, "sector": "Technology", "ticker": "SHAZ", "sources": ["main_view", "top_1d", "volspike_gapper"], "verdict": "PICK", "industry": "Information Technology Services", "theme_fit": 3, "market_cap": 666405611, "rsi_mktcap": 97, "company_name": "SharonAI Holdings, Inc. Class A Common Stock", "news_summary": "The sharp move in SharonAI (SHAZ) is being driven primarily by the recently disclosed $350M 6% convertible note financing led by Oaktree, which gives the company substantial growth capital to procure GPUs and build out AI cloud/HPC infrastructure, directly tying fresh funding to its core AI-compute story. That financing, with an initial conversion price around $48.24 and a capped share issuance, is being interpreted as a vote of confidence from sophisticated institutions despite some dilution risk. Layered on top of this is strong AI/HPC sector momentum and a sharp rebound after a brief profit-taking pullback, with elevated volume indicating both institutional positioning and short covering in a high-beta AI-infrastructure name rather than any single new customer or regulatory win. Overall the market is re-rating SHAZ as a better-capitalized, higher-growth AI compute infrastructure play, and the stock’s recent gap move looks like a momentum/positioning acceleration off that financing catalyst.", "current_price": 65.2368, "matched_themes": ["ai-compute", "ai-infrastructure-enablers", "ai-infrastructure-and-power-buildout", "story-driven-momentum"], "momentum_score": 81.21, "verdict_claude": "PICK", "composite_score": 82.48, "last_event_date": "2026-05-22", "last_event_type": "gapper", "news_theme_tags": ["ai-compute", "ai-infrastructure-enablers", "ai-infrastructure-and-power-buildout", "story-driven-momentum"], "headline_drivers": ["Announcement of a $350M 6.0% Convertible Senior Notes due 2031 financing led by Oaktree Capital and other institutional investors to fund GPU and AI cloud infrastructure expansion (8-K filing, late May 2026)", "Strong post-earnings momentum and AI/HPC sentiment: shares have more than doubled YTD and are viewed as a leveraged play on AI compute and data-center build-out, with recent profit-taking followed by renewed buying as stock regains momentum (May 2026)"], "momentum_factors": {"rsi_mktcap": {"points": 15, "reason": "rsi_mktcap=97"}, "vol_vs_avg": {"points": 6.0, "reason": "vol 1.97x"}, "dr5_atr_norm": {"points": 5.21, "reason": "dr5=21.0% atr=12.0% norm=0.78"}, "multi_screen": {"points": 20, "reason": "3 screens"}, "recent_event": {"points": 20, "reason": "event 1d ago"}, "trend_alignment": {"points": 15, "reason": "both up (20d=54.6, 60d=137.1)"}}, "news_materiality": 2, "theme_fit_reason": "This is squarely in the trader’s AI infrastructure lane: funding GPUs, AI cloud/HPC buildout, and leverage to the AI 