on September 30 and closed at $30.31 on October 2, down 0.49% that day. It is now near the top of its $10.95–$32.45 52-week range, while consensus analyst sentiment remains Hold and the average target of about $20.80 sits well below the current share price—clear evidence that valuation is the main counterweight to the momentum. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/SDGR)\n\n## Key drivers, ranked\n\n1. **Tectora spinout and licensing deal — September 9.** Schrödinger co-founded Tectora with NEA and RA Capital; Tectora raised a $55 million Series A. Schrödinger contributed two early-stage small-molecule programs, SDGR-4594 and SDGR-8139, receiving an equity stake plus eligibility for milestones and royalties. President of Therapeutics R&D and Chief Strategy Officer Karen Akinsanya said similar company-building partnerships have generated more than $750 million of proceeds for Schrödinger collectively. This concretely validates the asset-monetization strategy, although the consideration is largely future and contingent. [markets.ft](https://markets.ft.com/data/announce/detail?dockey=600-202609090700BIZWIRE_USPRX____20260909_BW340138-1)\n\n2. **AI/software narrative and conference remarks — September 14–17.** At Morgan Stanley’s healthcare conference, management highlighted new products including **Bunsen**, an agentic AI co-scientist, and Predictive Tox, as well as hosted-software growth and a path to profitability by 2028. The stock rose 9.1% on September 14, 12.1% on September 15, and 26.4% on September 17, closing at $30.24. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/SDGR)\n\n3. **Earlier Q2 earnings foundation — August 5.** Investors were also building on Q2 results: adjusted EPS of **$0.08**, versus consensus for a loss, revenue of **$58.9 million** versus roughly $48 million expected, and annual contract value growth of **27%**. Those figures gave the September partnership/AI narrative underlying operating credibility. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/SDGR)\n\n4. **Bristol Myers Squibb agreement — August 5.** BMS entered a strategic collaboration and software agreement to deploy Schrödinger’s Bunsen across its research organization. The company did not announce transaction economics in the material reviewed, but BMS adoption supports the commercial relevance of the product that management later showcased. [ir.schrodinger](https://ir.schrodinger.com/press-releases/default.aspx)\n\n5. **Momentum and valuation debate — late September.** After hitting a two-year/52-week high around $31.59–$32 in late September, shares pulled back on profit-taking, broader pressure on long-duration software names, and attention to President Karen Akinsanya’s roughly $928,000 September 17 sale under a prearranged 10b5-1 plan. These look like modifiers to the move rather than its original cause. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/SDGR)\n\n## 10-word summary\n\n**Tectora spinout, AI adoption, and Q2 beat drive 45% rally.**	2026-10-04 17:35:01.252975-04	2026-10-04 17:35:01.252975-04
