eliable launch-day return.  [finance.yahoo](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/dates-could-move-meta-stock-153443222.html) | Muse introduced a new consumer-facing AI product and a potential future commerce revenue stream. Its subsequent adoption became the central catalyst for September’s rally.  [finance.yahoo](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/meta-muse-dominating-app-store-144019978.html) |\n| September 11–14, 2026 | Analyst upgrades following Muse’s launch | +0.57% on September 11 and +2.71% on September 14.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | JPMorgan upgraded META to Overweight with an $820 target; other analysts highlighted early Muse traction. The September 14 gain came despite weakness elsewhere in technology stocks, making it a more clearly company-specific positive session.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) |\n| September 15–16, 2026 | Meta One subscription launch and in-house AI chip plans | +0.70% on September 15; +0.46% on September 16.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | The subscription offering created another potential revenue channel beyond advertising, while plans for the next-generation MTIA chip supported hopes of lowering AI infrastructure costs and reducing reliance on external suppliers.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) |\n| September 18, 2026 | French criminal probe involving AI smart glasses, alongside rising yields | −2.43%, closing at $665.75.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | Reports of a Paris investigation into potential nonconsensual filming added regulatory risk to Meta’s hardware strategy. Broader communication-services weakness and higher Treasury yields also contributed, so this was a mixed company/macro move.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) |\n| September 21, 2026 | Muse reaches the top of app-store rankings; Wells Fargo raises its target | Approximately +11.3%, closing near $741.25.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | Wells Fargo raised its target from $640 to $796 as rapid Muse adoption strengthened the argument that Meta’s AI spending could produce commercially valuable products. This was the standout positive catalyst in the period.  [finance.yahoo](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/meta-stock-jumped-11-monday-075049227.html) |\n| September 23–24, 2026 | Meta Connect: new glasses, deeper Muse integration and commerce partnerships | +1.02% on September 23, followed by +4.50% on September 24 to $777.59.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | New hardware and partnerships expanded the potential uses of Muse beyond a standalone app. Bullish analyst target increases reinforced the rally; on September 24, META substantially outperformed the broader market.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) |\n| September 25, 2026 | New Mexico verdict and skepticism about Muse monetization | −3.33%, closing at $751.66.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | A jury finding against Meta in the Cambridge Analytica case added legal uncertainty. At the same time, Oppenheimer questioned how much near-term revenue Muse could generate, and investors took profits after the sharp rally.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) |\n| September 28, 2026 | Broad market selloff coincides with Meta Enterprise Platform launch | −4.79%, closing at $715.62.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | Rising oil prices and Treasury yields drove a wider tech selloff. Meta’s enterprise launch was a potentially positive company development, but macro pressure, valuation concerns and legal risk dominated the session.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) |\n| September 29, 2026 | Enterprise-AI optimism and analyst target increases | +3.24%, closing at $738.79.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | Investors refocused on Meta’s enterprise opportunity. BNP Paribas raised its target to $885 and JPMorgan lifted its target to $920, helping the shares rebound after two down sessions.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) |\n| October 7, 2026 | Higher Treasury yields and renewed growth-stock selling | −2.38%, closing at $721.31.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) | This was primarily a macro/valuation event: higher yields and inflation concerns pressured growth stocks. Meta also faced an ongoing New Mexico legal overhang and questions about AI spending.  [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META) |\n\n## Other dated headlines with limited immediate price impact\n\nThese were relevant catalysts, but the available evidence does not support calling them major standalone stock movers:\n\n- October 1: New Mexico requested penalties of up to $40 billion. META finished approximately +0.10% that day, so the headline created a legal overhang rather than an immediate large selloff. A requested penalty is not an awarded penalty. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META)\n- October 6: Wells Fargo raised its target to $1,000 from $796. The stock nevertheless fell about 0.41% as legal, regulatory and interest-rate concerns offset the bullish research. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META)\n- October 8–9: Reports that Meta was blocking ByteDance/TikTok advertising in several markets coincided with new skepticism about Muse adoption and accessibility. META was nearly flat on October 8 and fell 0.31% on October 9—not a large immediate reaction. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META)\n\n## What drove the period\n\nThe clearest pattern was a shift from concern about AI costs to optimism about AI products:\n\n1. July’s earnings selloff reflected the gap between strong revenue growth and weak cash generation after infrastructure spending. [finance.yahoo](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/article/one-line-from-metas-earnings-call-that-ensured-the-stock-will-likely-stay-dead-money-134542007.html)\n2. September’s rally reflected Muse adoption, analyst upgrades, and new hardware and commerce opportunities—not yet demonstrated large-scale Muse revenue. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META)\n3. Late-September and October pullbacks showed that legal exposure, monetization doubts and higher interest rates could still interrupt that optimism. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META)\n\nFor a compact event-study shortlist, the most consequential dates are July 30, September 21, September 24, September 25, September 28 and September 29. They capture the earnings shock, the Muse-driven re-rating, and the subsequent reversal and rebound. [perplexity](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/META)	2026-10-12 05:22:08.604937-04	2026-10-12 05:22:08.604937-04
